    804: "אַשּׁוּר (ʼAshshûwr | ash-shoor')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or אַשֻּׁר; apparently from H833 אָשַׁר (in the sense of successful)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Ashshur, the second son of Shem; also his descendants and the country occupied by them (i.e. Assyria), its region and its empire<BR><B>KJV:</B> Asshur, Assur, Assyria, Assyrians. See H838 אָשֻׁר .<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2977 (Josiah), H810 (stone), H805 (Asshurim), H807 (Ashima), H804 (Asshur), H803 (foundation), H812 (Eshcol), H811 (cluster), H813 (Ashkenaz)",
    805: "אֲשׁוּרִי (ʼĂshûwrîy | ash-oo-ree')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or אַשּׁוּרִי; from a patrial word of the same form as H804 אַשּׁוּר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an Ashurite (collectively) or inhabitant of Ashur, a district in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Asshurim, Ashurites.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2977 (Josiah), H810 (stone), H805 (Asshurim), H807 (Ashima), H804 (Asshur), H803 (foundation), H812 (Eshcol), H811 (cluster), H813 (Ashkenaz)",
    806: "אַשְׁחוּר (ʼAshchûwr | ash-khoor')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from H7835 שָׁחַר ; black<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Ashchur, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Ashur.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7815 (coal), H806 (Ashur), H7840 (black), H7835 (be black), H7839 (youth), H7838 (black)",
