    808: "אָשִׁישׁ (ʼâshîysh | aw-sheesh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as H784 אֵשׁ (in the sense of pressing down firmly; compare H803 אֲשׁוּיָה)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a (ruined) foundation<BR><B>KJV:</B> foundation.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H850 (Eshton), H808 (foundation), H848 (Eshtaulites), H851 (Eshtemoa), H809 (flagon), H847 (Eshtaol), H377 (show self a man)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2730 κατοικέω",
    809: "אֲשִׁישָׁה (ʼăshîyshâh | ash-ee-shaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of H808 אָשִׁישׁ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something closely pressed together, i.e. a cake of raisins or other comfits<BR><B>KJV:</B> flagon.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H850 (Eshton), H808 (foundation), H848 (Eshtaulites), H851 (Eshtemoa), H809 (flagon), H847 (Eshtaol), H377 (show self a man)",
    810: "אֶשֶׁךְ (ʼeshek | eh'-shek)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root (probably meaning to bunch together)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a testicle (as a lump)<BR><B>KJV:</B> stone.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2977 (Josiah), H810 (stone), H805 (Asshurim), H807 (Ashima), H804 (Asshur), H803 (foundation), H812 (Eshcol), H811 (cluster), H813 (Ashkenaz)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3693 ὄπισθεν",
