    823: "אַשְׁנָה (ʼAshnâh | ash-naw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably a variation for H3466 יְשָׁנָה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Ashnah, the name of two places in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Ashnah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H823 (Ashnah)",
    824: "אֶשְׁעָן (ʼEshʻân | esh-awn')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H8172 שָׁעַן ; support<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Eshan, a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Eshean.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H8172 (lean), H824 (Eshean), H4938 (staff), H4937 (stay)",
    825: "אַשָּׁף (ʼashshâph | ash-shawf')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root (probably meaning to lisp, i.e. practice enchantment)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a conjurer<BR><B>KJV:</B> astrologer.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H825 (astrologer)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3097 μάγος, G5386 φιλόσοφος",
    826: "אַשָּׁף (ʼashshâph | ash-shawf')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H825 אַשָּׁף<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a conjurer<BR><B>KJV:</B> astrologer.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H783 (Artaxerxes), H773 (bottom), H846 (wall), H778 (earth), H772 (earth), H749 (be meet), H826 (astrologer), H756 (Archevite), H785 (flame), H787 (foundation)",
    827: "אַשְׁפָּה (ʼashpâh | ash-paw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> perhaps (feminine) from the same as H825 אַשָּׁף (in the sense of covering)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a quiver or arrow-case<BR><B>KJV:</B> quiver.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H827 (quiver), H832 (Eshkalonites), H828 (Ashpenaz), H831 (Ashkelon), H829 (good piece)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1939 ἐπιθυμία, G5115 τόξον",
    828: "אַשְׁפְּנַז (ʼAshpᵉnaz | ash-pen-az')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of foreign origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Ashpenaz, a Babylonian eunuch<BR><B>KJV:</B> Ashpenaz.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H827 (quiver), H832 (Eshkalonites), H828 (Ashpenaz), H831 (Ashkelon), H829 (good piece)",
    829: "אֶשְׁפָּר (ʼeshpâr | esh-pawr')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a measured portion<BR><B>KJV:</B> good piece (of flesh).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H827 (quiver), H832 (Eshkalonites), H828 (Ashpenaz), H831 (Ashkelon), H829 (good piece)",
    830: "אַשְׁפֹּת (ʼashpôth | ash-pohth')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or אַשְׁפֹּות; or שְׁפֹת; (contraction) plural of a noun of the same form as H827 אַשְׁפָּה, from H8192 שָׁפָה (in the sense of scraping)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a heap of rubbish or filth<BR><B>KJV:</B> dung (hill).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H8239 (bring), H4942 (burden), H8240 (hook), H830 (dung)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2874 κοπρία",
    831: "אַשְׁקְלֹון (ʼAshqᵉlôwn | ash-kel-one')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from H8254 שָׁקַל in the sense of weighing-place (i.e. mart)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Ashkelon, a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Ashkelon, Askalon.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H827 (quiver), H832 (Eshkalonites), H828 (Ashpenaz), H831 (Ashkelon), H829 (good piece)",
    832: "אֶשְׁקְלֹונִי (ʼEshqᵉlôwnîy | esh-kel-o-nee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> patrial from H831 אַשְׁקְלֹון<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Ashkelonite (collectively) or inhabitant of Ashkelon<BR><B>KJV:</B> Eshkalonites.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H827 (quiver), H832 (Eshkalonites), H828 (Ashpenaz), H831 (Ashkelon), H829 (good piece)",
    833: "אָשַׁר (ʼâshar | aw-shar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or אָשֵׁר; a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be straight (used in the widest sense, especially to be level, right, happy); figuratively, to go forward, be honest, proper<BR><B>KJV:</B> (call, be) bless(-ed, happy), go, guide, lead, relieve.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H843 (Asherites), H835 (blessed), H838 (going), H842 (grove), H837 (happy), H836 (Asher), H833 (bless), H839 (Ashurite), H8391 (box)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G804 ἀσφαλής, G2206 ζηλόω, G2720 κατευθύνω, G3106 μακαρίζω, G4105 πλανάω",
    834: "אֲשֶׁר (ʼăsher | ash-er')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive relative pronoun (of every gender and number)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> who, which, what, that; also (as an adverb and a conjunction) when, where, how, because, in order that, etc.<BR><B>KJV:</B> [idiom] after, [idiom] alike, as (soon as), because, [idiom] every, for, [phrase] forasmuch, [phrase] from whence, [phrase] how(-soever), [idiom] if, (so) that ((thing) which, wherein), [idiom] though, [phrase] until, [phrase] whatsoever, when, where ([phrase] -as, -in, -of, -on, -soever, -with), which, whilst, [phrase] whither(-soever), who(-m, -soever, -se). As it is indeclinable, it is often accompanied by the personal pronoun expletively, used to show the connection.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H834 ([idiom] after)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2509 καθάπερ, G2526 καθό, G2530 καθότι, G3778 οὗτος, G5101 τίς, G5101 τίς, G5158 τρόπος, G5158 τρόπος",
