    854: "אֵת (ʼêth | ayth)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from H579 אָנָה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, nearness (used only as a preposition or an adverb), near; hence, generally, with, by, at, among, etc.<BR><B>KJV:</B> against, among, before, by, for, from, in(-to), (out) of, with. Often with another prepositional prefix.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H863 (Ithai), H384 (Ithiel), H854 (against), H856 (Ethbaal)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3694 ὀπίσω",
