    920: "בִּדְקַר (Bidqar | bid-car')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from H1856 דָּקַר with a prepositional prefix; by stabbing, i.e. assassin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Bidkar, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Bidkar.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H918 (repair), H919 (breach), H920 (Bidkar)",
    921: "בְּדַר (bᵉdar | bed-ar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding (by transposition) to H6504 פָּרַד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to scatter<BR><B>KJV:</B> scatter.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H921 (scatter)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1287 διασκορπίζω",
    922: "בֹּהוּ (bôhûw | bo'-hoo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root (meaning to be empty)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a vacuity, i.e. (superficially) an undistinguishable ruin<BR><B>KJV:</B> emptiness, void.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H922 (emptiness), H923 (red)",
