    2166: "זְמָן (zᵉmân | zem-awn')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) from H2165 זְמָן ; the same as H2165 זְמָן<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an appointed occasion<BR><B>KJV:</B> season, time.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2166 (season), H2164 (prepare)",
    2167: "זָמַר (zâmar | zaw-mar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root (perhaps identical with H2168 זָמַר through the idea of striking with the fingers); properly, to touch the strings or parts of a musical instrument, i.e.<BR><B>Strong's:</B> play upon it; to make music, accompanied by the voice; hence to celebrate in song and music<BR><B>KJV:</B> give praise, sing forth praises, psalms.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2172 (melody), H4210 (psalm), H2158 (psalm), H2176 (song), H2167 (give praise)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5214 ὑμνέω, G5567 ψάλλω",
    2168: "זָמַר (zâmar | zaw-mar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root (compare H2167 זָמַר, H5568 סָמַר, H6785 צֶמֶר)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to trim (a vine)<BR><B>KJV:</B> prune.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2156 (vine), H4212 (snuffers), H2168 (prune), H2159 (branch), H4211 (pruning-hook)",
