    2194: "זָעַם (zâʻam | zaw-am')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to foam at the mouth, i.e. to be enraged<BR><B>KJV:</B> abhor, abominable, (be) angry, defy, (have) indignation.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2195 (angry), H2194 (abhor)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G546 ἀπειλέω, G1863 ἐπάγω, G2373 θυμόω, G2672 καταράομαι, G3404 μισέω, G3710 ὀργίζω",
