    2714: "חֵקֶר (chêqer | khay'-ker)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H2713 חָקַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> examination, enumeration, deliberation<BR><B>KJV:</B> finding out, number, (un-) search(-able, -ed, out, -ing).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2713 (find out), H4278 (deep place), H2714 (finding out)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2487 ἴχνος, G4009 πέρας",
    2715: "חֹר (chôr | khore)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or (fully) חֹור; from H2787 חָרַר ; (compare H2751 חֹרִי)<BR><BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, white or pure (from the cleansing or shining power of fire; hence (figuratively) noble (in rank)<BR><B>KJV:</B> noble.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2715 (noble)",
    2716: "חֶרֶא (chereʼ | kheh'-reh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused (and vulgar) root probably meaning to evacuate the bowels<BR><B>Strong's:</B> excrement<BR><B>KJV:</B> dung. Also חֲרִי.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4280 (draught house), H2716 (dung)",
