    2728: "חָרְגֹּל (chârᵉgôl | khar-gole')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H2727 חָרַג<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the leaping insect, i.e. a locust<BR><B>KJV:</B> beetle.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2728 (beetle)",
    2729: "חָרַד (chârad | khaw-rad')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to shudder with terror; hence, to fear; also to hasten (with anxiety)<BR><B>KJV:</B> be (make) afraid, be careful, discomfit, fray (away), quake, tremble.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2733 (Harodite), H5878 (well of Harod), H2731 (care), H2730 (afraid), H2729 (be afraid), H2732 (Haradah)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1377 διώκω",
    2730: "חָרֵד (chârêd | khaw-rade')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H2729 חָרַד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> fearful; also reverential<BR><B>KJV:</B> afraid, trembling.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2733 (Harodite), H5878 (well of Harod), H2731 (care), H2730 (afraid), H2729 (be afraid), H2732 (Haradah)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1169 δειλός, G1629 ἐκφοβέω, G1839 ἐξίστημι, G2983 λαμβάνω, G3926 παρενοχλέω, G4422 πτοέω, G5015 ταράσσω, G5399 φοβέω, G5401 φόβος",
