    2746: "חַרְחֻר (charchur | khar-khoor')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H2787 חָרַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> fever (as hot)<BR><B>KJV:</B> extreme burning.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2744 (Harhur), H2787 (be angry), H2788 (parched place), H2746 (extreme burning)",
    2747: "חֶרֶט (chereṭ | kheh'-ret)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a primitive root meaning to engrave<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a chisel or graver; also a style forwriting<BR><B>KJV:</B> graving tool, pen.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2747 (graving tool), H2748 (magician)",
