    2907: "טוּשׂ (ṭûws | toos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to pounce as a bird of prey<BR><B>KJV:</B> haste.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2907 (haste)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4072 πέτομαι",
    2908: "טְוָת (ṭᵉvâth | tev-awth')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H2901 טָוָה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> hunger (as twisting)<BR><B>KJV:</B> fasting.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2877 (guard), H2920 (dew), H2869 (fine), H2908 (fasting), H2906 (mountain), H2927 (have a shadow), H2868 (be glad), H2917 (miry)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2218 ζυγός, G3523 νῆστις",
    2909: "טָחָה (ṭâchâh | taw-khaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to stretch a bow, as an archer<BR><B>KJV:</B> (bow-) shot.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2909 (shot)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1000 βολή",
    2910: "טֻחָה (ṭuchâh | too-khaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H2909 טָחָה (or H2902 טוּחַ) in the sense of overlaying<BR><B>Strong's:</B> (in the plural only) the kidneys (as being covered); hence (figuratively) the inmost thought<BR><B>KJV:</B> inward parts.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2910 (inward parts), H2902 (daub), H2915 (daubing)",
