    2912: "טָחַן (ṭâchan | taw-khan')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to grind meal; hence, to be aconcubine (that being their employment)<BR><B>KJV:</B> grind(-er).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2912 (grind), H2902 (daub), H2913 (grinding), H2911 (to grind)",
