    2914: "טְחֹר (ṭᵉchôr | tekh-ore')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to burn<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a boil or ulcer (from the inflammation), especially a tumorin the anus or pudenda (the piles)<BR><B>KJV:</B> emerod.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2914 (emerod)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3491 ναῦς",
    2915: "טִיחַ (ṭîyach | tee'akh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from (the equiv. of) H2902 טוּחַ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> mortar or plaster<BR><B>KJV:</B> daubing.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2910 (inward parts), H2902 (daub), H2915 (daubing)",
