    2919: "טַל (ṭal | tal)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H2926 טָלַל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> dew (as covering vegetation)<BR><B>KJV:</B> dew.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2919 (dew)",
    2920: "טַל (ṭal | tal)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) the same as H2919 טַל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> dew (as covering vegetation)<BR><B>KJV:</B> dew.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2877 (guard), H2920 (dew), H2869 (fine), H2908 (fasting), H2906 (mountain), H2927 (have a shadow), H2868 (be glad), H2917 (miry)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2386 ἴαμα",
    2921: "טָלָא (ṭâlâʼ | taw-law')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to cover with pieces; i.e. (by implication) to spot or variegate (as tapestry)<BR><B>KJV:</B> clouted, with divers colours, spotted.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2923 (Telaim), H2921 (clouted)",
