    2934: "טָמַן (ṭâman | taw-man')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to hide (by covering over)<BR><B>KJV:</B> hide, lay privily, in secret.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4301 (hidden riches), H2934 (hide)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1470 ἐγκρύπτω, G1607 ἐκπορεύομαι, G2928 κρύπτω, G5278 ὑπομένω",
    2935: "טֶנֶא (ṭeneʼ | teh'-neh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root probably meaning to weave<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a basket (of interlaced osiers)<BR><B>KJV:</B> basket.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2935 (basket)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G596 ἀποθήκη",
    2936: "טָנַף (ṭânaph | taw-naf')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to soil<BR><B>KJV:</B> defile.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2936 (defile)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3435 μολύνω",
    2937: "טָעָה (ṭâʻâh | taw-aw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to wander; causatively to lead astray<BR><B>KJV:</B> seduce.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2937 (seduce)",
