    3513: "כָּבַד (kâbad | kaw-bad')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or כָּבֵד; a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be heavy, i.e. in a bad sense (burdensome, severe, dull) or in a good sense (numerous, rich, honorable; causatively, to make weighty (in the same two senses)<BR><B>KJV:</B> abounding with, more grievously afflict, boast, be chargeable, [idiom] be dim, glorify, be (make) glorious (things), glory, (very) great, be grievous, harden, be (make) heavy, be heavier, lay heavily, (bring to, come to, do, get, be had in) honour (self), (be) honourable (man), lade, [idiom] more be laid, make self many, nobles, prevail, promote (to honour), be rich, be (go) sore, stop.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3519 (glorious), H3517 ([idiom] heavily), H3514 (grievousness), H3515 (great), H3516 (liver), H3513 (abounding with), H3520 (carriage)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G191 ἀκούω, G916 βαρέω, G916 βαρέω, G917 βαρέως, G926 βαρύς, G1391 δόξα, G1392 δοξάζω, G1740 ἐνδοξάζω, G1741 ἔνδοξος, G1765 ἐνισχύω, G1784 ἔντιμος, G2127 εὐλογέω, G2729 κατισχύω, G3173 μέγας, G4060 περιτίθημι, G4121 πλεονάζω, G4645 σκληρύνω, G5091 τιμάω, G5092 τιμή",
    3514: "כֹּבֶד (kôbed | ko'-bed)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3513 כָּבַד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> weight, multitude, vehemence<BR><B>KJV:</B> grievousness, heavy, great number.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3519 (glorious), H3517 ([idiom] heavily), H3514 (grievousness), H3515 (great), H3516 (liver), H3513 (abounding with), H3520 (carriage)",
    3515: "כָּבֵד (kâbêd | kaw-bade')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3513 כָּבַד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> heavy; figuratively in a good sense (numerous) or in a bad sense (severe, difficult, stupid)<BR><B>KJV:</B> (so) great, grievous, hard(-ened), (too) heavy(-ier), laden, much, slow, sore, thick.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3519 (glorious), H3517 ([idiom] heavily), H3514 (grievousness), H3515 (great), H3516 (liver), H3513 (abounding with), H3520 (carriage)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G926 βαρύς, G2478 ἰσχυρός, G4128 πλῆθος, G4134 πλήρης, G4145 πλούσιος",
    3516: "כָּבֵד (kâbêd | kaw-bade')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> the same as H3515 כָּבֵד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the liver (as the heaviest of the viscera)<BR><B>KJV:</B> liver.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3519 (glorious), H3517 ([idiom] heavily), H3514 (grievousness), H3515 (great), H3516 (liver), H3513 (abounding with), H3520 (carriage)",
    3517: "כְּבֵדֻת (kᵉbêduth | keb-ay-dooth')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of H3515 כָּבֵד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> difficulty<BR><B>KJV:</B> [idiom] heavily.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3519 (glorious), H3517 ([idiom] heavily), H3514 (grievousness), H3515 (great), H3516 (liver), H3513 (abounding with), H3520 (carriage)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G970 βία",
    3518: "כָּבָה (kâbâh | kaw-baw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to expire or (causatively) to extinguish (fire, light, anger)<BR><B>KJV:</B> go (put) out, quench.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3518 (go out), H3521 (Cabul)",
