    3520: "כְּבוּדָּה (kᵉbûwddâh | keb-ood-daw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> irregular feminine passive participle of H3513 כָּבַד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> weightiness, i.e. magnificence, wealth<BR><B>KJV:</B> carriage, all glorious, stately.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3519 (glorious), H3517 ([idiom] heavily), H3514 (grievousness), H3515 (great), H3516 (liver), H3513 (abounding with), H3520 (carriage)",
    3521: "כָּבוּל (Kâbûwl | kaw-bool')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as H3525 כֶּבֶל in the sense of limitation; sterile<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Cabul, the name of two places in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Cabul.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3518 (go out), H3521 (Cabul)",
    3522: "כַּבֹּון (Kabbôwn | kab-bone')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to heap up; hilly<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Cabon, a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Cabbon.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4344 (Machbanai), H3522 (Cabbon), H4343 (Machbenah)",
    3523: "כְּבִיר (kᵉbîyr | keb-eer)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3527 כָּבַר in the original sense of plaiting<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a matrass (of intertwined materials)<BR><B>KJV:</B> pillow.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4346 (thick cloth), H3535 (lamb), H4345 (grate), H3523 (pillow), H3776 (lamb), H3775 (lamb), H3531 (sieve), H3532 (lamb)",
    3524: "כַּבִּיר (kabbîyr | kab-beer')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3527 כָּבַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> vast, whether in extent (figuratively, of power, mighty; of time, aged), or in number, many<BR><B>KJV:</B> [phrase] feeble, mighty, most, much, strong, valiant.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3528 (already), H3527 (in abundance), H4342 (abundance), H3529 (Chebar), H3530 ([idiom] little), H3524 (feeble)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G926 βαρύς, G1415 δυνατός, G1741 ἔνδοξος, G1784 ἔντιμος, G4128 πλῆθος",
    3525: "כֶּבֶל (kebel | keh'-bel)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to twine or braid together<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a fetter<BR><B>KJV:</B> fetter.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3525 (fetter)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3976 πέδη",
    3526: "כָּבַס (kâbaç | kaw-bas')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to trample; hence, to wash (properly, by stamping with the feet), whether literal (including the fulling process) or figurative<BR><B>KJV:</B> fuller, wash(-ing).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3526 (fuller)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G637 ἀποπλύνω, G1102 γναφεύς, G4150 πλύνω",
    3527: "כָּבַר (kâbar | kaw-bar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to plait together, i.e. (figuratively) to augment (especially in number or quantity, to accumulate)<BR><B>KJV:</B> in abundance, multiply.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3528 (already), H3527 (in abundance), H4342 (abundance), H3529 (Chebar), H3530 ([idiom] little), H3524 (feeble)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2480 ἰσχύω",
    3528: "כְּבָר (kᵉbâr | keb-awr')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3527 כָּבַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, extent of time, i.e. a great while; hence, long ago, formerly, hitherto<BR><B>KJV:</B> already, (seeing that which), now.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3528 (already), H3527 (in abundance), H4342 (abundance), H3529 (Chebar), H3530 ([idiom] little), H3524 (feeble)",
