    3532: "כֶּבֶשׂ (kebes | keh-bes')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to dominate<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a ram (just old enough to butt)<BR><B>KJV:</B> lamb, sheep.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4346 (thick cloth), H3535 (lamb), H4345 (grate), H3523 (pillow), H3776 (lamb), H3775 (lamb), H3531 (sieve), H3532 (lamb)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G286 ἀμνός, G704 ἀρήν, G721 ἀρνίον, G4263 πρόβατον",
