    3534: "כֶּבֶשׁ (kebesh | keh'-besh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3533 כָּבַשׁ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a footstool (as trodden upon)<BR><B>KJV:</B> footstool.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3533 (bring into bondage), H3534 (footstool), H3536 (furnace)",
    3535: "כִּבְשָׂה (kibsâh | kib-saw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or כַּבְשָׂה; feminine of H3532 כֶּבֶשׂ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a ewe<BR><B>KJV:</B> (ewe) lamb.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4346 (thick cloth), H3535 (lamb), H4345 (grate), H3523 (pillow), H3776 (lamb), H3775 (lamb), H3531 (sieve), H3532 (lamb)",
    3536: "כִּבְשָׁן (kibshân | kib-shawn')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3533 כָּבַשׁ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a smelting furnace (as reducing metals)<BR><B>KJV:</B> furnace.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3533 (bring into bondage), H3534 (footstool), H3536 (furnace)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2575 κάμινος",
    3537: "כַּד (kad | kad)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to deepen<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, a pail; but generally of earthenware; a jar for domestic purposes<BR><B>KJV:</B> barrel, pitcher.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3539 (agate), H3537 (barrel), H3590 (spark)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5201 ὑδρία",
