    3539: "כַּדְכֹּד (kadkôd | kad-kode')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as H3537 כַּד in the sense of striking fire from a metal forged<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a sparkling gem, probably the ruby<BR><B>KJV:</B> agate.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3539 (agate), H3537 (barrel), H3590 (spark)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2393 ἴασπις",
    3540: "כְּדׇרְלָעֹמֶר (Kᵉdorlâʻômer | ked-or-law-o'-mer)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of foreign origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Kedorlaomer, an early Persian king<BR><B>KJV:</B> Chedorlaomer.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3540 (Chedorlaomer), H1754 (ball), H3593 (battle)",
    3541: "כֹּה (kôh | ko)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the prefix k and H1931 הוּא<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, like this, i.e. by implication, (of manner) thus (or so); also (of place) here (or hither); or (of time) now<BR><B>KJV:</B> also, here, + hitherto, like, on the other side, so (and much), such, on that manner, (on) this (manner, side, way, way and that way), + mean while, yonder.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3541 (also), H3602 (after that manner)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1782 ἐντεῦθεν, G2400 ἰδού, G3778 οὗτος, G5602 ὧδε",
    3542: "כָּה (kâh | kaw)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H3541 כֹּה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, like this, i.e. by implication, (of manner) thus (or so); also (of place) here (or hither); or (of time) now<BR><B>KJV:</B> hitherto.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3542 (hitherto)",
