    3545: "כֵּהָה (kêhâh | kay-haw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of H3544 כֵּהֶה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, a weakening; figuratively, alleviation, i.e. cure<BR><B>KJV:</B> healing.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3545 (healing), H3543 (darken), H3544 (somewhat dark)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2392 ἴασις",
    3546: "כְּהַל (kᵉhal | keh-hal')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) a root corresponding to and H3557 כּוּל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be able<BR><B>KJV:</B> be able, could.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3567 (Cyrus), H3549 (priest), H3546 (be able), H3734 (cor), H3551 (window)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1410 δύναμαι",
