    3725: "כִּפֻּר (kippur | kip-poor')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3722 כָּפַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> expiation (only in plural)<BR><B>KJV:</B> atonement.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3724 (bribe), H3725 (atonement), H3727 (mercy seat), H3722 (appease)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2434 ἱλασμός, G2512 καθαρισμός",
    3726: "כְּפַר הָעַמֹּונִי (Kᵉphar hâ-ʻAmmôwnîy | kef-ar' haw-am-monee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3723 כָּפָר and H5984 עַמֹּונִי, with the article interposed; village of the Ammonite<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Kefar-ha-Ammoni, a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Chefarhaamonai.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3724 (bribe), H3715 (lion), H3726 (Chefarhaamonai), H3716 (Chephirah), H3723 (village)",
    3727: "כַּפֹּרֶת (kappôreth | kap-po'-reth)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3722 כָּפַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a lid (used only of the cover of the sacred Ark)<BR><B>KJV:</B> mercy seat.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3724 (bribe), H3725 (atonement), H3727 (mercy seat), H3722 (appease)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2435 ἱλαστήριον",
    3728: "כָּפַשׁ (kâphash | kaw-fash')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to tread down; figuratively, to humiliate<BR><B>KJV:</B> cover.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3736 (clothed), H3728 (cover), H3732 (Caphthorim), H3730 (knop), H3734 (cor), H3733 (captain), H3731 (Caphtor)",
    3729: "כְּפַת (kᵉphath | kef-ath')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) a root of uncertain correspondence<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to fetter<BR><B>KJV:</B> bind.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3729 (bind)",
    3730: "כַּפְתֹּר (kaphtôr | kaf-tore')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or (Amos 9:1) כַּפְתֹּור; probably from an unused root meaning to encircle<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a chaplet; but used only in an architectonic sense, i.e. the capital of acolumn, or a wreath-like button or disk on the candelabrum<BR><B>KJV:</B> knop, (upper) lintel.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3736 (clothed), H3728 (cover), H3732 (Caphthorim), H3730 (knop), H3734 (cor), H3733 (captain), H3731 (Caphtor)",
    3731: "כַּפְתֹּר (Kaphtôr | kaf-tore')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or (Amos 9:7) כַּפְתֹּור; apparently the same as H3730 כַּפְתֹּר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Caphtor (i.e. a wreath-shaped island), the original seat of the Philistines<BR><B>KJV:</B> Caphtor.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3736 (clothed), H3728 (cover), H3732 (Caphthorim), H3730 (knop), H3734 (cor), H3733 (captain), H3731 (Caphtor)",
    3732: "כַּפְתֹּרִי (Kaphtôrîy | kaf-to-ree')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> patrial from H3731 כַּפְתֹּר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Caphtorite (collectively) or native of Caphtor<BR><B>KJV:</B> Caphthorim, Caphtorim(-s).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3736 (clothed), H3728 (cover), H3732 (Caphthorim), H3730 (knop), H3734 (cor), H3733 (captain), H3731 (Caphtor)",
    3733: "כַּר (kar | kar)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3769 כָּרַר in the sense of plumpness<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a ram (as full-grown and fat), including a battering-ram (as butting); hence, a meadow (as for sheep); also a pad or camel's saddle (as puffed out)<BR><B>KJV:</B> captain, furniture, lamb, (large) pasture, ram. See also H1033 בֵּית כַּר, H3746 כָּרִי .<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3564 (furnace), H3600 (ranges for pots), H3595 (hearth), H3733 (captain)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2055 ἐρίφιον, G2056 ἔριφος, G2062 ἑρπετόν, G5117 τόπος, G5482 χάραξ",
    3734: "כֹּר (kôr | kore)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as H3564 כּוּר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, a deep round vessel, i.e. (specifically) a cor or measure for things dry<BR><B>KJV:</B> cor, measure. Aramaic the same.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3736 (clothed), H3728 (cover), H3732 (Caphthorim), H3730 (knop), H3734 (cor), H3733 (captain), H3731 (Caphtor)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2884 κόρος",
    3735: "כָּרָא (Kârâʼ | kaw-raw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) probably corresponding to H3738 כָּרָה in the sense of piercing(figuratively)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to grieve<BR><B>KJV:</B> be grieved.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3735 (be grieved), H3744 (herald), H3737 (hat), H3745 (make a proclamation)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5425 φρίσσω",
    3736: "כַּרְבֵּל (karbêl | kar-bale')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as H3525 כֶּבֶל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to gird or clothe<BR><B>KJV:</B> clothed.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3736 (clothed), H3728 (cover), H3732 (Caphthorim), H3730 (knop), H3734 (cor), H3733 (captain), H3731 (Caphtor)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4024 περιζώννυμι",
    3737: "כַּרְבְּלָא (karbᵉlâʼ | kar-bel-aw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) from a verb corresponding to that of H3736 כַּרְבֵּל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a mantle<BR><B>KJV:</B> hat.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3735 (be grieved), H3744 (herald), H3737 (hat), H3745 (make a proclamation)",
    3738: "כָּרָה (kârâh | kaw-raw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to dig; figuratively, to plot; generally, to bore or open<BR><B>KJV:</B> dig, [idiom] make (a banquet), open.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3566 (Cyrus), H3738 (dig), H4380 (habitation), H4351 (birth)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1334 διηγέομαι, G2998 λατομέω, G3409 μισθόω, G3736 ὀρύσσω, G3908 παρατίθημι",
    3739: "כָּרָה (kârâh | kaw-raw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> usually assigned as a primitive root, but probably only a special application of H3738 כָּרָה (through the common idea of planning implied in a bargain)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to purchase<BR><B>KJV:</B> buy, prepare.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3739 (buy)",
    3740: "כֵּרָה (kêrâh | kay-raw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3739 כָּרָה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a purchase<BR><B>KJV:</B> provision.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3742 (cherub), H3746 (captains), H3740 (provision), H3743 (Cherub), H3739 (buy)",
    3741: "כָּרָה (kârâh | kaw-raw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of H3733 כַּר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a meadow<BR><B>KJV:</B> cottage.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4379 (pit), H3738 (dig), H3741 (cottage)",
    3742: "כְּרוּב (kᵉrûwb | ker-oob')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a cherub or imaginary figure<BR><B>KJV:</B> cherub, (plural) cherubims.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3742 (cherub), H3746 (captains), H3740 (provision), H3743 (Cherub), H3739 (buy)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5502 χερουβίμ",
    3743: "כְּרוּב (Kᵉrûwb | ker-oob')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> the same as H3742 כְּרוּב<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Kerub, a place in Babylon<BR><B>KJV:</B> Cherub.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3742 (cherub), H3746 (captains), H3740 (provision), H3743 (Cherub), H3739 (buy)",
    3744: "כָּרֹוז (kârôwz | kaw-roze')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) from H3745 כְּרַז<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a herald<BR><B>KJV:</B> herald.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3735 (be grieved), H3744 (herald), H3737 (hat), H3745 (make a proclamation)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2783 κῆρυξ",
    3745: "כְּרַז (kᵉraz | ker-az')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) probably of Greek origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to proclaim<BR><B>KJV:</B> make a proclamation.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3735 (be grieved), H3744 (herald), H3737 (hat), H3745 (make a proclamation)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2784 κηρύσσω",
    3746: "כָּרִי (kârîy | kaw-ree')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> perhaps an abridged plural of H3733 כַּר in the sense of leader (of the flock)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a life-guardsman<BR><B>KJV:</B> captains, Cherethites (from the margin).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3742 (cherub), H3746 (captains), H3740 (provision), H3743 (Cherub), H3739 (buy)",
    3747: "כְּרִית (Kᵉrîyth | ker-eeth')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3772 כָּרַת ; a cut<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Kerith, a brook of Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Cherith.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3774 (Cherethims), H3773 (beam), H3748 (divorce), H3747 (Cherith), H3772 (be chewed), H3778 (Chaldeans), H3777 (Chesed)",
    3748: "כְּרִיתוּת (kᵉrîythûwth | ker-ee-thooth')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3772 כָּרַת<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a cutting (of the matrimonial bond), i.e. divorce<BR><B>KJV:</B> divorce(-ment).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3774 (Cherethims), H3773 (beam), H3748 (divorce), H3747 (Cherith), H3772 (be chewed), H3778 (Chaldeans), H3777 (Chesed)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G647 ἀποστάσιον",
    3749: "כַּרְכֹּב (karkôb | kar-kobe')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> expanded from the same as H3522 כַּבֹּון<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a rim or top margin<BR><B>KJV:</B> compass.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3750 (saffron), H3751 (Carchemish), H3752 (Carcas), H3749 (compass)",
    3750: "כַּרְכֹּם (karkôm | kar-kome')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably of foreign origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the crocus<BR><B>KJV:</B> saffron.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3750 (saffron), H3751 (Carchemish), H3752 (Carcas), H3749 (compass)",
