    3756: "כַּרְמִי (Karmîy | kar-mee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3754 כֶּרֶם ; gardener<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Karmi, the name of three Israelites<BR><B>KJV:</B> Carmi.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3759 (full ears), H3761 (Carmelite), H3754 (vines), H3762 (Carmelitess), H3763 (Cheran), H3760 (Carmel), H3756 (Carmi), H3757 (Carmites), H3758 (crimson), H3755 (vine dresser)",
    3757: "כַּרְמִי (Karmîy | kar-mee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> patronymically from H3756 כַּרְמִי<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Karmite or descendant of Karmi<BR><B>KJV:</B> Carmites.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3759 (full ears), H3761 (Carmelite), H3754 (vines), H3762 (Carmelitess), H3763 (Cheran), H3760 (Carmel), H3756 (Carmi), H3757 (Carmites), H3758 (crimson), H3755 (vine dresser)",
    3758: "כַּרְמִיל (karmîyl | kar-mele')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably of foreign origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> carmine, a deep red<BR><B>KJV:</B> crimson.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3759 (full ears), H3761 (Carmelite), H3754 (vines), H3762 (Carmelitess), H3763 (Cheran), H3760 (Carmel), H3756 (Carmi), H3757 (Carmites), H3758 (crimson), H3755 (vine dresser)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2847 κόκκινος",
    3759: "כַּרְמֶל (karmel | kar-mel')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3754 כֶּרֶם<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a planted field (garden, orchard, vineyard or park); by implication, garden produce<BR><B>KJV:</B> full (green) ears (of corn), fruitful field (place), plentiful (field).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3759 (full ears), H3761 (Carmelite), H3754 (vines), H3762 (Carmelitess), H3763 (Cheran), H3760 (Carmel), H3756 (Carmi), H3757 (Carmites), H3758 (crimson), H3755 (vine dresser)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G290 ἀμπελών",
    3760: "כַּרְמֶל (Karmel | kar-mel')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> the same as H3759 כַּרְמֶל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Karmel, the name of a hill and of a town in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Carmel, fruitful (plentiful) field, (place).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3759 (full ears), H3761 (Carmelite), H3754 (vines), H3762 (Carmelitess), H3763 (Cheran), H3760 (Carmel), H3756 (Carmi), H3757 (Carmites), H3758 (crimson), H3755 (vine dresser)",
