    3768: "כַּרְפַּס (karpaç | kar-pas')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of foreign origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> byssus or fine vegetable wool<BR><B>KJV:</B> green.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3766 (bow), H3768 (green), H3767 (leg)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1039 βύσσινος",
    3769: "כָּרַר (kârar | kaw-rar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to dance (i.e. whirl)<BR><B>KJV:</B> dance(-ing).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3603 (loaf), H3753 (swift beast), H3769 (dance), H3733 (captain)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3738 ὀρχέομαι",
    3770: "כְּרֵשׂ (kᵉrês | ker-ace')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> by variation from H7164 קָרַס<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the paunch or belly (as swelling out)<BR><B>KJV:</B> belly.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3771 (Carshena), H3770 (belly)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2836 κοιλία",
    3771: "כַּרְשְׁנָא (Karshᵉnâʼ | kar-shen-aw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of foreign origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Karshena, a courtier of Xerxes<BR><B>KJV:</B> Carshena.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3771 (Carshena), H3770 (belly)",
    3772: "כָּרַת (kârath | kaw-rath')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to cut (off, down or asunder); by implication, to destroy or consume; specifically, to covenant (i.e. make an alliance or bargain, originally by cutting flesh and passing between the pieces)<BR><B>KJV:</B> be chewed, be con-(feder-) ate, covenant, cut (down, off), destroy, fail, feller, be freed, hew (down), make a league (covenant), [idiom] lose, perish, [idiom] utterly, [idiom] want.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3774 (Cherethims), H3773 (beam), H3748 (divorce), H3747 (Cherith), H3772 (be chewed), H3778 (Chaldeans), H3777 (Chesed)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G355 ἀναλίσκω, G599 ἀποθνήσκω, G609 ἀποκόπτω, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G645 ἀποσπάω, G851 ἀφαιρέω, G853 ἀφανίζω, G868 ἀφίστημι, G1303 διατίθεμαι, G1459 ἐγκαταλείπω, G1581 ἐκκόπτω, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G1806 ἐξάγω, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G1831 ἐξέρχομαι, G1842 ἐξολοθρεύω, G2476 ἵστημι, G2507 καθαιρέω, G2629 κατακόπτω, G2875 κόπτω, G3645 ὀλοθρεύω, G4059 περιτέμνω, G4141 πλήσσω, G4160 ποιέω, G4931 συντελέω, G5087 τίθημι",
    3773: "כָּרֻתָה (kâruthâh | kaw-rooth-aw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> passive participle feminine of H3772 כָּרַת<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something cut, i.e. a hewn timber<BR><B>KJV:</B> beam.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3774 (Cherethims), H3773 (beam), H3748 (divorce), H3747 (Cherith), H3772 (be chewed), H3778 (Chaldeans), H3777 (Chesed)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2716 κατεργάζομαι",
    3774: "כְּרֵתִי (Kᵉrêthîy | ker-ay-thee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from H3772 כָּרַת in the sense of executioner; (compare H2876 טַבָּח) (only collectively in the singular as plural)<BR><BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Kerethite or life-guardsman<BR><B>KJV:</B> Cherethims, Cherethites.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3774 (Cherethims), H3773 (beam), H3748 (divorce), H3747 (Cherith), H3772 (be chewed), H3778 (Chaldeans), H3777 (Chesed)",
    3775: "כֶּשֶׂב (keseb | keh'-seb)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently by transposition for H3532 כֶּבֶשׂ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a young sheep<BR><B>KJV:</B> lamb.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4346 (thick cloth), H3535 (lamb), H4345 (grate), H3523 (pillow), H3776 (lamb), H3775 (lamb), H3531 (sieve), H3532 (lamb)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4263 πρόβατον",
    3776: "כִּשְׂבָּה (kisbâh | kis-baw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of H3775 כֶּשֶׂב<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a young ewe<BR><B>KJV:</B> lamb.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4346 (thick cloth), H3535 (lamb), H4345 (grate), H3523 (pillow), H3776 (lamb), H3775 (lamb), H3531 (sieve), H3532 (lamb)",
    3777: "כֶּשֶׂד (Kesed | keh'-sed)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root of uncertain meaning<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Kesed, a relative of Abraham<BR><B>KJV:</B> Chesed.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3774 (Cherethims), H3773 (beam), H3748 (divorce), H3747 (Cherith), H3772 (be chewed), H3778 (Chaldeans), H3777 (Chesed)",
    3778: "כַּשְׂדִּי (Kasdîy | kas-dee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (occasionally with enclitic) כַּשְׂדִּימָה; towards the Kasdites into Chaldea), patronymically from H3777 כֶּשֶׂד (only in the plural)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Kasdite, or descendant of Kesed; by implication, a Chaldaean (as if so descended); also an astrologer (as if proverbial of that people<BR><B>KJV:</B> Chaldeans, Chaldees, inhabitants of Chaldea.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3774 (Cherethims), H3773 (beam), H3748 (divorce), H3747 (Cherith), H3772 (be chewed), H3778 (Chaldeans), H3777 (Chesed)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5466 Χαλδαῖος",
    3779: "כַּשְׂדַּי (Kasday | kas-dah'-ee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H3778 כַּשְׂדִּי<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Chaldaean or inhabitant of Chaldaea; by implication, a Magian or professional astrologer<BR><B>KJV:</B> Chaldean.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3679 (Chaldean), H3604 (talent), H3779 (Chaldean)",
    3780: "כָּשָׂה (kâsâh | kaw-saw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to grow fat (i.e. be covered with flesh)<BR><B>KJV:</B> be covered. Compare H3680 כָּסָה .<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3780 (be covered)",
    3781: "כַּשִּׁיל (kashshîyl | kash-sheel')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3782 כָּשַׁל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, a feller, i.e. an axe<BR><B>KJV:</B> ax.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4383 (caused to fall), H4384 (ruin), H3783 (fall), H3782 (bereave), H3781 (ax)",
    3782: "כָּשַׁל (kâshal | kaw-shal')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to totter or waver (through weakness of the legs, especially the ankle); by implication, to falter, stumble, faint or fall<BR><B>KJV:</B> bereave (from the margin), cast down, be decayed, (cause to) fail, (cause, make to) fall (down, -ing), feeble, be (the) ruin(-ed, of), (be) overthrown, (cause to) stumble, [idiom] utterly, be weak.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4383 (caused to fall), H4384 (ruin), H3783 (fall), H3782 (bereave), H3781 (ax)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G101 ἀδυνατέω, G447 ἀνίημι, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G769 ἀσθένεια, G770 ἀσθενέω, G1847 ἐξουδενόω, G2559 κακόω, G2654 καταναλίσκω, G2872 κοπιάω, G3886 παραλύω, G4098 πίπτω, G4105 πλανάω, G4350 προσκόπτω, G4624 σκανδαλίζω, G4937 συντρίβω",
    3783: "כִּשָּׁלֹון (kishshâlôwn | kish-shaw-lone')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3782 כָּשַׁל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, a tottering, i.e. ruin<BR><B>KJV:</B> fall.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4383 (caused to fall), H4384 (ruin), H3783 (fall), H3782 (bereave), H3781 (ax)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4430 πτῶμα",
    3784: "כָּשַׁף (kâshaph | kaw-shaf')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to whisper aspell, i.e. to inchant or practise magic<BR><B>KJV:</B> sorcerer, (use) witch(-craft).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3784 (sorcerer), H3786 (sorcerer), H3785 (sorcery)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5333 φάρμακος",
    3785: "כֶּשֶׁף (kesheph | keh'-shef)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3784 כָּשַׁף<BR><B>Strong's:</B> magic<BR><B>KJV:</B> sorcery, witchcraft.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3784 (sorcerer), H3786 (sorcerer), H3785 (sorcery)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5331 φαρμακεία, G5332 φαρμακεύς",
    3786: "כַּשָּׁף (kashshâph | kash-shawf')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3784 כָּשַׁף<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a magician<BR><B>KJV:</B> sorcerer.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3784 (sorcerer), H3786 (sorcerer), H3785 (sorcery)",
    3787: "כָּשֵׁר (kâshêr | kaw-share')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root properly, to be straight or right<BR><B>Strong's:</B> by implication, to be acceptable; also to succeed or prosper<BR><B>KJV:</B> direct, be right, prosper.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3788 (equity), H3601 (spindle), H3574 ([idiom] chain), H3787 (direct)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4748 στοιχέω",
    3788: "כִּשְׁרֹון (kishrôwn | kish-rone')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3787 כָּשֵׁר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> success, advantage<BR><B>KJV:</B> equity, good, right.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3788 (equity), H3601 (spindle), H3574 ([idiom] chain), H3787 (direct)",
    3789: "כָּתַב (kâthab | kaw-thab')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to grave, by implication, to write (describe, inscribe, prescribe, subscribe)<BR><B>KJV:</B> describe, record, prescribe, subscribe, write(-ing, -ten).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3789 (describe), H3794 (Chittim), H4385 (writing), H3791 (register), H3793 ([idiom] any)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G583 ἀπογράφω, G1121 γράμμα, G1124 γραφή, G1125 γράφω, G1125 γράφω, G1242 διαθήκη, G1379 δογματίζω, G1722 ἐν, G1924 ἐπιγράφω, G2192 ἔχω, G3307 μερίζω",
