    3791: "כָּתָב (kâthâb | kaw-thawb')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3789 כָּתַב<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something written, i.e. a writing, record or book<BR><B>KJV:</B> register, scripture, writing.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3789 (describe), H3794 (Chittim), H4385 (writing), H3791 (register), H3793 ([idiom] any)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G582 ἀπογραφή, G1124 γραφή, G1378 δόγμα, G1992 ἐπιστολή",
    3792: "כְּתָב (kᵉthâb | keth-awb')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H3791 כָּתָב<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something written, i.e. a writing, record or book<BR><B>KJV:</B> prescribing, writing(-ten).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3790 (write), H3797 (wall), H3792 (prescribing)",
    3793: "כְּתֹבֶת (kᵉthôbeth | keth-o'-beth)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3789 כָּתַב<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a letter or other mark branded on the skin<BR><B>KJV:</B> [idiom] any (mark).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3789 (describe), H3794 (Chittim), H4385 (writing), H3791 (register), H3793 ([idiom] any)",
    3794: "כִּתִּי (Kittîy | kit-tee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or כִּתִּיִּי; patrial from an unused name denoting Cyprus (only in the plural)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Kittite or Cypriote; hence, an islander in general, i.e. the Greeks or Romans on the shores opposite Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Chittim, Kittim.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3789 (describe), H3794 (Chittim), H4385 (writing), H3791 (register), H3793 ([idiom] any)",
    3795: "כָּתִית (kâthîyth | kaw-theeth')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3807 כָּתַת<BR><B>Strong's:</B> beaten, i.e. pure (oil)<BR><B>KJV:</B> beaten.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3795 (beaten), H4386 (bursting), H3807 (beat)",
    3796: "כֹּתֶל (kôthel | ko'-thel)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to compact<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a wall (as gathering inmates)<BR><B>KJV:</B> wall.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3796 (wall), H3798 (Kithlish)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5109 τοῖχος",
