    3798: "כִּתְלִישׁ (Kithlîysh | kith-leesh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3796 כֹּתֶל and H376 אִישׁ ; wall of a man<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Kithlish, a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Kithlish.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3796 (wall), H3798 (Kithlish)",
    3799: "כָּתַם (kâtham | kaw-tham')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to carve or engrave, i.e. (by implication) to inscribe indelibly<BR><B>KJV:</B> mark.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3799 (mark)",
    3800: "כֶּתֶם (kethem | keh'-them)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3799 כָּתַם<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, something carved out, i.e. ore; hence, gold (pure as originally mined)<BR><B>KJV:</B> ((most) fine, pure) gold(-en wedge).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4387 (Michtam), H3800 (gold)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G694 ἀργύριον, G2441 ἱματισμός, G3037 λίθος, G4185 πολυτελής, G5553 χρυσίον",
    3801: "כְּתֹנֶת (kᵉthôneth | keth-o'-neth)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or כֻּתֹּנֶת; from an unused root meaning to cover (compare H3802 כָּתֵף)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a shirt<BR><B>KJV:</B> coat, garment, robe.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3801 (coat)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2440 ἱμάτιον, G4749 στολή, G5509 χιτών, G5509 χιτών",
    3802: "כָּתֵף (kâthêph | kaw-thafe')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to clothe<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the shoulder (proper, i.e. upper end of the arm; as being the spot where the garments hang); figuratively, side-piece or lateral projection of anything<BR><B>KJV:</B> arm, corner, shoulder(-piece), side, undersetter.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3802 (arm)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1137 γωνία, G3558 νότος, G3577 νῶτος, G5606 ὦμος",
    3803: "כָּתַר (kâthar | kaw-thar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to enclose; hence (in a friendly sense) to crown, (in a hostile one) to besiege; also to wait (as restraining oneself)<BR><B>KJV:</B> beset round, compass about, be crowned inclose round, suffer.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3803 (beset round), H3805 (chapiter), H3804 (crown)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2616 καταδυναστεύω, G2902 κρατέω, G3306 μένω, G4023 περιέχω",
    3804: "כֶּתֶר (kether | keh'-ther)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3803 כָּתַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, a circlet, i.e. a diadem<BR><B>KJV:</B> crown.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3803 (beset round), H3805 (chapiter), H3804 (crown)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1238 διάδημα",
    3805: "כֹתֶרֶת (kôthereth | ko-theh'-reth)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine active participle of H3803 כָּתַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the capital of a column<BR><B>KJV:</B> chapiter.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3803 (beset round), H3805 (chapiter), H3804 (crown)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2346 θλίβω, G2777 κεφαλίς, G4768 στυγνάζω",
    3806: "כָּתַשׁ (kâthash | kaw-thash')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to butt or pound<BR><B>KJV:</B> bray.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4388 (hollow place), H4389 (Maktesh), H3806 (bray)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3146 μαστιγόω",
    3807: "כָּתַת (kâthath | kaw-thath')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to bruise or violently strike<BR><B>KJV:</B> beat (down, to pieces), break in pieces, crushed, destroy, discomfit, smite, stamp. l<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3795 (beaten), H4386 (bursting), H3807 (beat)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G2629 κατακόπτω, G2875 κόπτω, G3765 οὐκέτι, G4937 συντρίβω",
    3808: "לֹא (lôʼ | lo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or לֹוא; or לֹה; (Deuteronomy 3:11), a primitive particle<BR><B>Strong's:</B> not (the simple or abs. negation); by implication, no; often used with other particles<BR><B>KJV:</B> [idiom] before, [phrase] or else, ere, [phrase] except, ig(-norant), much, less, nay, neither, never, no((-ne), -r, (-thing)), ([idiom] as though...,(can-), for) not (out of), of nought, otherwise, out of, [phrase] surely, [phrase] as truly as, [phrase] of a truth, [phrase] verily, for want, [phrase] whether, without.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3810 (Debir), H3808 ([idiom] before), H3819 (Lo-ruhamah), H3818 (Lo-ammi)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G512 ἀνωφελής, G544 ἀπειθέω, G544 ἀπειθέω, G564 ἀπερίτμητος, G762 ἄσβεστος, G878 ἄφρων, G1210 δέω, G1262 διαλύω, G1538 ἕκαστος, G1718 ἐμφανίζω, G1726 ἐναντίον, G1727 ἐναντίος, G2125 εὐλαβέομαι, G2756 κενός, G2756 κενός, G3763 οὐδέποτε, G3765 οὐκέτι",
    3809: "לָא (lâʼ | law)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) or לָה; (Aramaic) (Daniel 4:32), corresponding to H3808 לֹא<BR><B>Strong's:</B> not (the simple or abs. negation); by implication, no;<BR><B>KJV:</B> or even, neither, no(-ne, -r), (can-) not, as nothing, without.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3809 (or even)",
    3810: "לֹא דְבַר (Lôʼ Dᵉbar | lo deb-ar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or לֹו דבַר; (Samuel 9:4,5), or לִדְבִר; (Joshua 13:26), (probably rather לֹדְבַר); from H3808 לֹא and H1699 דֹּבֶר ; pastureless<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Lo-Debar, a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Debir, Lodebar.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3810 (Debir), H3808 ([idiom] before), H3819 (Lo-ruhamah), H3818 (Lo-ammi)",
    3811: "לָאָה (lâʼâh | law-aw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to tire; (figuratively) to be (or make) disgusted<BR><B>KJV:</B> faint, grieve, lothe, (be, make) weary (selves).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4972 (what a weariness), H8513 (travail), H3811 (faint), H3812 (Leah)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G73 ἀγών, G770 ἀσθενέω, G1410 δύναμαι, G1590 ἐκλύω, G1907 ἐπέχω, G2872 κοπιάω, G3076 λυπέω, G3886 παραλύω, G3926 παρενοχλέω, G3930 παρέχω, G3935 παρίημι",
