    3855: "לַהַד (Lahad | lah'-had)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to glow (compare H3851 לַהַב) or else to be earnest (compare H3854 לַהַג)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Lahad, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Lahad.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3855 (Lahad), H3854 (study)",
    3856: "לָהַהּ (lâhahh | law-hah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root meaning properly, to burn, i.e. (by implication)<BR><BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be rabid (figuratively, insane); also (from the exhaustion of frenzy) to languish<BR><B>KJV:</B> faint, mad.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3856 (faint)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1587 ἐκλείπω",
    3857: "לָהַט (lâhaṭ | law-hat')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to lick, i.e. (by implication) to blaze<BR><B>KJV:</B> burn (up), set on fire, flaming, kindle.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3858 (flaming), H3857 (burn)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G381 ἀνάπτω, G2618 κατακαίω, G5015 ταράσσω, G5394 φλογίζω",
    3858: "לַהַט (lahaṭ | lah'-hat)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3857 לָהַט<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a blaze; also (from the idea of enwrapping) magic (as covert)<BR><B>KJV:</B> flaming, enchantment.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3858 (flaming), H3857 (burn)",
    3859: "לָהַם (lâham | law-ham')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to burn in, i.e. (figuratively) to rankle<BR><B>KJV:</B> wound.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3862 (company), H3859 (wound), H3860 (for them)",
    3860: "לָהֵן (lâhên | law-hane')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the prepositional prefix meaning to or for and H2005 הֵן<BR><B>Strong's:</B> popularly for if; hence, therefore<BR><B>KJV:</B> for them (by mistake for prepositional suffix).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3862 (company), H3859 (wound), H3860 (for them)",
    3861: "לָהֵן (lâhên | law-hane')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H3860 לָהֵן<BR><B>Strong's:</B> therefore; also except<BR><B>KJV:</B> but, except, save, therefore, wherefore.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3904 (concubine), H3861 (but), H3916 (night), H3900 (feast), H3879 (Levite), H3961 (language), H3890 ([idiom] thee)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3568 νῦν, G4133 πλήν",
    3862: "לַהֲקָה (lahăqâh | lah-hak-aw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from an unused root meaning to gather<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an assembly<BR><B>KJV:</B> company.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3862 (company), H3859 (wound), H3860 (for them)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1577 ἐκκλησία",
    3863: "לוּא (lûwʼ | loo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or לֻא; or לוּ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a conditional particle; if; by implication (interj. as a wish) would that!<BR><B>KJV:</B> if (haply), peradventure, I pray thee, though, I would, would God (that).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3884 (except), H3863 (if), H3864 (Lubim), H3866 (Ludim), H3865 (Lud)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3784 ὀφείλω",
    3864: "לוּבִי (Lûwbîy | loo-bee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or לֻבִּי; (Daniel 11:43), partrial from a name probably derived from an unused root meaning to thirst, i.e. a dry region; apparently<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Libyan or inhabitant of interior Africa (only in plural)<BR><B>KJV:</B> Lubim(-s), Libyans.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3884 (except), H3863 (if), H3864 (Lubim), H3866 (Ludim), H3865 (Lud)",
    3865: "לוּד (Lûwd | lood)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably of foreign derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Lud, the name of two nations<BR><B>KJV:</B> Lud, Lydia.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3884 (except), H3863 (if), H3864 (Lubim), H3866 (Ludim), H3865 (Lud)",
    3866: "לוּדִי (Lûwdîy | loo-dee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or לוּדִיִּי; patrial from H3865 לוּד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Ludite or inhabitants of Lud (only in plural)<BR><B>KJV:</B> Ludim. Lydians.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3884 (except), H3863 (if), H3864 (Lubim), H3866 (Ludim), H3865 (Lud)",
    3867: "לָוָה (lâvâh | law-vaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to twine, i.e. (by implication) to unite, to remain; also to borrow (as a form of obligation) or (caus.) to lend<BR><B>KJV:</B> abide with, borrow(-er), cleave, join (self), lend(-er).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3867 (abide with)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1155 δανείζω, G2703 καταφεύγω, G4369 προστίθημι, G4388 προτίθεμαι, G5531 χράω",
    3868: "לוּז (lûwz | looz)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root; (compare H3867 לָוָה, H3874 לוּט and H3885 לוּן)<BR><BR><B>Strong's:</B> to turn aside, i.e. (literally) to depart, (figuratively) be perverse<BR><B>KJV:</B> depart, froward, perverse(-ness).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3869 (hazel), H3891 (perverse), H3870 (Luz), H3868 (depart)",
    3869: "לוּז (lûwz | looz)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably of foreign origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> some kind of nuttree, perhaps the almond<BR><B>KJV:</B> hazel.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3869 (hazel), H3891 (perverse), H3870 (Luz), H3868 (depart)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1111 γογγύζω, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G3007 λείπω, G3901 παραῤῥυέω",
    3870: "לוּז (Lûwz | looz)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from H3869 לוּז (as growing there)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Luz, the name of two places in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Luz.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3869 (hazel), H3891 (perverse), H3870 (Luz), H3868 (depart)",
    3871: "לוּחַ (lûwach | loo'-akh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or לֻחַ; from a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> probably meaning to glisten; a tablet (as polished), of stone, wood or metal<BR><B>KJV:</B> board, plate, table.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3872 (Luhith), H3871 (board)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G746 ἀρχή, G4109 πλάξ, G4114 πλάτος, G4548 σανίς",
    3872: "לוּחִית (Lûwchîyth | loo-kheeth')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or לֻחֹות; (Jeremiah 48:5), from the same as H3871 לוּחַ ; floored<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Luchith, a place East of the Jordan<BR><B>KJV:</B> Luhith.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3872 (Luhith), H3871 (board)",
    3873: "לֹוחֵשׁ (Lôwchêsh | lo-khashe')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> active participle of H3907 לָחַשׁ ; (the) enchanter<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Lochesh, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Hallohesh, Haloshesh (includ. the article).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3910 (myrrh), H3908 (charmed), H3907 (charmer), H3873 (Hallohesh)",
    3874: "לוּט (lûwṭ | loot)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to wrap up<BR><B>KJV:</B> cast, wrap.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3875 (covering), H3881 (Leviite), H3876 (Lot), H3874 (cast), H3883 (winding stair), H3878 (Levi), H3877 (Lotan), H3814 (softly), H3909 (enchantment)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1750 ἐνειλέω, G1943 ἐπικαλύπτω",
    3875: "לֹוט (lôwṭ | lote)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3874 לוּט<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a veil<BR><B>KJV:</B> covering.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3875 (covering), H3881 (Leviite), H3876 (Lot), H3874 (cast), H3883 (winding stair), H3878 (Levi), H3877 (Lotan), H3814 (softly), H3909 (enchantment)",
    3876: "לֹוט (Lôwṭ | lote)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> the same as H3875 לֹוט<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Lot, Abraham's nephew<BR><B>KJV:</B> Lot.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3875 (covering), H3881 (Leviite), H3876 (Lot), H3874 (cast), H3883 (winding stair), H3878 (Levi), H3877 (Lotan), H3814 (softly), H3909 (enchantment)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3091 Λώτ",
    3877: "לֹוטָן (Lôwṭân | lo-tawn')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3875 לֹוט ; covering<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Lotan, an Idumaean<BR><B>KJV:</B> Lotan.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3875 (covering), H3881 (Leviite), H3876 (Lot), H3874 (cast), H3883 (winding stair), H3878 (Levi), H3877 (Lotan), H3814 (softly), H3909 (enchantment)",
    3878: "לֵוִי (Lêvîy | lay-vee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3867 לָוָה ; attached<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Levi, a son of Jacob<BR><B>KJV:</B> Levi. See also H3879 לֵוִי, H3881 לֵוִיִּי .<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3875 (covering), H3881 (Leviite), H3876 (Lot), H3874 (cast), H3883 (winding stair), H3878 (Levi), H3877 (Lotan), H3814 (softly), H3909 (enchantment)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3017 Λευΐ, G3018 Λευΐς",
    3879: "לֵוִי (Lêvîy | lay-vee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H3880 לִוְיָה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something attached, i.e. a wreath<BR><B>KJV:</B> Levite.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3904 (concubine), H3861 (but), H3916 (night), H3900 (feast), H3879 (Levite), H3961 (language), H3890 ([idiom] thee)",
    3880: "לִוְיָה (livyâh | liv-yaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3867 לָוָה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something attached, i.e. a wreath<BR><B>KJV:</B> ornament.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3882 (leviathan), H3914 (addition), H3880 (ornament)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4735 στέφανος",
    3881: "לֵוִיִּי (Lêvîyîy | lay-vee-ee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or לֵוִי; patronymically from H3878 לֵוִי<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Levite or descendant of Levi<BR><B>KJV:</B> Leviite.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3875 (covering), H3881 (Leviite), H3876 (Lot), H3874 (cast), H3883 (winding stair), H3878 (Levi), H3877 (Lotan), H3814 (softly), H3909 (enchantment)",
    3882: "לִוְיָתָן (livyâthân | liv-yaw-thawn')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3867 לָוָה<BR><B>Definition:</B> a sea creature that had more than one head (Job 41:1-34; Psa 74:14, Psa 104:26); used figurativly of Babylon (Isa 27:1); figuratively, the constellation of the dragon (Job 26:13);<BR><B>KJV:</B> leviathan, mourning.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3882 (leviathan), H3914 (addition), H3880 (ornament)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1404 δράκων, G2785 κῆτος, G3173 μέγας",    3883: "לוּל (lûwl | lool)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to fold back<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a spiral step<BR><B>KJV:</B> winding stair. Compare H3924 לֻלָאָה .<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3875 (covering), H3881 (Leviite), H3876 (Lot), H3874 (cast), H3883 (winding stair), H3878 (Levi), H3877 (Lotan), H3814 (softly), H3909 (enchantment)",
    3884: "לוּלֵא (lûwlêʼ | loo-lay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or לוּלֵי; from H3863 לוּא and H3808 לֹא<BR><B>Strong's:</B> if not<BR><B>KJV:</B> except, had not, if (...not), unless, were it not that.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3884 (except), H3863 (if), H3864 (Lubim), H3866 (Ludim), H3865 (Lud)",
    3885: "לוּן (lûwn | loon)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or לִין; a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to stop (usually over night); by implication, to stay permanently; hence (in a bad sense) to be obstinate (especially in words, to complain)<BR><B>KJV:</B> abide (all night), continue, dwell, endure, grudge, be left, lie all night, (cause to) lodge (all night, in, -ing, this night), (make to) murmur, remain, tarry (all night, that night).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3885 (abide), H4411 (inn), H4412 (cottage)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G835 αὐλίζομαι, G1111 γογγύζω, G1234 διαγογγύζω, G2646 κατάλυμα, G2647 καταλύω, G2664 καταπαύω, G2837 κοιμάω, G3306 μένω, G4016 περιβάλλω, G5225 ὑπάρχω",
