    3891: "לְזוּת (lᵉzûwth | lez-ooth')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3868 לוּז<BR><B>Strong's:</B> perverseness<BR><B>KJV:</B> perverse.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3869 (hazel), H3891 (perverse), H3870 (Luz), H3868 (depart)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G94 ἄδικος",
    3892: "לַח (lach | lakh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to be new<BR><B>Strong's:</B> fresh, i.e. unused or undried<BR><B>KJV:</B> green, moist.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3892 (green), H3893 (natural force)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4372 πρόσφατος, G5200 ὑγρός, G5515 χλωρός",
    3893: "לֵחַ (lêach | lay'-akh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as H3892 לַח<BR><B>Strong's:</B> freshness, i.e. vigor<BR><B>KJV:</B> natural force.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3892 (green), H3893 (natural force)",
    3894: "לָחוּם (lâchûwm | law-khoom')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or לָחֻם; passive participle of H3898 לָחַם<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, eaten, i.e. food; also flesh, i.e. body<BR><B>KJV:</B> while...is eating, flesh.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3901 (war), H3898 (devour), H4421 (battle), H3894 (while)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4561 σάρξ",
    3895: "לְחִי (lᵉchîy | lekh-ee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to be soft<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the cheek (from its fleshiness); hence, the jaw-bone<BR><B>KJV:</B> cheek (bone), jaw (bone).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3895 (cheek), H3896 (Lehi)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4600 σιαγών, G5491 χεῖλος",
    3896: "לֶחִי (Lechîy | lekh'-ee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a form of H3895 לְחִי<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Lechi, a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Lehi. Compare also H7437 רָמַת לֶחִי .<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3895 (cheek), H3896 (Lehi)",
    3897: "לָחַךְ (lâchak | law-khak')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to lick<BR><B>KJV:</B> lick (up).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3897 (lick)",
