    3905: "לָחַץ (lâchats | law-khats')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to press, i.e. (figuratively) to distress<BR><B>KJV:</B> afflict, crush, force, hold fast, oppress(-or), thrust self.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3905 (afflict), H3906 (affliction)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G598 ἀποθλίβω, G2559 κακόω",
