    4171: "מוּר (mûwr | moor)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to alter; by implication, to barter, to dispose of<BR><B>KJV:</B> [idiom] at all, (ex-) change, remove.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4171 ([idiom] at all), H4185 (cease), H8545 (change), H4177 (razor), H4173 (threshing instrument)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G114 ἀθετέω, G236 ἀλλάσσω, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G5015 ταράσσω, G5087 τίθημι",
    4172: "מֹורָא (môwrâʼ | mo-raw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or מֹרָא; or מֹורָה; (Psalm 9:20), from H3372 יָרֵא<BR><B>Strong's:</B> fear; by implication, a fearful thing or deed<BR><B>KJV:</B> dread, (that ought to be) fear(-ed), terribleness, terror.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3373 (afraid), H3375 (Iron), H3374 ([idiom] dreadful), H3372 (affright), H8493 (Tiria), H4172 (dread)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2297 θαυμάσιος, G3705 ὅραμα, G5156 τρόμος, G5398 φοβερός",
    4173: "מֹורַג (môwrag | mo-rag')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or מֹרַג; from an unused root meaning to triturate<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a threshing sledge<BR><B>KJV:</B> threshing instrument.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4171 ([idiom] at all), H4185 (cease), H8545 (change), H4177 (razor), H4173 (threshing instrument)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G723 ἄροτρον, G5164 τροχός",
    4174: "מֹורָד (môwrâd | mo-rawd')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3381 יָרַד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a descent; as architecture, an ornamental appendage, perhaps a festoon<BR><B>KJV:</B> going down, steep place, thin work.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3382 (Jared), H3381 ([idiom] abundantly), H3383 (Jordan), H4174 (going down)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3598 ὁδός",
    4175: "מֹורֶה (môwreh | mo-reh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3384 יָרָה ; (see H3138 יֹורֶה)<BR><BR><B>Strong's:</B> an archer; also teacher or teaching; also the early rain<BR><B>KJV:</B> (early) rain.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4175 (rain), H3140 (Jorai), H8451 (law), H3138 (first rain), H4176 (Moreh), H3404 (Jeriah), H8452 (manner), H3385 (Jeruel), H3139 (Jorah), H3384 (archer), H3400 (Jeriel)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5308 ὑψηλός",
    4176: "מֹורֶה (Môwreh | mo-reh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or מֹרֶה; the same as H4175 מֹורֶה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Moreh, a Canaanite; also a hill (perhaps named from him)<BR><B>KJV:</B> Moreh.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4175 (rain), H3140 (Jorai), H8451 (law), H3138 (first rain), H4176 (Moreh), H3404 (Jeriah), H8452 (manner), H3385 (Jeruel), H3139 (Jorah), H3384 (archer), H3400 (Jeriel)",
    4177: "מֹורָה (môwrâh | mo-raw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H4171 מוּר in the sense of shearing<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a razor<BR><B>KJV:</B> razor.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4171 ([idiom] at all), H4185 (cease), H8545 (change), H4177 (razor), H4173 (threshing instrument)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4604 σίδηρος",
    4178: "מֹורָט (môwrâṭ | mo-rawt')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3399 יָרַט<BR><B>Strong's:</B> obstinate, i.e. independent<BR><B>KJV:</B> peeled.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4825 (Meres), H4813 (Miriam), H4179 (Moriah), H4803 (bright), H4178 (peeled), H4821 (Mirma), H4826 (Marsena), H4812 (Meraioth), H4824 (Meronothite), H4811 (Meraiah), H4593 (wrapped up), H4831 (Maralah), H4822 (Meremoth)",
    4179: "מֹורִיָּה (Môwrîyâh | mo-ree-yaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or מֹרִיָּה; from H7200 רָאָה and H3050 יָהּ ; seen of Jah<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Morijah, a hill in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Moriah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4825 (Meres), H4813 (Miriam), H4179 (Moriah), H4803 (bright), H4178 (peeled), H4821 (Mirma), H4826 (Marsena), H4812 (Meraioth), H4824 (Meronothite), H4811 (Meraiah), H4593 (wrapped up), H4831 (Maralah), H4822 (Meremoth)",
    4180: "מֹורָשׁ (môwrâsh | mo-rawsh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3423 יָרַשׁ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a possession; figuratively, delight<BR><B>KJV:</B> possession, thought.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3424 (possession), H3425 (heritage), H8492 (wine), H4181 (heritage), H3423 (cast out), H7568 (net), H4180 (possession), H4182 (Moresheth-gath), H3388 (Jerusha), H4183 (Morashthite)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2048 ἔρημος",
    4181: "מֹורָשָׁה (môwrâshâh | mo-raw-shaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of H4180 מֹורָשׁ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a possession<BR><B>KJV:</B> heritage, inheritance, possession.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3424 (possession), H3425 (heritage), H8492 (wine), H4181 (heritage), H3423 (cast out), H7568 (net), H4180 (possession), H4182 (Moresheth-gath), H3388 (Jerusha), H4183 (Morashthite)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2697 κατάσχεσις",
    4182: "מֹורֶשֶׁת גַּת (Môwresheth Gath | mo-reh'-sheth gath)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3423 יָרַשׁ and H1661 גַּת ; possession of Gath<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Moresheth-Gath, a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Moresheth-gath.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3424 (possession), H3425 (heritage), H8492 (wine), H4181 (heritage), H3423 (cast out), H7568 (net), H4180 (possession), H4182 (Moresheth-gath), H3388 (Jerusha), H4183 (Morashthite)",
    4183: "מֹורַשְׁתִּי (Môwrashtîy | mo-rash-tee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> patrial from H4182 מֹורֶשֶׁת גַּת<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Morashtite or inhabitant of Moresheth-Gath<BR><B>KJV:</B> Morashthite.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3424 (possession), H3425 (heritage), H8492 (wine), H4181 (heritage), H3423 (cast out), H7568 (net), H4180 (possession), H4182 (Moresheth-gath), H3388 (Jerusha), H4183 (Morashthite)",
    4184: "מוּשׁ (mûwsh | moosh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to touch<BR><B>KJV:</B> feel, handle.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4187 (Mushi), H4184 (feel), H4188 (Mushites)",
    4185: "מוּשׁ (mûwsh | moosh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root (perhaps rather the same as H4184 מוּשׁ through the idea of receding by contact)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to withdraw (both literally and figuratively, whether intransitive or transitive)<BR><B>KJV:</B> cease, depart, go back, remove, take away.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4171 ([idiom] at all), H4185 (cease), H8545 (change), H4177 (razor), H4173 (threshing instrument)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G868 ἀφίστημι, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G2795 κινέω, G2827 κλίνω, G2967 κωλύω, G3179 μεθίστημι, G3973 παύω, G5563 χωρίζω, G5584 ψηλαφάω",
    4186: "מֹושָׁב (môwshâb | mo-shawb')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or מֹשָׁב; from H3427 יָשַׁב<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a seat; figuratively, a site; abstractly, a session; by extension an abode (the place or the time); by implication, population<BR><B>KJV:</B> assembly, dwell in, dwelling(-place), wherein (that) dwelt (in), inhabited place, seat, sitting, situation, sojourning.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3430 (Ishbi-benob), H3428 (Jeshebeab), H3436 (Joshbekashah), H3429 (that sat in the seat), H3427 (abide), H7871 (while), H4186 (assembly), H8453 (foreigner), H7675 (place), H3143 (Josibiah)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2515 καθέδρα, G2697 κατάσχεσις, G2731 κατοίκησις, G2732 κατοικητήριον, G2733 κατοικία",
    4187: "מוּשִׁי (Mûwshîy | moo-shee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or מֻשִּׁי; from H4184 מוּשׁ ; sensitive<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Mushi, a Levite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Mushi.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4187 (Mushi), H4184 (feel), H4188 (Mushites)",
    4188: "מוּשִׁי (Mûwshîy | moo-shee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> patronymical from H4187 מוּשִׁי<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Mushite (collectively) or descendants of Mushi<BR><B>KJV:</B> Mushites.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4187 (Mushi), H4184 (feel), H4188 (Mushites)",
    4189: "מֹושְׁכָה (môwshᵉkâh | mo-shek-aw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> act participle feminine of H4900 מָשַׁךְ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something drawing, i.e. (figuratively) a cord<BR><B>KJV:</B> band.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4189 (band), H4900 (draw), H4902 (Mesech), H4901 (precious)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5418 φραγμός",
