    4191: "מוּת (mûwth | mooth)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to die (literally or figuratively); causatively, to kill<BR><B>KJV:</B> [idiom] at all, [idiom] crying, (be) dead (body, man, one), (put to, worthy of) death, destroy(-er), (cause to, be like to, must) die, kill, necro(-mancer), [idiom] must needs, slay, [idiom] surely, [idiom] very suddenly, [idiom] in (no) wise.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4463 (death), H4191 ([idiom] at all), H4194 (dead), H8546 (death)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G25 ἀγαπάω, G86 ᾅδης, G101 ἀδυνατέω, G337 ἀναιρέω, G355 ἀναλίσκω, G599 ἀποθνήσκω, G615 ἀποκτείνω, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G1578 ἐκκλίνω, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G1626 ἔκτρωμα, G1777 ἔνοχος, G1808 ἐξαίρω, G1929 ἐπιδίδωμι, G2287 θανατήφορος, G2288 θάνατος, G2288 θάνατος, G2289 θανατόω, G2289 θανατόω, G2348 θνήσκω, G2349 θνητός, G2795 κινέω, G2827 κλίνω, G3179 μεθίστημι, G3334 μετακινέω, G3337 μεταλλάσσω, G3346 μετατίθημι, G3498 νεκρός, G3960 πατάσσω, G4098 πίπτω, G4098 πίπτω, G4531 σαλεύω, G4931 συντελέω, G5053 τελευτάω, G5054 τελευτή",
    4192: "מוּת (Mûwth | mooth)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Psalm H48 אֲבִירָם or מוּת לַבֵּן; from H4191 מוּת and H1121 בֵּן with the preposition and article interposed<BR><B>Strong's:</B> 'To die for the son', probably the title of a popular song<BR><B>KJV:</B> death, Muthlabben.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3844 (Lebanon), H3843 (brick), H3838 (Lebana), H4192 (death), H3839 (poplar), H3846 (Libnites), H3840 (paved), H4404 (brickkiln), H3845 (Libni), H3835 (make brick), H3828 (incense), H3837 (Laban), H3836 (white), H3841 (Libnah), H3842 (moon), H3829 (Lebonah)",
    4193: "מֹות (môwth | mohth)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H4194 מָוֶת<BR><B>Strong's:</B> death<BR><B>KJV:</B> death.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4101 (how great), H4193 (death), H3964 (what)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G435 ἀνήρ, G706 ἀριθμός, G1024 βραχύς, G2041 ἔργον, G2190 ἐχθρός, G3641 ὀλίγος, G4892 συνέδριον",
    4194: "מָוֶת (mâveth | maw'-veth)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H4191 מוּת<BR><B>Strong's:</B> death (natural or violent); concretely, the dead, their place or state (hades); figuratively, pestilence, ruin<BR><B>KJV:</B> (be) dead(-ly), death, die(-d).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4463 (death), H4191 ([idiom] at all), H4194 (dead), H8546 (death)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G86 ᾅδης, G5054 τελευτή",
    4195: "מֹותָר (môwthâr | mo-thar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3498 יָתַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> literally gain; figuratively, superiority<BR><B>KJV:</B> plenteousness, preeminence, profit.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H1956 (Hothir), H4340 (cord), H3502 (abundance), H3503 (Jethro), H3504 (better), H3508 (caul), H4195 (plenteousness), H3505 (Ithrite), H3492 (Jattir), H3148 (better), H3506 (Ithran), H3500 (Jether), H3498 (excel), H3501 (Ithra), H3499 (abundant), H3509 (Jetheth), H3507 (Ithream)",
    4196: "מִזְבֵּחַ (mizbêach | miz-bay'-akh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H2076 זָבַח<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an altar<BR><B>KJV:</B> altar.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2081 (Zebina), H2078 (Zebah), H4196 (altar), H2077 (offer), H2076 (kill)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1041 βωμός, G2379 θυσιαστήριον",
    4197: "מֶזֶג (mezeg | meh'-zeg)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to mingle (water with wine)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> tempered wine<BR><B>KJV:</B> liquor.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4197 (liquor)",
    4198: "מָזֶה (mâzeh | maw-zeh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to suck out<BR><B>Strong's:</B> exhausted<BR><B>KJV:</B> burnt.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4198 (burnt), H4199 (Mizzah)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5080 τήκω",
    4199: "מִזָּה (Mizzâh | miz-zaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from an unused root meaning to faint with fear; terror<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Mizzah, an Edomite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Mizzah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4198 (burnt), H4199 (Mizzah)",
    4200: "מֶזֶו (mezev | meh'-zev)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from an unused root meaning to gather in<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a granary<BR><B>KJV:</B> garner.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2106 (corner), H4200 (garner)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5009 ταμεῖον",
    4201: "מְזוּזָה (mᵉzûwzâh | mez-oo-zaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or מְזֻזָה; from the same as H2123 זִיז<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a door-post (as prominent)<BR><B>KJV:</B> (door, side) post.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4201 (post), H2124 (Ziza), H2123 (abundance), H2117 (Zaza), H3151 (Jaziz), H2125 (Zizah), H2126 (Zina)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G380 ἀναπτύσσω, G4745 στοά",
    4202: "מָזֹון (mâzôwn | maw-zone')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H2109 זוּן<BR><B>Strong's:</B> food<BR><B>KJV:</B> meat, victual.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2109 (feed), H4202 (meat)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5160 τροφή",
    4203: "מָזֹון (mâzôwn | maw-zone')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H4202 מָזֹון<BR><B>Strong's:</B> food<BR><B>KJV:</B> meat.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4203 (meat), H2110 (feed)",
    4204: "מָזֹור (mâzôwr | maw-zore')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H2114 זוּר in the sense of turning aside from truth<BR><B>Strong's:</B> treachery, i.e. a plot<BR><B>KJV:</B> wound.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4204 (wound), H4216 (Mazzoroth)",
    4205: "מָזֹור (mâzôwr | maw-zore')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or מָזֹר; from H2115 זוּר in the sense of binding up<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a bandage, i.e. remedy; hence, a sore (as needing a compress)<BR><B>KJV:</B> bound up, wound.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2115 (close), H2116 (that which is crushed), H4205 (bound up), H2213 (crown), H2223 (greyhound)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3601 ὀδύνη",
    4206: "מָזִיחַ (mâzîyach | maw-zee'-akh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or מֵזַח; from H2118 זָחַח<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a belt (as movable)<BR><B>KJV:</B> girdle, strength.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4208 (planet), H4206 (girdle)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2223 ζώνη",
    4207: "מַזְלֵג (mazlêg | maz-layg')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or (feminine) מִזְלָגָה; from an unused root meaning to draw up<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a fork<BR><B>KJV:</B> fleshhook.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4207 (fleshhook)",
    4208: "מַזָּלָה (mazzâlâh | maz-zaw-law')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently from H5140 נָזַל in the sense of raining<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a constellation, i.e. Zodiacal sign (perhaps as affecting the weather)<BR><B>KJV:</B> planet. Compare H4216 מַזָּרָה .<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4208 (planet), H4206 (girdle)",
    4209: "מְזִמָּה (mᵉzimmâh | mez-im-maw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H2161 זָמַם<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a plan, usually evil (machination), sometimes good (sagacity)<BR><B>KJV:</B> (wicked) device, discretion, intent, witty invention, lewdness, mischievous (device), thought, wickedly.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4209 (device), H2155 (Zimmah), H2157 (Zamzummim), H2162 (wicked device), H2161 (consider), H2154 (heinous crime)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G946 βδέλυγμα, G1012 βουλή, G1771 ἔννοια, G2570 καλός, G3892 παρανομία, G5429 φρόνιμος",
