    5012: "נָבָא (nâbâʼ | naw-baw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to prophesy, i.e. speak (or sing) by inspiration (in prediction or simple discourse)<BR><B>KJV:</B> prophesy(-ing), make self a prophet.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5030 (prophecy), H5031 (prophetess), H5016 (prophecy), H5012 (prophesy)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G669 ἀποφθέγγομαι, G2980 λαλέω, G4395 προφητεύω",
    5013: "נְבָא (nᵉbâʼ | neb-aw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H5012 נָבָא<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to prophesy, i.e. speak (or sing) by inspiration (in prediction or simple discourse) to prophesy, i.e. speak (or sing) by inspiration (in prediction or simple discourse)<BR><B>KJV:</B> prophesy.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5023 (reward), H5013 (prophesy), H5017 (prophesying), H5020 (Nebuchadnezzar), H5043 (candlestick), H5029 (prophet)",
    5014: "נָבַב (nâbab | naw-bab')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to pierce; to be hollow, or (figuratively) foolish<BR><B>KJV:</B> hollow, vain.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5018 (Nebuzaradan), H5015 (Nebo), H5021 (Nebushazban), H5022 (Naboth), H5019 (Nebuchadnezzar), H5014 (hollow)",
    5015: "נְבֹו (Nᵉbôw | neb-o')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably of foreign derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nebo, the name of a Babylonian deity, also of a mountain in Moab, and of a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nebo.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5018 (Nebuzaradan), H5015 (Nebo), H5021 (Nebushazban), H5022 (Naboth), H5019 (Nebuchadnezzar), H5014 (hollow)",
