    5020: "נְבוּכַדְנֶצַּר (Nᵉbûwkadnetstsar | neb-oo-kad-nets-tsar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H5019 נְבוּכַדְנֶאצַּר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nebukadnetstsar (or -retstsar, or -retstsor), king of Babylon<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nebuchadnezzar.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5023 (reward), H5013 (prophesy), H5017 (prophesying), H5020 (Nebuchadnezzar), H5043 (candlestick), H5029 (prophet)",
    5021: "נְבוּשַׁזְבָּן (Nᵉbûwshazbân | neb-oo-shaz-bawn')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of foreign derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nebushazban, Nebuchadnezzar's chief eunuch<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nebushazban.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5018 (Nebuzaradan), H5015 (Nebo), H5021 (Nebushazban), H5022 (Naboth), H5019 (Nebuchadnezzar), H5014 (hollow)",
    5022: "נָבֹות (Nâbôwth | naw-both')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine plural from the same as H5011 נֹב ; fruits<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Naboth, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Naboth.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5018 (Nebuzaradan), H5015 (Nebo), H5021 (Nebushazban), H5022 (Naboth), H5019 (Nebuchadnezzar), H5014 (hollow)",
    5023: "נְבִזְבָּה (nᵉbizbâh | neb-iz-baw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a largess<BR><B>KJV:</B> reward.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5023 (reward), H5013 (prophesy), H5017 (prophesying), H5020 (Nebuchadnezzar), H5043 (candlestick), H5029 (prophet)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1431 δωρεά",
    5024: "נָבַח (nâbach | naw-bakh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to bark (as a dog)<BR><B>KJV:</B> bark.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5025 (Nobah), H5024 (bark), H5026 (Nibhaz)",
    5025: "נֹבַח (Nôbach | no'-bach)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5024 נָבַח ; a bark<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nobach, the name of an Israelite, and of a place East of the Jordan<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nobah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5025 (Nobah), H5024 (bark), H5026 (Nibhaz)",
    5026: "נִבְחַז (Nibchaz | nib-khaz')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of foreign origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nibchaz, a deity of the Avites<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nibhaz.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5025 (Nobah), H5024 (bark), H5026 (Nibhaz)",
