    5033: "נֵבֶךְ (nêbek | nay'-bek)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to burst forth<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a fountain<BR><B>KJV:</B> spring.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5027 (behold), H5032 (Nebaioth), H4007 (expectation), H5028 (Nebat), H5033 (spring)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4077 πηγή",
    5034: "נָבֵל (nâbêl | naw-bale')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to wilt; generally, to fall away, fail, faint; figuratively, to be foolish or (morally) wicked; causatively, to despise, disgrace<BR><B>KJV:</B> disgrace, dishounour, lightly esteem, fade (away, -ing), fall (down, -ling, off), do foolishly, come to nought, [idiom] surely, make vile, wither.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5037 (Nabal), H5034 (disgrace), H5040 (lewdness), H5039 (folly), H5036 (fool)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G167 ἀκαθαρσία, G577 ἀποβάλλω, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G634 ἀποπίπτω, G641 ἀποῤῥίπτω, G818 ἀτιμάζω, G868 ἀφίστημι, G2704 καταφθείρω, G3822 παλαιόω, G4098 πίπτω, G5351 φθείρω, G5356 φθορά",
    5035: "נֶבֶל (nebel | neh'-bel)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or נֵבֶל; from H5034 נָבֵל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a skin-bag for liquids (from collapsing when empty); hence, a vase (as similar in shape when full); also a lyre (as having a body of like form)<BR><B>KJV:</B> bottle, pitcher, psaltery, vessel, viol.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5035 (bottle)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G30 ἀγγεῖον, G779 ἀσκός, G2167 εὐφροσύνη, G2788 κιθάρα, G5568 ψαλμός",
    5036: "נָבָל (nâbâl | naw-bawl')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5034 נָבֵל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> stupid; wicked (especially impious)<BR><B>KJV:</B> fool(-ish, -ish man, -ish woman), vile person.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5037 (Nabal), H5034 (disgrace), H5040 (lewdness), H5039 (folly), H5036 (fool)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G521 ἀπαίδευτος, G801 ἀσύνετος, G878 ἄφρων, G3474 μωρός",
    5037: "נָבָל (Nâbâl | naw-bawl')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> the same as H5036 נָבָל ; dolt<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nabal, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nabal.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5037 (Nabal), H5034 (disgrace), H5040 (lewdness), H5039 (folly), H5036 (fool)",
    5038: "נְבֵלָה (nᵉbêlâh | neb-ay-law')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5034 נָבֵל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a flabby thing, i.e. a carcase or carrion (human or bestial, often collectively); figuratively, an idol<BR><B>KJV:</B> (dead) body, (dead) carcase, dead of itself, which died, (beast) that (which) dieth of itself.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5038 (body), H5041 (Neballat), H5034 (disgrace)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3498 νεκρός, G4983 σῶμα",
    5039: "נְבָלָה (nᵉbâlâh | neb-aw-law')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of H5036 נָבָל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> foolishness, i.e. (morally) wickedness; concretely, a crime; by extension, punishment<BR><B>KJV:</B> folly, vile, villany.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5037 (Nabal), H5034 (disgrace), H5040 (lewdness), H5039 (folly), H5036 (fool)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G94 ἄδικος, G458 ἀνομία, G809 ἀσχήμων, G877 ἀφροσύνη, G1135 γυνή",
    5040: "נַבְלוּת (nablûwth | nab-looth')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5036 נָבָל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, disgrace, i.e. the (female) pudenda<BR><B>KJV:</B> lewdness.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5037 (Nabal), H5034 (disgrace), H5040 (lewdness), H5039 (folly), H5036 (fool)",
    5041: "נְבַלָּט (Nᵉballâṭ | neb-al-lawt')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently from H5036 נָבָל and H3909 לָט ; foolish secrecy<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Neballat, a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Neballat.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5038 (body), H5041 (Neballat), H5034 (disgrace)",
    5042: "נָבַע (nâbaʻ | naw-bah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to gush forth; figuratively, to utter (good or bad words); specifically, to emit (a foul odor)<BR><B>KJV:</B> belch out, flowing, pour out, send forth, utter (abundantly).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4002 (fountain), H5042 (belch out)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G312 ἀναγγέλλω, G611 ἀποκρίνομαι, G669 ἀποφθέγγομαι, G2044 ἐρεύγομαι, G5350 φθέγγομαι",
    5043: "נֶבְרְשָׁא (nebrᵉshâʼ | neb-reh-shaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) from an unused root meaning to shine<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a light; plural (collectively) a chandelier<BR><B>KJV:</B> candlestick.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5023 (reward), H5013 (prophesy), H5017 (prophesying), H5020 (Nebuchadnezzar), H5043 (candlestick), H5029 (prophet)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2985 λαμπάς, G5457 φῶς",
    5044: "נִבְשָׁן (Nibshân | nib-shawn')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nibshan, a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nibshan.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5044 (Nibshan), H1316 (Bashan)",
    5045: "נֶגֶב (negeb | neh'-gheb)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to be parched<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the south (from its drought); specifically, the Negeb or southern district of Judah, occasionally, Egypt (as south to Palestine)<BR><B>KJV:</B> south (country, side, -ward).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5045 (south)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2048 ἔρημος, G3047 λίψ, G3314 μεσημβρία, G3558 νότος",
    5046: "נָגַד (nâgad | naw-gad')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to front, i.e. stand boldly out opposite; by implication (causatively), to manifest; figuratively, to announce (always by word of mouth to one present); specifically, to expose, predict, explain, praise<BR><B>KJV:</B> bewray, [idiom] certainly, certify, declare(-ing), denounce, expound, [idiom] fully, messenger, plainly, profess, rehearse, report, shew (forth), speak, [idiom] surely, tell, utter.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5046 (bewray), H5048 (about), H5057 (captain)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G31 ἀγγελία, G312 ἀναγγέλλω, G518 ἀπαγγέλλω, G601 ἀποκαλύπτω, G1097 γινώσκω, G1166 δεικνύω, G2980 λαλέω, G4302 προλέγω, G4591 σημαίνω, G5263 ὑποδείκνυμι",
    5047: "נְגַד (nᵉgad | neg-ad')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H5046 נָגַד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to flow (through the idea of clearing the way)<BR><B>KJV:</B> issue.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5049 (toward), H5053 (morning), H5047 (issue)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1670 ἑλκύω",
    5048: "נֶגֶד (neged | neh'-ghed)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5046 נָגַד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a front, i.e. part opposite; specifically a counterpart, or mate; usually (adverbial, especially with preposition) over against or before<BR><B>KJV:</B> about, (over) against, [idiom] aloof, [idiom] far (off), [idiom] from, over, presence, [idiom] other side, sight, [idiom] to view.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5046 (bewray), H5048 (about), H5057 (captain)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G991 βλέπω, G1726 ἐναντίον, G1726 ἐναντίον, G1727 ἐναντίος, G1727 ἐναντίος, G2064 ἔρχομαι, G2112 εὐθέως, G2117 εὐθύς, G2192 ἔχω, G3664 ὅμοιος, G3775 οὖς",
    5049: "נֶגֶד (neged | neh'-ghed)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H5048 נֶגֶד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> opposite<BR><B>KJV:</B> toward.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5049 (toward), H5053 (morning), H5047 (issue)",
    5050: "נָגַהּ (nâgahh | naw-gah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to glitter; causatively, to illuminate<BR><B>KJV:</B> (en-) lighten, (cause to) shine.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5054 (brightness), H5052 (Nogah), H5050 (lighten), H5051 (bright)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G305 ἀναβαίνω, G1325 δίδωμι, G1584 ἐκλάμπω, G2989 λάμπω, G5461 φωτίζω",
    5051: "נֹגַהּ (nôgahh | no'-gah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5050 נָגַהּ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> brilliancy (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> bright(-ness), light, (clear) shining.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5054 (brightness), H5052 (Nogah), H5050 (lighten), H5051 (bright)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G395 ἀνατολή, G2987 λαμπρότης, G5338 φέγγος, G5457 φῶς",
    5052: "נֹגַהּ (Nôgahh | no'-gah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> the same as H5051 נֹגַהּ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nogah, a son of David<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nogah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5054 (brightness), H5052 (Nogah), H5050 (lighten), H5051 (bright)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3477 Ναγγαί",
    5053: "נֹגַהּ (nôgahh | no'-gah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H5051 נֹגַהּ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> dawn<BR><B>KJV:</B> morning.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5049 (toward), H5053 (morning), H5047 (issue)",
    5054: "נְגֹהָה (nᵉgôhâh | neg-o-haw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of H5051 נֹגַהּ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> splendor<BR><B>KJV:</B> brightness.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5054 (brightness), H5052 (Nogah), H5050 (lighten), H5051 (bright)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G827 αὐγή",
    5055: "נָגַח (nâgach | naw-gakh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to butt with the horns; figuratively, to war against<BR><B>KJV:</B> gore, push (down, -ing).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5055 (gore), H5056 (used to push)",
    5056: "נַגָּח (naggâch | nag-gawkh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5055 נָגַח<BR><B>Strong's:</B> butting, i.e. vicious<BR><B>KJV:</B> used (wont) to push.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5055 (gore), H5056 (used to push)",
    5057: "נָגִיד (nâgîyd | naw-gheed')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or נָגִד; from H5046 נָגַד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a commander (as occupying the front), civil, military or religious; generally (abstractly, plural), honorable themes<BR><B>KJV:</B> captain, chief, excellent thing, (chief) governor, leader, noble, prince, (chief) ruler.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5046 (bewray), H5048 (about), H5057 (captain)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G758 ἄρχων, G935 βασιλεύς, G1988 ἐπιστάτης, G2233 ἡγέομαι, G4586 σεμνός",
    5058: "נְגִינָה (nᵉgîynâh | neg-ee-naw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or נְגִינַת; (Psalm 61:title), from H5059 נָגַן<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, instrumental music; by implication, a stringed instrument; by extension, a poem set to music; specifically, an epigram<BR><B>KJV:</B> stringed instrument, musick, Neginoth (plural), song.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4485 (music), H5058 (stringed instrument), H5059 (player on instruments)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2788 κιθάρα, G5215 ὕμνος, G5603 ᾠδή",
    5059: "נָגַן (nâgan | naw-gan')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to thrum, i.e. beat atune with the fingers; expectation. to play on astringed instrument; hence (generally), to make music<BR><B>KJV:</B> player on instruments, sing to the stringed instruments, melody, ministrel, play(-er, -ing).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4485 (music), H5058 (stringed instrument), H5059 (player on instruments)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2127 εὐλογέω, G2789 κιθαρίζω, G5567 ψάλλω, G5568 ψαλμός",
    5060: "נָגַע (nâgaʻ | naw-gah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to touch, i.e. lay the hand upon (for any purpose; euphemistically, to lie with a woman); by implication, to reach (figuratively, to arrive, acquire); violently, to strike (punish, defeat, destroy, etc.)<BR><B>KJV:</B> beat, ([idiom] be able to) bring (down), cast, come (nigh), draw near (nigh), get up, happen, join, near, plague, reach (up), smite, strike, touch.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5061 (plague), H5060 (beat)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G378 ἀναπληρόω, G402 ἀναχωρέω, G680 ἅπτομαι, G681 ἅπτω, G864 ἀφικνέομαι, G1096 γίνομαι, G1448 ἐγγίζω, G1620 ἐκτίθημι, G1651 ἐλέγχω, G2345 θιγγάνω, G2480 ἰσχύω, G2597 καταβαίνω, G2609 κατάγω, G2853 κολλάω, G3146 μαστιγόω, G3854 παραγίνομαι, G3918 πάρειμι, G4192 πόνος, G4317 προσάγω, G4331 προσεγγίζω, G4363 προσπίπτω, G4404 πρωΐ, G4863 συνάγω, G4876 συναντάω, G5087 τίθημι, G5348 φθάνω",
    5061: "נֶגַע (negaʻ | neh'-gah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5060 נָגַע<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a blow (figuratively, infliction); also (by implication) a spot (concretely, a leprous person or dress)<BR><B>KJV:</B> plague, sore, stricken, stripe, stroke, wound.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5061 (plague), H5060 (beat)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G860 ἁφή, G3148 μάστιξ, G3601 ὀδύνη, G4127 πληγή",
    5062: "נָגַף (nâgaph | naw-gaf')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to push, gore, defeat, stub (the toe), inflict (a disease)<BR><B>KJV:</B> beat, dash, hurt, plague, slay, smite (down), strike, stumble, [idiom] surely, put to the worse.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4046 (plague), H5063 (plague), H5062 (beat)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2352 θραύω, G2871 κοπή, G2875 κόπτω, G3811 παιδεύω, G3817 παίω, G3960 πατάσσω, G4098 πίπτω, G4141 πλήσσω, G4350 προσκόπτω, G4417 πταίω, G4937 συντρίβω, G5180 τύπτω",
    5063: "נֶגֶף (negeph | neh'-ghef)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5062 נָגַף<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a trip (of the foot); figuratively, an infliction (of disease)<BR><B>KJV:</B> plague, stumbling.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4046 (plague), H5063 (plague), H5062 (beat)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4127 πληγή, G4348 πρόσκομμα, G4431 πτῶσις",
    5064: "נָגַר (nâgar | naw-gar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to flow; figuratively, to stretch out; causatively, to pour out or down; figuratively, to deliver over<BR><B>KJV:</B> fall, flow away, pour down (out), run, shed, spilt, trickle down.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5064 (fall)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1904 ἐπέρχομαι, G2666 καταπίνω, G2702 καταφέρω, G3860 παραδίδωμι, G4867 συναθροίζω",
    5065: "נָגַשׂ (nâgas | naw-gas')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to drive (an animal, a workman, a debtor, an army); by implication, to tax, harass, tyrannize<BR><B>KJV:</B> distress, driver, exact(-or), oppress(-or), [idiom] raiser of taxes, taskmaster.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5065 (distress)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G523 ἀπαιτέω, G1325 δίδωμι, G1643 ἐλαύνω, G1985 ἐπίσκοπος, G1988 ἐπιστάτης, G4238 πράσσω, G4317 προσάγω",
    5066: "נָגַשׁ (nâgash | naw-gash')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be or come (causatively, bring) near (for any purpose); euphemistically, to lie with a woman; as an enemy, to attack; religious to worship; causatively, to present; figuratively, to adduce an argument; by reversal, to stand back<BR><B>KJV:</B> (make to) approach (nigh), bring (forth, hither, near), (cause to) come (hither, near, nigh), give place, go hard (up), (be, draw, go) near (nigh), offer, overtake, present, put, stand.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5066 (approach)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G654 ἀποστρέφω, G868 ἀφίστημι, G1011 βουλεύω, G1448 ἐγγίζω, G1525 εἰσέρχομαι, G1994 ἐπιστρέφω, G2638 καταλαμβάνω, G2853 κολλάω, G2961 κυριεύω, G4198 πορεύομαι, G4233 πράκτωρ, G4254 προάγω, G4317 προσάγω, G4331 προσεγγίζω, G4334 προσέρχομαι, G4365 προσπορεύομαι, G4374 προσφέρω, G5117 τόπος, G5342 φέρω",
    5067: "נֵד (nêd | nade)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5110 נוּד in the sense of piling up<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a mound, i.e. wave<BR><B>KJV:</B> heap.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5067 (heap)",
    5068: "נָדַב (nâdab | naw-dab')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to impel; hence, to volunteer (as a soldier), to present spontaneously<BR><B>KJV:</B> offer freely, be (give, make, offer self) willing(-ly).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5070 (Nadab), H5072 (Nedabiah), H5071 (free offering), H5068 (offer freely), H5114 (Nodab), H5082 (soul), H5081 (free)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1380 δοκέω, G1413 δυνάστης, G1595 ἑκούσιον, G5342 φέρω",
    5069: "נְדַב (nᵉdab | ned-ab')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H5068 נָדַב<BR><B>Strong's:</B> be (or give) liberal(-ly)<BR><B>KJV:</B> (be minded of...own) freewill (offering), offer freely (willingly).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5069 (freewill), H5073 (row)",
    5070: "נָדָב (Nâdâb | naw-dawb')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5068 נָדַב ; liberal<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nadab, the name of four Israelites<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nadab.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5070 (Nadab), H5072 (Nedabiah), H5071 (free offering), H5068 (offer freely), H5114 (Nodab), H5082 (soul), H5081 (free)",
    5071: "נְדָבָה (nᵉdâbâh | ned-aw-baw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5068 נָדַב<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly (abstractly) spontaneity, or (adjectively) spontaneous; also (concretely) a spontaneous or (by inference, in plural) abundant gift<BR><B>KJV:</B> free(-will) offering, freely, plentiful, voluntary(-ily, offering), willing(-ly), offering).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5070 (Nadab), H5072 (Nedabiah), H5071 (free offering), H5068 (offer freely), H5114 (Nodab), H5082 (soul), H5081 (free)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G139 αἵρεσις, G1390 δόμα, G1595 ἑκούσιον, G3671 ὁμολογία, G4968 σφάγιον",
    5072: "נְדַבְיָה (Nᵉdabyâh | ned-ab-yaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5068 נָדַב and H3050 יָהּ ; largess of Jah<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nedabjah, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nedabiah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5070 (Nadab), H5072 (Nedabiah), H5071 (free offering), H5068 (offer freely), H5114 (Nodab), H5082 (soul), H5081 (free)",
    5073: "נִדְבָּךְ (nidbâk | nid-bawk')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) from a root meaning to stick<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a layer (of building materials)<BR><B>KJV:</B> row.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5069 (freewill), H5073 (row)",
    5074: "נָדַד (nâdad | naw-dad')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to wave to and fro (rarely to flap up and down); figuratively, to rove, flee, or (causatively) to drive away<BR><B>KJV:</B> chase (away), [idiom] could not, depart, flee ([idiom] apace, away), (re-) move, thrust away, wander (abroad, -er, -ing).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5076 (tossing to and fro), H5074 (chase), H5206 (removed), H5079 ([idiom] far)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G868 ἀφίστημι, G948 βδελύσσω, G1309 διαφεύγω, G1839 ἐξίστημι, G1856 ἐξωθέω, G2064 ἔρχομαι, G2172 εὔχομαι, G2597 καταβαίνω, G4072 πέτομαι, G4107 πλανήτης, G4422 πτοέω, G5015 ταράσσω, G5343 φεύγω",
    5075: "נְדַד (nᵉdad | ned-ad')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H5074 נָדַד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to depart<BR><B>KJV:</B> go from.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5103 (river), H5085 (body), H5075 (go from), H5094 (light)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1096 γίνομαι",
    5076: "נָדֻד (nâdud | naw-dood')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> passive participle of H5074 נָדַד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, tossed; abstractly, a rolling (on the bed)<BR><B>KJV:</B> tossing to and fro.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5076 (tossing to and fro), H5074 (chase), H5206 (removed), H5079 ([idiom] far)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3601 ὀδύνη",
    5077: "נָדָה (nâdâh | naw-daw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or נָדָא; (2 Kings 17:21), a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to toss; figuratively, to exclude, i.e. banish, postpone, prohibit<BR><B>KJV:</B> cast out, drive, put far away.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5077 (cast out)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1856 ἐξωθέω",
    5078: "נֵדֶה (nêdeh | nay'-deh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5077 נָדָה in the sense of freely flinging money<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a bounty (for prostitution)<BR><B>KJV:</B> gifts.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5078 (gifts)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3410 μίσθωμα",
    5079: "נִדָּה (niddâh | nid-daw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5074 נָדַד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, rejection; by implication, impurity, especially personal (menstruation) or moral (idolatry, incest)<BR><B>KJV:</B> [idiom] far, filthiness, [idiom] flowers, menstruous (woman), put apart, [idiom] removed (woman), separation, set apart, unclean(-ness, thing, with filthiness).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5076 (tossing to and fro), H5074 (chase), H5206 (removed), H5079 ([idiom] far)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G49 ἁγνισμός, G167 ἀκαθαρσία, G3334 μετακινέω, G4473 ῥαντισμός",
    5080: "נָדַח (nâdach | naw-dakh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to push off; used in a great variety of applications, literally and figuratively (to expel, mislead, strike, inflict, etc.)<BR><B>KJV:</B> banish, bring, cast down (out), chase, compel, draw away, drive (away, out, quite), fetch a stroke, force, go away, outcast, thrust away (out), withdraw.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5083 (gift), H4065 (cause of banishment), H5084 (sheath), H5080 (banish)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G548 ἄπειμι, G622 ἀπόλλυμι, G635 ἀποπλανάω, G683 ἀπωθέομαι, G868 ἀφίστημι, G1287 διασκορπίζω, G1289 διασπείρω, G1290 διασπορά, G1544 ἐκβάλλω, G1856 ἐξωθέω, G1911 ἐπιβάλλω, G4105 πλανάω, G4687 σπείρω, G5343 φεύγω",
    5081: "נָדִיב (nâdîyb | naw-deeb')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5068 נָדַב<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, voluntary, i.e. generous; hence, magnanimous; as noun, a grandee (sometimes a tyrant)<BR><B>KJV:</B> free, liberal (things), noble, prince, willing (hearted).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5070 (Nadab), H5072 (Nedabiah), H5071 (free offering), H5068 (offer freely), H5114 (Nodab), H5082 (soul), H5081 (free)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G757 ἄρχω, G758 ἄρχων, G935 βασιλεύς, G1342 δίκαιος, G2152 εὐσεβής, G4289 πρόθυμος",
    5082: "נְדִיבָה (nᵉdîybâh | ned-ee-baw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of H5081 נָדִיב<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, nobility, i.e. reputation<BR><B>KJV:</B> soul.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5070 (Nadab), H5072 (Nedabiah), H5071 (free offering), H5068 (offer freely), H5114 (Nodab), H5082 (soul), H5081 (free)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1680 ἐλπίς, G4908 συνετός",
    5083: "נָדָן (nâdân | naw-dawn')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from an unused root meaning to give<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a present (for prostitution)<BR><B>KJV:</B> gift.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5083 (gift), H4065 (cause of banishment), H5084 (sheath), H5080 (banish)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3410 μίσθωμα",
    5084: "נָדָן (nâdân | naw-dawn')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a sheath (of a sword)<BR><B>KJV:</B> sheath.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5083 (gift), H4065 (cause of banishment), H5084 (sheath), H5080 (banish)",
    5085: "נִדְנֶה (nidneh | nid-neh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) from the same as H5084 נָדָן<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a sheath; figuratively, the body (as the receptacle of the soul)<BR><B>KJV:</B> body.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5103 (river), H5085 (body), H5075 (go from), H5094 (light)",
    5086: "נָדַף (nâdaph | naw-daf')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to shove asunder, i.e. disperse<BR><B>KJV:</B> drive (away, to and fro), thrust down, shaken, tossed to and fro.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5086 (drive)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1377 διώκω, G1587 ἐκλείπω, G1856 ἐξωθέω, G2795 κινέω, G3679 ὀνειδίζω, G3947 παροξύνω, G5342 φέρω",
    5087: "נָדַר (nâdar | naw-dar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to promise (pos., to do or give something to God)<BR><B>KJV:</B> (make a) vow.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5088 (vow), H5087 (vow)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2171 εὐχή, G2172 εὔχομαι, G3670 ὁμολογέω",
    5088: "נֶדֶר (neder | neh'-der)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or נֵדֶר; from H5087 נָדַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a promise (to God); also (concretely) a thing promised<BR><B>KJV:</B> vow(-ed).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5088 (vow), H5087 (vow)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1435 δῶρον, G2171 εὐχή, G3671 ὁμολογία",
    5089: "נֹהַּ (nôahh | no'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to lament<BR><B>Strong's:</B> lamentation<BR><B>KJV:</B> wailing.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5089 (wailing)",
    5090: "נָהַג (nâhag | naw-hag')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to drive forth (a person, an animal or chariot), i.e. lead, carry away; reflexively, to proceed (i.e. impel or guide oneself); also (from the panting induced by effort), to sigh<BR><B>KJV:</B> acquaint, bring (away), carry away, drive (away), lead (away, forth), (be) guide, lead (away, forth).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4491 (driving), H5090 (acquaint)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G71 ἄγω, G162 αἰχμαλωτεύω, G321 ἀνάγω, G520 ἀπάγω, G1521 εἰσάγω, G1863 ἐπάγω, G3870 παρακαλέω, G3880 παραλαμβάνω, G4165 ποιμαίνω",
    5091: "נָהָה (nâhâh | naw-haw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to groan, i.e. bewail; hence (through the idea of crying aloud), to assemble (as if on proclamation)<BR><B>KJV:</B> lament, wail.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5204 (wailing), H5091 (lament), H5093 (doleful), H5092 (lamentation)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1914 ἐπιβλέπω, G2354 θρηνέω",
    5092: "נְהִי (nᵉhîy | neh-hee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5091 נָהָה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an elegy<BR><B>KJV:</B> lamentation, wailing.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5204 (wailing), H5091 (lament), H5093 (doleful), H5092 (lamentation)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2355 θρῆνος, G2870 κοπετός",
    5093: "נִהְיָה (nihyâh | nih-yaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of H5092 נְהִי<BR><B>Strong's:</B> lamentation<BR><B>KJV:</B> doleful.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5204 (wailing), H5091 (lament), H5093 (doleful), H5092 (lamentation)",
    5094: "נְהִיר (nᵉhîyr | neh-heere')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) or נְהִירוּ; (Aramaic), from the same as H5105 נְהָרָה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> illumination, i.e. (figuratively) wisdom<BR><B>KJV:</B> light.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5103 (river), H5085 (body), H5075 (go from), H5094 (light)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5457 φῶς",
    5095: "נָהַל (nâhal | naw-hal')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to run with asparkle, i.e. flow; hence (transitively), to conduct, and (by inference) to protect, sustain<BR><B>KJV:</B> carry, feed, guide, lead (gently, on).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5097 (bush), H5095 (carry), H5096 (Nahalal)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G71 ἄγω, G482 ἀντιλαμβάνομαι, G1625 ἐκτρέφω, G1765 ἐνισχύω, G2664 καταπαύω, G3870 παρακαλέω",
    5096: "נַהֲלָל (Nahălâl | nah-hal-awl')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or נַהֲלֹל; the same as H5097 נַהֲלֹל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nahalal or Nahalol, a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nahalal, Nahallal, Nahalol.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5097 (bush), H5095 (carry), H5096 (Nahalal)",
    5097: "נַהֲלֹל (nahălôl | nah-hal-ole')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5095 נָהַל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> pasture<BR><B>KJV:</B> bush.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5097 (bush), H5095 (carry), H5096 (Nahalal)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3586 ξύλον",
    5098: "נָהַם (nâham | naw-ham')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to growl<BR><B>KJV:</B> mourn, roar(-ing).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5099 (roaring), H5100 (disquietness), H5098 (mourn)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G994 βοάω, G1030 βρυγμός, G1980 ἐπισκέπτομαι, G2372 θυμός, G3338 μεταμέλλομαι, G3983 πεινάω",
