    5100: "נְהָמָה (nᵉhâmâh | neh-haw-maw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of H5099 נַהַם<BR><B>Strong's:</B> snarling<BR><B>KJV:</B> disquietness, roaring.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5099 (roaring), H5100 (disquietness), H5098 (mourn)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4726 στεναγμός, G5456 φωνή",
    5101: "נָהַק (nâhaq | naw-hak')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to bray (as an ass), scream (from hunger)<BR><B>KJV:</B> bray.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5101 (bray)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G994 βοάω, G2896 κράζω",
    5102: "נָהַר (nâhar | naw-har')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to sparkle, i.e. (figuratively) be cheerful; hence (from the sheen of a running stream) to flow, i.e. (figuratively) assemble<BR><B>KJV:</B> flow (together), be lightened.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5104 (flood), H5102 (flow)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2240 ἥκω, G4863 συνάγω, G5461 φωτίζω",
    5103: "נְהַר (nᵉhar | neh-har')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H5102 נָהַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a river, especially the Euphrates<BR><B>KJV:</B> river, stream.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5103 (river), H5085 (body), H5075 (go from), H5094 (light)",
    5104: "נָהָר (nâhâr | naw-hawr')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5102 נָהַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a stream (including the sea; expectation the Nile, Euphrates, etc.); figuratively, prosperity<BR><B>KJV:</B> flood, river.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5104 (flood), H5102 (flow)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4215 ποταμός",
    5105: "נְהָרָה (nᵉhârâh | neh-haw-raw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5102 נָהַר in its original sense<BR><B>Strong's:</B> daylight<BR><B>KJV:</B> light.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4492 (den), H5105 (light), H5102 (flow)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5338 φέγγος",
    5106: "נוּא (nûwʼ | noo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to refuse, forbid, dissuade, or neutralize<BR><B>KJV:</B> break, disallow, discourage, make of none effect.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5106 (break), H8569 (breach of promise)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G114 ἀθετέω, G868 ἀφίστημι, G1294 διαστρέφω, G3310 μερίς",
    5107: "נוּב (nûwb | noob)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to germinate, i.e. (figuratively) to (causatively, make) flourish; also (of words), to utter<BR><B>KJV:</B> bring forth (fruit), make cheerful, increase.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5107 (bring forth), H8570 (fruit), H5109 (Nebai), H5108 (fruit)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4129 πληθύνω, G4482 ῥέω",
    5108: "נֹוב (nôwb | nobe)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or נֵיב; from H5107 נוּב<BR><B>Strong's:</B> produce, literally or figuratively<BR><B>KJV:</B> fruit.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5107 (bring forth), H8570 (fruit), H5109 (Nebai), H5108 (fruit)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2007 ἐπιτίθημι",
    5109: "נֹובַי (Nôwbay | no-bah'ee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5108 נֹוב ; fruitful<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nobai, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nebai (from the margin).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5107 (bring forth), H8570 (fruit), H5109 (Nebai), H5108 (fruit)",
    5110: "נוּד (nûwd | nood)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to nod, i.e. waver; figuratively, to wander, flee, disappear; also (from shaking the head in sympathy), to console, deplore, or (from tossing the head in scorn) taunt<BR><B>KJV:</B> bemoan, flee, get, mourn, make to move, take pity, remove, shake, skip for joy, be sorry, vagabond, way, wandering.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4493 (shaking), H5205 (moving), H5112 (wandering), H5113 (Nod), H5110 (bemoan)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G526 ἀπαλλοτριόω, G1168 δειλιάω, G2354 θρηνέω, G2795 κινέω, G3996 πενθέω, G4531 σαλεύω, G4727 στενάζω",
    5111: "נוּד (nûwd | nood)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H5116 נָוֶה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to flee<BR><B>KJV:</B> get away.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5111 (get away), H5122 (dunghill), H5135 (fiery)",
    5112: "נֹוד (nôwd | node)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (only defective נֹד); from H5110 נוּד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> exile<BR><B>KJV:</B> wandering.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4493 (shaking), H5205 (moving), H5112 (wandering), H5113 (Nod), H5110 (bemoan)",
    5113: "נֹוד (Nôwd | node)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> the same as H5112 נֹוד; vagrancy<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nod, the land of Cain<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nod.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4493 (shaking), H5205 (moving), H5112 (wandering), H5113 (Nod), H5110 (bemoan)",
    5114: "נֹודָב (Nôwdâb | no-dawb')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5068 נָדַב ; noble<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nodab, an Arab tribe<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nodab.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5070 (Nadab), H5072 (Nedabiah), H5071 (free offering), H5068 (offer freely), H5114 (Nodab), H5082 (soul), H5081 (free)",
    5115: "נָוָה (nâvâh | naw-vaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root; (compare H5116 נָוֶה)<BR><BR><B>Strong's:</B> to rest (as at home); causatively (through the implied idea of beauty), to celebrate (with praises)<BR><B>KJV:</B> keept at home, prepare an habitation.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5115 (keept at home)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1392 δοξάζω",
    5116: "נָוֶה (nâveh | naw-veh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or (feminine) נָוָה; from H5115 נָוָה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> (adjectively) at home; hence (by implication of satisfaction) lovely; also (noun) a home, of God (temple), men (residence), flocks (pasture), or wild animals (den)<BR><B>KJV:</B> comely, dwelling (place), fold, habitation, pleasant place, sheepcote, stable, tarried.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5116 (comely), H5115 (keept at home), H4999 (habitation), H5121 (Naioth)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G718 ἁρμόζω, G1886 ἔπαυλις, G2143 εὐπρέπεια, G2167 εὐφροσύνη, G2570 καλός, G2646 κατάλυμα, G3542 νομή, G4851 συμφέρω, G5117 τόπος",
