    5119: "נֹוחָה (Nôwchâh | no-chaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of H5118 נוּחַ ; quietude<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nochah, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nohah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2680 (half of the Manahethites), H5183 (lighting down), H5118 (rest), H4494 (rest), H5119 (Nohah), H5146 (Noah), H5207 (sweet), H4495 (Manoah), H3240 (bestow), H5117 (cease), H4496 (comfortable), H2010 (release), H4506 (Manahath), H2679 (half of the Manahethites), H3239 (Janoah)",
    5120: "נוּט (nûwṭ | noot)<B>Cognate Group:</B> H5120 (be moved)<BR><BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4531 σαλεύω<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to quake<BR><B>KJV:</B> be moved.",
    5121: "נָוִית (Nâvîyth | naw-veeth')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5115 נָוָה ; residence<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Navith, a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Naioth (from the margin).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5116 (comely), H5115 (keept at home), H4999 (habitation), H5121 (Naioth)",
    5122: "נְוָלוּ (nᵉvâlûw | nev-aw-loo')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) or נְוָלִי; (Aramaic), from an unused root probably meaning to be foul<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a sink<BR><B>KJV:</B> dunghill.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5111 (get away), H5122 (dunghill), H5135 (fiery)",
    5123: "נוּם (nûwm | noom)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to slumber (from drowsiness)<BR><B>KJV:</B> sleep, slumber.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5123 (sleep), H5124 (drowsiness), H8572 (slumber), H3241 (Janum)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G402 ἀναχωρέω, G1265 διαμένω, G3573 νυστάζω, G4579 σείω",
    5124: "נוּמָה (nûwmâh | noo-maw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5123 נוּם<BR><B>Strong's:</B> sleepiness<BR><B>KJV:</B> drowsiness.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5123 (sleep), H5124 (drowsiness), H8572 (slumber), H3241 (Janum)",
    5125: "נוּן (nûwn | noon)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to resprout, i.e. propagate by shoots; figuratively, to be perpetual<BR><B>KJV:</B> be continued.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5125 (be continued), H5126 (Non), H5209 (son)",
    5126: "נוּן (Nûwn | noon)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or נֹון; (1 Chronicles 7:27), from H5125 נוּן ; perpetuity,<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nun or Non, the father of Joshua<BR><B>KJV:</B> Non, Nun.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5125 (be continued), H5126 (Non), H5209 (son)",
    5127: "נוּס (nûwç | noos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to flit, i.e. vanish away (subside, escape; causatively, chase, impel, deliver)<BR><B>KJV:</B> [idiom] abate, away, be displayed, (make to) flee (away, -ing), put to flight, [idiom] hide, lift up a standard.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5127 ([idiom] abate), H4498 ([idiom] apace), H5211 (that fleeth), H4499 (fleeing)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1309 διαφεύγω, G1377 διώκω, G1628 ἐκφεύγω, G2703 καταφεύγω, G2795 κινέω, G3334 μετακινέω, G4863 συνάγω, G5343 φεύγω, G5351 φθείρω, G5437 φυγή",
    5128: "נוּעַ (nûwaʻ | noo'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to waver, in a great variety of applications, literally and figuratively (as subjoined)<BR><B>KJV:</B> continually, fugitive, [idiom] make, to (go) up and down, be gone away, (be) move(-able, -d), be promoted, reel, remove, scatter, set, shake, sift, stagger, to and fro, be vagabond, wag, (make) wander (up and down).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5128 (continually), H5269 (Neah), H4517 (cornet), H5270 (Noah)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G757 ἄρχω, G1287 διασκορπίζω, G1839 ἐξίστημι, G1869 ἐπαίρω, G2795 κινέω, G2827 κλίνω, G3039 λικμάω, G3334 μετακινέω, G4531 σαλεύω, G4579 σείω, G4867 συναθροίζω, G5399 φοβέω",
    5129: "נֹועַדְיָה (Nôwʻadyâh | no-ad-yaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H3259 יָעַד and H3050 יָהּ ; convened of Jah<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Noadjah, the name of an Israelite, and a false prophetess<BR><B>KJV:</B> Noadiah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5129 (Noadiah), H4151 (appointed time), H4150 (appointed), H3259 (agree), H4152 (appointed), H5712 (assembly), H3260 (Iddo See H3035)",
    5130: "נוּף (nûwph | noof)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to quiver (i.e. vibrate up and down, or rock to and fro); used in a great variety of applications (including sprinkling, beckoning, rubbing, bastinadoing, sawing, waving, etc.)<BR><B>KJV:</B> lift up, move, offer, perfume, send, shake, sift, strike, wave.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5130 (lift up), H8573 (offering), H5299 (border)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G142 αἴρω, G399 ἀναφέρω, G591 ἀποδίδωμι, G851 ἀφαιρέω, G873 ἀφορίζω, G1670 ἑλκύω, G1869 ἐπαίρω, G1911 ἐπιβάλλω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2018 ἐπιφέρω, G3870 παρακαλέω, G5342 φέρω",
    5131: "נֹוף (nôwph | nofe)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5130 נוּף<BR><B>Strong's:</B> elevation<BR><B>KJV:</B> situation. Compare H5297 נֹף .<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5316 (country), H5299 (border), H5131 (situation)",
    5132: "נוּץ (nûwts | noots)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to flash; hence, to blossom (from the brilliancy of color); also, to fly away (from the quickness of motion)<BR><B>KJV:</B> flee away, bud (forth).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5133 (feather), H5132 (flee away)",
    5133: "נֹוצָה (nôwtsâh | no-tsaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or נֹצָה; feminine active participle of H5327 נָצָה in the sense of flying<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a pinion (or wing feather); often (collectively) plumage<BR><B>KJV:</B> feather(-s), ostrich.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5133 (feather), H5132 (flee away)",
    5134: "נוּק (nûwq | nook)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to suckle<BR><B>KJV:</B> nurse.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5134 (nurse)",
    5135: "נוּר (nûwr | noor)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) from an unused root (corresponding to that of H5216 נִיר) meaning to shine<BR><B>Strong's:</B> fire<BR><B>KJV:</B> fiery, fire.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5111 (get away), H5122 (dunghill), H5135 (fiery)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4442 πῦρ",
    5136: "נוּשׁ (nûwsh | noosh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be sick, i.e. (figuratively) distressed<BR><B>KJV:</B> be full of heaviness.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5136 (be full of heaviness)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5004 ταλαιπωρία",
    5137: "נָזָה (nâzâh | naw-zaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to spirt, i.e. besprinkle (especially in expiation)<BR><B>KJV:</B> sprinkle.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3150 (Jeziah), H5137 (sprinkle)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2296 θαυμάζω, G2609 κατάγω, G4472 ῥαντίζω",
    5138: "נָזִיד (nâzîyd | naw-zeed')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H2102 זוּד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something boiled, i.e. soup<BR><B>KJV:</B> pottage.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H2121 (proud), H2132 (olive), H5138 (pottage), H2133 (Zethan), H2087 (presumptuously), H2102 (be proud), H2128 (Ziph), H2086 (presumptuous), H2129 (Ziphah), H2130 (Ziphim)",
    5139: "נָזִיר (nâzîyr | naw-zeer')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or נָזִר; from H5144 נָזַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> separate, i.e. consecrated (as prince, a Nazirite); hence (figuratively from the latter) an unpruned vine (like an unshorn Nazirite)<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nazarite (by a false alliteration with Nazareth), separate(-d), vine undressed.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5139 (Nazarite), H5145 (consecration), H4502 (crowned), H5144 (consecrate)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G37 ἁγιάζω, G38 ἁγιασμός, G39 ἅγιον, G47 ἁγνεία, G1392 δοξάζω, G2233 ἡγέομαι",
    5140: "נָזַל (nâzal | naw-zal')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to drip, or shed by trickling<BR><B>KJV:</B> distil, drop, flood, (cause to) flow(-ing), gush out, melt, pour (down), running water, stream.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5140 (distil)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1806 ἐξάγω, G1831 ἐξέρχομαι, G2597 καταβαίνω, G4482 ῥέω, G5080 τήκω, G5204 ὕδωρ",
    5141: "נֶזֶם (nezem | neh'-zem)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root of uncertain meaning<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a nose-ring<BR><B>KJV:</B> earring, jewel.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5143 (damage), H5141 (earring)",
