    5243: "נָמַל (nâmal | naw-mal')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to become clipped or (specifically) circumcised<BR><B>KJV:</B> (branch to) be cut down (off), circumcise.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5243 (be cut down)",
    5244: "נְמָלָה (nᵉmâlâh | nem-aw-law')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine from H5243 נָמַל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an ant (probably from its almost bisected form)<BR><B>KJV:</B> ant.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5244 (ant)",
    5245: "נְמַר (nᵉmar | nem-ar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H5246 נָמֵר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a leopard (from its stripes)<BR><B>KJV:</B> leopard.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5208 (sweet odour), H5202 (keep), H5232 (goods), H5245 (leopard)",
    5246: "נָמֵר (nâmêr | naw-mare')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning properly, to filtrate, i.e. be limpid (comp H5247 נִמְרָה and H5249 נִמְרִים); and thus to spot or stain as if by dripping<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a leopard (from its stripes)<BR><B>KJV:</B> leopard.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5246 (leopard), H5250 (Nimshi), H5248 (Nimrod), H5247 (Nimrah), H5249 (Nimrim)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3917 πάρδαλις",
    5247: "נִמְרָה (Nimrâh | nim-raw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as H5246 נָמֵר ; clear water<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nimrah, a place East of the Jordan<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nimrah. See also H1039 בֵּית נִמְרָה, H5249 נִמְרִים .<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5246 (leopard), H5250 (Nimshi), H5248 (Nimrod), H5247 (Nimrah), H5249 (Nimrim)",
    5248: "נִמְרֹוד (Nimrôwd | nim-rode')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or נִמְרֹד; probably of foreign origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nimrod, a son of Cush<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nimrod.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5246 (leopard), H5250 (Nimshi), H5248 (Nimrod), H5247 (Nimrah), H5249 (Nimrim)",
    5249: "נִמְרִים (Nimrîym | nim-reem')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> plural of a masculine corresponding to H5247 נִמְרָה ; clear waters<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nimrim, a place East of the Jordan<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nimrim. Compare H1039 בֵּית נִמְרָה .<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5246 (leopard), H5250 (Nimshi), H5248 (Nimrod), H5247 (Nimrah), H5249 (Nimrim)",
    5250: "נִמְשִׁי (Nimshîy | nim-shee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from H4871 מָשָׁה ; extricated<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nimshi, the (grand-) father of Jehu<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nimshi.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5246 (leopard), H5250 (Nimshi), H5248 (Nimrod), H5247 (Nimrah), H5249 (Nimrim)",
    5251: "נֵס (nêç | nace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5264 נָסַס<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a flag; also a sail; by implication, a flagstaff; generally a signal; figuratively, a token<BR><B>KJV:</B> banner, pole, sail, (en-) sign, standard.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5251 (banner), H3071 (Jehovah-nissi), H5264 (lift up as an ensign)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G757 ἄρχω, G1391 δόξα, G4592 σημεῖον, G4953 σύσσημον",
    5252: "נְסִבָּה (nᵉçibbâh | nes-ib-baw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine participle passive of H5437 סָבַב<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, an environment, i.e. circumstance or turn of affairs<BR><B>KJV:</B> cause.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5439 (about), H5437 (bring), H4142 (being changed), H5252 (cause), H4524 (that compass about), H4036 (Magormissabib), H5438 (cause), H4141 (winding about)",
    5253: "נָסַג (nâçag | naw-sag')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to retreat<BR><B>KJV:</B> departing away, remove, take (hold), turn away.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7873 (pursuing), H5472 (backslider), H5253 (departing away), H7734 (turn back), H5509 (dross)",
    5254: "נָסָה (nâçâh | naw-saw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to test; by implication, to attempt<BR><B>KJV:</B> adventure, assay, prove, tempt, try.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4531 (temptation), H5254 (adventure), H4532 (Massah)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1598 ἐκπειράζω, G2983 λαμβάνω, G3984 πεῖρα, G3985 πειράζω, G3987 πειράω",
    5255: "נָסַח (nâçach | naw-sakh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to tear away<BR><B>KJV:</B> destroy, pluck, root.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5255 (destroy)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1808 ἐξαίρω, G1856 ἐξωθέω",
    5256: "נְסַח (nᵉçach | nes-akh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H5255 נָסַח<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to tear away<BR><B>KJV:</B> pull down.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5256 (pull down)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2507 καθαιρέω",
    5257: "נְסִיךְ (nᵉçîyk | nes-eek')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5258 נָסַךְ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, something poured out, i.e. a libation; also a molten image; by implication, a prince (as anointed)<BR><B>KJV:</B> drink offering, duke, prince(-ipal).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5257 (drink offering), H5258 (cover), H4541 (covering), H5262 (cover)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G757 ἄρχω, G758 ἄρχων",
    5258: "נָסַךְ (nâçak | naw-sak')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to pour out, especially a libation, or to cast (metal); by analogy, to anoint aking<BR><B>KJV:</B> cover, melt, offer, (cause to) pour (out), set (up).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5257 (drink offering), H5258 (cover), H4541 (covering), H5262 (cover)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2311 θεμελιόω, G2525 καθίστημι, G4160 ποιέω, G4222 ποτίζω, G4689 σπένδω",
    5259: "נָסַךְ (nâçak | naw-sak')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root (probably identical with H5258 נָסַךְ through the idea of fusion)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to interweave, i.e. (figuratively) to overspread<BR><B>KJV:</B> that is spread.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4545 (web), H5259 (that is spread), H4541 (covering)",
    5260: "נְסַךְ (nᵉçak | nes-ak')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H5258 נָסַךְ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to pour out a libation<BR><B>KJV:</B> offer.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5261 (drink offering), H5260 (offer)",
    5261: "נְסַךְ (nᵉçak | nes-ak')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H5262 נֶסֶךְ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a libation<BR><B>KJV:</B> drink offering.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5261 (drink offering), H5260 (offer)",
    5262: "נֶסֶךְ (neçek | neh'-sek)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or נֵסֶךְ; from H5258 נָסַךְ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a libation; also a cast idol<BR><B>KJV:</B> cover, drink offering, molten image.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5257 (drink offering), H5258 (cover), H4541 (covering), H5262 (cover)",
    5263: "נָסַס (nâçaç | naw-sas')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to wane, i.e. be sick<BR><B>KJV:</B> faint.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5263 (faint)",
    5264: "נָסַס (nâçaç | naw-sas')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root; to gleam from afar, i.e. to be conspicuous as a signal; or rather perhaps a denominative from H5251 נֵס (and identical with H5263 נָסַס, through the idea of a flag as fluttering in the wind)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to raise a beacon<BR><B>KJV:</B> lift up as an ensign.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5251 (banner), H3071 (Jehovah-nissi), H5264 (lift up as an ensign)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2947 κυλιόω, G5343 φεύγω",
    5265: "נָסַע (nâçaʻ | naw-sah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to pull up, especially the tent-pins, i.e. start on ajourney<BR><B>KJV:</B> cause to blow, bring, get, (make to) go (away, forth, forward, onward, out), (take) journey, march, remove, set aside (forward), [idiom] still, be on his (go their) way.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4551 (before it was brought), H5265 (cause to blow), H4550 (journey)",
    5266: "נָסַק (nâçaq | naw-sak')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to go up<BR><B>KJV:</B> ascend.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5562 (Samgar-nebo), H5266 (ascend), H5563 (tender grape), H5560 (flour)",
    5267: "נְסַק (nᵉçaq | nes-ak')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H5266 נָסַק<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to go up<BR><B>KJV:</B> take up.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5267 (take up), H5559 (come)",
    5268: "נִסְרֹךְ (Niçrôk | nis-roke')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of foreign origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Nisrok, a Babylonian idol<BR><B>KJV:</B> Nisroch.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5272 (Neiel), H5268 (Nisroch)",
    5269: "נֵעָה (Nêʻâh | nay-aw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5128 נוּעַ ; motion<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Neah, a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Neah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5128 (continually), H5269 (Neah), H4517 (cornet), H5270 (Noah)",
    5270: "נֹעָה (Nôʻâh | no-aw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5128 נוּעַ ; movement<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Noah, an Israelitess<BR><B>KJV:</B> Noah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5128 (continually), H5269 (Neah), H4517 (cornet), H5270 (Noah)",
    5271: "נָעוּר (nâʻûwr | naw-oor')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or נָעֻר; and (feminine) נְעֻרָה; properly, passive participle from H5288 נַעַר as denominative<BR><B>Strong's:</B> (only in plural collectively or emphatic form) youth, the state (juvenility) or the persons (young people)<BR><B>KJV:</B> childhood, youth.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5294 (Neariah), H5298 (Nepheg), H5271 (childhood), H5292 (Naarah), H5290 (child), H5291 (damsel), H5288 (babe), H5295 (Naaran), H5293 (Naarai)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1078 γένεσις, G3503 νεότης, G3932 παρθενία",
