    5274: "נָעַל (nâʻal | naw-al')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root; also denominative from H5275 נַעַל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to fasten up, i.e. with abar or cord; hence, to sandal, i.e. furnish with slippers<BR><B>KJV:</B> bolt, inclose, lock, shoe, shut up.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4514 (lock), H5274 (bolt), H5275 (dryshod), H4515 (shoe)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G608 ἀποκλείω, G2808 κλείω, G3112 μακράν, G4547 σανδάλιον, G5265 ὑποδέω, G5266 ὑπόδημα",
