    5526: "סָכַךְ (çâkak | saw-kak')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or שָׂכַךְ; (Exodus 33:22), a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to entwine as ascreen; by implication, to fence in, cover over, (figuratively) protect<BR><B>KJV:</B> cover, defence, defend, hedge in, join together, set, shut up.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5526 (cover), H5485 (Susi), H4534 (thorn hedge), H5483 (crane), H5484 (company of horses), H5482 (Syene)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1892 ἐπεγείρω, G1982 ἐπισκιάζω, G2521 κάθημαι, G2681 κατασκηνόω, G4028 περικαλύπτω, G5420 φράσσω",
