    5530: "סָכָל (çâkâl | saw-kawl')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5528 סָכַל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> silly<BR><B>KJV:</B> fool(-ish), sottish.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5531 (folly), H5528 (do fool), H5529 (folly), H5530 (fool)",
    5531: "סִכְלוּת (çiklûwth | sik-looth')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or שִׂכְלוּת; (Ecclesiastes 1:17), from H5528 סָכַל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> silliness<BR><B>KJV:</B> folly, foolishness.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5531 (folly), H5528 (do fool), H5529 (folly), H5530 (fool)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2167 εὐφροσύνη",
    5532: "סָכַן (çâkan | saw-kan')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be familiar with; by implication, to minister to, be serviceable to, be customary<BR><B>KJV:</B> acquaint (self), be advantage, [idiom] ever, (be, (un-)) profit(-able), treasurer, be wont.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5532 (acquaint), H4543 (store)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1321 διδάσκω, G1984 ἐπισκοπή, G2282 θάλπω, G4276 προελπίζω",
    5533: "סָכַן (çâkan | saw-kan')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably a denominative from H7915 שַׂכִּין<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to cut, i.e. damage; also to grow (causatively, make) poor<BR><B>KJV:</B> endanger, impoverish.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5533 (endanger)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2793 κινδυνεύω",
