    6175: "עָרוּם (ʻârûwm | aw-room')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> passive participle of H6191 עָרַם<BR><B>Strong's:</B> cunning (usually in a bad sense)<BR><B>KJV:</B> crafty, prudent, subtil.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6175 (crafty), H6193 (craftiness), H6195 (guile), H6191 ([idiom] very)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3835 πανοῦργος, G4908 συνετός, G5429 φρόνιμος",
    6176: "עֲרֹועֵר (ʻărôwʻêr | ar-o-ayr')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or עַרְעָר; from H6209 עָרַר reduplicated<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a juniper (from its nudity of situation)<BR><B>KJV:</B> health.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6177 (Aroer), H6209 (make bare), H6199 (destitute), H5735 (Adadah), H6200 (Aroerite), H6185 (childless), H6176 (health)",
    6177: "עֲרֹועֵר (ʻĂrôwʻêr | ar-o-ayr')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or עֲרֹעֵר; or עַרְעֹור; the same as H6176 עֲרֹועֵר ; nudity of situation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Aroer, the name of three places in or near Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Aroer.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6177 (Aroer), H6209 (make bare), H6199 (destitute), H5735 (Adadah), H6200 (Aroerite), H6185 (childless), H6176 (health)",
    6178: "עָרוּץ (ʻârûwts | aw-roots')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> passive participle of H6206 עָרַץ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> feared, i.e. (concretely) a horrible place or chasm<BR><B>KJV:</B> cliffs.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6206 (be affrighted), H6178 (cliffs), H4637 (terror), H6184 (mighty)",
    6179: "עֵרִי (ʻÊrîy | ay-ree')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5782 עוּר ; watchful<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Eri, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Eri.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5782 (wake), H6197 (Eran), H6180 (Erites), H6179 (Eri), H6198 (Eranites), H6147 (Er), H3265 (Jair), H5892 (Ai)",
    6180: "עֵרִי (ʻÊrîy | ay-ree')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> patronymically of H6179 עֵרִי<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Erite (collectively) or descendants of Eri<BR><B>KJV:</B> Erites.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5782 (wake), H6197 (Eran), H6180 (Erites), H6179 (Eri), H6198 (Eranites), H6147 (Er), H3265 (Jair), H5892 (Ai)",
    6181: "עֶרְיָה (ʻeryâh | er-yaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> for H6172 עֶרְוָה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> nudity<BR><B>KJV:</B> bare, naked, [idiom] quite.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4638 (Maarath), H6168 (leave destitute), H6181 (bare), H8593 (knife), H6172 (nakedness), H4629 (meadows), H4626 (nakedness), H6171 (wild ass), H6169 (paper reed)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G153 αἰσχύνομαι, G807 ἀσχημονέω",
    6182: "עֲרִיסָה (ʻărîyçâh | ar-ee-saw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to comminute<BR><B>Strong's:</B> meal<BR><B>KJV:</B> dough.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6182 (dough)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4621 σῖτος, G5445 φύραμα",
    6183: "עָרִיף (ʻârîyph | aw-reef')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H6201 עָרַף<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the sky (as dropping at the horizon)<BR><B>KJV:</B> heaven.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6183 (heaven), H6201 (drop), H6205 (dark)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G640 ἀπορία",
    6184: "עָרִיץ (ʻârîyts | aw-reets')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H6206 עָרַץ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> fearful, i.e. powerful or tyrannical<BR><B>KJV:</B> mighty, oppressor, in great power, strong, terrible, violent.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6206 (be affrighted), H6178 (cliffs), H4637 (terror), H6184 (mighty)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G91 ἀδικέω, G459 ἄνομος, G1413 δυνάστης, G2478 ἰσχυρός, G2480 ἰσχύω, G2616 καταδυναστεύω, G2900 κραταιός, G3061 λοιμός, G5244 ὑπερήφανος, G5251 ὑπερυψόω, G5401 φόβος",
    6185: "עֲרִירִי (ʻărîyrîy | ar-e-ree')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H6209 עָרַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> bare, i.e. destitute (of children)<BR><B>KJV:</B> childless.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6177 (Aroer), H6209 (make bare), H6199 (destitute), H5735 (Adadah), H6200 (Aroerite), H6185 (childless), H6176 (health)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G815 ἄτεκνος",
    6186: "עָרַךְ (ʻârak | aw-rak')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to set in a row, i.e. arrange, put in order (in a very wide variety of applications)<BR><B>KJV:</B> put (set) (the battle, self) in array, compare, direct, equal, esteem, estimate, expert (in war), furnish, handle, join (battle), ordain, (lay, put, reckon up, set) (in) order, prepare, tax, value.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4633 (preparation), H4630 (army), H4634 (army), H6187 (equal), H6186 (put in array), H4635 (row)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G142 αἴρω, G353 ἀναλαμβάνω, G430 ἀνέχομαι, G997 βοηθέω, G1166 δεικνύω, G2007 ἐπιτίθημι, G2010 ἐπιτρέπω, G2090 ἑτοιμάζω, G2092 ἕτοιμος, G2545 καίω, G2885 κοσμέω, G3112 μακράν, G3114 μακροθυμέω, G3306 μένω, G3666 ὁμοιόω, G3903 παρασκευάζω, G3936 παρίστημι, G4023 περιέχω, G4115 πλατύνω, G4121 πλεονάζω, G4129 πληθύνω, G4369 προστίθημι, G4388 προτίθεμαι, G5091 τιμάω, G5242 ὑπερέχω, G5312 ὑψόω, G5465 χαλάω",
    6187: "עֵרֶךְ (ʻêrek | eh'rek)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H6186 עָרַךְ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a pile, equipment, estimate<BR><B>KJV:</B> equal, estimation, (things that are set in) order, price, proportion, [idiom] set at, suit, taxation, [idiom] valuest.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4633 (preparation), H4630 (army), H4634 (army), H6187 (equal), H6186 (put in array), H4635 (row)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2201 ζεῦγος, G2473 ἰσόψυχος, G3115 μακροθυμία, G4286 πρόθεσις, G4749 στολή, G5092 τιμή",
    6188: "עָרֵל (ʻârêl | aw-rale')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root; properly, to strip; but used as denominative from H6189 עָרֵל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to expose or remove the prepuce, whether literal (to go naked) or figurative (to refrain from using)<BR><B>KJV:</B> count uncircumcised, foreskin to be uncovered.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6188 (count uncircumcised), H6189 (uncircumcised), H6190 (foreskin)",
    6189: "עָרֵל (ʻârêl | aw-rale')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H6188 עָרֵל ; properly, exposed, i.e. projecting loose (as to the prepuce); used only technically,<BR><B>Strong's:</B> uncircumcised (i.e. still having the prepuce uncurtailed)<BR><B>KJV:</B> uncircumcised (person).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6188 (count uncircumcised), H6189 (uncircumcised), H6190 (foreskin)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G564 ἀπερίτμητος",
    6190: "עׇרְלָה (ʻorlâh | or-law')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of H6189 עָרֵל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the prepuce<BR><B>KJV:</B> foreskin, [phrase] uncircumcised.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6188 (count uncircumcised), H6189 (uncircumcised), H6190 (foreskin)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G167 ἀκαθαρσία, G203 ἀκροβυστία",
    6191: "עָרַם (ʻâram | aw-ram')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to be (or make) bare; but used only in the derivative sense (through the idea perhaps of smoothness) to be cunning (usually in a bad sense)<BR><B>KJV:</B> [idiom] very, beware, take crafty (counsel), be prudent, deal subtilly.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6175 (crafty), H6193 (craftiness), H6195 (guile), H6191 ([idiom] very)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G246 ἀλλόφυλος, G1339 διΐστημι, G3835 πανοῦργος",
    6192: "עָרַם (ʻâram | aw-ram')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to pile up<BR><B>KJV:</B> gather together.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6194 (heap), H6192 (gather together)",
    6193: "עֹרֶם (ʻôrem | o'-rem)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H6191 עָרַם<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a stratagem<BR><B>KJV:</B> craftiness.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6175 (crafty), H6193 (craftiness), H6195 (guile), H6191 ([idiom] very)",
    6194: "עָרֵם (ʻârêm | aw-rame')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Jeremiah 50:26) or (feminine) עֲרֵמָה; from H6192 עָרַם<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a heap; specifically, a sheaf<BR><B>KJV:</B> heap (of corn), sheaf.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6194 (heap), H6192 (gather together)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2310 θεμέλιος",
    6195: "עׇרְמָה (ʻormâh | or-maw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of H6193 עֹרֶם<BR><B>Strong's:</B> trickery; or (in a good sense) discretion<BR><B>KJV:</B> guile, prudence, subtilty, wilily, wisdom.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6175 (crafty), H6193 (craftiness), H6195 (guile), H6191 ([idiom] very)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1012 βουλή, G1388 δόλος, G3834 πανουργία, G5428 φρόνησις",
    6196: "עַרְמֹון (ʻarmôwn | ar-mone')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from H6191 עָרַם<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the plane tree (from its smooth and shed bark)<BR><B>KJV:</B> chestnut tree.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6196 (chestnut tree)",
    6197: "עֵרָן (ʻÊrân | ay-rawn')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from H5782 עוּר ; watchful<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Eran, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Eran.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5782 (wake), H6197 (Eran), H6180 (Erites), H6179 (Eri), H6198 (Eranites), H6147 (Er), H3265 (Jair), H5892 (Ai)",
    6198: "עֵרָנִי (ʻÊrânîy | ay-raw-nee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> patronymically from H6197 עֵרָן<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an Eranite or descendant (collectively) of Eran<BR><B>KJV:</B> Eranites.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5782 (wake), H6197 (Eran), H6180 (Erites), H6179 (Eri), H6198 (Eranites), H6147 (Er), H3265 (Jair), H5892 (Ai)",
    6199: "עַרעָר (ʻarʻâr | ar-awr')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H6209 עָרַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> naked, i.e. (figuratively) poor<BR><B>KJV:</B> destitute. See also H6176 עֲרֹועֵר .<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6177 (Aroer), H6209 (make bare), H6199 (destitute), H5735 (Adadah), H6200 (Aroerite), H6185 (childless), H6176 (health)",
    6200: "עֲרֹעֵרִי (ʻĂrôʻêrîy | ar-o-ay-ree')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> patronymically from H6177 עֲרֹועֵר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an Aroerite or inhabitant of Aroer<BR><B>KJV:</B> Aroerite.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6177 (Aroer), H6209 (make bare), H6199 (destitute), H5735 (Adadah), H6200 (Aroerite), H6185 (childless), H6176 (health)",
    6201: "עָרַף (ʻâraph | aw-raf')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to droop; hence, to drip<BR><B>KJV:</B> drop (down).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6183 (heaven), H6201 (drop), H6205 (dark)",
    6202: "עָרַף (ʻâraph | aw-raf')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root (identical with through the idea of sloping); properly, to bend downward; but used only as a denominative from H6203 עֹרֶף,<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to break the neck; hence (figuratively) to destroy<BR><B>KJV:</B> that is beheaded, break down, break (cut off, strike off) neck.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6202 (that is beheaded), H6204 (Orpah), H6203 (back neck)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G615 ἀποκτείνω, G2679 κατασκάπτω, G3084 λυτρόω",
    6203: "עֹרֶף (ʻôreph | o-ref')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H6202 עָרַף<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the nape or back of the neck (as declining); hence, the back generally (whether literal or figurative)<BR><B>KJV:</B> back ((stiff-) neck((-ed).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6202 (that is beheaded), H6204 (Orpah), H6203 (back neck)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2588 καρδία, G2864 κόμη, G3577 νῶτος, G5137 τράχηλος",
    6204: "עׇרְפָּה (ʻOrpâh | or-paw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of H6203 עֹרֶף ; mane<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Orpah, a Moabites<BR><B>KJV:</B> Orpah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6202 (that is beheaded), H6204 (Orpah), H6203 (back neck)",
    6205: "עֲרָפֶל (ʻărâphel | ar-aw-fel')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from H6201 עָרַף<BR><B>Strong's:</B> gloom (as of a lowering sky)<BR><B>KJV:</B> (gross, thick) dark (cloud, -ness).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6183 (heaven), H6201 (drop), H6205 (dark)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1105 γνόφος, G2366 θύελλα, G3509 νέφος, G4655 σκότος",
    6206: "עָרַץ (ʻârats | aw-rats')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to awe or (intransitive) to dread; hence, to harass<BR><B>KJV:</B> be affrighted (afraid, dread, feared, terrified), break, dread, fear, oppress, prevail, shake terribly.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6206 (be affrighted), H6178 (cliffs), H4637 (terror), H6184 (mighty)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1168 δειλιάω, G1578 ἐκκλίνω, G1740 ἐνδοξάζω, G2125 εὐλαβέομαι, G2352 θραύω, G3166 μεγαλαυχέω, G4422 πτοέω, G5015 ταράσσω, G5399 φοβέω",
    6207: "עָרַק (ʻâraq | aw-rak')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to gnaw, i.e. (figuratively) eat (by hyberbole); also (participle) a pain<BR><B>KJV:</B> fleeing, sinew.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6207 (fleeing), H6208 (Arkite)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5343 φεύγω",
    6208: "עַרְקִי (ʻArqîy | ar-kee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> patrial from an unused name meaning a tush<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an Arkite or inhabitant of Erek<BR><B>KJV:</B> Arkite.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6207 (fleeing), H6208 (Arkite)",
    6209: "עָרַר (ʻârar | aw-rar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to bare; figuratively, to demolish<BR><B>KJV:</B> make bare, break, raise up (perhaps by clerical error for raze), [idiom] utterly.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6177 (Aroer), H6209 (make bare), H6199 (destitute), H5735 (Adadah), H6200 (Aroerite), H6185 (childless), H6176 (health)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2679 κατασκάπτω",
    6210: "עֶרֶשׂ (ʻeres | eh'res)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning perhaps to arch<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a couch (properly, with a canopy)<BR><B>KJV:</B> bed(-stead), couch.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6210 (bed)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2825 κλίνη",
    6211: "עָשׁ (ʻâsh | awsh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H6244 עָשֵׁשׁ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a moth<BR><B>KJV:</B> moth. See also H5906 עַיִשׁ .<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6211 (moth), H6244 (be consumed)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4597 σής",
    6212: "עֶשֶׂב (ʻeseb | eh'seb)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to glisten (or be green)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> grass (or any tender shoot)<BR><B>KJV:</B> grass, herb.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H6212 (grass)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1008 βοτάνη, G5515 χλωρός, G5527 χόρτασμα, G5528 χόρτος",
