    7118: "קְצָת (qᵉtsâth | kets-awth')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H7117 קְצָת<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a termination (literally or figuratively); also (by implication) a portion; adverbially (with prepositional prefix) after<BR><B>KJV:</B> end, partly.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7118 (end), H7113 (cut off)",
    7119: "קַר (qar | kar)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> contracted from an unused root meaning to chill<BR><B>Strong's:</B> cool; figuratively, quiet<BR><B>KJV:</B> cold, excellent (from the margin).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7120 (cold), H4747 ([idiom] summer), H6979 (break down), H7119 (cold), H7135 (cold)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5593 ψυχρός",
