    7413: "רָמָה (râmâh | raw-maw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine active participle of H7311 רוּם<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a height (as a seat of idolatry)<BR><B>KJV:</B> high place.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7312 (haughtiness), H7315 (on high), H7433 (Ramoth-gilead), H7419 (height), H8641 (gift), H7410 (Ram), H7216 (Ramoth), H7318 (be extolled), H7413 (high place), H7319 (high), H7437 (Ramath-lehi), H7414 (Ramah), H4791 (above), H8642 (oblation), H7418 (south Ramoth), H7432 (Remeth), H7427 (lifting up of self), H7435 (Ramathite), H7320 (Romamti-ezer), H7317 (haughtily), H7434 (Ramath-mizpeh), H7316 (Rumah), H7311 (bring up)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G336 ἀναίρεσις, G939 βάσις, G4471 Ῥαμᾶ, G5401 φόβος",
    7414: "רָמָה (Râmâh | raw-maw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> the same as H7413 רָמָה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Ramah, the name of four places in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Ramah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7312 (haughtiness), H7315 (on high), H7433 (Ramoth-gilead), H7419 (height), H8641 (gift), H7410 (Ram), H7216 (Ramoth), H7318 (be extolled), H7413 (high place), H7319 (high), H7437 (Ramath-lehi), H7414 (Ramah), H4791 (above), H8642 (oblation), H7418 (south Ramoth), H7432 (Remeth), H7427 (lifting up of self), H7435 (Ramathite), H7320 (Romamti-ezer), H7317 (haughtily), H7434 (Ramath-mizpeh), H7316 (Rumah), H7311 (bring up)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4471 Ῥαμᾶ, G707 Ἀριμαθαία",
    7415: "רִמָּה (rimmâh | rim-maw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7426 רָמַם in the sense of breading (compare H7311 רוּם)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a maggot (as rapidly bred), literally or figuratively<BR><B>KJV:</B> worm.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7415 (worm), H7311 (bring up)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4663 σκώληξ",
    7416: "רִמֹּון (rimmôwn | rim-mone')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or רִמֹּן; from H7426 רָמַם<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a pomegranate, the tree (from its upright growth) or the fruit (also an artificial ornament)<BR><B>KJV:</B> pomegranate.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7416 (pomegranate), H7424 (dromedary), H7423 (deceit), H7428 (Rimmon-parez), H7417 (Remmon), H3414 (Jeremiah), H7420 (buckler), H7422 (Ramiah)",
    7417: "רִמֹּון (Rimmôwn | rim-mone')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or (shorter) (רִמֹּן; or רִמֹּונֹו; (1 Chronicles 6:62 (H77 אֶבֶץ)), the same as H7416 רִמֹּון ; in Joshua 19:13: הַמְּתֹאָר is mistaken for part of a name; article with the passive participle of H8388 תָּאַר ; the (one) marked off, i.e. which pertains).<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Rimmon, the name of a Syrian deity, also of five places in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Remmon, Rimmon.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7416 (pomegranate), H7424 (dromedary), H7423 (deceit), H7428 (Rimmon-parez), H7417 (Remmon), H3414 (Jeremiah), H7420 (buckler), H7422 (Ramiah)",
    7418: "רָמֹות (Râmôwth | raw-moth)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or רָמַת נֶגֶב; from the plural or construct form of H7413 רָמָה and H5045 נֶגֶב ; heights (or height) of the South<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Ramoth-Negeb or Ramath-Negeb, a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> south Ramoth, Ramath of the south.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7312 (haughtiness), H7315 (on high), H7433 (Ramoth-gilead), H7419 (height), H8641 (gift), H7410 (Ram), H7216 (Ramoth), H7318 (be extolled), H7413 (high place), H7319 (high), H7437 (Ramath-lehi), H7414 (Ramah), H4791 (above), H8642 (oblation), H7418 (south Ramoth), H7432 (Remeth), H7427 (lifting up of self), H7435 (Ramathite), H7320 (Romamti-ezer), H7317 (haughtily), H7434 (Ramath-mizpeh), H7316 (Rumah), H7311 (bring up)",
    7419: "רָמוּת (râmûwth | raw-mooth')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7311 רוּם<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a heap (of carcases)<BR><B>KJV:</B> height.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7312 (haughtiness), H7315 (on high), H7433 (Ramoth-gilead), H7419 (height), H8641 (gift), H7410 (Ram), H7216 (Ramoth), H7318 (be extolled), H7413 (high place), H7319 (high), H7437 (Ramath-lehi), H7414 (Ramah), H4791 (above), H8642 (oblation), H7418 (south Ramoth), H7432 (Remeth), H7427 (lifting up of self), H7435 (Ramathite), H7320 (Romamti-ezer), H7317 (haughtily), H7434 (Ramath-mizpeh), H7316 (Rumah), H7311 (bring up)",
    7420: "רֹמַח (rômach | ro'-makh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to hurl<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a lance (as thrown); especially the iron point<BR><B>KJV:</B> buckler, javelin, lancet, spear.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7416 (pomegranate), H7424 (dromedary), H7423 (deceit), H7428 (Rimmon-parez), H7417 (Remmon), H3414 (Jeremiah), H7420 (buckler), H7422 (Ramiah)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3057 λόγχη",
    7421: "רַמִּי (rammîy | ram-mee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> for H761 אֲרַמִּי<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Ramite, i.e. Aramaean<BR><B>KJV:</B> Syrian.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H763 (Aham-naharaim), H762 (in the Syrian language), H760 (Aram-zobah), H758 (Aram), H7421 (Syrian), H761 (Syrian)",
    7422: "רַמְיָה (Ramyâh | ram-yaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7311 רוּם and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has raised<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Ramjah, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Ramiah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7416 (pomegranate), H7424 (dromedary), H7423 (deceit), H7428 (Rimmon-parez), H7417 (Remmon), H3414 (Jeremiah), H7420 (buckler), H7422 (Ramiah)",
    7423: "רְמִיָּה (rᵉmîyâh | rem-ee-yaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7411 רָמָה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> remissness, treachery<BR><B>KJV:</B> deceit(-ful, -fully), false, guile, idle, slack, slothful.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7423 (deceit), H7411 (beguile), H8649 (deceit), H4820 (craft)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G94 ἄδικος, G459 ἄνομος, G1386 δόλιος, G1388 δόλος",
    7424: "רַמָּךְ (rammâk | ram-mawk')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of foreign origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a brood mare<BR><B>KJV:</B> dromedary.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7416 (pomegranate), H7424 (dromedary), H7423 (deceit), H7428 (Rimmon-parez), H7417 (Remmon), H3414 (Jeremiah), H7420 (buckler), H7422 (Ramiah)",
    7425: "רְמַלְיָהוּ (Rᵉmalyâhûw | rem-al-yaw'-hoo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root and H3050 יָהּ (perhaps meaning to deck); Jah has bedecked<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Remaljah, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Remaliah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7425 (Remaliah)",
