    7428: "רִמֹּן פֶּרֶץ (Rimmôn Perets | rim-mone' peh'-rets)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7416 רִמֹּון and H6556 פֶּרֶץ ; pomegranate of the breach<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Rimmon-Perets, a place in the Desert<BR><B>KJV:</B> Rimmon-parez.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7416 (pomegranate), H7424 (dromedary), H7423 (deceit), H7428 (Rimmon-parez), H7417 (Remmon), H3414 (Jeremiah), H7420 (buckler), H7422 (Ramiah)",
    7429: "רָמַס (râmaç | raw-mas')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to tread upon (as a potter, in walking or abusively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> oppressor, stamp upon, trample (under feet), tread (down, upon).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4823 (tread -ing), H7429 (oppressor)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1291 διαστέλλομαι, G1330 διέρχομαι, G2062 ἑρπετόν, G2662 καταπατέω, G3961 πατέω, G4937 συντρίβω",
