    7437: "רָמַת לֶחִי (Râmath Lechîy | raw'-math lekh'-ee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7413 רָמָה and H3895 לְחִי ; height of a jaw-bone<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Ramath-Lechi, a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Ramath-lehi.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7312 (haughtiness), H7315 (on high), H7433 (Ramoth-gilead), H7419 (height), H8641 (gift), H7410 (Ram), H7216 (Ramoth), H7318 (be extolled), H7413 (high place), H7319 (high), H7437 (Ramath-lehi), H7414 (Ramah), H4791 (above), H8642 (oblation), H7418 (south Ramoth), H7432 (Remeth), H7427 (lifting up of self), H7435 (Ramathite), H7320 (Romamti-ezer), H7317 (haughtily), H7434 (Ramath-mizpeh), H7316 (Rumah), H7311 (bring up)",
    7438: "רֹן (rôn | rone)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7442 רָנַן<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a shout (of deliverance)<BR><B>KJV:</B> song.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7446 (Rissah), H7444 (singing), H7441 (Rinnah), H7445 (joyful), H7443 ([idiom] goodly), H7442 (aloud for joy), H7440 (cry), H7438 (song)",
    7439: "רָנָה (rânâh | raw-naw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to whiz<BR><B>KJV:</B> rattle.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7439 (rattle)",
    7440: "רִנָּה (rinnâh | rin-naw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7442 רָנַן<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, a creaking (or shrill sound), i.e. shout (of joy or grief)<BR><B>KJV:</B> cry, gladness, joy, proclamation, rejoicing, shouting, sing(-ing), triumph.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7446 (Rissah), H7444 (singing), H7441 (Rinnah), H7445 (joyful), H7443 ([idiom] goodly), H7442 (aloud for joy), H7440 (cry), H7438 (song)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G20 ἀγαλλίασις, G133 αἴνεσις, G1162 δέησις, G5479 χαρά",
    7441: "רִנָּה (Rinnâh | rin-naw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> the same as H7440 רִנָּה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Rinnah, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Rinnah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7446 (Rissah), H7444 (singing), H7441 (Rinnah), H7445 (joyful), H7443 ([idiom] goodly), H7442 (aloud for joy), H7440 (cry), H7438 (song)",
