    7446: "רִסָּה (Riççâh | ris-saw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7450 רָסַס ; a ruin (as dripping to pieces)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Rissah, a place in the Desert<BR><B>KJV:</B> Rissah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7446 (Rissah), H7444 (singing), H7441 (Rinnah), H7445 (joyful), H7443 ([idiom] goodly), H7442 (aloud for joy), H7440 (cry), H7438 (song)",
    7447: "רָסִיס (râçîyç | raw-sees')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7450 רָסַס<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, dripping to pieces, i.e. a ruin; also a dew-drop<BR><B>KJV:</B> breach, drop.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7450 (temper), H7447 (breach)",
    7448: "רֶסֶן (reçen | reh'-sen)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to curb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a halter (as restraining); by implication, the jaw<BR><B>KJV:</B> bridle.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7449 (Resen), H7448 (bridle)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2382 θώραξ, G5469 χαλινός",
