    7602: "שָׁאַף (shâʼaph | shaw-af')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to inhale eagerly; figuratively, to cover; by implication, to be angry; also to hasten<BR><B>KJV:</B> desire (earnestly), devour, haste, pant, snuff up, swallow up.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7602 (desire)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1670 ἑλκύω, G1828 ἐξέλκω, G2662 καταπατέω, G3404 μισέω, G3583 ξηραίνω, G4151 πνεῦμα",
    7603: "שְׂאֹר (sᵉʼôr | seh-ore')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7604 שָׁאַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> barm or yeast-cake (as swelling by fermentation)<BR><B>KJV:</B> leaven.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7603 (leaven)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2219 ζύμη",
