    7718: "שֹׁהַם (shôham | sho'-ham)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root probably mean to blanch<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a gem, probably the beryl (from its pale green color)<BR><B>KJV:</B> onyx.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H8346 (sixty), H8341 (give the sixth participle), H7864 (Sheva), H7724 (Sheva), H7719 (Shoham), H8337 (six), H7718 (onyx), H8345 (sixth)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4556 σάρδιος, G4665 σμάραγδος",
