    7720: "שַׂהֲרֹן (sahărôn | sah-har-one')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as H5469 סַהַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a round pendant for the neck<BR><B>KJV:</B> ornament, round tire like the moon.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7720 (ornament)",
    7721: "שֹׂוא (sôwʼ | so)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root (akin to H5375 נָשָׂא and H7722 שֹׁוא) meaning to rise<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a rising<BR><B>KJV:</B> arise.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5375 (accept), H5387 (captain), H4858 (burden), H4864 (burden), H7863 (excellency), H4853 (burden), H7613 (be accepted), H5379 (gift), H7865 (Sion), H4856 (respect), H5385 (carriage), H4984 (exalted), H7721 (arise)",
    7722: "שֹׁוא (shôwʼ | sho)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or (feminine) שֹׁואָה; or שֹׁאָה; from an unused root meaning to rush over<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a tempest; by implication, devastation<BR><B>KJV:</B> desolate(-ion), destroy, destruction, storm, wasteness.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4875 (desolation), H8663 (crying), H7722 (desolate), H7738 ([idiom] substance)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G684 ἀπώλεια, G2347 θλῖψις, G3730 ὁρμή, G3803 παγίς, G4928 συνοχή, G5004 ταλαιπωρία, G5205 ὑετός",
