    7801: "שׁוּשַׁנְכִי (Shûwshankîy | shoo-shan-kee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) of foreign origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Shushankite (collectively) or inhabitants of some unknown place in Assyrian<BR><B>KJV:</B> Susanchites.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7792 (wall), H8243 (leg), H7801 (Susanchites)",
    7802: "שׁוּשַׁן עֵדוּת (Shûwshan ʻÊdûwth | shoo-shan' ay-dooth')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or (plural of former) שֹׁושַׁנִּים עֵדוּת; from H7799 שׁוּשַׁן and H5715 עֵדוּת ; lily (or trumpet) of assemblage<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Shushan-Eduth or Shoshannim-Eduth, the title of a popular song<BR><B>KJV:</B> Shoshannim-Eduth, Shushan-eduth.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7803 (Shuthelah), H8364 (Shuthalhites), H7793 (Shur), H7802 (Shoshannim-Eduth), H7799 (lily), H7800 (Shushan), H8284 (sing), H7791 (wall), H7794 (bull)",
    7803: "שׁוּתֶלַח (Shûwthelach | shoo-theh'-lakh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from H7582 שָׁאָה and the same as H8520 תֶּלַח ; crash of breakage<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Shuthelach, the name of two Israelites<BR><B>KJV:</B> Shuthelah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7803 (Shuthelah), H8364 (Shuthalhites), H7793 (Shur), H7802 (Shoshannim-Eduth), H7799 (lily), H7800 (Shushan), H8284 (sing), H7791 (wall), H7794 (bull)",
    7804: "שְׁזַב (shᵉzab | shez-ab')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H5800 עָזַב<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to leave, i.e. (causatively) free<BR><B>KJV:</B> deliver.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7844 (corrupt), H7804 (deliver)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G482 ἀντιλαμβάνομαι, G1807 ἐξαιρέω, G3084 λυτρόω, G4506 ῥύομαι, G4982 σώζω",
    7805: "שָׁזַף (shâzaph | shaw-zaf')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to tan (by sunburning); figuratively (as if by a piercing ray) to scan<BR><B>KJV:</B> look up, see.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7805 (look up)",
    7806: "שָׁזַר (shâzar | shaw-zar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to twist (a thread of straw)<BR><B>KJV:</B> twine.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7806 (twine)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3514 νήθω",
    7807: "שַׁח (shach | shakh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7817 שָׁחַח<BR><B>Strong's:</B> sunk, i.e. downcast<BR><B>KJV:</B> [phrase] humble.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7807 (humble), H7817 (bend), H3439 (Jeshoaiah)",
    7808: "שֵׂחַ (sêach | say'-akh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> for H7879 שִׂיחַ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> communion, i.e. (reflexively) meditation<BR><B>KJV:</B> thought.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7879 (babbling), H7881 (meditation), H7878 (commune), H7808 (thought)",
    7809: "שָׁחַד (shâchad | shaw-khad')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to donate, i.e. bribe<BR><B>KJV:</B> hire, give a reward.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7810 (bribe), H7809 (hire)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G5412 φορτίζω",
    7810: "שַׁחַד (shachad | shakh'-ad)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7809 שָׁחַד<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a donation (venal or redemptive)<BR><B>KJV:</B> bribe(-ry), gift, present, reward.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7810 (bribe), H7809 (hire)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1435 δῶρον",
    7811: "שָׂחָה (sâchâh | saw-khaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to swim; causatively, to inundate<BR><B>KJV:</B> (make to) swim.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7811 (swim), H7813 (to swim in)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3068 λούω",
    7812: "שָׁחָה (shâchâh | shaw-khaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to depress, i.e. prostrate (especially reflexive, in homage to royalty or God)<BR><B>KJV:</B> bow (self) down, crouch, fall down (flat), humbly beseech, do (make) obeisance, do reverence, make to stoop, worship.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7812 (bow down), H7825 (destruction), H7816 (pit)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2705 καταφιλέω, G2955 κύπτω, G4160 ποιέω, G4352 προσκυνέω, G5015 ταράσσω",
    7813: "שָׂחוּ (sâchûw | saw'-khoo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7811 שָׂחָה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a pond (for swimming)<BR><B>KJV:</B> to swim in.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7811 (swim), H7813 (to swim in)",
    7814: "שְׂחֹוק (sᵉchôwq | sekh-oke')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or שְׂחֹק; from H7832 שָׂחַק<BR><B>Strong's:</B> laughter (in merriment or defiance)<BR><B>KJV:</B> derision, laughter(-ed to scorn, -ing), mocked, sport.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4890 (scorn), H7832 (deride), H7814 (derision)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1071 γέλως, G2167 εὐφροσύνη, G5479 χαρά",
    7815: "שְׁחֹור (shᵉchôwr | shekh-ore')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7835 שָׁחַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> dinginess, i.e. perhaps soot<BR><B>KJV:</B> coal.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7815 (coal), H806 (Ashur), H7840 (black), H7835 (be black), H7839 (youth), H7838 (black)",
    7816: "שְׁחוּת (shᵉchûwth | shekh-ooth')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7812 שָׁחָה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> pit<BR><B>KJV:</B> pit.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7812 (bow down), H7825 (destruction), H7816 (pit)",
    7817: "שָׁחַח (shâchach | shaw-khakh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to sink or depress (reflexive or causative)<BR><B>KJV:</B> bend, bow (down), bring (cast) down, couch, humble self, be (bring) low, stoop.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7807 (humble), H7817 (bend), H3439 (Jeshoaiah)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1416 δύνω, G2559 κακόω, G2578 κάμπτω, G2609 κατάγω, G2955 κύπτω, G5013 ταπεινόω, G5015 ταράσσω, G5080 τήκω",
    7818: "שָׂחַט (sâchaṭ | saw-khat')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to tread out, i.e. squeeze (grapes)<BR><B>KJV:</B> press.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7818 (press), H7824 (cieled with)",
    7819: "שָׁחַט (shâchaṭ | shaw-khat')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to slaughter (in sacrifice or massacre)<BR><B>KJV:</B> kill, offer, shoot out, slay, slaughter.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7821 (killing), H7820 (beat), H7819 (kill)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4969 σφάζω",
    7820: "שָׁחַט (shâchaṭ | shaw-khat')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root (identical with H7819 שָׁחַט through the idea of striking)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to hammer out<BR><B>KJV:</B> beat.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7821 (killing), H7820 (beat), H7819 (kill)",
    7821: "שְׁחִיטָה (shᵉchîyṭâh | shekh-ee-taw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7819 שָׁחַט<BR><B>Strong's:</B> slaughter<BR><B>KJV:</B> killing.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7821 (killing), H7820 (beat), H7819 (kill)",
    7822: "שְׁחִין (shᵉchîyn | shekh-een')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root probably meaning to burn<BR><B>Strong's:</B> inflammation, i.e. an ulcer<BR><B>KJV:</B> boil, botch.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7822 (boil)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1668 ἕλκος",
    7823: "שָׁחִיס (shâchîyç | shaw-khece')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or סָחִישׁ; from an unused root apparently meaning to sprout<BR><B>Strong's:</B> aftergrowth<BR><B>KJV:</B> (that) which springeth of the same.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7823 (which springeth of the same), H5501 (offscouring), H5500 (scrape)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G393 ἀνατέλλω, G2640 κατάλειμμα",
    7824: "שָׁחִיף (shâchîyph | shaw-kheef')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as H7828 שַׁחַף<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a board (as chipped thin)<BR><B>KJV:</B> cieled with.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7818 (press), H7824 (cieled with)",
    7825: "שְׁחִית (shᵉchîyth | shekh-eeth')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7812 שָׁחָה<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a pit-fall (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> destruction, pit.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7812 (bow down), H7825 (destruction), H7816 (pit)",
    7826: "שַׁחַל (shachal | shakh'-al)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root probably meaning to roar<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a lion (from his characteristic roar)<BR><B>KJV:</B> (fierce) lion.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7826 (lion), H7827 (onycha)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3023 λέων",
    7827: "שְׁחֵלֶת (shᵉchêleth | shekh-ay'-leth)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently from the same as H7826 שַׁחַל through some obscure idea, perhaps that of peeling off by concussion of sound<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a scale or shell, i.e. the aromatic mussel.<BR><B>KJV:</B> onycha.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7826 (lion), H7827 (onycha)",
    7828: "שַׁחַף (shachaph | shakh'-af)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to peel, i.e. emaciate<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the gull (as thin)<BR><B>KJV:</B> cuckoo.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7828 (cuckoo), H7829 (consumption)",
    7829: "שַׁחֶפֶת (shachepheth | shakh-eh'-feth)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as H7828 שַׁחַף<BR><B>Strong's:</B> emaciation<BR><B>KJV:</B> consumption.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7828 (cuckoo), H7829 (consumption)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G640 ἀπορία",
    7830: "שַׁחַץ (shachats | shakh'-ats)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root apparently meaning to strut<BR><B>Strong's:</B> haughtiness (as evinced by the attitude)<BR><B>KJV:</B> [idiom] lion, pride.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7830 ([idiom] lion), H7831 (Shahazimah)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G213 ἀλαζών",
    7831: "שַׁחֲצֹום (Shachătsôwm | shakh-ats-ome')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as H7830 שַׁחַץ ; proudly<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Shachatsom, a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Shahazimah (from the margin).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7830 ([idiom] lion), H7831 (Shahazimah)",
    7832: "שָׂחַק (sâchaq | saw-khak')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to laugh (in pleasure or detraction); by implication, to play<BR><B>KJV:</B> deride, have in derision, laugh, make merry, mock(-er), play, rejoice, (laugh to) scorn, be in (make) sport.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4890 (scorn), H7832 (deride), H7814 (derision)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1070 γελάω, G1702 ἐμπαίζω, G2606 καταγελάω, G3738 ὀρχέομαι, G3815 παίζω",
    7833: "שָׁחַק (shâchaq | shaw-khak')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to comminate (by trituration or attrition)<BR><B>KJV:</B> beat, wear.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7833 (beat), H7834 (cloud)",
    7834: "שַׁחַק (shachaq | shakh'-ak)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7833 שָׁחַק<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a powder (as beaten small); by analogy, a thin vapor; by extension, the firmament<BR><B>KJV:</B> cloud, small dust, heaven, sky.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7833 (beat), H7834 (cloud)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G109 ἀήρ, G798 ἄστρον, G3507 νεφέλη, G3509 νέφος, G3772 οὐρανός, G4493 ῥιπή, G4733 στερέωμα",
    7835: "שָׁחַר (shâchar | shaw-khar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root (identical with H7836 שָׁחַר through the idea of the duskiness of early dawn)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be dim or dark (in color)<BR><B>KJV:</B> be black.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7815 (coal), H806 (Ashur), H7840 (black), H7835 (be black), H7839 (youth), H7838 (black)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4656 σκοτόω",
    7836: "שָׁחַר (shâchar | shaw-khar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to dawn, i.e. (figuratively) be (up) early at any task (with the implication of earnestness); by extension, to search for (with painstaking)<BR><B>KJV:</B> (do something) betimes, enquire early, rise (seek) betimes, seek diligently) early, in the morning).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7842 (Shaharaim), H4891 (morning), H7837 (day), H7841 (Shehariah), H7836 (betimes)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1960 ἐπιμελῶς, G2212 ζητέω, G3719 ὀρθρίζω, G4406 πρώϊμος",
    7837: "שַׁחַר (shachar | shakh'-ar)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7836 שָׁחַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> dawn (literal, figurative or adverbial)<BR><B>KJV:</B> day(-spring), early, light, morning, whence riseth.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7842 (Shaharaim), H4891 (morning), H7837 (day), H7841 (Shehariah), H7836 (betimes)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3722 ὄρθρος, G4404 πρωΐ",
    7838: "שָׁחֹר (shâchôr | shaw-khore')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or שָׁחֹור; from H7835 שָׁחַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, dusky, but also (absol.) jetty<BR><B>KJV:</B> black.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7815 (coal), H806 (Ashur), H7840 (black), H7835 (be black), H7839 (youth), H7838 (black)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3189 μέλας",
    7839: "שַׁחֲרוּת (shachărûwth | shakh-ar-ooth')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7836 שָׁחַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a dawning, i.e. (figuratively) juvenescence<BR><B>KJV:</B> youth.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7815 (coal), H806 (Ashur), H7840 (black), H7835 (be black), H7839 (youth), H7838 (black)",
    7840: "שְׁחַרְחֹרֶת (shᵉcharchôreth | shekh-ar-kho'-reth)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7835 שָׁחַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> swarthy<BR><B>KJV:</B> black.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7815 (coal), H806 (Ashur), H7840 (black), H7835 (be black), H7839 (youth), H7838 (black)",
    7841: "שְׁחַרְיָה (Shᵉcharyâh | shekh-ar-yaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7836 שָׁחַר and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has sought<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Shecharjah, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Shehariah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7842 (Shaharaim), H4891 (morning), H7837 (day), H7841 (Shehariah), H7836 (betimes)",
    7842: "שַׁחֲרַיִם (Shachărayim | shakh-ar-ah'-yim)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> dual of H7837 שַׁחַר ; double dawn<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Shacharajim, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Shaharaim.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7842 (Shaharaim), H4891 (morning), H7837 (day), H7841 (Shehariah), H7836 (betimes)",
