    7844: "שְׁחַת (shᵉchath | shekh-ath')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H7843 שָׁחַת<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to decay, i.e. (causatively) ruin (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> corrupt, fault.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7844 (corrupt), H7804 (deliver)",
    7845: "שַׁחַת (shachath | shakh'-ath)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7743 שׁוּחַ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a pit (especially as a trap); figuratively, destruction<BR><B>KJV:</B> corruption, destruction, ditch, grave, pit.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7744 (Shuah), H7845 (corruption), H7745 (ditch), H7746 (Shuah), H7743 (bow down), H7882 (pit), H7749 (Shuhamites), H7747 (Shuhite), H7748 (Shuham)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G999 βόθυνος, G2288 θάνατος, G2513 καθαρός, G4509 ῥύπος, G5356 φθορά",
    7846: "שֵׂט (sêṭ | sayte)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or סֵט; from H7750 שׂוּט<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a departure from right, i.e. sin<BR><B>KJV:</B> revolter, that turn aside.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7750 (turn aside to), H7846 (revolter)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3847 παράβασις",
