    7897: "שִׁית (shîyth | sheeth)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7896 שִׁית<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a dress (as put on)<BR><B>KJV:</B> attire.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H8352 (Seth), H8356 (foundation), H7896 (apply), H7898 (thorns), H7897 (attire)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1491 εἶδος",
    7898: "שַׁיִת (shayith | shah'-yith)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7896 שִׁית<BR><B>Strong's:</B> scrub or trash, i.e. wild growth of weeds or briers (as if put on the field)<BR><B>KJV:</B> thorns.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H8352 (Seth), H8356 (foundation), H7896 (apply), H7898 (thorns), H7897 (attire)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G173 ἄκανθα, G1643 ἐλαύνω, G2562 καλάμη",
    7899: "שֵׂךְ (sêk | sake)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5526 סָכַךְ in the sense of H7753 שׂוּךְ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a brier (as of a hedge)<BR><B>KJV:</B> prick.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7905 (barbed iron), H7899 (prick)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4647 σκόλοψ",
    7900: "שֹׂךְ (sôk | soke)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H5526 סָכַךְ in the sense of H7753 שׂוּךְ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a booth (as interlaced)<BR><B>KJV:</B> tabernacle.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H5526 (cover), H7900 (tabernacle)",
    7901: "שָׁכַב (shâkab | shaw-kab')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to lie down (for rest, sexual connection, decease or any other purpose)<BR><B>KJV:</B> [idiom] at all, cast down, (lover-)lay (self) (down), (make to) lie (down, down to sleep, still with), lodge, ravish, take rest, sleep, stay.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7902 ([idiom] carnally), H7901 ([idiom] at all), H7903 ([idiom] lie), H4904 (bed)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G373 ἀναπαύω, G599 ἀποθνήσκω, G2518 καθεύδω, G2521 κάθημαι, G2621 κατάκειμαι, G2647 καταλύω, G2730 κατοικέω, G2827 κλίνω, G2837 κοιμάω, G2845 κοίτη, G2942 κυβερνήτης, G3435 μολύνω",
