    7911: "שָׁכַח (shâkach | shaw-kakh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or שָׁכֵחַ; a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to mislay, i.e. to be oblivious of, from want of memory or attention<BR><B>KJV:</B> [idiom] at all, (cause to) forget.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7911 ([idiom] at all), H7913 (forget)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G415 ἀνελεήμων, G1459 ἐγκαταλείπω, G1950 ἐπιλανθάνομαι, G2641 καταλείπω, G3024 λήθη",
    7912: "שְׁכַח (shᵉkach | shek-akh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H7911 שָׁכַח through the idea of disclosure of a covered or forgotten thing<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to discover (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> find.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7912 (find)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2147 εὑρίσκω, G2638 καταλαμβάνω, G5083 τηρέω",
