    7914: "שְׂכִיָּה (sᵉkîyâh | sek-ee-yaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine from the same as H7906 שֵׂכוּ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a conspicuous object<BR><B>KJV:</B> picture.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7914 (picture), H7907 (heart), H4906 (conceit), H7906 (Sechu), H7634 (Shachia), H7915 (knife)",
    7915: "שַׂכִּין (sakkîyn | sak-keen')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> intensive perhaps from the same as H7906 שֵׂכוּ in the sense of H7753 שׂוּךְ<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a knife (as pointed or edged)<BR><B>KJV:</B> knife.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7914 (picture), H7907 (heart), H4906 (conceit), H7906 (Sechu), H7634 (Shachia), H7915 (knife)",
    7916: "שָׂכִיר (sâkîyr | saw-keer')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7936 שָׂכַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a man at wages by the day or year<BR><B>KJV:</B> hired (man, servant), hireling.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7958 (quails), H7938 (reward), H8073 (Shalmai), H8009 (Salmon), H7940 (Sacar), H7917 (that is hired), H4909 (reward), H8012 (Salmon), H8007 (Salma), H7939 (hire), H7936 (earn wages), H8014 (Shalmai), H7916 (hired)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3407 μίσθιος, G3411 μισθωτός",
