    7918: "שָׁכַךְ (shâkak | shaw-kak')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to weave (i.e. lay) a trap; figuratively, (through the idea of secreting) to allay (passions; physically, abate a flood)<BR><B>KJV:</B> appease, assuage, make to cease, pacify, set.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7918 (appease)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2869 κοπάζω, G4014 περιαιρέω",
