    7920: "שְׂכַל (sᵉkal | sek-al')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H7919 שָׂכַל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be (causatively, make or act) circumspect and hence, intelligent<BR><B>KJV:</B> consider.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7920 (consider), H7924 (understanding)",
    7921: "שָׁכֹל (shâkôl | shaw-kole')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to miscarry, i.e. suffer abortion; by analogy, to bereave (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> bereave (of children), barren, cast calf (fruit, young), be (make) childless, deprive, destroy, [idiom] expect, lose children, miscarry, rob of children, spoil.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7909 (barren), H7921 (bereave), H7908 (loss of children), H7923 (to have after loss of others)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G770 ἀσθενέω, G815 ἄτεκνος, G2719 κατεσθίω, G5097 τιμωρέω",
