    7923: "שִׁכֻּלִים (shikkulîym | shik-koo-leem')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> plural from H7921 שָׁכֹל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> childlessness (by continued bereavements)<BR><B>KJV:</B> to have after loss of others.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7909 (barren), H7921 (bereave), H7908 (loss of children), H7923 (to have after loss of others)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G622 ἀπόλλυμι",
    7924: "שׇׂכְלְתָנוּ (soklᵉthânûw | sok-leth-aw-noo')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) from H7920 שְׂכַל<BR><B>Strong's:</B> intelligence<BR><B>KJV:</B> understanding.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7920 (consider), H7924 (understanding)",
    7925: "שָׁכַם (shâkam | shaw-kam')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root; properly, to incline (the shoulder to a burden); but used only as denominative from H7926 שְׁכֶם<BR><B>Strong's:</B> literally, to load up (on the back of man or beast), i.e. to start early in the morning<BR><B>KJV:</B> (arise, be up, get (oneself) up, rise up) early (betimes), morning.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7929 (shoulder blade), H7925 (early), H7927 (Shechem), H7930 (Shichemites), H7926 (back), H7928 (Shechem)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G450 ἀνίστημι, G1817 ἐξανίστημι, G3719 ὀρθρίζω, G3720 ὀρθρινός",
