    7932: "שְׁכַן (shᵉkan | shek-an')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H7931 שָׁכַן<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to reside or permanently stay (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> cause to dwell, have habitation.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4907 (habitation), H7932 (cause to dwell)",
    7933: "שֶׁכֶן (sheken | sheh'-ken)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7931 שָׁכַן<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a residence<BR><B>KJV:</B> habitation.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7931 (abide), H4908 (dwelleth), H7933 (habitation), H7935 (Shecaniah), H7934 (inhabitant)",
    7934: "שָׁכֵן (shâkên | shaw-kane')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H7931 שָׁכַן<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a resident; by extension, a fellow-citizen<BR><B>KJV:</B> inhabitant, neighbour, nigh.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7931 (abide), H4908 (dwelleth), H7933 (habitation), H7935 (Shecaniah), H7934 (inhabitant)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1069 γείτων, G1069 γείτων, G3941 πάροικος, G4040 περίοικος",
    7935: "שְׁכַנְיָה (Shᵉkanyâh | shek-an-yaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or (prolonged) שְׁכַנְיָהוּ; from H7931 שָׁכַן and H3050 יָהּ ; Jah has dwelt<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Shekanjah, the name of nine Israelites<BR><B>KJV:</B> Shecaniah, Shechaniah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7931 (abide), H4908 (dwelleth), H7933 (habitation), H7935 (Shecaniah), H7934 (inhabitant)",
    7936: "שָׂכַר (sâkar | saw-kar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or (by permutation) סָכַר; (Ezra 4:5), a primitive root (apparently akin (by prosthesis) to H3739 כָּרָה through the idea of temporary purchase; compare H7937 שָׁכַר)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to hire<BR><B>KJV:</B> earn wages, hire (out self), reward, [idiom] surely.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7936 (earn wages)",
