    7951: "שָׁלָה (shâlâh | shaw-law')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or שָׁלַו; (Job 3:26), a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be tranquil, i.e. secure or successful<BR><B>KJV:</B> be happy, prosper, be in safety.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H7956 (Shelah), H7952 (deceive), H7959 (prosperity), H8024 (Shelanites), H7961 (at ease), H7962 (abundance), H7987 (quietly), H7951 (be happy)",
