    8175: "שָׂעַר (sâʻar | saw-ar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to storm; by implication, to shiver, i.e. fear<BR><B>KJV:</B> be (horribly) afraid, fear, hurl as a storm, be tempestuous, come like (take away as with) a whirlwind.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H8181 (hair), H8165 (Seir), H8185 (hair), H8188 (Seorim), H8166 (kid), H8184 (barley), H8175 (be afraid), H8163 (devil), H8178 (affrighted), H8167 (Seirath)",
    8176: "שָׁעַר (shâʻar | shaw-ar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root; to split or open, i.e. (literally, but only as denominative from H8179 שַׁעַר); compare see H7778 שֹׁועֵר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to act as gatekeeper; (figuratively) to estimate<BR><B>KJV:</B> think.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H8176 (think), H8180 (fold)",
    8177: "שְׂעַר (sᵉʻar | seh-ar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (Aramaic) corresponding to H8181 שֵׂעָר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> hair<BR><B>KJV:</B> hair.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H8177 (hair), H8131 (hate)",
