    8179: "שַׁעַר (shaʻar | shah'-ar)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H8176 שָׁעַר in its original sense<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an opening, i.e. door or gate<BR><B>KJV:</B> city, door, gate, port ([idiom] -er).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H8187 (Sheariah), H7778 (doorkeeper), H8179 (city), H8189 (Shaaraim)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G833 αὐλή, G2374 θύρα, G4172 πόλις, G4439 πύλη, G4440 πυλών",
    8180: "שַׁעַר (shaʻar | shah'-ar)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from H8176 שָׁעַר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a measure (as a section)<BR><B>KJV:</B> (hundred-) fold.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H8176 (think), H8180 (fold)",
    8181: "שֵׂעָר (sêʻâr | say-awr')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or שַׂעַר; (Isaiah 7:20), from H8175 שָׂעַר in the sense of dishevelling<BR><B>Strong's:</B> hair (as if tossed or bristling)<BR><B>KJV:</B> hair(-y), [idiom] rough.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H8181 (hair), H8165 (Seir), H8185 (hair), H8188 (Seorim), H8166 (kid), H8184 (barley), H8175 (be afraid), H8163 (devil), H8178 (affrighted), H8167 (Seirath)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2355 θρῆνος, G5155 τρίχινος",
