    8446: "תּוּר (tûwr | toor)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to meander (causatively, guide) about, especially for trade or reconnoitring<BR><B>KJV:</B> chap(-man), sent to descry, be excellent, merchant(-man), search (out), seek, (e-) spy (out).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H8446 (chap), H3491 (range), H8447 (border), H8448 (estate)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G1294 διαστρέφω, G1586 ἐκλέγομαι, G1614 ἐκτείνω, G1621 ἐκτινάσσω, G1980 ἐπισκέπτομαι, G2090 ἑτοιμάζω",
    8447: "תֹּור (tôwr | tore)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or תֹּר; from H8446 תּוּר<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a succession, i.e. a string or (abstractly) order<BR><B>KJV:</B> border, row, turn.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H8446 (chap), H3491 (range), H8447 (border), H8448 (estate)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G2540 καιρός, G3706 ὅρασις, G5167 τρυγών, G5550 χρόνος",
    8448: "תֹּור (tôwr | tore)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably the same as H8447 תֹּור<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a manner (as a sort of turn)<BR><B>KJV:</B> estate.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H8446 (chap), H3491 (range), H8447 (border), H8448 (estate)",
