    8452: "תֹּורָה (tôwrâh | to-raw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably feminine of H8448 תֹּור<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a custom<BR><B>KJV:</B> manner.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H4175 (rain), H3140 (Jorai), H8451 (law), H3138 (first rain), H4176 (Moreh), H3404 (Jeriah), H8452 (manner), H3385 (Jeruel), H3139 (Jorah), H3384 (archer), H3400 (Jeriel)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G975 βιβλίον, G1242 διαθήκη, G1785 ἐντολή, G3056 λόγος, G3551 νόμος, G5010 τάξις",
    8453: "תֹּושָׁב (tôwshâb | to-shawb')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or תֹּשָׁב; (1 Kings 17:1), from H3427 יָשַׁב ; a dweller (but not outlandish (H5237 נׇכְרִי)); especially (as distinguished from a native citizen (active participle of H3427 יָשַׁב) and a temporary inmate (H1616 גֵּר) or mere lodger (H3885 לוּן))<BR><BR><B>Strong's:</B> resident alien<BR><B>KJV:</B> foreigner, inhabitant, sojourner, stranger.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3430 (Ishbi-benob), H3428 (Jeshebeab), H3436 (Joshbekashah), H3429 (that sat in the seat), H3427 (abide), H7871 (while), H4186 (assembly), H8453 (foreigner), H7675 (place), H3143 (Josibiah)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G3927 παρεπίδημος, G3941 πάροικος",
    8454: "תּוּשִׁיָּה (tûwshîyâh | too-shee-yaw')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> or תֻּשִׁיָּה; from an unused root probably meaning to substantiate<BR><B>Strong's:</B> support or (by implication) ability, i.e. (direct) help, (in purpose) an undertaking, (intellectual) understanding<BR><B>KJV:</B> enterprise, that which (thing as it) is, substance, (sound) wisdom, working.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H3144 (Joshah), H8454 (enterprise), H3145 (Joshaviah)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G227 ἀληθής, G803 ἀσφάλεια, G996 βοήθεια, G1012 βουλή, G1872 ἐπακολουθέω, G2479 ἰσχύς, G2540 καιρός, G4991 σωτηρία",
    8455: "תֹּותָח (tôwthâch | to-thawkh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an unused root meaning to smite<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a club<BR><B>KJV:</B> darts.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H8455 (darts)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G4974 σφυρόν",
    8456: "תָּזַז (tâzaz | taw-zaz')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primitive root<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to lop off<BR><B>KJV:</B> cut down.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> H8476 (badger), H8472 (Tahpenes), H8456 (cut down), H8477 (Thahash), H8471 (Tahapanes), H8473 (habergeon)<BR><B>Greek Equivalents:</B> G609 ἀποκόπτω, G2629 κατακόπτω",
