    124: "Αἰγύπτιος (Aigýptios | ahee-goop'-tee-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G125<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an Ægyptian or inhabitant of Ægyptus<BR><B>KJV:</B> Egyptian.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G125<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G118 (strive), G119 (fight), G4866 (labour with)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Αἰγύπτιος",
    125: "Αἴγυπτος (Aígyptos | ah'-ee-goop-tos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Ægyptus, the land of the Nile<BR><B>KJV:</B> Egypt.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G118 (strive), G119 (fight), G4866 (labour with)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Αἴγυπτος",
    126: "ἀΐδιος (aḯdios | ah-id'-ee-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G104<BR><B>Strong's:</B> everduring (forward and backward, or forward only)<BR><B>KJV:</B> eternal, everlasting.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G104<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G126 (eternal)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἀΐδιος, ἀί̈διος, ἀΐδιος",
    127: "αἰδώς (aidṓs | ahee-doce')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> perhaps from G1 (as a negative particle) and G1492 (through the idea of downcast eyes)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> bashfulness, i.e. (towards men), modesty or (towards God) awe<BR><B>KJV:</B> reverence, shamefacedness.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G1<BR><I>See:</I> G1492<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G127 (reverence)<BR><B>Variants:</B> αἰδώς, δέος",
