    131: "αἱμοῤῥέω (haimorrhéō | hahee-mor-hreh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G129 and G4482<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to flow blood, i.e. have a hæmorrhage<BR><B>KJV:</B> diseased with an issue of blood.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G129<BR><I>See:</I> G4482<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G130 (shedding of blood), G129 (blood)<BR><B>Variants:</B> αἱμοῤῥέω, αἱμορροέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1739 דָּוֶה",
    132: "Αἰνέας (Ainéas | ahee-neh'-as)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Ænĕas, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Æneas.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G130 (shedding of blood), G129 (blood)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Αἰνέας",
