    136: "αἶνος (aînos | ah'-ee-nos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a prime word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, a story, but used in the sense of G1868 ; praise (of God)<BR><B>KJV:</B> praise.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G1868<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G134 (praise), G136 (praise)<BR><B>Variants:</B> αἶνος, αὶνος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1984 הָלַל, H5797 עֹז",
    137: "Αἰνών (Ainṓn | ahee-nohn')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (a derivative of G5869, place of springs)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Ænon, a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Ænon.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5869<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G134 (praise), G136 (praise)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Αἰνών<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5869 עַיִן",
    138: "αἱρέομαι (hairéomai | hahee-reh'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably akin to G142<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to take for oneself, i.e. to prefer<BR><B>KJV:</B> choose. Some of the forms are borrowed from a cognate ἕλλομαι (héllomai | hel'-lom-ahee)<BR>; which is otherwise obsolete.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G142<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G139 (heresy), G1243 (difference), G1244 (divide), G141 (heretic), G140 (choose), G138 (choose)<BR><B>Variants:</B> αἱρέομαι, αἱρέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H559 אָמַר, H977 בָּחַר, H2654 חָפֵץ, H2836 חָשַׁק, H5186 נָטָה, H5493 סוּר",
    139: "αἵρεσις (haíresis | hah'-ee-res-is)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G138<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, a choice, i.e. (specially) a party or (abstractly) disunion<BR><B>KJV:</B> heresy (which is the Greek word itself), sect.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G138<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G139 (heresy), G1243 (difference), G1244 (divide), G141 (heretic), G140 (choose), G138 (choose)<BR><B>Variants:</B> αἵρεσις<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5071 נְדָבָה",
