    154: "αἰτέω (aitéō | ahee-teh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to ask (in genitive case)<BR><B>KJV:</B> ask, beg, call for, crave, desire, require. Compare G4441 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4441<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3868 (avoid), G155 (petition), G523 (ask again), G1809 (desire), G154 (ask)<BR><B>Variants:</B> αἰτέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H559 אָמַר, H1156 בְּעָא, H5414 נָתַן, H7592 שָׁאַל",
    155: "αἴτημα (aítēma | ah'-ee-tay-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G154<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a thing asked or (abstractly) an asking<BR><B>KJV:</B> petition, request, required.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G154<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3868 (avoid), G155 (petition), G523 (ask again), G1809 (desire), G154 (ask)<BR><B>Variants:</B> αἴτημα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1159 בָּעוּ, H4100 מָה, H7596 שְׁאֵלָה",
    156: "αἰτία (aitía | ahee-tee'-a)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as G154<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a cause (as if asked for), i.e. (logical) reason (motive, matter), (legal) crime (alleged or proved)<BR><B>KJV:</B> accusation, case, cause, crime, fault, (wh-)ere(-fore).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G154<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3868 (avoid), G155 (petition), G523 (ask again), G1809 (desire), G154 (ask)<BR><B>Variants:</B> αἰτία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5771 עָוֺן, H6231 עָשַׁק",
    157: "αἰτίαμα (aitíama | ahee-tee'-am-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of G156<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a thing charged<BR><B>KJV:</B> complaint.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G156<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3868 (avoid), G155 (petition), G523 (ask again), G1809 (desire), G154 (ask)<BR><B>Variants:</B> αἰτίαμα, αἰτίωμα",
    158: "αἴτιον (aítion | ah'-ee-tee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of G159<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a reason or crime (like G156)<BR><B>KJV:</B> cause, fault.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G159<BR><I>See:</I> G156<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3868 (avoid), G155 (petition), G523 (ask again), G1809 (desire), G154 (ask)<BR><B>Variants:</B> αἴτιον, αἴτιος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5437 סָבַב",
    159: "αἴτιος (aítios | ah'-ee-tee-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as G154<BR><B>Strong's:</B> causative, i.e. (concretely) a causer<BR><B>KJV:</B> author.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G154<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3868 (avoid), G155 (petition), G523 (ask again), G1809 (desire), G154 (ask)<BR><B>Variants:</B> αἴτιος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5437 סָבַב",
    160: "αἰφνίδιος (aiphnídios | aheef-nid'-ee-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a compound of G1 (as a negative particle) and G5316 (compare G1810) (meaning non-apparent)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> unexpected, i.e. (adverbially) suddenly<BR><B>KJV:</B> sudden, unawares.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G1<BR><I>See:</I> G5316<BR><I>See:</I> G1810<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3868 (avoid), G155 (petition), G523 (ask again), G1809 (desire), G154 (ask)<BR><B>Variants:</B> αἰφνίδιος",
