    843: "αὐτοκατάκριτος (autokatákritos | ow-tok-at-ak'-ree-tos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G846 and a derivative or G2632<BR><B>Strong's:</B> self-condemned<BR><B>KJV:</B> condemned of self.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G846<BR><I>See:</I> G2632<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G612 (answer), G2631 (condemnation), G470 (answer again), G351 (examination), G2923 (judge), G610 (sentence), G2924 (discerner), G1469 (make of the number), G350 (ask), G1253 (discern), G843 (condemned of self), G2632 (condemn), G2919 (avenge), G2917 (avenge), G1252 (contend), G87 (without partiality), G611 (answer), G178 (uncondemned), G2633 (condemn), G2920 (accusation), G2922 (to judge)<BR><B>Variants:</B> αὐτοκατάκριτος",
    844: "αὐτόματος (autómatos | ow-tom'-at-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G846 and the same as G3155<BR><B>Strong's:</B> self-moved (\"automatic\"), i.e. spontaneous<BR><B>KJV:</B> of own accord, of self.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G846<BR><I>See:</I> G3155<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G612 (answer), G2631 (condemnation), G470 (answer again), G351 (examination), G2923 (judge), G610 (sentence), G2924 (discerner), G1469 (make of the number), G350 (ask), G1253 (discern), G843 (condemned of self), G2632 (condemn), G2919 (avenge), G2917 (avenge), G1252 (contend), G87 (without partiality), G611 (answer), G178 (uncondemned), G2633 (condemn), G2920 (accusation), G2922 (to judge)<BR><B>Variants:</B> αὐτόματος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5599 סָפִיחַ",
    845: "αὐτόπτης (autóptēs | ow-top'-tace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G846 and G3700<BR><B>Strong's:</B> self-seeing, i.e. an eye-witness<BR><B>KJV:</B> eye-witness.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G846<BR><I>See:</I> G3700<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)<BR><B>Variants:</B> αὐτόπτης",
    846: "αὐτός (autós | ow-tos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the particle αὖ (perhaps akin to the base of G109 through the idea of a baffling wind) (backward)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the reflexive pronoun self, used (alone or in the comparative G1438) of the third person, and (with the proper personal pronoun) of the other persons<BR><B>KJV:</B> her, it(-self), one, the other, (mine) own, said, (self-), the) same, ((him-, my-, thy-)self, (your-)selves, she, that, their(-s), them(-selves), there(-at, - by, -in, -into, -of, -on, -with), they, (these) things, this (man), those, together, very, which. Compare G848 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G109<BR><I>See:</I> G1438<BR><I>See:</I> G848<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)<BR><B>Variants:</B> αὐτός",
    847: "αὐτοῦ (autoû | ow-too')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> genitive (i.e. possessive) of G846, used as an adverb of location<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, belonging to the same spot, i.e. in this (or that) place<BR><B>KJV:</B> (t-)here.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G846<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)<BR><B>Variants:</B> αὐτοῦ, αὐτόπτης<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6311 פֹּה",
    848: "αὑτοῦ (hautoû | how-too')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> contracted for G1438<BR><B>Strong's:</B> self (in some oblique case or reflexively, relation)<BR><B>KJV:</B> her (own), (of) him(-self), his (own), of it, thee, their (own), them(-selves), they.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G1438<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)<BR><B>Variants:</B> αὑτοῦ, αὐτόπτης G899, G900",
