    1909: "ἐπί (epí | ep-ee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary preposition<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, meaning superimposition (of time, place, order, etc.), as a relation of distribution (with the genitive case), i.e. over, upon, etc.; of rest (with the dative case) at, on, etc.; of direction (with the accusative case) towards, upon, etc.<BR><B>KJV:</B> about (the times), above, after, against, among, as long as (touching), at, beside, X have charge of, (be-, (where-))fore, in (a place, as much as, the time of, -to), (because) of, (up-)on (behalf of), over, (by, for) the space of, through(-out), (un-)to(-ward), with. In compounds it retains essentially the same import, at, upon, etc. (literally or figuratively).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1906 (answer), G1905 (ask), G2065 (ask)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἐπί",
