    2183: "ἐφημερία (ephēmería | ef-ay-mer-ee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G2184<BR><B>Strong's:</B> diurnality, i.e. (specially) the quotidian rotation or class of the Jewish priests' service at the Temple, as distributed by families<BR><B>KJV:</B> course.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2184<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2178 (once), G530 (once)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἐφημερία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4256 מַחֲלֹקֶת, H4929 מִשְׁמָר, H4931 מִשְׁמֶרֶת",
    2184: "ἐφήμερος (ephḗmeros | ef-ay'-mer-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G1909 and G2250<BR><B>Strong's:</B> for a day (\"ephemeral\"), i.e. diurnal<BR><B>KJV:</B> daily.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G1909<BR><I>See:</I> G2250<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2178 (once), G530 (once)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἐφήμερος",
