    2191: "ἔχιδνα (échidna | ekh'-id-nah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an adder or other poisonous snake (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> viper.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2191 (viper)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἔχιδνα",
    2192: "ἔχω (échō | ekh'-o), including an alternate form σχέω (schéō | skheh'-o); (used in certain tenses only)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to hold (used in very various applications, literally or figuratively, direct or remote; such as possession; ability, contiuity, relation, or condition)<BR><B>KJV:</B> be (able, X hold, possessed with), accompany, + begin to amend, can(+ -not), X conceive, count, diseased, do + eat, + enjoy, + fear, following, have, hold, keep, + lack, + go to law, lie, + must needs, + of necessity, + need, next, + recover, + reign, + rest, + return, X sick, take for, + tremble, + uncircumcised, use.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1777 (in danger of), G2722 (have), G568 (be), G3353 (fellow), G3348 (be partaker), G472 (hold fast), G2192 (hold)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἔχω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H157 אָהַב, H270 אָחַז, H309 אָחַר, H383 אִיתַי, H410 אֵל, H1167 בַּעַל, H1692 דָּבַק, H1961 הָיָה, H1961 הָיָה, H2009 הִנֵּה, H2266 חָבַר, H2388 חָזַק, H2505 חָלַק, H2974 יָאַל, H3426 יֵשׁ, H3559 כּוּן, H3789 כָּתַב, H3830 לְבוּשׁ, H3947 לָקַח, H4135 מוּל, H4422 מָלַט, H4626 מַעַר, H4672 מָצָא, H4962 מַת, H5048 נֶגֶד, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5414 נָתַן, H5921 עַל, H5973 עִם, H5975 עָמַד, H6102 עָצֵל, H6113 עָצָר, H6256 עֵת, H6845 צָפַן, H7227 רַב, H7257 רָבַץ, H7693 שָׁגַל, H7760 שׂוּם, H7965 שָׁלֹום",
    2193: "ἕως (héōs | heh'-oce)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain affinity<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a conjunction, preposition and adverb of continuance, until (of time and place)<BR><B>KJV:</B> even (until, unto), (as) far (as), how long, (un-)til(-l), (hither-, un-, up) to, while(-s).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1777 (in danger of), G2722 (have), G568 (be), G3353 (fellow), G3348 (be partaker), G472 (hold fast), G2192 (hold)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἕως",
    2194: "Ζαβουλών (Zaboulṓn | dzab-oo-lone')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (H2074)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Zabulon (i.e. Zebulon), a region of Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Zabulon.<BR><I>See:</I> H2074<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1777 (in danger of), G2722 (have), G568 (be), G3353 (fellow), G3348 (be partaker), G472 (hold fast), G2192 (hold)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Ζαβουλών<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2074 זְבוּלוּן",
    2195: "Ζακχαῖος (Zakchaîos | dzak-chah'-ee-yos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (compare H2140)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Zacchæus, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Zacchæus.<BR><I>See:</I> H2140<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1777 (in danger of), G2722 (have), G568 (be), G3353 (fellow), G3348 (be partaker), G472 (hold fast), G2192 (hold)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Ζακχαῖος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2140 זַכַּי",
    2196: "Ζαρά (Zará | dzar-ah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (H2226)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Zara, (i.e. Zerach), an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Zara.<BR><I>See:</I> H2226<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1777 (in danger of), G2722 (have), G568 (be), G3353 (fellow), G3348 (be partaker), G472 (hold fast), G2192 (hold)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Ζαρά, Ζάρα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2226 זֶרַח",
    2197: "Ζαχαρίας (Zacharías | dzakh-ar-ee'-as)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (H2148)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Zacharias (i.e. Zechariah), the name of two Israelites<BR><B>KJV:</B> Zacharias.<BR><I>See:</I> H2148<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1777 (in danger of), G2722 (have), G568 (be), G3353 (fellow), G3348 (be partaker), G472 (hold fast), G2192 (hold)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Ζαχαρίας<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2148 זְכַרְיָה",
    2198: "ζάω (záō | dzah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to live (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> life(-time), (a-)live(-ly), quick.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2190 (enemy), G2198 (life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζάω, ζῶ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2421 חָיָה",
    2199: "Ζεβεδαῖος (Zebedaîos | dzeb-ed-ah'-yos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (compare H2067)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Zebedæus, an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Zebedee.<BR><I>See:</I> H2067<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2190 (enemy), G2198 (life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Ζεβεδαῖος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2067 זַבְדִּי",
    2200: "ζεστός (zestós | dzes-tos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G2204<BR><B>Strong's:</B> boiled, i.e. (by implication) calid (figuratively, fervent)<BR><B>KJV:</B> hot.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2204<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2200 (hot), G2204 (be fervent)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζεστός",
    2201: "ζεῦγος (zeûgos | dzyoo'-gos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as G2218<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a couple, i.e. a team (of oxen yoked together) or brace (of birds tied together)<BR><B>KJV:</B> yoke, pair.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2218<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2200 (hot), G2204 (be fervent)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζεῦγος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6187 עֵרֶךְ, H6776 צֶמֶד, H8147 שְׁנַיִם",
    2202: "ζευκτηρία (zeuktēría | dzook-tay-ree'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of a derivative (at the second stage) from the same as G2218<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a fastening (tiller-rope)<BR><B>KJV:</B> band.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2218<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2200 (hot), G2204 (be fervent)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζευκτηρία",
    2203: "Ζεύς (Zeús | dzyooce)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain affinity<BR><B>Strong's:</B> in the oblique cases there is used instead of it a (probably cognate) name Δίς (Dís | deece)<BR>, which is otherwise obsolete; Zeus or Dis (among the Latins, Jupiter or Jove), the supreme deity of the Greeks<BR><B>KJV:</B> Jupiter.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2200 (hot), G2204 (be fervent)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Ζεύς",
    2204: "ζέω (zéō | dzeh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be hot (boil, of liquids; or glow, of solids), i.e. (figuratively) be fervid (earnest)<BR><B>KJV:</B> be fervent.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2200 (hot), G2204 (be fervent)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7311 רוּם, H7570 רָתַח",
    2205: "ζῆλος (zēlos | dzay'-los)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G2204<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, heat, i.e. (figuratively) \"zeal\" (in a favorable sense, ardor; in an unfavorable one, jealousy, as of a husband (figuratively, of God), or an enemy, malice)<BR><B>KJV:</B> emulation, envy(-ing), fervent mind, indignation, jealousy, zeal.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2204<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζῆλος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7068 קִנְאָה",
    2206: "ζηλόω (zēlóō | dzay-lo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G2205<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to have warmth of feeling for or against<BR><B>KJV:</B> affect, covet (earnestly), (have) desire, (move with) envy, be jealous over, (be) zealous(-ly affect).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2205<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζηλόω, ζηλεύω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H833 אָשַׁר, H977 בָּחַר, H5006 נָאַץ, H7065 קָנָא",
    2207: "ζηλωτής (zēlōtḗs | dzay-lo-tace')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G2206<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a \"zealot\"<BR><B>KJV:</B> zealous.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2206<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζηλωτής<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7067 קַנָּא, H7072 קַנֹּוא",
    2208: "Ζηλωτής (Zēlōtḗs | dzay-lo-tace')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> the same as G2207<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Zealot, i.e. (specially) partisan for Jewish political independence<BR><B>KJV:</B> Zelotes.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2207<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Ζηλωτής, ζηλωτής G2421<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7067 קַנָּא, H7072 קַנֹּוא",
    2209: "ζημία (zēmía | dzay-mee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably akin to the base of G1150 (through the idea of violence)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> detriment<BR><B>KJV:</B> damage, loss.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G1150<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζημία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6064 עָנַשׁ, H6066 עֹנֶשׁ",
    2210: "ζημιόω (zēmióō | dzay-mee-o'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G2209<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to injure, i.e. (reflexively or passively) to experience detriment<BR><B>KJV:</B> be cast away, receive damage, lose, suffer loss.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2209<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζημιόω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5375 נָשָׂא, H6064 עָנַשׁ",
    2211: "Ζηνᾶς (Zēnâs | dzay-nas')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably contracted from a poetic form of G2203 and G1435<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Jove-given; Zenas, a Christian<BR><B>KJV:</B> Zenas.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2203<BR><I>See:</I> G1435<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Ζηνᾶς",
    2212: "ζητέω (zētéō | dzay-teh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain affinity<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to seek (literally or figuratively); specially, (by Hebraism) to worship (God), or (in a bad sense) to plot (against life)<BR><B>KJV:</B> be (go) about, desire, endeavour, enquire (for), require, (X will) seek (after, for, means). Compare G4441 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4441<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζητέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H157 אָהַב, H995 בִּין, H1097 בְּלִי, H1156 בְּעָא, H1158 בָּעָה, H1243 בַּקָּרָה, H1245 בָּקַשׁ, H1246 בַּקָּשָׁה, H1875 דָּרַשׁ, H2470 חָלָה, H2658 חָפַר, H4672 מָצָא, H5341 נָצַר, H5921 עַל, H6485 פָּקַד, H6634 צְבָא, H7592 שָׁאַל, H7836 שָׁחַר",
    2213: "ζήτημα (zḗtēma | dzay'-tay-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G2212<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a search (properly concretely), i.e. (in words) a debate<BR><B>KJV:</B> question.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2212<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζήτημα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1875 דָּרַשׁ",
    2214: "ζήτησις (zḗtēsis | dzay'-tay-sis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G2212<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a searching (properly, the act), i.e. a dispute or its theme<BR><B>KJV:</B> question.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2212<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζήτησις, ἐκζήτησις",
    2215: "ζιζάνιον (zizánion | dziz-an'-ee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> darnel or false grain<BR><B>KJV:</B> tares.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζιζάνιον",
    2216: "Ζοροβάβελ (Zorobábel | dzor-ob-ab'-el)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (H2216)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Zorobabel (i.e. Zerubbabel), an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Zorobabel.<BR><I>See:</I> H2216<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Ζοροβάβελ, Ζοροβαβέλ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2216 זְרֻבָּבֶל",
    2217: "ζόφος (zóphos | dzof'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> akin to the base of G3509<BR><B>Strong's:</B> gloom (as shrouding like a cloud)<BR><B>KJV:</B> blackness, darkness, mist.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3509<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3863 (provoke to emulation), G2205 (emulation), G2207 (zealous), G2206 (affect)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζόφος",
    2218: "ζυγός (zygós | dzoo-gos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the root of ζεύγνυμι (to join, especially by a \"yoke\")<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a coupling, i.e. (figuratively) servitude (a law or obligation); also (literally) the beam of the balance (as connecting the scales)<BR><B>KJV:</B> pair of balances, yoke.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2218 (pair of balances), G2086 (unequally yoke together with)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζυγός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2908 טְוָת, H3976 מֹאזֵן, H4294 מַטֶּה, H4884 מְשׂוּרָה, H5448 סֹבֶל, H5688 עֲבֹת, H5923 עֹל, H7070 קָנֶה, H7626 שֵׁבֶט, H7926 שְׁכֶם",
    2219: "ζύμη (zýmē | dzoo'-may)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from G2204<BR><B>Strong's:</B> ferment (as if boiling up)<BR><B>KJV:</B> leaven.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2204<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2220 (leaven), G2219 (leaven), G106 (unleavened)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζύμη<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2557 חָמֵץ, H7603 שְׂאֹר",
    2220: "ζυμόω (zymóō | dzoo-mo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G2219<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to cause to ferment<BR><B>KJV:</B> leaven.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2219<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2220 (leaven), G2219 (leaven), G106 (unleavened)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζυμόω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2556 חָמֵץ",
    2221: "ζωγρέω (zōgréō | dzogue-reh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as G2226 and G64<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to take alive (make a prisoner of war), i.e. (figuratively) to capture or ensnare<BR><B>KJV:</B> take captive, catch.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2226<BR><I>See:</I> G64<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2220 (leaven), G2219 (leaven), G106 (unleavened)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζωγρέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2421 חָיָה",
    2222: "ζωή (zōḗ | dzo-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G2198<BR><B>Strong's:</B> life (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> life(-time). Compare G5590 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2198<BR><I>See:</I> G5590<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζωή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1870 דֶּרֶךְ, H1935 הֹוד, H2247 חָבָה, H2416 חַי, H2421 חָיָה, H2451 חׇכְמָה, H2617 חֵסֵד, H3117 יֹום, H3899 לֶחֶם, H4997 נֹאד",
    2223: "ζώνη (zṓnē | dzo'-nay)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably akin to the base of G2218<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a belt; by implication, a pocket<BR><B>KJV:</B> girdle, purse.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2218<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2224 (gird), G2223 (girdle), G1241 (gird), G4024 (gird)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζώνη<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H73 אַבְנֵט, H232 אֵזֹור, H240 אָזֵן, H2290 חֲגֹור, H2290 חֲגֹור, H4206 מָזִיחַ, H7083 קֶסֶת",
    2224: "ζώννυμι (zṓnnymi | dzone'-noo-mi)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G2223<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to bind about (especially with a belt)<BR><B>KJV:</B> gird.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2223<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2224 (gird), G2223 (girdle), G1241 (gird), G4024 (gird)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζώννυμι, ζωννύω, ζώννυμι/ζωννύω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H247 אָזַר, H631 אָסַר, H2280 חָבַשׁ, H2296 חָגַר, H7760 שׂוּם",
    2225: "ζωογονέω (zōogonéō | dzo-og-on-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as G2226 and a derivative of G1096<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to engender alive, i.e. (by analogy) to rescue (passively, be saved) from death<BR><B>KJV:</B> live, preserve.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2226<BR><I>See:</I> G1096<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζωογονέω, ζῳογονέω, ζώογονέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2416 חַי, H2421 חָיָה",
    2226: "ζῶον (zōon | dzo'-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a derivative of G2198<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a live thing, i.e. an animal<BR><B>KJV:</B> beast.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2198<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζῶον, ζῷον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2416 חַי",
    2227: "ζωοποιέω (zōopoiéō | dzo-op-oy-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as G2226 and G4160<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to (re-)vitalize (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> make alive, give life, quicken.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2226<BR><I>See:</I> G4160<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ζωοποιέω, ζῳοποιέω, ζώοποιέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2421 חָיָה",
    2228: "ἤ (ḗ | ay)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary particle of distinction between two connected terms<BR><B>Strong's:</B> disjunctive, or; comparative, than<BR><B>KJV:</B> and, but (either), (n-)either, except it be, (n-)or (else), rather, save, than, that, what, yea. Often used in connection with other particles. Compare especially G2235, G2260, G2273 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2235<BR><I>See:</I> G2260<BR><I>See:</I> G2273<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἤ",
    2229: "ἦ (ē | ay)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> an adverb of confirmation; perhaps intensive of G2228 ; used only (in the New Testament) before G3303<BR><B>Strong's:</B> assuredly<BR><B>KJV:</B> surely.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2228<BR><I>See:</I> G3303<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἦ, εἰ μήν, ἦ μήν G1623, G1638, G2446, G2447",
    2230: "ἡγεμονεύω (hēgemoneúō | hayg-em-on-yoo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G2232<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to act as ruler<BR><B>KJV:</B> be governor.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2232<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἡγεμονεύω",
    2231: "ἡγεμονία (hēgemonía | hayg-em-on-ee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G2232<BR><B>Strong's:</B> government, i.e. (in time) official term<BR><B>KJV:</B> reign.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2232<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἡγεμονία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H441 אַלּוּף, H1714 דֶּגֶל",
    2232: "ἡγεμών (hēgemṓn | hayg-em-ohn')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G2233<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a leader, i.e. chief person (or figuratively, place) of a province<BR><B>KJV:</B> governor, prince, ruler.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2233<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2225 (live), G1186 (tree), G2226 (beast), G2222 (life), G326 (live again), G2227 (make alive), G2198 (life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἡγεμών<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H410 אֵל, H441 אַלּוּף, H6346 פֶּחָה, H7277 רִגְמָה, H8269 שַׂר",
    2233: "ἡγέομαι (hēgéomai | hayg-eh'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> middle voice of a (presumed) strengthened form of G71<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to lead, i.e. command (with official authority); figuratively, to deem, i.e. consider<BR><B>KJV:</B> account, (be) chief, count, esteem, governor, judge, have the rule over, suppose, think.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G71<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4285 (prefer), G2233 (account), G1834 (declare), G1335 (declaration)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἡγέομαι, ἐπιτροπεύω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H136 אֲדֹנָי, H148 אֲדַרְגָּזֵר, H191 אֱוִיל, H376 אִישׁ, H410 אֵל, H441 אַלּוּף, H802 אִשָּׁה, H1167 בַּעַל, H1172 בַּעֲלָה, H1377 גְּבִירָה, H1696 דָבַר, H1980 הָלַךְ, H2015 הָפַךְ, H2710 חָקַק, H2803 חָשַׁב, H3384 יָרָה, H3988 מָאַס, H4428 מֶלֶךְ, H4606 מֵעָל, H4911 מָשַׁל, H5057 נָגִיד, H5139 נָזִיר, H5162 נָחַם, H5333 נְצִיב, H5387 נָשִׂיא, H5461 סָגָן, H5971 עַם, H6040 עֳנִי, H6346 פֶּחָה, H7101 קָצִין, H7218 רֹאשׁ, H7704 שָׂדֶה, H7760 שׂוּם, H8269 שַׂר, H8308 שָׂרַךְ",
    2234: "ἡδέως (hēdéōs | hay-deh'-oce)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from a derivative of the base of G2237<BR><B>Strong's:</B> sweetly, i.e. (figuratively) with pleasure<BR><B>KJV:</B> gladly.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2237<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4285 (prefer), G2233 (account), G1834 (declare), G1335 (declaration)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἡδέως<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2896 טֹוב, H5276 נָעֵם, H6148 עָרַב",
    2235: "ἤδη (ḗdē | ay'-day)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently from G2228 (or possibly G2229) and G1211<BR><B>Strong's:</B> even now<BR><B>KJV:</B> already, (even) now (already), by this time.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2228<BR><I>See:</I> G2229<BR><I>See:</I> G1211<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4285 (prefer), G2233 (account), G1834 (declare), G1335 (declaration)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἤδη",
    2236: "ἥδιστα (hḗdista | hay'-dis-tah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter plural of the superlative of the same as G2234<BR><B>Strong's:</B> with great pleasure<BR><B>KJV:</B> most (very) gladly.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2234<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4285 (prefer), G2233 (account), G1834 (declare), G1335 (declaration)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἥδιστα, ἡδέως",
    2237: "ἡδονή (hēdonḗ | hay-don-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from ἁνδάνω (to please)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> sensual delight; by implication, desire<BR><B>KJV:</B> lust, pleasure.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5369 (lover of pleasure), G2237 (lust)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἡδονή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2940 טַעַם, H7879 שִׂיחַ",
    2238: "ἡδύοσμον (hēdýosmon | hay-doo'-os-mon)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of the compound of the same as G2234 and G3744<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a sweet-scented plant, i.e. mint<BR><B>KJV:</B> mint.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2234<BR><I>See:</I> G3744<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5369 (lover of pleasure), G2237 (lust)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἡδύοσμον",
    2239: "ἦθος (ēthos | ay'-thos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a strengthened form of G1485<BR><B>Strong's:</B> usage, i.e. (plural) moral habits<BR><B>KJV:</B> manners.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G1485<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5369 (lover of pleasure), G2237 (lust)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ἦθος, ὴθος",
