    2982: "λαμά (lamá | lam-ah') or λαμμᾶ (lammâ | lam-mah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (H4100 with prepositional prefix)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> lama (i.e. why)<BR><B>KJV:</B> lama.<BR><I>See:</I> H4100<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2636 (backbiting), G2637 (backbiter), G2980 (preach), G2635 (speak against)<BR><B>Variants:</B> λαμά, λεμά, λιμά<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4100 מָה",
    2983: "λαμβάνω (lambánō | lam-ban'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a prolonged form of a primary verb, which is use only as an alternate in certain tenses; to take (in very many applications, literally and figuratively (properly objective or active, to get hold of; whereas G1209 is rather subjective or passive, to have offered to one<BR><B>Strong's:</B> while G138 is more violent, to seize or remove))<BR><B>KJV:</B> accept, + be amazed, assay, attain, bring, X when I call, catch, come on (X unto), + forget, have, hold, obtain, receive (X after), take (away, up).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G1209<BR><I>See:</I> G138<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)<BR><B>Variants:</B> λαμβάνω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H270 אָחַז, H781 אָרַשׂ, H935 בֹּוא, H954 בּוּשׁ, H1887 הֵא, H2029 הָרָה, H2151 זָלַל, H2342 חוּל, H2388 חָזַק, H2505 חָלַק, H2730 חָרֵד, H3318 יָצָא, H3423 יָרַשׁ, H3427 יָשַׁב, H3920 לָכַד, H3947 לָקַח, H4351 מְכוּרָה, H4390 מָלֵא, H4672 מָצָא, H5221 נָכָה, H5254 נָסָה, H5307 נָפַל, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5381 נָשַׂג, H5493 סוּר, H5710 עָדָה, H5927 עָלָה, H6329 פּוּק, H6696 צוּר, H6902 קְבַל, H6965 קוּם, H7121 קָרָא, H7126 קָרַב, H7737 שָׁוָה, H7760 שׂוּם, H8610 תָּפַשׂ",
    2984: "Λάμεχ (Lámech | lam'-ekh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (H3929)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Lamech (i.e. Lemek), a patriarch<BR><B>KJV:</B> Lamech.<BR><I>See:</I> H3929<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Λάμεχ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3929 לֶמֶךְ",
