    2992: "λαός (laós | lah-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a people (in general; thus differing from G1218, which denotes one's own populace)<BR><B>KJV:</B> people.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G1218<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2992 (people)<BR><B>Variants:</B> λαός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H120 אָדָם, H524 אֻמָּה, H582 אֱנֹושׁ, H1004 בַּיִת, H1121 בֵּן, H1471 גֹּוי, H1995 הָמֹון, H2213 זֵר, H2945 טַף, H3816 לְאֹם, H4264 מַחֲנֶה, H4725 מָקֹום, H4940 מִשְׁפָּחָה, H5650 עֶבֶד, H5971 עַם, H6629 צֹאן, H6951 קָהָל",
    2993: "Λαοδίκεια (Laodíkeia | lah-od-ik'-i-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a compound of G2992 and G1349<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Laodicia, a place in Asia Minor<BR><B>KJV:</B> Laodicea.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2992<BR><I>See:</I> G1349<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2993 (Laodicea), G2994 (Laodicean)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Λαοδίκεια, Λαοδικεία",
    2994: "Λαοδικεύς (Laodikeús | lah-od-ik-yooce')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G2993<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Laodicean, i.e. inhabitant of Laodicia<BR><B>KJV:</B> Laodicean.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2993<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2993 (Laodicea), G2994 (Laodicean)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Λαοδικεύς",
    2995: "λάρυγξ (lárynx | lar'-oongks)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the throat (\"larynx\")<BR><B>KJV:</B> throat.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2995 (throat)<BR><B>Variants:</B> λάρυγξ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1627 גָּרֹון, H2441 חֵךְ, H4455 מַלְקֹוחַ",
    2996: "Λασαία (Lasaía | las-ah'-yah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Lasæa, a place in Crete<BR><B>KJV:</B> Lasea.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2995 (throat)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Λασαία, Λασέα, Λασαία/Λασέα",
    2997: "λάσχω (láschō | las'-kho)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a strengthened form of a primary verb, which only occurs in this and another prolonged form as alternate in certain tenses<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to crack open (from a fall)<BR><B>KJV:</B> burst asunder.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2997 (burst asunder)<BR><B>Variants:</B> λάσχω, λακάω, λάσκω",
    2998: "λατομέω (latoméō | lat-om-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as the first part of G2991 and the base of G5114<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to quarry<BR><B>KJV:</B> hew.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2991<BR><I>See:</I> G5114<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2998 (hew)<BR><B>Variants:</B> λατομέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2672 חָצַב, H3738 כָּרָה",
    2999: "λατρεία (latreía | lat-ri'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3000<BR><B>Strong's:</B> ministration of God, i.e. worship<BR><B>KJV:</B> (divine) service.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3000<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2999 (service), G3000 (serve)<BR><B>Variants:</B> λατρεία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5656 עֲבֹדָה",
    3000: "λατρεύω (latreúō | lat-ryoo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from λάτρις (a hired menial)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to minister (to God), i.e. render religious homage<BR><B>KJV:</B> serve, do the service, worship(-per).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2999 (service), G3000 (serve)<BR><B>Variants:</B> λατρεύω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H309 אָחַר, H5647 עָבַד, H6399 פְּלַח, H8334 שָׁרַת",
    3001: "λάχανον (láchanon | lakh'-an-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from λαχαίνω (to dig)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a vegetable<BR><B>KJV:</B> herb.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3001 (herb)<BR><B>Variants:</B> λάχανον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3418 יֶרֶק, H3419 יָרָק",
    3002: "Λεββαῖος (Lebbaîos | leb-bah'-yos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Lebbæus, a Christian<BR><B>KJV:</B> Lebbæus.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3001 (herb)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Λεββαῖος G3304",
    3003: "λεγεών (legeṓn | leg-eh-ohn')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a \"legion\", i.e. Roman regiment (figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> legion.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3003 (legion)<BR><B>Variants:</B> λεγεών, λεγιών",
    3004: "λέγω (légō | leg'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to \"lay\" forth, i.e. (figuratively) relate (in words (usually of systematic or set discourse; whereas G2036 and G5346 generally refer to an individual expression or speech respectively; while G4483 is properly to break silence merely, and G2980 means an extended or random harangue)); by implication, to mean<BR><B>KJV:</B> ask, bid, boast, call, describe, give out, name, put forth, say(-ing, on), shew, speak, tell, utter.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2036<BR><I>See:</I> G5346<BR><I>See:</I> G4483<BR><I>See:</I> G2980<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3055 (strife of words), G3052 (eloquent), G3004 (ask), G1588 (chosen), G1586 (make choice), G249 (brute), G3050 (reasonable), G3054 (strive about words), G1589 (chosen), G3056 (account), G2980 (preach), G3051 (oracle)<BR><B>Variants:</B> λέγω, εἴρω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H559 אָמַר, H1326 בָּתָה, H1696 דָבַר, H3576 כָּזַב, H4687 מִצְוָה, H4911 מָשַׁל, H5001 נָאַם, H5002 נְאֻם, H5608 סָפַר",
    3005: "λεῖμμα (leîmma | lime'-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3007<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a remainder<BR><B>KJV:</B> remnant.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3007<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4035 (remain), G2640 (remnant), G2641 (forsake), G3005 (remnant), G1257 (cease)<BR><B>Variants:</B> λεῖμμα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7611 שְׁאֵרִית",
    3006: "λεῖος (leîos | li'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> smooth, i.e. \"level\"<BR><B>KJV:</B> smooth.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3006 (smooth)<BR><B>Variants:</B> λεῖος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1237 בִּקְעָה, H2505 חָלַק, H2512 חַלֻּק",
    3007: "λείπω (leípō | li'-po)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to leave, i.e. (intransitively or passively) to fail or be absent<BR><B>KJV:</B> be destitute (wanting), lack.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3006 (smooth)<BR><B>Variants:</B> λείπω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3869 לוּז, H6504 פָּרַד, H6504 פָּרַד",
