    3303: "μέν (mén | men)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary particle<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, indicative of affirmation or concession (in fact); usually followed by a contrasted clause with G1161 (this one, the former, etc.)<BR><B>KJV:</B> even, indeed, so, some, truly, verily. Often compounded with other particles in an intensive or asseverative sense.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G1161<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G274 (blameless), G3437 (quarrel), G3201 (find fault), G3202 (complainer), G273 (blameless)<BR><B>Variants:</B> μέν",
