    3631: "οἶνος (oînos | oy'-nos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary word (or perhaps of Hebrew origin (H3196))<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"wine\" (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> wine.<BR><I>See:</I> H3196<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3630 (winebibber), G3631 (wine)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οἶνος, οὶνος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2561 חֶמֶר, H3196 יַיִן, H3342 יֶקֶב, H5435 סֹבֶא, H6071 עָסִיס, H7941 שֵׁכָר, H8105 שֶׁמֶר, H8492 תִּירֹושׁ",
