    3649: "ὀλολύζω (ololýzō | ol-ol-odd'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a reduplicated primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to \"howl\" or \"halloo\", i.e. shriek<BR><B>KJV:</B> howl.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3649 (howl)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀλολύζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3213 יָלַל, H6682 צְוָחָה",
    3650: "ὅλος (hólos | hol'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"whole\" or \"all\", i.e. complete (in extent, amount, time or degree), especially (neuter) as noun or adverb<BR><B>KJV:</B> all, altogether, every whit, + throughout, whole.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3650 (all), G3651 (wholly)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὅλος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3605 כֹּל, H8548 תָּמִיד, H8549 תָּמִים",
