    3691: "ὀξύς (oxýs | oz-oos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably akin to the base of G188 (\"acid\")<BR><B>Strong's:</B> keen; by analogy, rapid<BR><B>KJV:</B> sharp, swift.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G188<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3690 (vinegar)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀξύς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2299 חַד, H2789 חֶרֶשׂ, H4106 מָהִיר, H7031 קַל, H7858 שֶׁטֶף, H8150 שָׁנַן",
    3692: "ὀπή (opḗ | op-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from G3700<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a hole (as if for light), i.e. cavern; by analogy, a spring (of water)<BR><B>KJV:</B> cave, place.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3700<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3690 (vinegar)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀπή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H699 אֲרֻבָּה, H2288 חֲגָו, H2356 חֹור, H5366 נְקָרָה, H5595 סָפָה",
    3693: "ὄπισθεν (ópisthen | op'-is-then)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from ὄπις (regard<BR><B>Strong's:</B> from G3700) with enclitic of source; from the rear (as a secure aspect), i.e. at the back (adverb and preposition of place or time)<BR><B>KJV:</B> after, backside, behind.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3700<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3693 (after), G3694 (after)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὄπισθεν<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H268 אָחֹור, H310 אַחַר, H310 אַחַר, H810 אֶשֶׁךְ",
    3694: "ὀπίσω (opísō | op-is'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as G3693 with enclitic of direction<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to the back, i.e. aback (as adverb or preposition of time or place; or as noun)<BR><B>KJV:</B> after, back(-ward), (+ get) behind, + follow.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3693<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3693 (after), G3694 (after)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀπίσω, τοὐπισω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H268 אָחֹור, H309 אָחַר, H310 אַחַר, H310 אַחַר, H410 אֵל, H854 אֵת, H1334 בָּתַר, H5973 עִם, H6040 עֳנִי, H8478 תַּחַת",
    3695: "ὁπλίζω (hoplízō | hop-lid'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3696<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to equip (with weapons (middle voice and figuratively))<BR><B>KJV:</B> arm self.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3696<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3695 (arm self), G3696 (armour), G2528 (arm), G3833 (all armour)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὁπλίζω, ὁπλίζομαι",
    3696: "ὅπλον (hóplon | hop'-lon)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from a primary ἕπω (to be busy about)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an implement or utensil or tool (literally or figuratively, especially, offensive for war)<BR><B>KJV:</B> armour, instrument, weapon.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3695 (arm self), G3696 (armour), G2528 (arm), G3833 (all armour)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὅπλον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2595 חֲנִית, H3627 כְּלִי, H4043 מָגֵן, H5402 נֶשֶׁק, H5630 סִרְיֹן, H6793 צִנָּה, H7973 שֶׁלַח, H7982 שֶׁלֶט",
    3697: "ὁποῖος (hopoîos | hop-oy'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3739 and G4169<BR><B>Strong's:</B> of what kind that, i.e. how (as) great (excellent) (specially, as an indefinite correlative to the definite antecedent G5108 of quality)<BR><B>KJV:</B> what manner (sort) of, such as whatsoever.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3739<BR><I>See:</I> G4169<BR><I>See:</I> G5108<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3695 (arm self), G3696 (armour), G2528 (arm), G3833 (all armour)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὁποῖος",
    3698: "ὁπότε (hopóte | hop-ot'-eh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3739 and G4218<BR><B>Strong's:</B> what(-ever) then, i.e. (of time) as soon as<BR><B>KJV:</B> when.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3739<BR><I>See:</I> G4218<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3695 (arm self), G3696 (armour), G2528 (arm), G3833 (all armour)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὁπότε G3962",
    3699: "ὅπου (hópou | hop'-oo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3739 and G4225<BR><B>Strong's:</B> what(-ever) where, i.e. at whichever spot<BR><B>KJV:</B> in what place, where(-as, -soever), whither (+ soever).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3739<BR><I>See:</I> G4225<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3695 (arm self), G3696 (armour), G2528 (arm), G3833 (all armour)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὅπου",
    3700: "ὀπτάνομαι (optánomai | op-tan'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a (middle voice) prolonged form of the primary (middle voice) ὄπτομαι (óptomai | op'-tom-ahee)<BR>; which is used for it in certain tenses; and both as alternate of G3708<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to gaze (i.e. with wide-open eyes, as at something remarkable; and thus differing from G991, which denotes simply voluntary observation; and from G1492, which expresses merely mechanical, passive or casual vision; while G2300, and still more emphatically its intensive G2334, signifies an earnest but more continued inspection; and G4648 a watching from a distance)<BR><B>KJV:</B> appear, look, see, shew self.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3708<BR><I>See:</I> G991<BR><I>See:</I> G1492<BR><I>See:</I> G2300<BR><I>See:</I> G2334<BR><I>See:</I> G4648<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀπτάνομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3700 כָּסַף",
    3701: "ὀπτασία (optasía | op-tas-ee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a presumed derivative of G3700<BR><B>Strong's:</B> visuality, i.e. (concretely) an apparition<BR><B>KJV:</B> vision.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3700<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀπτασία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4758 מַרְאֶה, H4759 מַרְאָה, H7200 רָאָה",
    3702: "ὀπτός (optós | op-tos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an obsolete verb akin to ἕπσω (to \"steep\")<BR><B>Strong's:</B> cooked, i.e. roasted<BR><B>KJV:</B> broiled.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀπτός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6748 צָלִי",
    3703: "ὀπώρα (opṓra | op-o'-rah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently from the base of G3796 and G5610<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, even-tide of the (summer) season (dog-days), i.e. (by implication) ripe fruit<BR><B>KJV:</B> fruit.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3796<BR><I>See:</I> G5610<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀπώρα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7019 קַיִץ",
    3704: "ὅπως (hópōs | hop'-oce)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3739 and G4459<BR><B>Strong's:</B> what(-ever) how, i.e. in the manner that (as adverb or conjunction of coincidence, intentional or actual)<BR><B>KJV:</B> because, how, (so) that, to, when.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3739<BR><I>See:</I> G4459<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G845 (eye-witness), G2030 (eye-witness), G991 (behold), G2029 (behold), G3701 (vision), G3700 (appear)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὅπως",
    3705: "ὅραμα (hórama | hor'-am-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3708<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something gazed at, i.e. a spectacle (especially supernatural)<BR><B>KJV:</B> sight, vision.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3708<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὅραμα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2377 חָזֹון, H2377 חָזֹון, H2472 חֲלֹום, H4172 מֹורָא, H4758 מַרְאֶה, H4853 מַשָּׂא",
    3706: "ὅρασις (hórasis | hor'-as-is)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3708<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the act of gazing, i.e. (externally) an aspect or (internally) an inspired appearance<BR><B>KJV:</B> sight, vision.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3708<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὅρασις<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2122 זִיו, H2377 חָזֹון, H4707 מִצְפֶּה, H4758 מַרְאֶה, H4853 מַשָּׂא, H5869 עַיִן, H7299 רֵו, H8447 תֹּור",
    3707: "ὁρατός (horatós | hor-at-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3708<BR><B>Strong's:</B> gazed at, i.e. (by implication) capable of being seen<BR><B>KJV:</B> visible.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3708<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὁρατός",
    3708: "ὁράω (horáō | hor-ah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> properly, to stare at (compare G3700), i.e. (by implication) to discern clearly (physically or mentally)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> by extension, to attend to; by Hebraism, to experience; passively, to appear<BR><B>KJV:</B> behold, perceive, see, take heed.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3700<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2300 (behold), G3705 (sight), G517 (invisible), G3707 (visible), G2334 (behold), G3708 (behold), G2529 (clearly see), G4308 (foresee), G3706 (sight)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὁράω, εἶδον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H389 אַךְ, H935 בֹּוא, H2009 הִנֵּה, H2372 חָזָה, H2492 חָלַם, H5239 נָלָה, H6437 פָּנָה, H7200 רָאָה, H7789 שׁוּר, H7931 שָׁכַן",
