    3710: "ὀργίζω (orgízō | or-gid'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3709<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to provoke or enrage, i.e. (passively) become exasperated<BR><B>KJV:</B> be angry (wroth).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3709<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3949 (anger), G3710 (be angry), G3950 (wrath), G3709 (anger), G3711 (soon angry)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀργίζω, ὀργίζομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H639 אַף, H2194 זָעַם, H2196 זָעַף, H2534 חֵמָה, H2734 חָרָה, H4843 מָרַר, H6058 עָנֵף, H6226 עָשֵׁן, H7107 קָצַף, H7264 רָגַז, H7378 רִיב",
    3711: "ὀργίλος (orgílos | org-ee'-los)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3709<BR><B>Strong's:</B> irascible<BR><B>KJV:</B> soon angry.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3709<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3949 (anger), G3710 (be angry), G3950 (wrath), G3709 (anger), G3711 (soon angry)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀργίλος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H639 אַף, H2534 חֵמָה, H3708 כַּעַס",
    3712: "ὀργυιά (orguiá | org-wee-ah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3713<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a stretch of the arms, i.e. a fathom<BR><B>KJV:</B> fathom.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3713<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3949 (anger), G3710 (be angry), G3950 (wrath), G3709 (anger), G3711 (soon angry)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀργυιά, ὀργυιά (ὄργυια)",
    3713: "ὀρέγομαι (orégomai | or-eg'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> middle voice of apparently a prolonged form of an obsolete primary (compare G3735)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to stretch oneself, i.e. reach out after (long for)<BR><B>KJV:</B> covet after, desire.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3735<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3713 (covet after), G3715 (lust)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀρέγομαι, ὀρέγω",
    3714: "ὀρεινός (oreinós | or-i-nos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3735<BR><B>Strong's:</B> mountainous, i.e. (feminine by implication, of G5561) the Highlands (of Judæa)<BR><B>KJV:</B> hill country.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3735<BR><I>See:</I> G5561<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3713 (covet after), G3715 (lust)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀρεινός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2022 הַר, H2022 הַר",
    3715: "ὄρεξις (órexis | or'-ex-is)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3713<BR><B>Strong's:</B> excitement of the mind, i.e. longing after<BR><B>KJV:</B> lust.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3713<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3713 (covet after), G3715 (lust)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὄρεξις",
    3716: "ὀρθοποδέω (orthopodéō | or-thop-od-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a compound of G3717 and G4228<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be straight-footed, i.e. (figuratively) to go directly forward<BR><B>KJV:</B> walk uprightly.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3717<BR><I>See:</I> G4228<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀρθοποδέω",
    3717: "ὀρθός (orthós | or-thos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from the base of G3735<BR><B>Strong's:</B> right (as rising), i.e. (perpendicularly) erect (figuratively, honest), or (horizontally) level or direct<BR><B>KJV:</B> straight, upright.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3735<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀρθός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H995 בִּין, H3476 יֹשֶׁר, H3477 יָשָׁר, H5227 נֹכַח, H6424 פָּלַס, H7054 קָמָה, H7317 רֹומָה",
    3718: "ὀρθοτομέω (orthotoméō | or-thot-om-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a compound of G3717 and the base of G5114, to make a straight cut, i.e. (figuratively) to dissect (expound) correctly (the divine message)<BR><B>KJV:</B> rightly divide.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3717<BR><I>See:</I> G5114<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀρθοτομέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3474 יָשַׁר",
    3719: "ὀρθρίζω (orthrízō | or-thrid'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3722<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to use the dawn, i.e. (by implication) to repair betimes<BR><B>KJV:</B> come early in the morning.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3722<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀρθρίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7836 שָׁחַר, H7925 שָׁכַם",
    3720: "ὀρθρινός (orthrinós | or-thrin-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3722<BR><B>Strong's:</B> relating to the dawn, i.e. matutinal (as an epithet of Venus, especially brilliant in the early day)<BR><B>KJV:</B> morning.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3722<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀρθρινός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7925 שָׁכַם",
    3721: "ὄρθριος (órthrios | or'-three-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3722<BR><B>Strong's:</B> in the dawn, i.e. up at day-break<BR><B>KJV:</B> early.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3722<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὄρθριος G3985",
    3722: "ὄρθρος (órthros | or'-thros)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as G3735<BR><B>Strong's:</B> dawn (as sun-rise, rising of light); by extension, morn<BR><B>KJV:</B> early in the morning.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3735<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὄρθρος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H821 אַשְׁמֻרָה, H1242 בֹּקֶר, H3364 יָקַץ, H7837 שַׁחַר",
    3723: "ὀρθῶς (orthōs | or-thoce')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from G3717<BR><B>Strong's:</B> in a straight manner, i.e. (figuratively) correctly (also morally)<BR><B>KJV:</B> plain, right(-ly).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3717<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3718 (rightly divide), G3723 (plain), G3717 (straight), G3716 (walk uprightly), G3722 (early in the morning), G1882 (correction), G1357 (reformation), G3721 (early), G3720 (morning), G3719 (come early in the morning)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀρθῶς",
    3724: "ὁρίζω (horízō | hor-id'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3725<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to mark out or bound (\"horizon\"), i.e. (figuratively) to appoint, decree, specify<BR><B>KJV:</B> declare, determine, limit, ordain.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3725<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3724 (declare), G4309 (determine before), G592 (separate), G873 (divide)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὁρίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H631 אָסַר, H1362 גָּבָהּ, H1366 גְּבוּל, H6504 פָּרַד, H7169 קָרַץ, H7560 רְשַׁם",
    3725: "ὅριον (hórion | hor'-ee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a derivative of an apparently primary ὅρος (a bound or limit)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a boundary-line, i.e. (by implication) a frontier (region)<BR><B>KJV:</B> border, coast.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3724 (declare), G4309 (determine before), G592 (separate), G873 (divide)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὅριον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H776 אֶרֶץ, H1323 בַּת, H1366 גְּבוּל, H1486 גֹּורָל, H1552 גְלִילָה, H2706 חֹק, H3027 יָד, H4135 מוּל, H6285 פֵּאָה, H7093 קֵץ, H7704 שָׂדֶה",
    3726: "ὁρκίζω (horkízō | hor-kid'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3727<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to put on oath, i.e. make swear; by analogy, to solemnly enjoin<BR><B>KJV:</B> adjure, charge.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3727<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1964 (forswear self), G1844 (adjure), G3728 (oath), G3726 (adjure), G1845 (exorcist), G1965 (perjured person), G3727 (oath)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὁρκίζω, ἐνορκίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7650 שָׁבַע, H7650 שָׁבַע",
    3727: "ὅρκος (hórkos | hor'-kos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from ἕρκος (a fence<BR><B>Strong's:</B> perhaps akin to G3725); a limit, i.e. (sacred) restraint (specially, an oath)<BR><B>KJV:</B> oath.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3725<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1964 (forswear self), G1844 (adjure), G3728 (oath), G3726 (adjure), G1845 (exorcist), G1965 (perjured person), G3727 (oath)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὅρκος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5927 עָלָה, H7655 שִׁבְעָה, H7773 שֶׁוַע",
    3728: "ὁρκωμοσία (horkōmosía | hor-ko-mos-ee'ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a compound of G3727 and a derivative of G3660<BR><B>Strong's:</B> asseveration on oath<BR><B>KJV:</B> oath.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3727<BR><I>See:</I> G3660<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1964 (forswear self), G1844 (adjure), G3728 (oath), G3726 (adjure), G1845 (exorcist), G1965 (perjured person), G3727 (oath)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὁρκωμοσία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5927 עָלָה",
    3729: "ὁρμάω (hormáō | hor-mah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3730<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to start, spur or urge on, i.e. (reflexively) to dash or plunge<BR><B>KJV:</B> run (violently), rush.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3730<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3729 (run), G874 (occasion), G3730 (assault), G3731 (violence)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὁρμάω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2363 חוּשׁ, H5860 עִיט, H6437 פָּנָה, H6584 פָּשַׁט, H7725 שׁוּב, H7760 שׂוּם",
    3730: "ὁρμή (hormḗ | hor-may')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain affinity<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a violent impulse, i.e. onset<BR><B>KJV:</B> assault.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3729 (run), G874 (occasion), G3730 (assault), G3731 (violence)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὁρμή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2534 חֵמָה, H4853 מַשָּׂא, H6388 פֶּלֶג, H7110 קֶצֶף, H7722 שֹׁוא, H8161 שַׁעֲטָה",
    3731: "ὅρμημα (hórmēma | hor'-may-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3730<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an attack, i.e. (abstractly) precipitancy<BR><B>KJV:</B> violence.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3730<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3729 (run), G874 (occasion), G3730 (assault), G3731 (violence)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὅρμημα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1676 דָּאָה, H5678 עֶבְרָה, H6388 פֶּלֶג",
    3732: "ὄρνεον (órneon | or'-neh-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a presumed derivative of G3733<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a birdling<BR><B>KJV:</B> bird, fowl.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3733<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3729 (run), G874 (occasion), G3730 (assault), G3731 (violence)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὄρνεον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5775 עֹוף, H5861 עַיִט, H6833 צִפֹּור, H6893 קָאַת",
    3733: "ὄρνις (órnis | or'-nis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from a prolonged form of the base of G3735<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a bird (as rising in the air), i.e. (specially), a hen (or female domestic fowl)<BR><B>KJV:</B> hen.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3735<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3729 (run), G874 (occasion), G3730 (assault), G3731 (violence)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὄρνις, ὄρινξ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1257 בַּרְבֻּר",
    3734: "ὁροθεσία (horothesía | hor-oth-es-ee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a compound of the base of G3725 and a derivative of G5087<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a limit-placing, i.e. (concretely) boundary-line<BR><B>KJV:</B> bound.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3725<BR><I>See:</I> G5087<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3729 (run), G874 (occasion), G3730 (assault), G3731 (violence)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὁροθεσία",
    3735: "ὄρος (óros | or'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from an obsolete ὄρω (to rise or \"rear\"<BR><B>Strong's:</B> perhaps akin to G142 ; compare G3733); a mountain (as lifting itself above the plain)<BR><B>KJV:</B> hill, mount(-ain).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G142<BR><I>See:</I> G3733<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3735 (hill)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὄρος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1389 גִּבְעָה, H1926 הָדָר, H2022 הַר, H2022 הַר, H2905 טוּר, H4791 מָרֹום, H6697 צוּר, H8205 שְׁפִי",
    3736: "ὀρύσσω (orýssō | or-oos'-so)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to \"burrow\" in the ground, i.e. dig<BR><B>KJV:</B> dig.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3735 (hill)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀρύσσω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1624 גָּרָה, H2658 חָפַר, H2672 חָצַב, H2864 חָתַר, H3738 כָּרָה, H5365 נָקַר, H6605 פָּתַח",
    3737: "ὀρφανός (orphanós | or-fan-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain affinity<BR><B>Strong's:</B> bereaved (\"orphan\"), i.e. parentless<BR><B>KJV:</B> comfortless, fatherless.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3737 (comfortless)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀρφανός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3490 יָתֹום",
    3738: "ὀρχέομαι (orchéomai | or-kheh'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> middle voice from ὄρχος (a row or ring)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to dance (from the ranklike or regular motion)<BR><B>KJV:</B> dance.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3737 (comfortless)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀρχέομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3769 כָּרַר, H6339 פָּזַז, H7540 רָקַד, H7832 שָׂחַק",
    3739: "ὅς (hós | hos), including feminine ἥ (hḗ | hay), and neuter ὅ (hó | ho)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably a primary word (or perhaps a form of the article G3588)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the relatively (sometimes demonstrative) pronoun, who, which, what, that<BR><B>KJV:</B> one, (an-, the) other, some, that, what, which, who(-m, -se), etc. See also G3757 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3588<BR><I>See:</I> G3757<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3737 (comfortless)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὅς, ὅσγε",
    3740: "ὁσάκις (hosákis | hos-ak'-is)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> multiple adverb from G3739<BR><B>Strong's:</B> how (i.e. with G302, so) many times as<BR><B>KJV:</B> as oft(-en) as.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3739<BR><I>See:</I> G302<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3737 (comfortless)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὁσάκις",
    3741: "ὅσιος (hósios | hos'-ee-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain affinity; properly, right (by intrinsic or divine character; thus distinguished from 1342, which refers rather to human statutes and relations; from G2413, which denotes formal consecration<BR><B>Strong's:</B> and from G40, which relates to purity from defilement), i.e. hallowed (pious, sacred, sure)<BR><B>KJV:</B> holy, mercy, shalt be. 342<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2413<BR><I>See:</I> G40<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3741 (holy), G462 (unholy), G3743 (holily), G3742 (holiness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὅσιος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2134 זַךְ, H2616 חָסַד, H2617 חֵסֵד, H2623 חָסִיד, H2889 טָהֹור, H3477 יָשָׁר, H4720 מִקְדָּשׁ, H7965 שָׁלֹום, H8537 תֹּם, H8549 תָּמִים",
    3742: "ὁσιότης (hosiótēs | hos-ee-ot'-ace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3741<BR><B>Strong's:</B> piety<BR><B>KJV:</B> holiness.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3741<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3741 (holy), G462 (unholy), G3743 (holily), G3742 (holiness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὁσιότης<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3476 יֹשֶׁר, H8537 תֹּם, H8549 תָּמִים",
    3743: "ὁσίως (hosíōs | hos-ee-oce')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from G3741<BR><B>Strong's:</B> piously<BR><B>KJV:</B> holily.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3741<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3741 (holy), G462 (unholy), G3743 (holily), G3742 (holiness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὁσίως",
    3744: "ὀσμή (osmḗ | os-may')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3605<BR><B>Strong's:</B> fragrance (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> odour, savour.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3605<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3744 (odour)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀσμή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H887 בָּאַשׁ, H1314 בֶּשֶׂם, H7381 רֵיחַ",
    3745: "ὅσος (hósos | hos'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> by reduplication from G3739<BR><B>Strong's:</B> as (much, great, long, etc.) as<BR><B>KJV:</B> all (that), as (long, many, much) (as), how great (many, much), (in-)asmuch as, so many as, that (ever), the more, those things, what (great, -soever), wheresoever, wherewithsoever, which, X while, who(-soever).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3739<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3744 (odour)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὅσος",
    3746: "ὅσπερ (hósper | hos'-per)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3739 and G4007<BR><B>Strong's:</B> who especially<BR><B>KJV:</B> whomsoever.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3739<BR><I>See:</I> G4007<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3744 (odour)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὅσπερ G4013",
    3747: "ὀστέον (ostéon | os-teh'-on), or contracted ὀστοῦν (ostoûn | os-toon')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain affinity<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a bone<BR><B>KJV:</B> bone.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3744 (odour)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀστέον, ὀστοῦν<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1634 גֶּרֶם, H6106 עֶצֶם",
    3748: "ὅστις (hóstis | hos'-tis), including the feminine ἥτις (hḗtis | hay'-tis), and the neuter ὅτι (hóti | hot'-ee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3739 and G5100<BR><B>Strong's:</B> which some, i.e. any that; also (definite) which same<BR><B>KJV:</B> X and (they), (such) as, (they) that, in that they, what(-soever), whereas ye, (they) which, who(-soever). Compare G3754 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3739<BR><I>See:</I> G5100<BR><I>See:</I> G3754<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3744 (odour)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὅστις",
    3749: "ὀστράκινος (ostrákinos | os-tra'-kin-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from ὄστρακον (\"oyster\") (a tile, i.e. terra cotta)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> earthen-ware, i.e. clayey; by implication, frail<BR><B>KJV:</B> of earth, earthen.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3744 (odour)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀστράκινος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2635 חֲסַף, H2789 חֶרֶשׂ",
    3750: "ὄσφρησις (ósphrēsis | os'-fray-sis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of G3605<BR><B>Strong's:</B> smell (the sense)<BR><B>KJV:</B> smelling.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3605<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3744 (odour)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὄσφρησις",
    3751: "ὀσφῦς (osphŷs | os-foos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain affinity<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the loin (externally), i.e. the hip; internally (by extension) procreative power<BR><B>KJV:</B> loin.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀσφῦς, ὀσφύς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H451 אַלְיָה, H1975 הַלָּז, H2502 חָלַץ, H2783 חֲרַץ",
    3752: "ὅταν (hótan | hot'-an)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3753 and G302<BR><B>Strong's:</B> whenever (implying hypothesis or more or less uncertainty); also causatively (conjunctionally) inasmuch as<BR><B>KJV:</B> as long (soon) as, that, + till, when(-soever), while.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3753<BR><I>See:</I> G302<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὅταν",
    3753: "ὅτε (hóte | hot'-eh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3739 and G5037<BR><B>Strong's:</B> at which (thing) too, i.e. when<BR><B>KJV:</B> after (that), as soon as, that, when, while.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3739<BR><I>See:</I> G5037<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὅτε",
    3754: "ὅτι (hóti | hot'-ee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of G3748 as conjunction<BR><B>Strong's:</B> demonstrative, that (sometimes redundant); causative, because<BR><B>KJV:</B> as concerning that, as though, because (that), for (that), how (that), (in) that, though, why.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3748<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὅτι",
    3755: "ὅτου (hótou | hot'-oo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> for the genitive case of G3748 (as adverb)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> during which same time, i.e. whilst<BR><B>KJV:</B> whiles.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3748<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὅτου, ὅστις",
    3756: "οὐ (ou | oo), also (before a vowel) οὐκ (ouk | ook), and (before an aspirate) οὐχ (ouch | ookh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the absolute negative (compare G3361) adverb; no or not<BR><B>KJV:</B> + long, nay, neither, never, no (X man), none, (can-)not, + nothing, + special, un(-worthy), when, + without, + yet but. See also G3364, G3372 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3361<BR><I>See:</I> G3364<BR><I>See:</I> G3372<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὐ, οὐ/οὐκ/οὐχ, οὔ",
    3757: "οὗ (hoû | hoo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> genitive case of G3739 as adverb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> at which place, i.e. where<BR><B>KJV:</B> where(-in), whither(-soever).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3739<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὗ",
    3758: "οὐά (ouá | oo-ah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary exclamation of surprise<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"ah\"<BR><B>KJV:</B> ah.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὐά",
    3759: "οὐαί (ouaí | oo-ah'-ee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary exclamation of grief<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"woe\"<BR><B>KJV:</B> alas, woe.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὐαί<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H330 אֵטוּן, H1930 הֹו, H1945 הֹוי",
    3760: "οὐδαμῶς (oudamōs | oo-dam-oce')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from (the feminine) of G3762<BR><B>Strong's:</B> by no means<BR><B>KJV:</B> not.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3762<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὐδαμῶς",
    3761: "οὐδέ (oudé | oo-deh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3756 and G1161<BR><B>Strong's:</B> not however, i.e. neither, nor, not even<BR><B>KJV:</B> neither (indeed), never, no (more, nor, not), nor (yet), (also, even, then) not (even, so much as), + nothing, so much as.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3756<BR><I>See:</I> G1161<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὐδέ",
    3762: "οὐδείς (oudeís | oo-dice'), including feminine οὐδεμία (oudemía | oo-dem-ee'-ah), and neuter οὐδέν (oudén | oo-den')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3761 and G1520<BR><B>Strong's:</B> not even one (man, woman or thing), i.e. none, nobody, nothing<BR><B>KJV:</B> any (man), aught, man, neither any (thing), never (man), no (man), none (+ of these things), not (any, at all, -thing), nought.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3761<BR><I>See:</I> G1520<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὐδείς, οὐθείς, οὐδείς/οὐθενός",
    3763: "οὐδέποτε (oudépote | oo-dep'-ot-eh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3761 and G4218<BR><B>Strong's:</B> not even at any time, i.e. never at all<BR><B>KJV:</B> neither at any time, never, nothing at any time.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3761<BR><I>See:</I> G4218<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὐδέποτε<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3808 לֹא",
    3764: "οὐδέπω (oudépō | oo-dep'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3761 and G4452<BR><B>Strong's:</B> not even yet<BR><B>KJV:</B> as yet not, never before (yet), (not) yet.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3761<BR><I>See:</I> G4452<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὐδέπω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2962 טֶרֶם",
    3765: "οὐκέτι (oukéti | ook-et'-ee), also (separately) οὐκ ἔτι (ouk éti | ook et'-ee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3756 and G2089<BR><B>Strong's:</B> not yet, no longer<BR><B>KJV:</B> after that (not), (not) any more, henceforth (hereafter) not, no longer (more), not as yet (now), now no more (not), yet (not).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3756<BR><I>See:</I> G2089<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὐκέτι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H657 אֶפֶס, H3254 יָסַף, H3807 כָּתַת, H3808 לֹא, H5750 עֹוד, H5869 עַיִן",
    3766: "οὐκοῦν (oukoûn | ook-oon')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3756 and G3767<BR><B>Strong's:</B> is it not therefore that, i.e. (affirmatively) hence or so<BR><B>KJV:</B> then.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3756<BR><I>See:</I> G3767<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὐκοῦν",
    3767: "οὖν (oûn | oon)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> (adverbially) certainly, or (conjunctionally) accordingly<BR><B>KJV:</B> and (so, truly), but, now (then), so (likewise then), then, therefore, verily, wherefore.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὖν",
    3768: "οὔπω (oúpō | oo'-po)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3756 and G4452<BR><B>Strong's:</B> not yet<BR><B>KJV:</B> hitherto not, (no…) as yet, not yet.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3756<BR><I>See:</I> G4452<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὔπω",
    3769: "οὐρά (ourá | oo-rah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a tail<BR><B>KJV:</B> tail.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3751 (loin)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὐρά<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2180 זָנָב",
    3770: "οὐράνιος (ouránios | oo-ran'-ee-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3772<BR><B>Strong's:</B> celestial, i.e. belonging to or coming from the sky<BR><B>KJV:</B> heavenly.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3772<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2032 (celestial), G3771 (from heaven), G3772 (air), G3770 (heavenly)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὐράνιος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H8064 שָׁמַיִם",
    3771: "οὐρανόθεν (ouranóthen | oo-ran-oth'-en)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3772 and the enclitic of source<BR><B>Strong's:</B> from the sky<BR><B>KJV:</B> from heaven.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3772<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2032 (celestial), G3771 (from heaven), G3772 (air), G3770 (heavenly)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὐρανόθεν",
    3772: "οὐρανός (ouranós | oo-ran-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> perhaps from the same as G3735 (through the idea of elevation)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the sky; by extension, heaven (as the abode of God); by implication, happiness, power, eternity; specially, the Gospel (Christianity)<BR><B>KJV:</B> air, heaven(-ly), sky.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3735<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2032 (celestial), G3771 (from heaven), G3772 (air), G3770 (heavenly)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὐρανός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H410 אֵל, H776 אֶרֶץ, H4791 מָרֹום, H7549 רָקִיעַ, H7834 שַׁחַק, H8064 שָׁמַיִם",
    3773: "Οὐρβανός (Ourbanós | oor-ban-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Urbanus (of the city, \"urbane\"), a Christian<BR><B>KJV:</B> Urbanus.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2032 (celestial), G3771 (from heaven), G3772 (air), G3770 (heavenly)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Οὐρβανός",
    3774: "Οὐρίας (Ourías | oo-ree'-as)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (H223)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Urias (i.e. Urijah), a Hittite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Urias.<BR><I>See:</I> H223<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3774 (Urias)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Οὐρίας<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H223 אוּרִיָּה",
    3775: "οὖς (oûs | ooce)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the ear (physically or mentally)<BR><B>KJV:</B> ear.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3775 (ear), G5621 (ear), G1801 (hearken)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὖς, οὺς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H241 אֹזֶן, H410 אֵל, H5048 נֶגֶד",
    3776: "οὐσία (ousía | oo-see'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the feminine of G5607<BR><B>Strong's:</B> substance, i.e. property (possessions)<BR><B>KJV:</B> goods, substance.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5607<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3775 (ear), G5621 (ear), G1801 (hearken)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὐσία",
    3777: "οὔτε (oúte | oo'-teh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3756 and G5037<BR><B>Strong's:</B> not too, i.e. neither or nor; by analogy, not even<BR><B>KJV:</B> neither, none, nor (yet), (no, yet) not, nothing.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3756<BR><I>See:</I> G5037<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3775 (ear), G5621 (ear), G1801 (hearken)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὔτε",
    3778: "οὗτος (hoûtos | hoo'-tos), including nominative masculine plural οὗτοι (hoûtoi | hoo'-toy), nominative feminine singular αὕτη (haútē | how'-tay), and nominative feminine plural αὕται (haútai | how'-tahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the article G3588 and G846<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the he (she or it), i.e. this or that (often with article repeated)<BR><B>KJV:</B> he (it was that), hereof, it, she, such as, the same, these, they, this (man, same, woman), which, who.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G846<BR><I>See:</I> G3588<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3775 (ear), G5621 (ear), G1801 (hearken)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὗτος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H389 אַךְ, H403 אָכֵן, H403 אָכֵן, H834 אֲשֶׁר, H2063 זֹאת, H2088 זֶה, H3541 כֹּה, H3588 כִּי, H3602 כָּכָה, H3653 כֵּן, H3660 כְּנֵמָא, H5794 עַז",
    3779: "οὕτω (hoútō | hoo'-to), or (before a vowel οὕτως (hoútōs | hoo'-toce)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from G3778<BR><B>Strong's:</B> in this way (referring to what precedes or follows)<BR><B>KJV:</B> after that, after (in) this manner, as, even (so), for all that, like(-wise), no more, on this fashion(-wise), so (in like manner), thus, what.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3778<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3775 (ear), G5621 (ear), G1801 (hearken)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὕτω, οὕτως, οὕτω(ς), οὕτω/οὕτως<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3653 כֵּן",
    3780: "οὐχί (ouchí | oo-khee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> intensive of G3756<BR><B>Strong's:</B> not indeed<BR><B>KJV:</B> nay, not.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3756<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3775 (ear), G5621 (ear), G1801 (hearken)<BR><B>Variants:</B> οὐχί",
    3781: "ὀφειλέτης (opheilétēs | of-i-let'-ace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3784<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an ower, i.e. person indebted; figuratively, a delinquent; morally, a transgressor (against God)<BR><B>KJV:</B> debtor, which owed, sinner.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3784<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3782 (debt), G3781 (debtor), G3783 (debt), G3784 (behove)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀφειλέτης",
    3782: "ὀφειλή (opheilḗ | of-i-lay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3784<BR><B>Strong's:</B> indebtedness, i.e. (concretely) a sum owed; figuratively, obligation, i.e. (conjugal) duty<BR><B>KJV:</B> debt, due.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3784<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3782 (debt), G3781 (debtor), G3783 (debt), G3784 (behove)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀφειλή",
    3783: "ὀφείλημα (opheílēma | of-i'-lay-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from (the alternate of) G3784<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something owed, i.e. (figuratively) a due; morally, a fault<BR><B>KJV:</B> debt.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3784<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3782 (debt), G3781 (debtor), G3783 (debt), G3784 (behove)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀφείλημα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4859 מַשָּׁאָה, H5382 נָשָׁה",
    3784: "ὀφείλω (opheílō | of-i'-lo), or (in certain tenses), its prolonged form ὀφειλέω (opheiléō | of-i-leh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from the base of G3786 (through the idea of accruing)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to owe (pecuniarily); figuratively, to be under obligation (ought, must, should); morally, to fail in duty<BR><B>KJV:</B> behove, be bound, (be) debt(-or), (be) due(-ty), be guilty (indebted), (must) need(-s), ought, owe, should. See also G3785 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3786<BR><I>See:</I> G3785<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3782 (debt), G3781 (debtor), G3783 (debt), G3784 (behove)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀφείλω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H305 אַחֲלַי, H954 בּוּשׁ, H2243 חֹב, H3863 לוּא, H4310 מִי, H4310 מִי, H5377 נָשָׁא, H5382 נָשָׁה",
    3785: "ὄφελον (óphelon | of'-el-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> first person singular of a past tense of G3784<BR><B>Strong's:</B> I ought (wish), i.e. (interjection) oh that!<BR><B>KJV:</B> would (to God).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3784<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3782 (debt), G3781 (debtor), G3783 (debt), G3784 (behove)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὄφελον",
    3786: "ὄφελος (óphelos | of'-el-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from ὀφέλλω (to heap up, i.e. accumulate or benefit)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> gain<BR><B>KJV:</B> advantageth, profit.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3782 (debt), G3781 (debtor), G3783 (debt), G3784 (behove)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὄφελος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2974 יָאַל",
    3787: "ὀφθαλμοδουλεία (ophthalmodouleía | of-thal-mod-oo-li'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3788 and G1397<BR><B>Strong's:</B> sight-labor, i.e. that needs watching (remissness)<BR><B>KJV:</B> eye-service.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3788<BR><I>See:</I> G1397<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1399 (handmaid), G4889 (fellowservant), G1402 (bring into bondage), G1397 (bondage), G1396 (bring into subjection), G1401 (bond), G2615 (bring into bondage), G3787 (eye-service), G1398 (be in bondage)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀφθαλμοδουλεία, ὀφθαλμοδουλία",
    3788: "ὀφθαλμός (ophthalmós | of-thal-mos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3700<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the eye (literally or figuratively); by implication, vision; figuratively, envy (from the jealous side-glance)<BR><B>KJV:</B> eye, sight.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3700<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3787 (eye-service), G3788 (eye)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀφθαλμός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H308 אֲחַסְבַּי, H4758 מַרְאֶה, H5869 עַיִן, H6079 עַפְעַף, H6440 פָּנִים",
    3789: "ὄφις (óphis | of'-is)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from G3700 (through the idea of sharpness of vision)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a snake, figuratively, (as a type of sly cunning) an artful malicious person, especially Satan<BR><B>KJV:</B> serpent.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3700<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3789 (serpent)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὄφις<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H660 אֶפְעֶה, H5175 נָחָשׁ, H8314 שָׂרָף",
    3790: "ὀφρῦς (ophrŷs | of-roos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> perhaps from G3700 (through the idea of the shading or proximity to the organ of vision)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the eye-\"brow\" or forehead, i.e. (figuratively) the brink of a precipice<BR><B>KJV:</B> brow.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3700<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3789 (serpent)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀφρῦς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1354 גַב",
    3791: "ὀχλέω (ochléō | okh-leh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3793<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to mob, i.e. (by implication) to harass<BR><B>KJV:</B> vex.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3793<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3789 (serpent)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀχλέω, ὀχλέομαι",
    3792: "ὀχλοποιέω (ochlopoiéō | okh-lop-oy-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3793 and G4160<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to make a crowd, i.e. raise a public disturbance<BR><B>KJV:</B> gather a company.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3793<BR><I>See:</I> G4160<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3792 (gather a company), G3793 (company)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀχλοποιέω",
    3793: "ὄχλος (óchlos | okh'los)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of G2192 (meaning a vehicle)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a throng (as borne along); by implication, the rabble; by extension, a class of people; figuratively, a riot<BR><B>KJV:</B> company, multitude, number (of people), people, press.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2192<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3792 (gather a company), G3793 (company)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὄχλος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H622 אָסַף, H1995 הָמֹון, H2428 חַיִל, H2945 טַף, H5971 עַם, H6951 קָהָל, H7235 רָבָה",
    3794: "ὀχύρωμα (ochýrōma | okh-oo'-ro-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a remote derivative of G2192 (meaning to fortify, through the idea of holding safely)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a castle (figuratively, argument)<BR><B>KJV:</B> stronghold.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2192<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3794 (stronghold)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀχύρωμα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H953 בֹּור, H1004 בַּיִת, H1219 בָּצַר, H1964 הֵיכָל, H4013 מִבְצָר, H4525 מַסְגֵּר, H4639 מַעֲשֶׂה, H4679 מְצַד, H4692 מָצֹור, H5797 עֹז, H6877 צְרִיחַ",
    3795: "ὀψάριον (opsárion | op-sar'-ee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a presumed derivative of the base of G3702<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a relish to other food (as if cooked sauce), i.e. (specially), fish (presumably salted and dried as a condiment)<BR><B>KJV:</B> fish.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3702<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3794 (stronghold)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀψάριον",
    3796: "ὀψέ (opsé | op-seh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as G3694 (through the idea of backwardness)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> (adverbially) late in the day; by extension, after the close of the day<BR><B>KJV:</B> (at) even, in the end.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3694<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3794 (stronghold)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀψέ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1121 בֵּן, H5399 נֶשֶׁף, H6153 עֶרֶב",
    3797: "ὄψιμος (ópsimos | op'-sim-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3796<BR><B>Strong's:</B> later, i.e. vernal (showering)<BR><B>KJV:</B> latter.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3796<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3794 (stronghold)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὄψιμος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H648 אָפִיל, H4456 מַלְקֹושׁ",
    3798: "ὄψιος (ópsios | op'-see-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3796<BR><B>Strong's:</B> late; feminine (as noun) afternoon (early eve) or nightfall (later eve)<BR><B>KJV:</B> even(-ing, (-tide)).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3796<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3794 (stronghold)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὄψιος, ὀψία",
    3799: "ὄψις (ópsis | op'-sis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3700<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, sight (the act), i.e. (by implication) the visage, an external show<BR><B>KJV:</B> appearance, countenance, face.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3700<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3794 (stronghold)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὄψις<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2122 זִיו, H4696 מֵצַח, H4758 מַרְאֶה, H5869 עַיִן, H6285 פֵּאָה, H6754 צֶלֶם, H7613 שְׂאֵת, H8389 תֹּאַר",
    3800: "ὀψώνιον (opsṓnion | op-so'-nee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a presumed derivative of the same as G3795<BR><B>Strong's:</B> rations for a soldier, i.e. (by extension) his stipend or pay<BR><B>KJV:</B>  wages.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3795<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3800 (wages)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὀψώνιον",
    3801: "ὁ ὢν καί ὁ ἦν καί ὁ ἐρχόμενος (ho ṑn kaí ho ēn kaí ho erchómenos | ho own kahee ho ane kahee ho er-khom'-en-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a phrase combining G3588 with the present participle and imperfect of G1510 and the present participle of G2064 by means of G2532<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the one being and the one that was and the one coming, i.e. the Eternal, as a divine epithet of Christ<BR><B>KJV:</B> which art (is, was), and (which) wast (is, was), and art (is) to come (shalt be).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G1510<BR><I>See:</I> G2532<BR><I>See:</I> G3588<BR><I>See:</I> G2064<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3800 (wages)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὁ ὢν καί ὁ ἦν καί ὁ ἐρχόμενος, ὁ, εἰμί, καί, ἔρχομαι",
    3802: "παγιδεύω (pagideúō | pag-id-yoo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3803<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to ensnare (figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> entangle.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3803<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3803 (snare), G3802 (entangle)<BR><B>Variants:</B> παγιδεύω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3369 יָקֹשׁ, H5367 נָקַשׁ",
    3803: "παγίς (pagís | pag-ece')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4078<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a trap (as fastened by a noose or notch); figuratively, a trick or statagem (temptation)<BR><B>KJV:</B> snare.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4078<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3803 (snare), G3802 (entangle)<BR><B>Variants:</B> παγίς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3369 יָקֹשׁ, H3619 כְּלוּב, H4170 מֹוקֵשׁ, H4170 מֹוקֵשׁ, H4686 מָצוּד, H6341 פַּח, H7568 רֶשֶׁת, H7722 שֹׁוא",
