    3830: "πανδοχεύς (pandocheús | pan-dokh-yoos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as G3829<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an innkeeper (warden of a caravanserai)<BR><B>KJV:</B> host.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3829<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1085 (born), G1078 (generation), G3824 (regeneration), G1096 (arise), G581 (being dead), G1081 (fruit)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πανδοχεύς, πανδοκεύς",
    3831: "πανήγυρις (panḗgyris | pan-ay'-goo-ris)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3956 and a derivative of G58<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a mass-meeting, i.e. (figuratively) universal companionship<BR><B>KJV:</B> general assembly.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3956<BR><I>See:</I> G58<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3831 (general assembly)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πανήγυρις<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4150 מֹועֵד, H6116 עֲצָרָה",
