    4011: "Πέργη (Pérgē | perg'-ay)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from the same as G4010<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a tower; Perga, a place in Asia Minor<BR><B>KJV:</B> Perga.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4010<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G545 (disobedient), G3981 (enticing), G4006 (confidence), G3980 (hearken), G544 (not believe), G543 (disobedience), G3982 (agree), G3988 (persuasion)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Πέργη",
    4012: "περί (perí | per-ee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G4008<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, through (all over), i.e. around; figuratively with respect to; used in various applications, of place, cause or time (with the genitive case denoting the subject or occasion or superlative point; with the accusative case the locality, circuit, matter, circumstance or general period)<BR><B>KJV:</B> (there-)about, above, against, at, on behalf of, X and his company, which concern, (as) concerning, for, X how it will go with, ((there-, where-)) of, on, over, pertaining (to), for sake, X (e-)state, (as) touching, (where-)by (in), with. In comparative, it retains substantially the same meaning of circuit (around), excess (beyond), or completeness (through).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4008<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4012 (about)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περί, περαιτέρω",
    4013: "περιάγω (periágō | per-ee-ag'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4012 and G71<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to take around (as a companion); reflexively, to walk around<BR><B>KJV:</B> compass, go (round) about, lead about.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G71<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4012 (about)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιάγω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1980 הָלַךְ, H5437 סָבַב, H5674 עָבַר",
    4014: "περιαιρέω (periairéō | per-ee-ahee-reh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4012 and G138 (including its alternate)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to remove all around, i.e. unveil, cast off (anchor); figuratively, to expiate<BR><B>KJV:</B> take away (up).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G138<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4012 (about)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιαιρέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1556 גָּלַל, H5337 נָצַל, H5437 סָבַב, H5493 סוּר, H5674 עָבַר, H6561 פָּרַק, H6565 פָּרַר, H7311 רוּם, H7918 שָׁכַךְ",
    4015: "περιαστράπτω (periastráptō | per-ee-as-trap'-to)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4012 and G797<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to flash all around, i.e. envelop in light<BR><B>KJV:</B> shine round (about).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G797<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4012 (about)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιαστράπτω",
