    4037: "περιμένω (periménō | per-ee-men'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4012 and G3306<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to stay around, i.e. await<BR><B>KJV:</B> wait for.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G3306<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5278 (abide), G3887 (abide), G5281 (enduring), G1696 (continue), G4037 (wait for), G3306 (abide), G3438 (abode)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιμένω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6960 קָוָה",
    4038: "πέριξ (périx | per'-ix)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from G4012<BR><B>Strong's:</B> all around, i.e. (as an adjective) circumjacent<BR><B>KJV:</B> round about.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5278 (abide), G3887 (abide), G5281 (enduring), G1696 (continue), G4037 (wait for), G3306 (abide), G3438 (abode)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πέριξ",
    4039: "περιοικέω (perioikéō | per-ee-oy-keh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4012 and G3611<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to reside around, i.e. be a neighbor<BR><B>KJV:</B> dwell round about.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G3611<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5278 (abide), G3887 (abide), G5281 (enduring), G1696 (continue), G4037 (wait for), G3306 (abide), G3438 (abode)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιοικέω",
    4040: "περίοικος (períoikos | per-ee'-oy-kos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4012 and G3624<BR><B>Strong's:</B> housed around, i.e. neighboring (used elliptically as a noun)<BR><B>KJV:</B> neighbour.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G3624<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5278 (abide), G3887 (abide), G5281 (enduring), G1696 (continue), G4037 (wait for), G3306 (abide), G3438 (abode)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περίοικος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1323 בַּת, H3603 כִּכָּר, H5439 סָבִיב, H7934 שָׁכֵן",
    4041: "περιούσιος (perioúsios | per-ee-oo'-see-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the present participle feminine of a compound of 4012 and G1510<BR><B>Strong's:</B> being beyond usual, i.e. special (one's own)<BR><B>KJV:</B> peculiar.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G1510<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4041 (peculiar)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιούσιος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5459 סְגֻלָּה",
    4042: "περιοχή (periochḗ | per-ee-okh-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4023<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a being held around, i.e. (concretely) a passage (of Scripture, as circumscribed)<BR><B>KJV:</B> place.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4023<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4041 (peculiar)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιοχή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4013 מִבְצָר, H4679 מְצַד, H4686 מָצוּד, H4692 מָצֹור",
    4043: "περιπατέω (peripatéō | per-ee-pat-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4012 and G3961<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to tread all around, i.e. walk at large (especially as proof of ability); figuratively, to live, deport oneself, follow (as a companion or votary)<BR><B>KJV:</B> go, be occupied with, walk (about).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G3961<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3961 (tread), G1704 (walk in), G2662 (trample), G4043 (go)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιπατέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1869 דָּרַךְ, H1980 הָלַךְ",
    4044: "περιπείρω (peripeírō | per-ee-pi'-ro)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4012 and the base of G4008<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to penetrate entirely, i.e. transfix (figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> pierce through.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G4008<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3961 (tread), G1704 (walk in), G2662 (trample), G4043 (go)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιπείρω",
    4045: "περιπίπτω (peripíptō | per-ee-pip'-to)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4012 and G4098<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to fall into something that is all around, i.e. light among or upon, be surrounded with<BR><B>KJV:</B> fall among (into).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G4098<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3895 (fall away), G4098 (fail), G4045 (fall among), G1601 (be cast), G3900 (fall), G2667 (fall), G4431 (fall), G4430 (dead body)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιπίπτω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5307 נָפַל, H7136 קָרָה",
    4046: "περιποιέομαι (peripoiéomai | per-ee-poy-eh'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> middle voice from G4012 and G4160<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to make around oneself, i.e. acquire (buy)<BR><B>KJV:</B> purchase.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G4160<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3895 (fall away), G4098 (fail), G4045 (fall among), G1601 (be cast), G3900 (fall), G2667 (fall), G4431 (fall), G4430 (dead body)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιποιέομαι, περιποιέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2421 חָיָה, H2550 חָמַל, H2820 חָשַׂךְ, H3498 יָתַר, H3502 יִתְרָה, H5459 סְגֻלָּה, H6452 פָּסַח, H7121 קָרָא, H7408 רָכַשׁ, H8210 שָׁפַךְ",
    4047: "περιποίησις (peripoíēsis | per-ee-poy'-ay-sis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4046<BR><B>Strong's:</B> acquisition (the act or the thing); by extension, preservation<BR><B>KJV:</B> obtain(-ing), peculiar, purchased, possession, saving.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4046<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3895 (fall away), G4098 (fail), G4045 (fall among), G1601 (be cast), G3900 (fall), G2667 (fall), G4431 (fall), G4430 (dead body)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιποίησις<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4241 מִחְיָה, H5459 סְגֻלָּה",
    4048: "περιῤῥήγνυμι (perirrhḗgnymi | per-ir-hrayg'-noo-mee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4012 and G4486<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to tear all around, i.e. completely away<BR><B>KJV:</B> rend off.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G4486<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4048 (rend off)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιῤῥήγνυμι, περιρήγνυμι, περι(ρ)ρήγνυμι, περιρρήγνυμι",
    4049: "περισπάω (perispáō | per-ee-spah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4012 and G4685<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to drag all around, i.e. (figuratively) to distract (with care)<BR><B>KJV:</B> cumber.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G4685<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4048 (rend off)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περισπάω, περισπάομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6030 עָנָה, H8058 שָׁמַט",
    4050: "περισσεία (perisseía | per-is-si'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4052<BR><B>Strong's:</B> surplusage, i.e. superabundance<BR><B>KJV:</B> abundance(-ant, (-ly)), superfluity.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4052<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5248 (abound much more), G4050 (abundance), G4057 (exceedingly), G5249 (beyond measure), G4052 (abound), G4051 (abundance), G4053 (exceeding abundantly above)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περισσεία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3504 יִתְרֹון, H7468 רְעוּת",
    4051: "περίσσευμα (perísseuma | per-is'-syoo-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4052<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a surplus, or superabundance<BR><B>KJV:</B> abundance, that was left, over and above.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4052<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5248 (abound much more), G4050 (abundance), G4057 (exceedingly), G5249 (beyond measure), G4052 (abound), G4051 (abundance), G4053 (exceeding abundantly above)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περίσσευμα",
    4052: "περισσεύω (perisseúō | per-is-syoo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4053<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to superabound (in quantity or quality), be in excess, be superfluous; also (transitively) to cause to superabound or excel<BR><B>KJV:</B> (make, more) abound, (have, have more) abundance (be more) abundant, be the better, enough and to spare, exceed, excel, increase, be left, redound, remain (over and above).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4053<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5248 (abound much more), G4050 (abundance), G4057 (exceedingly), G5249 (beyond measure), G4052 (abound), G4051 (abundance), G4053 (exceeding abundantly above)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περισσεύω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3498 יָתַר, H4768 מַרְבִּית",
    4053: "περισσός (perissós | per-is-sos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4012 (in the sense of beyond)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> superabundant (in quantity) or superior (in quality); by implication, excessive; adverbially (with G1537) violently; neuter (as noun) preeminence<BR><B>KJV:</B> exceeding abundantly above, more abundantly, advantage, exceedingly, very highly, beyond measure, more, superfluous, vehement(-ly).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G1537<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5248 (abound much more), G4050 (abundance), G4057 (exceedingly), G5249 (beyond measure), G4052 (abound), G4051 (abundance), G4053 (exceeding abundantly above)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περισσός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3499 יֶתֶר",
    4054: "περισσότερον (perissóteron | per-is-sot'-er-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of G4055 (as adverb)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> in a more superabundant way<BR><B>KJV:</B> more abundantly, a great deal, far more.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4055<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5248 (abound much more), G4050 (abundance), G4057 (exceedingly), G5249 (beyond measure), G4052 (abound), G4051 (abundance), G4053 (exceeding abundantly above)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περισσότερον",
    4055: "περισσότερος (perissóteros | per-is-sot'-er-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> comparative of G4053<BR><B>Strong's:</B> more superabundant (in number, degree or character)<BR><B>KJV:</B> more abundant, greater (much) more, overmuch.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4053<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5248 (abound much more), G4050 (abundance), G4057 (exceedingly), G5249 (beyond measure), G4052 (abound), G4051 (abundance), G4053 (exceeding abundantly above)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περισσότερος G4358",
    4056: "περισσοτέρως (perissotérōs | per-is-sot-er'-oce)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from G4055<BR><B>Strong's:</B> more superabundantly<BR><B>KJV:</B> more abundant(-ly), X the more earnest, (more) exceedingly, more frequent, much more, the rather.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4055<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5248 (abound much more), G4050 (abundance), G4057 (exceedingly), G5249 (beyond measure), G4052 (abound), G4051 (abundance), G4053 (exceeding abundantly above)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περισσοτέρως",
    4057: "περισσῶς (perissōs | per-is-soce')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from G4053<BR><B>Strong's:</B> superabundantly<BR><B>KJV:</B> exceedingly, out of measure, the more.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4053<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5248 (abound much more), G4050 (abundance), G4057 (exceedingly), G5249 (beyond measure), G4052 (abound), G4051 (abundance), G4053 (exceeding abundantly above)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περισσῶς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3499 יֶתֶר, H5921 עַל",
    4058: "περιστερά (peristerá | per-is-ter-ah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a pigeon<BR><B>KJV:</B> dove, pigeon.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5167 (turtle-dove), G4058 (dove)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιστερά<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1469 גֹּוזָל, H3123 יֹונָה",
    4059: "περιτέμνω (peritémnō | per-ee-tem'-no)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4012 and the base of G5114<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to cut around, i.e. (specially) to circumcise<BR><B>KJV:</B> circumcise.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G5114<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4059 (circumcise), G4061 (X circumcised), G564 (uncircumcised)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιτέμνω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3054 יָהַד, H3772 כָּרַת, H4135 מוּל, H5493 סוּר",
