    4061: "περιτομή (peritomḗ | per-it-om-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4059<BR><B>Strong's:</B> circumcision (the rite, the condition or the people, literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> X circumcised, circumcision.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4059<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4059 (circumcise), G4061 (X circumcised), G564 (uncircumcised)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιτομή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4135 מוּל, H4139 מוּלָה",
    4062: "περιτρέπω (peritrépō | per-ee-trep'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4012 and the base of G5157<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to turn around, i.e. (mentally) to craze<BR><B>KJV:</B> + make mad.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G5157<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4059 (circumcise), G4061 (X circumcised), G564 (uncircumcised)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιτρέπω",
    4063: "περιτρέχω (peritréchō | per-ee-trekh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4012 and G5143 (including its alternate)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to run around, i.e. traverse<BR><B>KJV:</B> run through.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G5143<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4059 (circumcise), G4061 (X circumcised), G564 (uncircumcised)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιτρέχω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7751 שׁוּט",
    4064: "περιφέρω (periphérō | per-ee-fer'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4012 and G5342<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to convey around, i.e. transport hither and thither<BR><B>KJV:</B> bear (carry) about.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G5342<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4059 (circumcise), G4061 (X circumcised), G564 (uncircumcised)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιφέρω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1984 הָלַל",
    4065: "περιφρονέω (periphronéō | per-ee-fron-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4012 and G5426<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to think beyond, i.e. depreciate (contemn)<BR><B>KJV:</B> despise.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G5426<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2706 (despise), G2707 (despiser), G4065 (despise)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περιφρονέω",
    4066: "περίχωρος (períchōros | per-ikh'-o-ros)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4012 and G5561<BR><B>Strong's:</B> around the region, i.e. circumjacent (as noun, with G1093 implied vicinity)<BR><B>KJV:</B> country (round) about, region (that lieth) round about.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><I>See:</I> G5561<BR><I>See:</I> G1093<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2706 (despise), G2707 (despiser), G4065 (despise)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περίχωρος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2256 חֶבֶל, H3603 כִּכָּר, H4054 מִגְרָשׁ, H4543 מִסְכְּנָה, H6418 פֶּלֶךְ",
    4067: "περίψωμα (perípsōma | per-ip'-so-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a comparative of G4012 and ψάω (to rub)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something brushed all around, i.e. off-scrapings (figuratively, scum)<BR><B>KJV:</B> offscouring.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4012<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4067 (offscouring)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περίψωμα, περίψημα",
    4068: "περπερεύομαι (perpereúomai | per-per-yoo'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> middle voice from πέρπερος (braggart<BR><B>Strong's:</B> perhaps by reduplication of the base of G4008); to boast<BR><B>KJV:</B> vaunt itself.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4008<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4067 (offscouring)<BR><B>Variants:</B> περπερεύομαι",
    4069: "Περσίς (Persís | per-sece')<BR><BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Persian woman; Persis, a Christian female<BR><B>KJV:</B> Persis.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4067 (offscouring)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Περσίς",
    4070: "πέρυσι (pérysi | per'-oo-si)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from G4009<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the by-gone, i.e. (as noun) last year<BR><B>KJV:</B> + a year ago.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4009<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4067 (offscouring)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πέρυσι, πέρυσι(ν)",
    4071: "πετεινόν (peteinón | pet-i-non')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a derivative of G4072<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a flying animal, i.e. bird<BR><B>KJV:</B> bird, fowl.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4072<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4067 (offscouring)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πετεινόν<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3671 כָּנָף, H5775 עֹוף, H5861 עַיִט, H6833 צִפֹּור",
    4072: "πέτομαι (pétomai | pet'-om-ahee), or prolongation πετάομαι (petáomai | pet-ah'-om-ahee), or contracted πτάομαι (ptáomai | ptah'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> middle voice of a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to fly<BR><B>KJV:</B> fly(-ing).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4067 (offscouring)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πέτομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2907 טוּשׂ, H5074 נָדַד, H5774 עוּף",
    4073: "πέτρα (pétra | pet'-ra)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of the same as G4074<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a (mass of) rock (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> rock.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4074<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2786 (Cephas), G4073 (rock), G4074 (Peter)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πέτρα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2496 חַלָּמִישׁ, H3710 כֵּף, H5553 סֶלַע, H6697 צוּר",
    4074: "Πέτρος (Pétros | pet'-ros)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a (piece of) rock (larger than G3037); as a name, Petrus, an apostle<BR><B>KJV:</B> Peter, rock. Compare G2786 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3037<BR><I>See:</I> G2786<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2786 (Cephas), G4073 (rock), G4074 (Peter)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Πέτρος",
    4075: "πετρώδης (petrṓdēs | pet-ro'-dace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4073 and G1491<BR><B>Strong's:</B> rock-like, i.e. rocky<BR><B>KJV:</B> stony.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4073<BR><I>See:</I> G1491<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2786 (Cephas), G4073 (rock), G4074 (Peter)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πετρώδης, πετρῶδες",
    4076: "πήγανον (pḗganon | pay'-gan-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4078<BR><B>Strong's:</B> rue (from its thick or fleshy leaves)<BR><B>KJV:</B> rue.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4078<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2786 (Cephas), G4073 (rock), G4074 (Peter)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πήγανον",
    4077: "πηγή (pēgḗ | pay-gay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from G4078 (through the idea of gushing plumply)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a fount (literally or figuratively), i.e. source or supply (of water, blood, enjoyment) (not necessarily the original spring)<BR><B>KJV:</B> fountain, well.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4078<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4077 (fountain)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πηγή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H343 אֵיד, H663 אֲפֵק, H4002 מַבּוּעַ, H4161 מֹוצָא, H4726 מָקֹור, H5033 נֵבֶךְ, H5869 עַיִן",
    4078: "πήγνυμι (pḗgnymi | payg'-noo-mee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a prolonged form of a primary verb (which in its simpler form occurs only as an alternate in certain tenses)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to fix (\"peg\"), i.e. (specially) to set up (a tent)<BR><B>KJV:</B> pitch.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4077 (fountain)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πήγνυμι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2342 חוּל, H2883 טָבַע, H3332 יָצַק, H4223 מְחָא, H5186 נָטָה, H5193 נָטַע, H5324 נָצַב, H6821 צָפַד, H7087 קָפָא, H7931 שָׁכַן, H8628 תָּקַע",
    4079: "πηδάλιον (pēdálion | pay-dal'-ee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a (presumed) derivative of πηδόν (the blade of an oar<BR><B>Strong's:</B> from the same as G3976); a \"pedal\", i.e. helm<BR><B>KJV:</B> rudder.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3976<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4077 (fountain)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πηδάλιον",
    4080: "πηλίκος (pēlíkos | pay-lee'-kos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a quantitative form (the feminine) of the base of G4225<BR><B>Strong's:</B> how much (as an indefinite), i.e. in size or (figuratively) dignity<BR><B>KJV:</B> how great (large).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4225<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4077 (fountain)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πηλίκος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3642 כָּמַהּ",
    4081: "πηλός (pēlós | pay-los')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> perhaps a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> clay<BR><B>KJV:</B> clay.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4081 (clay)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πηλός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2563 חֹמֶר, H2916 טִיט, H6083 עָפָר",
    4082: "πήρα (pḗra | pay'-rah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain affinity<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a wallet or leather pouch for food<BR><B>KJV:</B> scrip.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4082 (scrip)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πήρα",
    4083: "πῆχυς (pēchys | pay'-khoos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain affinity<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the fore-arm, i.e. (as a measure) a cubit<BR><B>KJV:</B> cubit.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4082 (scrip)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πῆχυς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H520 אַמָּה, H3027 יָד, H3709 כַּף, H7070 קָנֶה",
    4084: "πιάζω (piázō | pee-ad'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably another form of G971<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to squeeze, i.e. seize (gently by the hand (press), or officially (arrest), or in hunting (capture))<BR><B>KJV:</B> apprehend, catch, lay hand on, take. Compare G4085 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G971<BR><I>See:</I> G4085<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4082 (scrip)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πιάζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H270 אָחַז",
    4085: "πιέζω (piézō | pee-ed'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> another form for G4084<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to pack<BR><B>KJV:</B> press down.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4084<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4082 (scrip)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πιέζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1869 דָּרַךְ",
    4086: "πιθανολογία (pithanología | pith-an-ol-og-ee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a compound of a derivative of G3982 and G3056<BR><B>Strong's:</B> persuasive language<BR><B>KJV:</B> enticing words.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3982<BR><I>See:</I> G3056<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4082 (scrip)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πιθανολογία, πιθαναλογία",
    4087: "πικραίνω (pikraínō | pik-rah'-ee-no)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4089<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to embitter (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> be (make) bitter.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4089<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4087 (be bitter), G3893 (provoke), G4089 (bitter), G4088 (bitterness), G4090 (bitterly), G3894 (provocation)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πικραίνω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3707 כַּעַס, H4775 מָרַד, H7107 קָצַף, H7264 רָגַז",
    4088: "πικρία (pikría | pik-ree'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4089<BR><B>Strong's:</B> acridity (especially poison), literally or figuratively<BR><B>KJV:</B> bitterness.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4089<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4087 (be bitter), G3893 (provoke), G4089 (bitter), G4088 (bitterness), G4090 (bitterly), G3894 (provocation)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πικρία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2195 זַעַם, H3939 לַעֲנָה, H3992 מָאַר, H4751 מַר, H4754 מָרָא, H4759 מַרְאָה, H4820 מִרְמָה, H6001 עָמֵל, H7600 שַׁאֲנָן",
    4089: "πικρός (pikrós | pik-ros')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> perhaps from G4078 (through the idea of piercing)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> sharp (pungent), i.e. acrid (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> bitter.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4078<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4087 (be bitter), G3893 (provoke), G4089 (bitter), G4088 (bitterness), G4090 (bitterly), G3894 (provocation)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πικρός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4751 מַר, H4843 מָרַר, H7218 רֹאשׁ",
    4090: "πικρῶς (pikrōs | pik-roce')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from G4089<BR><B>Strong's:</B> bitterly, i.e. (figuratively) violently<BR><B>KJV:</B> bitterly.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4089<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4087 (be bitter), G3893 (provoke), G4089 (bitter), G4088 (bitterness), G4090 (bitterly), G3894 (provocation)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πικρῶς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4751 מַר, H4843 מָרַר",
    4091: "Πιλᾶτος (Pilâtos | pil-at'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> close-pressed, i.e. firm; Pilatus, a Roman<BR><B>KJV:</B> Pilate.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4087 (be bitter), G3893 (provoke), G4089 (bitter), G4088 (bitterness), G4090 (bitterly), G3894 (provocation)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Πιλᾶτος, Πειλᾶτος",
    4092: "πίμπρημι (pímprēmi | pim'-pray-mee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a reduplicated and prolonged form of a primary πρέω (préō | preh'-o)<BR>; which occurs only as an alternate in certain tenses)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to fire, i.e. burn (figuratively and passively, become inflamed with fever)<BR><B>KJV:</B> be (X should have) swollen.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4087 (be bitter), G3893 (provoke), G4089 (bitter), G4088 (bitterness), G4090 (bitterly), G3894 (provocation)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πίμπρημι",
    4093: "πινακίδιον (pinakídion | pin-ak-id'-ee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> diminutive of G4094<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a tablet (for writing on)<BR><B>KJV:</B> writing table.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4094<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4087 (be bitter), G3893 (provoke), G4089 (bitter), G4088 (bitterness), G4090 (bitterly), G3894 (provocation)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πινακίδιον, πινακίς",
    4094: "πίναξ (pínax | pin'-ax)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a form of G4109<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a plate<BR><B>KJV:</B> charger, platter.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4109<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4087 (be bitter), G3893 (provoke), G4089 (bitter), G4088 (bitterness), G4090 (bitterly), G3894 (provocation)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πίναξ",
    4095: "πίνω (pínō | pee'-no)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a prolonged form of πίω (píō | pee'-o); which (together with another form) πόω (póō | po'-o)<BR>; occurs only as an alternate in certain tenses<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to imbibe (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> drink.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2666 (devour), G4188 (drink), G4221 (cup), G4095 (drink), G4224 (banqueting), G4213 (drink), G4222 (give to drink)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πίνω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5405 נָשַׁת, H8248 שָׁקָה, H8354 שָׁתָה",
    4096: "πιότης (piótēs | pee-ot'-ace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from πίων (fat<BR><B>Strong's:</B> perhaps akin to the alternate of G4095 through the idea of repletion); plumpness, i.e. (by implication) richness (oiliness)<BR><B>KJV:</B> fatness.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4095<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2666 (devour), G4188 (drink), G4221 (cup), G4095 (drink), G4224 (banqueting), G4213 (drink), G4222 (give to drink)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πιότης<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1880 דֶּשֶׁן, H2461 חָלָב, H2896 טֹוב, H3323 יִצְהָר, H8080 שָׁמַן",
    4097: "πιπράσκω (pipráskō | pip-ras'-ko), a reduplicated and prolonged form of πράω (práō | prah'-o); (which occurs only as an alternate in certain tenses)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> contracted from περάω (to traverse<BR><B>Strong's:</B> from the base of G4008); to traffic (by travelling), i.e. dispose of as merchandise or into slavery (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> sell.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4008<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4097 (sell)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πιπράσκω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4376 מָכַר, H5234 נָכַר",
    4098: "πίπτω (píptō | pip'-to), a reduplicated and contracted form of πέτω (pétō | pet'-o); (which occurs only as an alternate in certain tenses)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably akin to G4072 through the idea of alighting<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to fall (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> fail, fall (down), light on.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4072<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3895 (fall away), G4098 (fail), G4045 (fall among), G1601 (be cast), G3900 (fall), G2667 (fall), G4431 (fall), G4430 (dead body)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πίπτω, συμπίπτω",
    4099: "Πισιδία (Pisidía | pis-id-ee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably of foreign origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Pisidia, a region of Asia Minor<BR><B>KJV:</B> Pisidia.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3895 (fall away), G4098 (fail), G4045 (fall among), G1601 (be cast), G3900 (fall), G2667 (fall), G4431 (fall), G4430 (dead body)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Πισιδία, Πισίδιος",
    4100: "πιστεύω (pisteúō | pist-yoo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4102<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to have faith (in, upon, or with respect to, a person or thing), i.e. credit; by implication, to entrust (especially one's spiritual well-being to Christ)<BR><B>KJV:</B> believe(-r), commit (to trust), put in trust with.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4102<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G570 (unbelief), G571 (that believeth not), G4104 (assure of), G4103 (believe), G4100 (believe), G569 (believe not), G4102 (assurance), G3640 (of little faith)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πιστεύω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6004 עָמַם, H8085 שָׁמַע",
    4101: "πιστικός (pistikós | pis-tik-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4102<BR><B>Strong's:</B> trustworthy, i.e. genuine (unadulterated)<BR><B>KJV:</B> spike-(nard).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4102<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G570 (unbelief), G571 (that believeth not), G4104 (assure of), G4103 (believe), G4100 (believe), G569 (believe not), G4102 (assurance), G3640 (of little faith)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πιστικός",
    4102: "πίστις (pístis | pis'-tis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3982<BR><B>Strong's:</B> persuasion, i.e. credence; moral conviction (of religious truth, or the truthfulness of God or a religious teacher), especially reliance upon Christ for salvation; abstractly, constancy in such profession; by extension, the system of religious (Gospel) truth itself<BR><B>KJV:</B> assurance, belief, believe, faith, fidelity.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3982<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G570 (unbelief), G571 (that believeth not), G4104 (assure of), G4103 (believe), G4100 (believe), G569 (believe not), G4102 (assurance), G3640 (of little faith)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πίστις<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H530 אֱמוּנָה",
    4103: "πιστός (pistós | pis-tos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G3982<BR><B>Strong's:</B> objectively, trustworthy; subjectively, trustful<BR><B>KJV:</B> believe(-ing, -r), faithful(-ly), sure, true.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3982<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G570 (unbelief), G571 (that believeth not), G4104 (assure of), G4103 (believe), G4100 (believe), G569 (believe not), G4102 (assurance), G3640 (of little faith)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πιστός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H539 אָמַן, H3499 יֶתֶר, H6662 צַדִּיק, H8419 תַּהְפֻּכָה",
    4104: "πιστόω (pistóō | pis-to'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4103<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to assure<BR><B>KJV:</B> assure of.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4103<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G570 (unbelief), G571 (that believeth not), G4104 (assure of), G4103 (believe), G4100 (believe), G569 (believe not), G4102 (assurance), G3640 (of little faith)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πιστόω, πιστόομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H559 אָמַר, H5975 עָמַד, H6004 עָמַם, H6965 קוּם",
    4105: "πλανάω (planáō | plan-ah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4106<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to (properly, cause to) roam (from safety, truth, or virtue)<BR><B>KJV:</B> go astray, deceive, err, seduce, wander, be out of the way.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4106<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4105 (go astray), G4107 (wandering), G4108 (deceiver), G4106 (deceit), G635 (err)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλανάω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H833 אָשַׁר, H943 בּוּךְ, H2926 טָלַל, H3782 כָּשַׁל, H4603 מָעַל, H5080 נָדַח, H5186 נָטָה, H5493 סוּר, H6340 פָּזַר, H6437 פָּנָה, H6586 פָּשַׁע, H6601 פָּתָה, H7686 שָׁגָה, H7953 שָׁלָה, H7971 שָׁלַח, H8582 תָּעָה, H8582 תָּעָה",
    4106: "πλάνη (plánē | plan'-ay)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of G4108 (as abstractly)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> objectively, fraudulence; subjectively, a straying from orthodoxy or piety<BR><B>KJV:</B> deceit, to deceive, delusion, error.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4108<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4105 (go astray), G4107 (wandering), G4108 (deceiver), G4106 (deceit), G635 (err)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλάνη<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4820 מִרְמָה, H6588 פֶּשַׁע, H8307 שְׁרִירוּת",
    4107: "πλανήτης (planḗtēs | plan-ay'-tace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4108<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a rover (\"planet\"), i.e. (figuratively) an erratic teacher<BR><B>KJV:</B> wandering.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4108<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4105 (go astray), G4107 (wandering), G4108 (deceiver), G4106 (deceit), G635 (err)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλανήτης, πλάνης<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5074 נָדַד",
    4108: "πλάνος (plános | plan'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain affinity<BR><B>Strong's:</B> roving (as a tramp), i.e. (by implication) an impostor or misleader;<BR><B>KJV:</B> deceiver, seducing.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4105 (go astray), G4107 (wandering), G4108 (deceiver), G4106 (deceit), G635 (err)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλάνος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4879 מְשׁוּגָה",
    4109: "πλάξ (pláx | plax)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4111<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a moulding-board, i.e. flat surface (\"plate\", or tablet, literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> table.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4111<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4105 (go astray), G4107 (wandering), G4108 (deceiver), G4106 (deceit), G635 (err)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλάξ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3871 לוּחַ",
    4110: "πλάσμα (plásma | plas'-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4111<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something moulded<BR><B>KJV:</B> thing formed.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4111<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4112 (feigned), G4111 (form), G4110 (thing formed)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλάσμα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1870 דֶּרֶךְ, H3336 יֵצֶר",
    4111: "πλάσσω (plássō | plas'-so)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to mould, i.e. shape or fabricate<BR><B>KJV:</B> form.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4112 (feigned), G4111 (form), G4110 (thing formed)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλάσσω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H908 בָּדָא, H2342 חוּל, H3335 יָצַר, H3559 כּוּן, H5341 נָצַר, H6087 עָצַב, H6213 עָשָׂה, H6696 צוּר",
    4112: "πλαστός (plastós | plas-tos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4111<BR><B>Strong's:</B> moulded, i.e. (by implication) artificial or (figuratively) fictitious (false)<BR><B>KJV:</B> feigned.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4111<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4112 (feigned), G4111 (form), G4110 (thing formed)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλαστός",
    4113: "πλατεῖα (plateîa | plat-i'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of G4116<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a wide \"plat\" or \"place\", i.e. open square<BR><B>KJV:</B> street.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4116<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4112 (feigned), G4111 (form), G4110 (thing formed)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλατεῖα",
    4114: "πλάτος (plátos | plat'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4116<BR><B>Strong's:</B> width<BR><B>KJV:</B> breadth.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4116<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4112 (feigned), G4111 (form), G4110 (thing formed)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλάτος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3709 כַּף, H3871 לוּחַ, H5672 עֲבִי, H6613 פְּתַי, H7341 רֹחַב",
    4115: "πλατύνω (platýnō | plat-oo'-no)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4116<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to widen (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> make broad, enlarge.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4116<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4112 (feigned), G4111 (form), G4110 (thing formed)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλατύνω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3680 כָּסָה, H6186 עָרַךְ, H6555 פָּרַץ, H6601 פָּתָה, H7337 רָחַב",
    4116: "πλατύς (platýs | plat-oos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4111<BR><B>Strong's:</B> spread out \"flat\" (\"plot\"), i.e. broad<BR><B>KJV:</B> wide.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4111<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4112 (feigned), G4111 (form), G4110 (thing formed)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλατύς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7342 רָחָב",
    4117: "πλέγμα (plégma | pleg'-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4120<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a plait (of hair)<BR><B>KJV:</B> broidered hair.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4120<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4112 (feigned), G4111 (form), G4110 (thing formed)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλέγμα",
    4118: "πλεῖστος (pleîstos | plice'-tos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> irregular superlative of G4183<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the largest number or very large<BR><B>KJV:</B> very great, most.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4183<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4112 (feigned), G4111 (form), G4110 (thing formed)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλεῖστος, πολύς",
    4119: "πλείων (pleíōn | pli-own), or neuter πλεῖον (pleîon | pli'-on), or πλέον (pléon | pleh'-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> comparative of G4183<BR><B>Strong's:</B> more in quantity, number, or quality; also (in plural) the major portion<BR><B>KJV:</B> X above, + exceed, more excellent, further, (very) great(-er), long(-er), (very) many, greater (more) part, + yet but.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4183<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4112 (feigned), G4111 (form), G4110 (thing formed)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλείων, πολύς",
    4120: "πλέκω (plékō | plek'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to twine or braid<BR><B>KJV:</B> plait.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4112 (feigned), G4111 (form), G4110 (thing formed)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλέκω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5688 עֲבֹת, H6843 צְפִירָה",
    4121: "πλεονάζω (pleonázō | pleh-on-ad'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4119<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to do, make or be more, i.e. increase (transitively or intransitively); by extension, to superabound<BR><B>KJV:</B> abound, abundant, make to increase, have over.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4119<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4121 (abound), G5250 (be exceeding abundant)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλεονάζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3513 כָּבַד, H4767 מִרְבָּה, H5736 עֲדַף, H6186 עָרַךְ, H7235 רָבָה, H7971 שָׁלַח",
    4122: "πλεονεκτέω (pleonektéō | pleh-on-cek-teh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4123<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be covetous, i.e. (by implication) to over-reach<BR><B>KJV:</B> get an advantage, defraud, make a gain.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4123<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4121 (abound), G4123 (covetous), G4122 (get an advantage)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλεονεκτέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1214 בָּצַע",
    4123: "πλεονέκτης (pleonéktēs | pleh-on-ek'-tace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4119 and G2192<BR><B>Strong's:</B> holding (desiring) more, i.e. eager for gain (avaricious, hence a defrauder)<BR><B>KJV:</B> covetous.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4119<BR><I>See:</I> G2192<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4121 (abound), G4123 (covetous), G4122 (get an advantage)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλεονέκτης",
    4124: "πλεονεξία (pleonexía | pleh-on-ex-ee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4123<BR><B>Strong's:</B> avarice, i.e. (by implication) fraudulency, extortion<BR><B>KJV:</B> covetous(-ness) practices, greediness.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4123<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4121 (abound), G4123 (covetous), G4122 (get an advantage)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλεονεξία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1215 בֶּצַע",
    4125: "πλευρά (pleurá | plyoo-rah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain affinity<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a rib, i.e. (by extension) side<BR><B>KJV:</B> side.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4121 (abound), G4123 (covetous), G4122 (get an advantage)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλευρά<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H663 אֲפֵק, H2502 חָלַץ, H3326 יָצוּעַ, H3326 יָצוּעַ, H5966 עָלַע, H6106 עֶצֶם, H6654 צַד, H6763 צֵלָע",
    4126: "πλέω (pléō | pleh'-o), another form for πλεύω (pleúō | plyoo'-o); which is used as an alternate in certain tenses<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably a form of G4150 (through the idea of plunging through the water)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to pass in a vessel<BR><B>KJV:</B> sail. See also G4130 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4150<BR><I>See:</I> G4130<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4121 (abound), G4123 (covetous), G4122 (get an advantage)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H935 בֹּוא",
    4127: "πληγή (plēgḗ | play-gay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4141<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a stroke; by implication, a wound; figuratively, a calamity<BR><B>KJV:</B> plague, stripe, wound(-ed).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4141<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4121 (abound), G4123 (covetous), G4122 (get an advantage)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πληγή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3511 כְּאֵב, H4046 מַגֵּפָה, H4294 מַטֶּה, H4347 מַכָּה, H5061 נֶגַע, H5063 נֶגֶף, H7626 שֵׁבֶט",
    4128: "πλῆθος (plēthos | play'-thos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4130<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a fulness, i.e. a large number, throng, populace<BR><B>KJV:</B> bundle, company, multitude.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4130<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4128 (bundle), G4129 (abound)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλῆθος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1215 בֶּצַע, H1363 גֹּבַהּ, H1995 הָמֹון, H3515 כָּבֵד, H3524 כַּבִּיר, H4393 מְלֹא, H4557 מִסְפָּר, H5971 עַם, H6099 עָצוּם, H6635 צָבָא, H6951 קָהָל, H7230 רֹב, H7285 רֶגֶשׁ, H8229 שִׁפְעָה",
    4129: "πληθύνω (plēthýnō | play-thoo'-no)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from another form of G4128<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to increase (transitively or intransitively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> abound, multiply.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4128<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4128 (bundle), G4129 (abound)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πληθύνω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1711 דָּגָה, H3498 יָתַר, H4390 מָלֵא, H5107 נוּב, H5848 עָטַף, H6105 עָצַם, H6186 עָרַךְ, H6555 פָּרַץ, H7232 רָבַב, H7235 רָבָה, H7372 רָטַב, H7646 שָׂבַע, H7685 שָׂגָה, H8317 שָׁרַץ",
    4130: "πλήθω (plḗthō | play'-tho)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a prolonged form of a primary πλέω (pléō | pleh'-o)<BR> (which appears only as an alternate in certain tenses and in the reduplicated form pimplemi)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to \"fill\" (literally or figuratively (imbue, influence, supply)); specially, to fulfil (time)<BR><B>KJV:</B> accomplish, full (…come), furnish.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλήθω, πίμπλημι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4390 מָלֵא, H7491 רָעַף, H7646 שָׂבַע",
    4131: "πλήκτης (plḗktēs | plake'-tace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4141<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a smiter, i.e. pugnacious (quarrelsome)<BR><B>KJV:</B> striker.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4141<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλήκτης",
    4132: "πλήμμυρα (plḗmmyra | plame-moo'-rah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> prolonged from G4130<BR><B>Strong's:</B> flood-tide, i.e. (by analogy) a freshet<BR><B>KJV:</B> flood.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4130<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλήμμυρα, πλημμύρα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6231 עָשַׁק",
    4133: "πλήν (plḗn | plane)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4119<BR><B>Strong's:</B> moreover (besides), i.e. albeit, save that, rather, yet<BR><B>KJV:</B> but (rather), except, nevertheless, notwithstanding, save, than.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4119<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλήν<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H56 אָבַל, H197 אוּלָם, H389 אַךְ, H403 אָכֵן, H639 אַף, H657 אֶפֶס, H905 בַּד, H1115 בִּלְתִּי, H1297 בְּרַם, H2009 הִנֵּה, H2108 זוּלָה, H3588 כִּי, H3861 לָהֵן, H4327 מִין, H5921 עַל, H5973 עִם, H6118 עֵקֶב, H7535 רַק",
    4134: "πλήρης (plḗrēs | play'-race)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4130<BR><B>Strong's:</B> replete, or covered over; by analogy, complete<BR><B>KJV:</B> full.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4130<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4137 (accomplish), G4136 (assurance), G1604 (accomplishment), G4845 (come), G466 (fill up), G378 (fill up), G4134 (full), G4135 (most surely believe), G1603 (fulfill), G4138 (which is put in to fill up)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλήρης<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3515 כָּבֵד, H4390 מָלֵא, H4390 מָלֵא, H5674 עָבַר, H7647 שָׂבָע, H7649 שָׂבֵעַ, H8003 שָׁלֵם",
    4135: "πληροφορέω (plērophoréō | play-rof-or-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4134 and G5409<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to carry out fully (in evidence), i.e. completely assure (or convince), entirely accomplish<BR><B>KJV:</B> most surely believe, fully know (persuade), make full proof of.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4134<BR><I>See:</I> G5409<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4137 (accomplish), G4136 (assurance), G1604 (accomplishment), G4845 (come), G466 (fill up), G378 (fill up), G4134 (full), G4135 (most surely believe), G1603 (fulfill), G4138 (which is put in to fill up)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πληροφορέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4390 מָלֵא",
    4136: "πληροφορία (plērophoría | play-rof-or-ee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4135<BR><B>Strong's:</B> entire confidence<BR><B>KJV:</B> (full) assurance.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4135<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4137 (accomplish), G4136 (assurance), G1604 (accomplishment), G4845 (come), G466 (fill up), G378 (fill up), G4134 (full), G4135 (most surely believe), G1603 (fulfill), G4138 (which is put in to fill up)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πληροφορία",
    4137: "πληρόω (plēróō | play-ro'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4134<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to make replete, i.e. (literally) to cram (a net), level up (a hollow), or (figuratively) to furnish (or imbue, diffuse, influence), satisfy, execute (an office), finish (a period or task), verify (or coincide with a prediction), etc.<BR><B>KJV:</B> accomplish, X after, (be) complete, end, expire, fill (up), fulfil, (be, make) full (come), fully preach, perfect, supply.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4134<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4137 (accomplish), G4136 (assurance), G1604 (accomplishment), G4845 (come), G466 (fill up), G378 (fill up), G4134 (full), G4135 (most surely believe), G1603 (fulfill), G4138 (which is put in to fill up)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πληρόω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3615 כָּלָה, H4390 מָלֵא, H5375 נָשָׂא, H7093 קֵץ, H7646 שָׂבַע, H8002 שֶׁלֶם, H8552 תָּמַם",
    4138: "πλήρωμα (plḗrōma | play'-ro-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4137<BR><B>Strong's:</B> repletion or completion, i.e. (subjectively) what fills (as contents, supplement, copiousness, multitude), or (objectively) what is filled (as container, performance, period)<BR><B>KJV:</B> which is put in to fill up, piece that filled up, fulfilling, full, fulness.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4137<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4137 (accomplish), G4136 (assurance), G1604 (accomplishment), G4845 (come), G466 (fill up), G378 (fill up), G4134 (full), G4135 (most surely believe), G1603 (fulfill), G4138 (which is put in to fill up)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλήρωμα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H663 אֲפֵק, H4393 מְלֹא",
    4139: "πλησίον (plēsíon | play-see'-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a derivative of πέλας (near)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> (adverbially) close by; as noun, a neighbor, i.e. fellow (as man, countryman, Christian or friend)<BR><B>KJV:</B> near, neighbour.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4139 (near)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλησίον",
    4140: "πλησμονή (plēsmonḗ | place-mon-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a presumed derivative of G4130<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a filling up, i.e. (figuratively) gratification<BR><B>KJV:</B> satisfying.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4130<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλησμονή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1879 דָּשֵׁן, H2960 טֹרַח, H7241 רָבִיב, H7647 שָׂבָע, H7649 שָׂבֵעַ",
    4141: "πλήσσω (plḗssō | place'-so)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently another form of G4111 (through the idea of flattening out)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to pound, i.e. (figuratively) to inflict with (calamity)<BR><B>KJV:</B> smite. Compare G5180 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5180<BR><I>See:</I> G4111<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλήσσω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3027 יָד, H3772 כָּרַת, H5062 נָגַף, H5221 נָכָה, H5307 נָפַל, H5391 נָשַׁךְ, H6398 פָּלַח",
    4142: "πλοιάριον (ploiárion | ploy-ar'-ee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a presumed derivative of G4143<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a boat<BR><B>KJV:</B> boat, little (small) ship.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4143<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλοιάριον",
    4143: "πλοῖον (ploîon | ploy'-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4126<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a sailer, i.e. vessel<BR><B>KJV:</B> ship(-ing).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4126<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλοῖον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H591 אֳנִיָּה, H5600 סְפִינָה, H6040 עֳנִי, H6716 צִי",
    4144: "πλόος (plóos | plo'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4126<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a sail, i.e. navigation<BR><B>KJV:</B> course, sailing, voyage.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4126<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1705 (fill), G4130 (accomplish), G4140 (satisfying)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλόος, πλοῦς",
    4145: "πλούσιος (ploúsios | ploo'-see-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4149<BR><B>Strong's:</B> wealthy; figuratively, abounding with<BR><B>KJV:</B> rich.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4149<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4147 (be increased with goods), G4145 (rich), G4149 (riches), G4148 (en- rich), G4146 (abundantly)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλούσιος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3515 כָּבֵד, H3715 כְּפִיר, H5947 עַלִּיז, H6223 עָשִׁיר, H7600 שַׁאֲנָן",
    4146: "πλουσίως (plousíōs | ploo-see'-oce)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from G4145<BR><B>Strong's:</B> copiously<BR><B>KJV:</B> abundantly, richly.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4145<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4147 (be increased with goods), G4145 (rich), G4149 (riches), G4148 (en- rich), G4146 (abundantly)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλουσίως",
    4147: "πλουτέω (ploutéō | ploo-teh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4148<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be (or become) wealthy (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> be increased with goods, (be made, wax) rich.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4148<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4147 (be increased with goods), G4145 (rich), G4149 (riches), G4148 (en- rich), G4146 (abundantly)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλουτέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1952 הֹון, H6238 עָשַׁר, H6555 פָּרַץ",
    4148: "πλουτίζω (ploutízō | ploo-tid'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4149<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to make wealthy (figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> en- (make) rich.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4149<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4147 (be increased with goods), G4145 (rich), G4149 (riches), G4148 (en- rich), G4146 (abundantly)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλουτίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6238 עָשַׁר",
    4149: "πλοῦτος (ploûtos | ploo'-tos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G4130<BR><B>Strong's:</B> wealth (as fulness), i.e. (literally) money, possessions, or (figuratively) abundance, richness, (specially), valuable bestowment<BR><B>KJV:</B> riches.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4130<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4147 (be increased with goods), G4145 (rich), G4149 (riches), G4148 (en- rich), G4146 (abundantly)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλοῦτος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H214 אֹוצָר, H1420 גְּדוּלָה, H1952 הֹון, H1995 הָמֹון, H2428 חַיִל, H3519 כָּבֹוד, H6239 עֹשֶׁר, H7404 רְכֻלָּה, H8228 שֶׁפַע",
    4150: "πλύνω (plýnō | ploo'-no)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a prolonged form of an obsolete πλύω (to \"flow\")<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to \"plunge\", i.e. launder clothing<BR><B>KJV:</B> wash. Compare G3068, G3538 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3068<BR><I>See:</I> G3538<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4147 (be increased with goods), G4145 (rich), G4149 (riches), G4148 (en- rich), G4146 (abundantly)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πλύνω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1740 דּוּחַ, H3526 כָּבַס, H7364 רָחַץ",
    4151: "πνεῦμα (pneûma | pnyoo'-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4154<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a current of air, i.e. breath (blast) or a breeze; by analogy or figuratively, a spirit, i.e. (human) the rational soul, (by implication) vital principle, mental disposition, etc., or (superhuman) an angel, demon, or (divine) God, Christ's spirit, the Holy Spirit<BR><B>KJV:</B> ghost, life, spirit(-ual, -ually), mind. Compare G5590 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4154<BR><I>See:</I> G5590<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4151 (ghost), G2315 (given by inspiration of God), G4154 (blow), G4153 (spiritually), G1606 (give up the ghost), G4152 (spiritual)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πνεῦμα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5397 נְשָׁמָה, H6921 קָדִים, H7307 רוּחַ, H7602 שָׁאַף",
    4152: "πνευματικός (pneumatikós | pnyoo-mat-ik-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4151<BR><B>Strong's:</B> non-carnal, i.e. (humanly) ethereal (as opposed to gross), or (dæmoniacally) a spirit (concretely), or (divinely) supernatural, regenerate, religious<BR><B>KJV:</B> spiritual. Compare G5591 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4151<BR><I>See:</I> G5591<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4151 (ghost), G2315 (given by inspiration of God), G4154 (blow), G4153 (spiritually), G1606 (give up the ghost), G4152 (spiritual)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πνευματικός",
    4153: "πνευματικῶς (pneumatikōs | pnyoo-mat-ik-oce')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from G4152<BR><B>Strong's:</B> non-physically, i.e. divinely, figuratively<BR><B>KJV:</B> spiritually.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4152<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4151 (ghost), G2315 (given by inspiration of God), G4154 (blow), G4153 (spiritually), G1606 (give up the ghost), G4152 (spiritual)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πνευματικῶς",
    4154: "πνέω (pnéō | pneh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to breathe hard, i.e. breeze<BR><B>KJV:</B> blow. Compare G5594 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5594<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4151 (ghost), G2315 (given by inspiration of God), G4154 (blow), G4153 (spiritually), G1606 (give up the ghost), G4152 (spiritual)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πνέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5380 נָשַׁב, H5398 נָשַׁף",
