    4188: "πόμα (póma | pom'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the alternate of G4095<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a beverage<BR><B>KJV:</B> drink.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4095<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2666 (devour), G4188 (drink), G4221 (cup), G4095 (drink), G4224 (banqueting), G4213 (drink), G4222 (give to drink)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πόμα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4960 מִשְׁתֶּה, H8250 שִׁקּוּי",
    4189: "πονηρία (ponēría | pon-ay-ree'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4190<BR><B>Strong's:</B> depravity, i.e. (specially), malice; plural (concretely) plots, sins<BR><B>KJV:</B> iniquity, wickedness.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4190<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4189 (iniquity), G4191 (more wicked), G4190 (bad)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πονηρία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H205 אָוֶן, H3336 יֵצֶר, H5999 עָמָל, H7200 רָאָה, H7451 רַע, H8441 תֹּועֵבַה",
    4190: "πονηρός (ponērós | pon-ay-ros')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of G4192<BR><B>Strong's:</B> hurtful, i.e. evil (properly, in effect or influence, and thus differing from G2556, which refers rather to essential character, as well as from G4550, which indicates degeneracy from original virtue); figuratively, calamitous; also (passively) ill, i.e. diseased; but especially (morally) culpable, i.e. derelict, vicious, facinorous; neuter (singular) mischief, malice, or (plural) guilt; masculine (singular) the devil, or (plural) sinners<BR><B>KJV:</B> bad, evil, grievous, harm, lewd, malicious, wicked(-ness). See also G4191 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4192<BR><I>See:</I> G2556<BR><I>See:</I> G4550<BR><I>See:</I> G4191<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4189 (iniquity), G4191 (more wicked), G4190 (bad)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πονηρός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H343 אֵיד, H873 בִּאוּשׁ, H1681 דִּבָּה, H1800 דַּל, H7200 רָאָה, H7227 רַב, H7451 רַע, H7489 רָעַע, H7489 רָעַע, H7563 רָשָׁע, H8441 תֹּועֵבַה",
    4191: "πονηρότερος (ponēróteros | pon-ay-rot'-er-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> comparative of G4190<BR><B>Strong's:</B> more evil<BR><B>KJV:</B> more wicked.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4190<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4189 (iniquity), G4191 (more wicked), G4190 (bad)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πονηρότερος, πονηρός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H343 אֵיד, H873 בִּאוּשׁ, H1681 דִּבָּה, H1800 דַּל, H7200 רָאָה, H7227 רַב, H7451 רַע, H7489 רָעַע, H7489 רָעַע, H7563 רָשָׁע, H8441 תֹּועֵבַה",
    4192: "πόνος (pónos | pon'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G3993<BR><B>Strong's:</B> toil, i.e. (by implication) anguish<BR><B>KJV:</B> pain.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3993<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4189 (iniquity), G4191 (more wicked), G4190 (bad)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πόνος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H205 אָוֶן, H343 אֵיד, H2256 חֶבֶל, H2483 חֳלִי, H3015 יָגֹון, H3018 יְגִיעַ, H3510 כָּאַב, H3511 כְּאֵב, H4245 מַחֲלֶה, H5060 נָגַע, H5450 סְבָלָה, H5999 עָמָל, H6001 עָמֵל, H6089 עֶצֶב, H6468 פְּעֻלָּה, H8463 תַּחֲלוּא",
    4193: "Ποντικός (Pontikós | pon-tik-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4195<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Pontican, i.e. native of Pontus<BR><B>KJV:</B> born in Pontus.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4195<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4189 (iniquity), G4191 (more wicked), G4190 (bad)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Ποντικός",
    4194: "Πόντιος (Póntios | pon'-tee-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> apparently bridged; Pontius, a Roman<BR><B>KJV:</B> Pontius.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4189 (iniquity), G4191 (more wicked), G4190 (bad)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Πόντιος",
    4195: "Πόντος (Póntos | pon'-tos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a sea; Pontus, a region of Asia Minor<BR><B>KJV:</B> Pontus.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4189 (iniquity), G4191 (more wicked), G4190 (bad)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Πόντος",
    4196: "Πόπλιος (Póplios | pop'-lee-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> apparently \"popular\"; Poplius (i.e. Publius), a Roman<BR><B>KJV:</B> Publius.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4189 (iniquity), G4191 (more wicked), G4190 (bad)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Πόπλιος",
    4197: "πορεία (poreía | por-i'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4198<BR><B>Strong's:</B> travel (by land); figuratively (plural) proceedings, i.e. career<BR><B>KJV:</B> journey(-ing), ways.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4198<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4189 (iniquity), G4191 (more wicked), G4190 (bad)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πορεία, πορία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1979 הֲלִיכָה, H4161 מֹוצָא, H6806 צַעַד",
    4198: "πορεύομαι (poreúomai | por-yoo'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> middle voice from a derivative of the same as G3984<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to traverse, i.e. travel (literally or figuratively; especially to remove (figuratively, die), live, etc.);<BR><B>KJV:</B> depart, go (away, forth, one's way, up), (make a, take a) journey, walk.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3984<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4198 (depart), G1607 (come), G1531 (come in)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πορεύομαι, πορεύω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H235 אָזַל, H935 בֹּוא, H1980 הָלַךְ, H1980 הָלַךְ, H3318 יָצָא, H3381 יָרַד, H4390 מָלֵא, H5066 נָגַשׁ, H5503 סָחַר, H5674 עָבַר, H5927 עָלָה, H6805 צָעַד, H6923 קָדַם, H7126 קָרַב, H7725 שׁוּב",
    4199: "πορθέω (porthéō | por-theh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> prolongation from πέρθω (to sack)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to ravage (figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> destroy, waste.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4198 (depart), G1607 (come), G1531 (come in)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πορθέω",
    4200: "πορισμός (porismós | por-is-mos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of πόρος (a way, i.e. means)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> furnishing (procuring), i.e. (by implication) money-getting (acquisition)<BR><B>KJV:</B> gain.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4198 (depart), G1607 (come), G1531 (come in)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πορισμός",
    4201: "Πόρκιος (Pórkios | por'-kee-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> apparently swinish; Porcius, a Roman<BR><B>KJV:</B> Porcius.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4198 (depart), G1607 (come), G1531 (come in)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Πόρκιος",
    4202: "πορνεία (porneía | por-ni'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4203<BR><B>Strong's:</B> harlotry (including adultery and incest); figuratively, idolatry<BR><B>KJV:</B> fornication.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4203<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4203 (commit), G4202 (fornication), G1608 (give self over to fornication), G4204 (harlot), G4205 (fornicator)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πορνεία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2183 זָנוּן, H8457 תַּזְנוּת",
    4203: "πορνεύω (porneúō | porn-yoo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4204<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to act the harlot, i.e. (literally) indulge unlawful lust (of either sex), or (figuratively) practise idolatry<BR><B>KJV:</B> commit (fornication).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4204<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4203 (commit), G4202 (fornication), G1608 (give self over to fornication), G4204 (harlot), G4205 (fornicator)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πορνεύω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2181 זָנָה, H6945 קָדֵשׁ",
    4204: "πόρνη (pórnē | por'-nay)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of G4205<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a strumpet; figuratively, an idolater<BR><B>KJV:</B> harlot, whore.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4205<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4203 (commit), G4202 (fornication), G1608 (give self over to fornication), G4204 (harlot), G4205 (fornicator)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πόρνη<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2181 זָנָה, H2219 זָרָה, H4464 מַמְזֵר, H6945 קָדֵשׁ",
    4205: "πόρνος (pórnos | por'-nos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from πέρνημι (to sell<BR><B>Strong's:</B> akin to the base of G4097); a (male) prostitute (as venal), i.e. (by analogy) a debauchee (libertine)<BR><B>KJV:</B> fornicator, whoremonger.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4097<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4203 (commit), G4202 (fornication), G1608 (give self over to fornication), G4204 (harlot), G4205 (fornicator)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πόρνος",
    4206: "πόῤῥω (pórrhō | por'-rho)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from G4253<BR><B>Strong's:</B> forwards, i.e. at a distance<BR><B>KJV:</B> far, a great way off. See also G4207 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4253<BR><I>See:</I> G4207<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4203 (commit), G4202 (fornication), G1608 (give self over to fornication), G4204 (harlot), G4205 (fornicator)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πόῤῥω, πόρρω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5704 עַד, H7350 רָחֹוק, H7368 רָחַק, H7368 רָחַק, H7368 רָחַק",
    4207: "πόῤῥωθεν (pórrhōthen | por'-rho-then)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4206 with adverbial enclitic of source<BR><B>Strong's:</B> from far, or (by implication) at a distance, i.e. distantly<BR><B>KJV:</B> afar off.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4206<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4203 (commit), G4202 (fornication), G1608 (give self over to fornication), G4204 (harlot), G4205 (fornicator)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πόῤῥωθεν, πόρρωθεν<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7350 רָחֹוק, H7350 רָחֹוק",
    4208: "ποῤῥωτέρω (porrhōtérō | por-rho-ter'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb comparative of G4206<BR><B>Strong's:</B> further, i.e. a greater distance<BR><B>KJV:</B> farther.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4206<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4203 (commit), G4202 (fornication), G1608 (give self over to fornication), G4204 (harlot), G4205 (fornicator)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ποῤῥωτέρω, πορρωτέρω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5704 עַד, H7350 רָחֹוק, H7368 רָחַק, H7368 רָחַק, H7368 רָחַק",
    4209: "πορφύρα (porphýra | por-foo'-rah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the \"purple\" mussel, i.e. (by implication) the red-blue color itself, and finally a garment dyed with it<BR><B>KJV:</B> purple.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4203 (commit), G4202 (fornication), G1608 (give self over to fornication), G4204 (harlot), G4205 (fornicator)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πορφύρα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H710 אַרְגְּוָן, H713 אַרְגָּמָן",
    4210: "πορφυροῦς (porphyroûs | por-foo-rooce')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4209<BR><B>Strong's:</B> purpureal, i.e. bluish red<BR><B>KJV:</B> purple.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4209<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4203 (commit), G4202 (fornication), G1608 (give self over to fornication), G4204 (harlot), G4205 (fornicator)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πορφυροῦς, πορφύρεος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H713 אַרְגָּמָן",
    4211: "πορφυρόπωλις (porphyrópōlis | por-foo-rop'-o-lis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of a compound of G4209 and G4453<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a female trader in purple cloth<BR><B>KJV:</B> seller of purple.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4209<BR><I>See:</I> G4453<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4203 (commit), G4202 (fornication), G1608 (give self over to fornication), G4204 (harlot), G4205 (fornicator)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πορφυρόπωλις",
    4212: "ποσάκις (posákis | pos-ak'-is)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> multiplicative from G4214<BR><B>Strong's:</B> how many times<BR><B>KJV:</B> how oft(-en).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4214<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4203 (commit), G4202 (fornication), G1608 (give self over to fornication), G4204 (harlot), G4205 (fornicator)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ποσάκις",
    4213: "πόσις (pósis | pos'-is)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the alternate of G4095<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a drinking (the act), i.e. (concretely) a draught<BR><B>KJV:</B> drink.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4095<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2666 (devour), G4188 (drink), G4221 (cup), G4095 (drink), G4224 (banqueting), G4213 (drink), G4222 (give to drink)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πόσις<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4960 מִשְׁתֶּה",
    4214: "πόσος (pósos | pos'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an absolute πός (who, what) and G3739<BR><B>Strong's:</B> interrogative pronoun (of amount) how much (large, long or (plural) many)<BR><B>KJV:</B> how great (long, many), what.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3739<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2666 (devour), G4188 (drink), G4221 (cup), G4095 (drink), G4224 (banqueting), G4213 (drink), G4222 (give to drink)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πόσος",
    4215: "ποταμός (potamós | pot-am-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from a derivative of the alternate of G4095 (compare G4224)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a current, brook or freshet (as drinkable), i.e. running water<BR><B>KJV:</B> flood, river, stream, water.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4095<BR><I>See:</I> G4224<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4215 (flood), G4216 (carried away of the flood)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ποταμός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2975 יְאֹר, H5104 נָהָר, H5158 נַחַל, H6388 פֶּלֶג",
    4216: "ποταμοφόρητος (potamophórētos | pot-am-of-or'-ay-tos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4215 and a derivative of G5409<BR><B>Strong's:</B> river-borne, i.e. overwhelmed by a stream<BR><B>KJV:</B> carried away of the flood.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4215<BR><I>See:</I> G5409<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4215 (flood), G4216 (carried away of the flood)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ποταμοφόρητος",
    4217: "ποταπός (potapós | pot-ap-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently from G4219 and the base of G4226<BR><B>Strong's:</B> interrogatively, whatever, i.e. of what possible sort<BR><B>KJV:</B> what (manner of).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4219<BR><I>See:</I> G4226<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4215 (flood), G4216 (carried away of the flood)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ποταπός, ποδαπός",
    4218: "ποτέ (poté | pot-eh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G4225 and G5037<BR><B>Strong's:</B> indefinite adverb, at some time, ever<BR><B>KJV:</B> afore-(any, some-)time(-s), at length (the last), (+ n-)ever, in the old time, in time past, once, when.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4225<BR><I>See:</I> G5037<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4215 (flood), G4216 (carried away of the flood)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ποτέ",
    4219: "πότε (póte | pot'-eh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G4226 and G5037<BR><B>Strong's:</B> interrogative adverb, at what time<BR><B>KJV:</B> + how long, when.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4226<BR><I>See:</I> G5037<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4215 (flood), G4216 (carried away of the flood)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πότε",
    4220: "πότερον (póteron | pot'-er-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a comparative of the base of G4226<BR><B>Strong's:</B> interrogative as adverb, which (of two), i.e. is it this or that<BR><B>KJV:</B> whether.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4226<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4215 (flood), G4216 (carried away of the flood)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πότερον",
    4221: "ποτήριον (potḗrion | pot-ay'-ree-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a derivative of the alternate of G4095<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a drinking-vessel; by extension, the contents thereof, i.e. a cupful (draught); figuratively, a lot or fate<BR><B>KJV:</B> cup.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4095<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2666 (devour), G4188 (drink), G4221 (cup), G4095 (drink), G4224 (banqueting), G4213 (drink), G4222 (give to drink)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ποτήριον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3563 כֹּוס, H3627 כְּלִי, H6907 קֻבַּעַת",
    4222: "ποτίζω (potízō | pot-id'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of the alternate of G4095<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to furnish drink, irrigate<BR><B>KJV:</B> give (make) to drink, feed, water.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4095<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2666 (devour), G4188 (drink), G4221 (cup), G4095 (drink), G4224 (banqueting), G4213 (drink), G4222 (give to drink)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ποτίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1572 גָּמָא, H5258 נָסַךְ, H8248 שָׁקָה",
    4223: "Ποτίολοι (Potíoloi | pot-ee'-ol-oy)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> little wells, i.e. mineral springs; Potioli (i.e. Puteoli), a place in Italy<BR><B>KJV:</B> Puteoli.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2666 (devour), G4188 (drink), G4221 (cup), G4095 (drink), G4224 (banqueting), G4213 (drink), G4222 (give to drink)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Ποτίολοι",
    4224: "πότος (pótos | pot'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the alternate of G4095<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a drinking-bout or carousal<BR><B>KJV:</B> banqueting.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4095<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2666 (devour), G4188 (drink), G4221 (cup), G4095 (drink), G4224 (banqueting), G4213 (drink), G4222 (give to drink)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πότος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4960 מִשְׁתֶּה",
    4225: "πού (poú | poo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> genitive case of an indefinite pronoun πός (some) otherwise obsolete (compare G4214)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> as adverb of place, somewhere, i.e. nearly<BR><B>KJV:</B> about, a certain place.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4214<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2666 (devour), G4188 (drink), G4221 (cup), G4095 (drink), G4224 (banqueting), G4213 (drink), G4222 (give to drink)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πού",
    4226: "ποῦ (poû | poo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> genitive case of an interrogative pronoun πός (what) otherwise obsolete (perhaps the same as G4225 used with the rising slide of inquiry)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> as adverb of place; at (by implication, to) what locality<BR><B>KJV:</B> where, whither.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4225<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2666 (devour), G4188 (drink), G4221 (cup), G4095 (drink), G4224 (banqueting), G4213 (drink), G4222 (give to drink)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ποῦ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H346 אַיֵּה, H6030 עָנָה",
    4227: "Πούδης (Poúdēs | poo'-dace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> modest; Pudes (i.e. Pudens), a Christian<BR><B>KJV:</B> Pudens.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2666 (devour), G4188 (drink), G4221 (cup), G4095 (drink), G4224 (banqueting), G4213 (drink), G4222 (give to drink)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Πούδης",
    4228: "πούς (poús | pooce)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a \"foot\" (figuratively or literally)<BR><B>KJV:</B> foot(-stool).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4228 (foot)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πούς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H838 אָשֻׁר, H3767 כָּרָע, H4772 מַרְגְלָה, H6119 עָקֵב, H6471 פַּעַם, H6541 פַּרְסָה, H7272 רֶגֶל",
    4229: "πρᾶγμα (prâgma | prag'-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4238<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a deed; by implication, an affair; by extension, an object (material)<BR><B>KJV:</B> business, matter, thing, work.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4238<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4230 (affair), G1281 (gain by trading), G4238 (commit), G4234 (deed), G4229 (business), G4231 (occupy)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρᾶγμα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1697 דָּבָר, H2656 חֵפֶץ, H4405 מִלָּה, H4611 מַעֲלָל, H4639 מַעֲשֶׂה, H5673 עֲבִידָה, H6640 צְבוּ",
    4230: "πραγματεία (pragmateía | prag-mat-i'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4231<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a transaction, i.e. negotiation<BR><B>KJV:</B> affair.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4231<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4230 (affair), G1281 (gain by trading), G4238 (commit), G4234 (deed), G4229 (business), G4231 (occupy)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πραγματεία",
    4231: "πραγματεύομαι (pragmateúomai | prag-mat-yoo'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4229<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to busy oneself with, i.e. to trade<BR><B>KJV:</B> occupy.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4229<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4230 (affair), G1281 (gain by trading), G4238 (commit), G4234 (deed), G4229 (business), G4231 (occupy)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πραγματεύομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2836 חָשַׁק, H6213 עָשָׂה",
    4232: "πραιτώριον (praitṓrion | prahee-to'-ree-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the prætorium or governor's courtroom (sometimes including the whole edifice and camp)<BR><B>KJV:</B> (common, judgment) hall (of judgment), palace, prætorium.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4230 (affair), G1281 (gain by trading), G4238 (commit), G4234 (deed), G4229 (business), G4231 (occupy)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πραιτώριον",
    4233: "πράκτωρ (práktōr | prak'-tor)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of G4238<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a practiser, i.e. (specially), an official collector<BR><B>KJV:</B> officer.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4238<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4230 (affair), G1281 (gain by trading), G4238 (commit), G4234 (deed), G4229 (business), G4231 (occupy)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πράκτωρ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5066 נָגַשׁ",
    4234: "πρᾶξις (prâxis | prax'-is)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4238<BR><B>Strong's:</B> practice, i.e. (concretely) an act; by extension, a function<BR><B>KJV:</B> deed, office, work.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4238<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4230 (affair), G1281 (gain by trading), G4238 (commit), G4234 (deed), G4229 (business), G4231 (occupy)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρᾶξις<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1870 דֶּרֶךְ, H6467 פֹּעַל",
    4235: "πρᾷος (prâios | prah'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a form of G4239, used in certain parts<BR><B>Strong's:</B> gentle, i.e. humble<BR><B>KJV:</B> meek.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4239<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4230 (affair), G1281 (gain by trading), G4238 (commit), G4234 (deed), G4229 (business), G4231 (occupy)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρᾷος, πρᾶος G4553<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6035 עָנָו, H6041 עָנִי",
    4236: "πρᾳότης (praiótēs | prah-ot'-ace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4235<BR><B>Strong's:</B> gentleness, by implication, humility<BR><B>KJV:</B> meekness.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4235<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3663 (of like passions), G4834 (have compassion), G2552 (suffering affliction), G4236 (meekness), G3804 (affection), G3958 (feel), G3356 (have compassion), G4777 (be partaker of afflictions), G2553 (be afflicted), G4310 (suffer before), G4835 (having compassion one of another), G4841 (suffer with), G3805 (suffer), G3806 (affection)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρᾳότης, πραότης, πραϋπαθία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6037 עַנְוָה",
    4237: "πρασιά (prasiá | pras-ee-ah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> perhaps from πράσον (a leek, and so an onion-patch)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a garden plot, i.e. (by implication, of regular beds) a row (repeated in plural by Hebraism, to indicate an arrangement)<BR><B>KJV:</B> in ranks.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3663 (of like passions), G4834 (have compassion), G2552 (suffering affliction), G4236 (meekness), G3804 (affection), G3958 (feel), G3356 (have compassion), G4777 (be partaker of afflictions), G2553 (be afflicted), G4310 (suffer before), G4835 (having compassion one of another), G4841 (suffer with), G3805 (suffer), G3806 (affection)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρασιά",
    4238: "πράσσω (prássō | pras'-so)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to \"practise\", i.e. perform repeatedly or habitually (thus differing from G4160, which properly refers to a single act); by implication, to execute, accomplish, etc.; specially, to collect (dues), fare (personally)<BR><B>KJV:</B> commit, deeds, do, exact, keep, require, use arts.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4160<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4230 (affair), G1281 (gain by trading), G4238 (commit), G4234 (deed), G4229 (business), G4231 (occupy)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πράσσω, ἀναπράσσω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1980 הָלַךְ, H5065 נָגַשׂ, H6213 עָשָׂה, H6466 פָּעַל",
    4239: "πραΰς (praÿs | prah-ooce')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> mild, i.e. (by implication) humble<BR><B>KJV:</B> meek. See also G4235 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4235<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4240 (meekness), G4236 (meekness), G4239 (meek)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πραΰς, πραΰς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6035 עָנָו, H6041 עָנִי",
    4240: "πραΰτης (praÿtēs | prah-oo'-tace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4239<BR><B>Strong's:</B> mildness, i.e. (by implication) humility<BR><B>KJV:</B> meekness.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4239<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4240 (meekness), G4236 (meekness), G4239 (meek)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πραΰτης, πραΰτης, πρᾳΰτης<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6037 עַנְוָה",
    4241: "πρέπω (prépō | prep'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to tower up (be conspicuous), i.e. (by implication) to be suitable or proper (third person singular present indicative, often used impersonally, it is fit or right)<BR><B>KJV:</B> become, comely.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4240 (meekness), G4236 (meekness), G4239 (meek)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρέπω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1747 דּוּמִיָּה, H4998 נָאָה",
    4242: "πρεσβεία (presbeía | pres-bi'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4243<BR><B>Strong's:</B> seniority (eldership), i.e. (by implication) an embassy (concretely, ambassadors)<BR><B>KJV:</B> ambassage, message.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4243<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4240 (meekness), G4236 (meekness), G4239 (meek)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρεσβεία",
    4243: "πρεσβεύω (presbeúō | pres-byoo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G4245<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be a senior, i.e. (by implication) act as a representative (figuratively, preacher)<BR><B>KJV:</B> be an ambassador.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4245<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4245 (elder), G4850 (presbyter), G4244 (elder), G4246 (aged), G4243 (be an ambassador), G4247 (aged woman)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρεσβεύω",
    4244: "πρεσβυτέριον (presbytérion | pres-boo-ter'-ee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a presumed derivative of G4245<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the order of elders, i.e. (specially), Israelite Sanhedrin or Christian \"presbytery\"<BR><B>KJV:</B> (estate of) elder(-s), presbytery.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4245<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4245 (elder), G4850 (presbyter), G4244 (elder), G4246 (aged), G4243 (be an ambassador), G4247 (aged woman)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρεσβυτέριον",
    4245: "πρεσβύτερος (presbýteros | pres-boo'-ter-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> comparative of πρέσβυς (elderly)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> older; as noun, a senior; specially, an Israelite Sanhedrist (also figuratively, member of the celestial council) or Christian \"presbyter\"<BR><B>KJV:</B>  elder(-est), old.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4245 (elder), G4850 (presbyter), G4244 (elder), G4246 (aged), G4243 (be an ambassador), G4247 (aged woman)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρεσβύτερος",
    4246: "πρεσβύτης (presbýtēs | pres-boo'-tace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as G4245<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an old man<BR><B>KJV:</B> aged (man), old man.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4245<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4245 (elder), G4850 (presbyter), G4244 (elder), G4246 (aged), G4243 (be an ambassador), G4247 (aged woman)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρεσβύτης, πρεσβευτής<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H376 אִישׁ, H2205 זָקֵן, H3453 יָשִׁישׁ, H3887 לוּץ, H7868 שִׂיב",
    4247: "πρεσβῦτις (presbŷtis | pres-boo'-tis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of G4246<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an old woman<BR><B>KJV:</B> aged woman.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4246<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4245 (elder), G4850 (presbyter), G4244 (elder), G4246 (aged), G4243 (be an ambassador), G4247 (aged woman)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρεσβῦτις",
    4248: "πρηνής (prēnḗs | pray-nace')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4253<BR><B>Strong's:</B> leaning (falling) forward (\"prone\"), i.e. head foremost<BR><B>KJV:</B> headlong.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4253<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4245 (elder), G4850 (presbyter), G4244 (elder), G4246 (aged), G4243 (be an ambassador), G4247 (aged woman)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρηνής",
    4249: "πρίζω (prízō | prid'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a strengthened form of a primary prio (to saw)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to saw in two<BR><B>KJV:</B> saw asunder.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4245 (elder), G4850 (presbyter), G4244 (elder), G4246 (aged), G4243 (be an ambassador), G4247 (aged woman)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρίζω, πρίω, πρίζω/πρίω",
    4250: "πρίν (prín | prin)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from G4253<BR><B>Strong's:</B> prior, sooner<BR><B>KJV:</B> before (that), ere.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4253<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4245 (elder), G4850 (presbyter), G4244 (elder), G4246 (aged), G4243 (be an ambassador), G4247 (aged woman)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρίν",
    4251: "Πρίσκα (Príska | pris'-kah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> feminine of Priscus, ancient; Priska, a Christian woman<BR><B>KJV:</B> Prisca. See also G4252 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4252<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4245 (elder), G4850 (presbyter), G4244 (elder), G4246 (aged), G4243 (be an ambassador), G4247 (aged woman)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Πρίσκα, Πρίσκα/Πρίσκιλλα (dim.)",
    4252: "Πρίσκιλλα (Prískilla | pris'-cil-lah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> diminutive of G4251<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Priscilla (i.e. little Prisca), a Christian woman<BR><B>KJV:</B> Priscilla.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4251<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4245 (elder), G4850 (presbyter), G4244 (elder), G4246 (aged), G4243 (be an ambassador), G4247 (aged woman)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Πρίσκιλλα, Πρίσκα, Πρίσκα/Πρίσκιλλα (dim.)",
    4253: "πρό (pró | pro)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary preposition<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"fore\", i.e. in front of, prior (figuratively, superior) to<BR><B>KJV:</B> above, ago, before, or ever. In the comparative, it retains the same significations.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4253 (above)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρό<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6040 עֳנִי",
    4254: "προάγω (proágō | pro-ag'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4253 and G71<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to lead forward (magisterially); intransitively, to precede (in place or time (participle, previous))<BR><B>KJV:</B> bring (forth, out), go before.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4253<BR><I>See:</I> G71<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4318 (access), G4317 (bring), G4254 (bring), G3855 (depart), G72 (manner of life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προάγω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5066 נָגַשׁ",
    4255: "προαιρέομαι (proairéomai | pro-ahee-reh'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4253 and G138<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to choose for oneself before another thing (prefer), i.e. (by implication) to propose (intend)<BR><B>KJV:</B> purpose.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4253<BR><I>See:</I> G138<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4318 (access), G4317 (bring), G4254 (bring), G3855 (depart), G72 (manner of life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προαιρέομαι, προαιρέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1334 בָּתַר, H2836 חָשַׁק, H3985 מָאֵן, H3988 מָאַס",
    4256: "προαιτιάομαι (proaitiáomai | pro-ahee-tee-ah'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4253 and a derivative of G156<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to accuse already, i.e. previously charge<BR><B>KJV:</B> prove before.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4253<BR><I>See:</I> G156<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4318 (access), G4317 (bring), G4254 (bring), G3855 (depart), G72 (manner of life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προαιτιάομαι, αἰτιάομαι",
    4257: "προακούω (proakoúō | pro-ak-oo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4253 and G191<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to hear already,i.e. anticipate<BR><B>KJV:</B> hear before.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4253<BR><I>See:</I> G191<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4318 (access), G4317 (bring), G4254 (bring), G3855 (depart), G72 (manner of life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προακούω",
    4258: "προαμαρτάνω (proamartánō | pro-am-ar-tan'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4253 and G264<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to sin previously (to conversion)<BR><B>KJV:</B> sin already, heretofore sin.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4253<BR><I>See:</I> G264<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4318 (access), G4317 (bring), G4254 (bring), G3855 (depart), G72 (manner of life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προαμαρτάνω",
    4259: "προαύλιον (proaúlion | pro-ow'-lee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a presumed compound of G4253 and G833<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a forecourt, i.e. vestibule (alley-way)<BR><B>KJV:</B> porch.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4253<BR><I>See:</I> G833<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4318 (access), G4317 (bring), G4254 (bring), G3855 (depart), G72 (manner of life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προαύλιον",
    4260: "προβαίνω (probaínō | prob-ah'-ee-no)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4253 and the base of G939<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to walk forward, i.e. advance (literally, or in years)<BR><B>KJV:</B> + be of a great age, go farther (on), be well stricken.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4253<BR><I>See:</I> G939<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4318 (access), G4317 (bring), G4254 (bring), G3855 (depart), G72 (manner of life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προβαίνω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H935 בֹּוא, H1980 הָלַךְ, H3381 יָרַד",
    4261: "προβάλλω (probállō | prob-al'-lo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4253 and G906<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to throw forward, i.e. push to the front, germinate<BR><B>KJV:</B> put forward, shoot forth.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4253<BR><I>See:</I> G906<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4318 (access), G4317 (bring), G4254 (bring), G3855 (depart), G72 (manner of life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προβάλλω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2330 חוּד, H3384 יָרָה, H4838 מָרַק, H7971 שָׁלַח",
    4262: "προβατικός (probatikós | prob-at-ik-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4263<BR><B>Strong's:</B> relating to sheep, i.e. (a gate) through which they were led into Jerusalem<BR><B>KJV:</B> sheep (market).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4263<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4318 (access), G4317 (bring), G4254 (bring), G3855 (depart), G72 (manner of life)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προβατικός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6629 צֹאן",
    4263: "πρόβατον (próbaton | prob'-at-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably neuter of a presumed derivative of G4260<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something that walks forward (a quadruped), i.e. (specially), a sheep (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> sheep(-fold).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4260<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4263 (sheep)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρόβατον, προβάτιον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3532 כֶּבֶשׂ, H3775 כֶּשֶׂב, H6629 צֹאן, H7353 רָחֵל, H7716 שֶׂה",
    4264: "προβιβάζω (probibázō | prob-ib-ad'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4253 and a reduplicated form of G971<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to force forward, i.e. bring to the front, instigate<BR><B>KJV:</B> draw, before instruct.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4253<BR><I>See:</I> G971<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4263 (sheep)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προβιβάζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3384 יָרָה, H8150 שָׁנַן",
    4265: "προβλέπω (problépō | prob-lep'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4253 and G991<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to look out beforehand, i.e. furnish in advance<BR><B>KJV:</B> provide.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4253<BR><I>See:</I> G991<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4263 (sheep)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προβλέπω, προβλέπομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7200 רָאָה",
