    4337: "προσέχω (proséchō | pros-ekh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and G2192<BR><B>Strong's:</B> (figuratively) to hold the mind (G3563 implied) towards, i.e. pay attention to, be cautious about, apply oneself to, adhere to<BR><B>KJV:</B> (give) attend(-ance, -ance at, -ance to, unto), beware, be given to, give (take) heed (to unto); have regard.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G2192<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2172 (pray), G4335 (X pray earnestly), G4336 (pray), G2171 (prayer)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσέχω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H238 אָזַן, H995 בִּין, H1692 דָּבַק, H2095 זְהַר, H2308 חָדַל, H2363 חוּשׁ, H2388 חָזַק, H2388 חָזַק, H3045 יָדַע, H3313 יָפַע, H3364 יָקַץ, H5144 נָזַר, H5186 נָטָה, H5753 עָוָה, H6437 פָּנָה, H7126 קָרַב, H7181 קָשַׁב, H7760 שׂוּם, H7896 שִׁית, H8104 שָׁמַר, H8159 שָׁעָה",
    4338: "προσηλόω (prosēlóō | pros-ay-lo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and a derivative of G2247<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to peg to, i.e. spike fast<BR><B>KJV:</B> nail to.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G2247<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2172 (pray), G4335 (X pray earnestly), G4336 (pray), G2171 (prayer)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσηλόω",
    4339: "προσήλυτος (prosḗlytos | pros-ay'-loo-tos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the alternate of G4334<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an arriver from a foreign region, i.e. (specially), an acceder (convert) to Judaism (\"proselyte\")<BR><B>KJV:</B> proselyte.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4334<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4339 (proselyte)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσήλυτος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1616 גֵּר",
    4340: "πρόσκαιρος (próskairos | pros'-kahee-ros)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and G2540<BR><B>Strong's:</B> for the occasion only, i.e. temporary<BR><B>KJV:</B> dur-(eth) for awhile, endure for a time, for a season, temporal.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G2540<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2120 (opportunity), G2121 (convenient), G170 (lack opportunity), G4340 (dur- for awhile), G171 (out of season), G2540 (X always), G2122 (conveniently)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρόσκαιρος",
    4341: "προσκαλέομαι (proskaléomai | pros-kal-eh'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> middle voice from G4314 and G2564<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to call toward oneself, i.e. summon, invite<BR><B>KJV:</B> call (for, to, unto).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G2564<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1458 (accuse), G2822 (called), G2564 (bid), G1528 (call in), G4779 (call together), G3333 (call), G2821 (calling), G1462 (crime laid against), G1941 (appeal), G4341 (call), G1577 (assembly), G4292 (provoke), G479 (bid again)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσκαλέομαι, προσκαλέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H935 בֹּוא, H7121 קָרָא, H7136 קָרָה",
    4342: "προσκαρτερέω (proskarteréō | pros-kar-ter-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and G2594<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be earnest towards, i.e. (to a thing) to persevere, be constantly diligent, or (in a place) to attend assiduously all the exercises, or (to a person) to adhere closely to (as a servitor)<BR><B>KJV:</B> attend (give self) continually (upon), continue (in, instant in, with), wait on (continually).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G2594<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4343 (perseverance), G4342 (attend continually), G2594 (endure)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσκαρτερέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2388 חָזַק",
    4343: "προσκαρτέρησις (proskartérēsis | pros-kar-ter'-ay-sis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4342<BR><B>Strong's:</B> persistancy<BR><B>KJV:</B> perseverance.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4342<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4343 (perseverance), G4342 (attend continually), G2594 (endure)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσκαρτέρησις",
    4344: "προσκεφάλαιον (proskephálaion | pros-kef-al'-ahee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a presumed compound of G4314 and G2776<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something for the head, i.e. a cushion<BR><B>KJV:</B> pillow.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G2776<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4343 (perseverance), G4342 (attend continually), G2594 (endure)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσκεφάλαιον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3704 כֶּסֶת",
    4345: "προσκληρόω (prosklēróō | pros-klay-ro'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and G2820<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to give a common lot to, i.e. (figuratively) to associate with<BR><B>KJV:</B> consort with.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G2820<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3647 (perfect soundness), G2819 (heritage), G2817 (inheritance), G4789 (fellow -heir), G2820 (obtain an inheritance), G3648 (entire), G2624 (divide by lot), G2816 (be heir), G4345 (consort with), G2818 (heir)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσκληρόω, προσκληρόομαι",
    4346: "πρόσκλισις (prósklisis | pros'-klis-is)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a compound of G4314 and G2827<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a leaning towards, i.e. (figuratively) proclivity (favoritism)<BR><B>KJV:</B> partiality.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G2827<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3647 (perfect soundness), G2819 (heritage), G2817 (inheritance), G4789 (fellow -heir), G2820 (obtain an inheritance), G3648 (entire), G2624 (divide by lot), G2816 (be heir), G4345 (consort with), G2818 (heir)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρόσκλισις, πρόσκλησις",
    4347: "προσκολλάω (proskolláō | pros-kol-lah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and G2853<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to glue to, i.e. (figuratively) to adhere<BR><B>KJV:</B> cleave, join (self).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G2853<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4347 (cleave), G2853 (cleave)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσκολλάω, προσκλίνω, προσκολλάομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1245 בָּקַשׁ, H1692 דָּבַק, H7132 קְרָבָה",
    4348: "πρόσκομμα (próskomma | pros'-kom-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4350<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a stub, i.e. (figuratively) occasion of apostasy<BR><B>KJV:</B> offence, stumbling(-block, (-stone)).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4350<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4350 (beat upon), G677 (none), G4348 (offence), G4349 (offence)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρόσκομμα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4170 מֹוקֵשׁ, H5063 נֶגֶף, H6983 קֹושׁ",
    4349: "προσκοπή (proskopḗ | pros-kop-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4350<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a stumbling, i.e. (figuratively and concretely) occasion of sin<BR><B>KJV:</B> offence.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4350<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4350 (beat upon), G677 (none), G4348 (offence), G4349 (offence)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσκοπή",
    4350: "προσκόπτω (proskóptō | pros-kop'-to)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and G2875<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to strike at, i.e. surge against (as water); specially, to stub on, i.e. trip up (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> beat upon, dash, stumble (at).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G2875<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4350 (beat upon), G677 (none), G4348 (offence), G4349 (offence)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσκόπτω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3782 כָּשַׁל, H5062 נָגַף, H7293 רַהַב",
    4351: "προσκυλίω (proskylíō | pros-koo-lee'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and G2947<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to roll towards, i.e. block against<BR><B>KJV:</B> roll (to).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G2947<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4350 (beat upon), G677 (none), G4348 (offence), G4349 (offence)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσκυλίω",
    4352: "προσκυνέω (proskynéō | pros-koo-neh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and a probable derivative of G2965 (meaning to kiss, like a dog licking his master's hand)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to fawn or crouch to, i.e. (literally or figuratively) prostrate oneself in homage (do reverence to, adore)<BR><B>KJV:</B> worship.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G2965<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4352 (worship), G4353 (worshipper)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσκυνέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2111 זוּעַ, H3766 כָּרַע, H5401 נָשַׁק, H5456 סָגַד, H5647 עָבַד, H7812 שָׁחָה",
    4353: "προσκυνητής (proskynētḗs | pros-koo-nay-tace')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4352<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an adorer<BR><B>KJV:</B> worshipper.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4352<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4352 (worship), G4353 (worshipper)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσκυνητής",
    4354: "προσλαλέω (proslaléō | pros-lal-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and G2980<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to talk to, i.e. converse with<BR><B>KJV:</B> speak to (with).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G2980<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4352 (worship), G4353 (worshipper)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσλαλέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1696 דָבַר",
    4355: "προσλαμβάνω (proslambánō | pros-lam-ban'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and G2983<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to take to oneself, i.e. use (food), lead (aside), admit (to friendship or hospitality)<BR><B>KJV:</B> receive, take (unto).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G2983<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσλαμβάνω, προσαναλαμβάνω, προσλαμβάνομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H622 אָסַף, H3947 לָקַח, H4871 מָשָׁה, H6213 עָשָׂה, H7126 קָרַב",
    4356: "πρόσληψις (próslēpsis | pros'-lape-sis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4355<BR><B>Strong's:</B> admission<BR><B>KJV:</B> receiving.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4355<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρόσληψις, πρόσλημψις, πρόσλημψις/πρόσληψις",
    4357: "προσμένω (prosménō | pros-men'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and G3306<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to stay further, i.e. remain in a place, with a person; figuratively, to adhere to, persevere in<BR><B>KJV:</B> abide still, be with, cleave unto, continue in (with).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G3306<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσμένω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2342 חוּל",
    4358: "προσορμίζω (prosormízō | pros-or-mid'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and a derivative of the same as G3730 (meaning to tie (anchor) or lull)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to moor to, i.e. (by implication) land at<BR><B>KJV:</B> draw to the shore.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G3730<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσορμίζω, προσορμίζομαι",
    4359: "προσοφείλω (prosopheílō | pros-of-i'-lo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and G3784<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be indebted additionally<BR><B>KJV:</B> over besides.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G3784<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσοφείλω",
    4360: "προσοχθίζω (prosochthízō | pros-okh-thid'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and a form of ὀχθέω (to be vexed with something irksome)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to feel indignant at<BR><B>KJV:</B> be grieved at.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσοχθίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1350 גָּאַל, H3988 מָאַס, H6958 קֹוא, H6962 קוּט, H6973 קוּץ, H8262 שָׁקַץ, H8581 תַּעָב",
    4361: "πρόσπεινος (próspeinos | pros'-pi-nos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and the same as G3983<BR><B>Strong's:</B> hungering further, i.e. intensely hungry<BR><B>KJV:</B> very hungry.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G3983<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πρόσπεινος",
    4362: "προσπήγνυμι (prospḗgnymi | pros-payg'-noo-mee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and G4078<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to fasten to, i.e. (specially), to impale (on a cross)<BR><B>KJV:</B> crucify.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G4078<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσπήγνυμι",
    4363: "προσπίπτω (prospíptō | pros-pip'-to)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and G4098<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to fall towards, i.e. (gently) prostrate oneself (in supplication or homage), or (violently) to rush upon (in storm)<BR><B>KJV:</B> beat upon, fall (down) at (before).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G4098<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσπίπτω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3318 יָצָא, H3766 כָּרַע, H5060 נָגַע, H5307 נָפַל",
    4364: "προσποιέομαι (prospoiéomai | pros-poy-eh'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> middle voice from G4314 and G4160<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to do forward for oneself, i.e. pretend (as if about to do a thing)<BR><B>KJV:</B> make as though.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G4160<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσποιέομαι, προσποιέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1984 הָלַל",
    4365: "προσπορεύομαι (prosporeúomai | pros-por-yoo'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4314 and G4198<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to journey towards, i.e. approach (not the same as G4313)<BR><B>KJV:</B> go before.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4314<BR><I>See:</I> G4198<BR><I>See:</I> G4313<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)<BR><B>Variants:</B> προσπορεύομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H935 בֹּוא, H1481 גּוּר, H1980 הָלַךְ, H5066 נָגַשׁ, H7126 קָרַב",
