    4439: "πύλη (pýlē | poo'-lay)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a gate, i.e. the leaf or wing of a folding entrance (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> gate.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4440 (gate), G4439 (gate)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πύλη<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1817 דֶּלֶת, H5592 סַף, H6607 פֶּתַח, H8179 שַׁעַר",
    4440: "πυλών (pylṓn | poo-lone')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4439<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a gate-way, door-way of a building or city; by implication, a portal or vestibule<BR><B>KJV:</B> gate, porch.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4439<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4440 (gate), G4439 (gate)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πυλών<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5592 סַף, H6607 פֶּתַח, H8179 שַׁעַר",
    4441: "πυνθάνομαι (pynthánomai | poon-than'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> middle voice prolonged from a primary πύθω (which occurs only as an alternate in certain tenses)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to question, i.e. ascertain by inquiry (as a matter of information merely; and thus differing from G2065, which properly means a request as a favor; and from G154, which is strictly a demand for something due; as well as from G2212, which implies a search for something hidden; and from G1189, which involves the idea of urgent need); by implication, to learn (by casual intelligence)<BR><B>KJV:</B> ask, demand, enquire, understand.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2065<BR><I>See:</I> G154<BR><I>See:</I> G2212<BR><I>See:</I> G1189<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4440 (gate), G4439 (gate)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πυνθάνομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1875 דָּרַשׁ",
    4442: "πῦρ (pŷr | poor)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"fire\" (literally or figuratively, specially, lightning)<BR><B>KJV:</B> fiery, fire.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4449 (be red), G4451 (burning), G4448 (burn), G4443 (fire), G4447 (of fire), G4450 (red), G4442 (fiery)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πῦρ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H217 אוּר, H784 אֵשׁ, H1200 בְּעֵרָה, H3827 לַבָּה, H3852 לֶהָבָה, H5135 נוּר, H7565 רֶשֶׁף, H8316 שְׂרֵפָה",
    4443: "πυρά (pyrá | poo-rah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4442<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a fire (concretely)<BR><B>KJV:</B> fire.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4442<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4449 (be red), G4451 (burning), G4448 (burn), G4443 (fire), G4447 (of fire), G4450 (red), G4442 (fiery)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πυρά",
    4444: "πύργος (pýrgos | poor'-gos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary word (\"burgh\")<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a tower or castle<BR><B>KJV:</B> tower.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4444 (tower)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πύργος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4026 מִגְדָּל, H4694 מְצוּרָה, H4864 מַשְׂאֵת",
    4445: "πυρέσσω (pyréssō | poo-res'-so)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4443<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be on fire, i.e. (specially), to have a fever<BR><B>KJV:</B> be sick of a fever.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4443<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4445 (be sick of a fever), G546 (threaten), G4446 (fever)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πυρέσσω",
    4446: "πυρετός (pyretós | poo-ret-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4445<BR><B>Strong's:</B> inflamed, i.e. (by implication) feverish (as noun, fever)<BR><B>KJV:</B> fever.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4445<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4445 (be sick of a fever), G546 (threaten), G4446 (fever)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πυρετός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6920 קַדַּחַת",
    4447: "πύρινος (pýrinos | poo'-ree-nos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4443<BR><B>Strong's:</B> fiery, i.e. (by implication) flaming<BR><B>KJV:</B> of fire.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4443<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4449 (be red), G4451 (burning), G4448 (burn), G4443 (fire), G4447 (of fire), G4450 (red), G4442 (fiery)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πύρινος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H784 אֵשׁ",
    4448: "πυρόω (pyróō | poo-ro'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4442<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to kindle, i.e. (passively) to be ignited, glow (literally), be refined (by implication), or (figuratively) to be inflamed (with anger, grief, lust)<BR><B>KJV:</B> burn, fiery, be on fire, try.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4442<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4449 (be red), G4451 (burning), G4448 (burn), G4443 (fire), G4447 (of fire), G4450 (red), G4442 (fiery)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πυρόω, πυρόομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H119 אָדַם, H977 בָּחַר, H6884 צָרַף, H8443 תֹּועָפָה",
    4449: "πυῤῥάζω (pyrrházō | poor-hrad'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4450<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to redden (intransitively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> be red.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4450<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4449 (be red), G4451 (burning), G4448 (burn), G4443 (fire), G4447 (of fire), G4450 (red), G4442 (fiery)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πυῤῥάζω, πυρράζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H125 אֲדַמְדָּם",
    4450: "πυῤῥός (pyrrhós | poor-hros')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4442<BR><B>Strong's:</B> fire-like, i.e. (specially), flame- colored<BR><B>KJV:</B> red.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4442<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4449 (be red), G4451 (burning), G4448 (burn), G4443 (fire), G4447 (of fire), G4450 (red), G4442 (fiery)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πυῤῥός, πυρρός, πυρός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H123 אֱדֹם",
    4451: "πύρωσις (pýrōsis | poo'-ro-sis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4448<BR><B>Strong's:</B> ignition, i.e. (specially), smelting (figuratively, conflagration, calamity as a test)<BR><B>KJV:</B> burning, trial.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4448<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4449 (be red), G4451 (burning), G4448 (burn), G4443 (fire), G4447 (of fire), G4450 (red), G4442 (fiery)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πύρωσις<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3564 כּוּר, H7711 שְׁדֵפָה",
    4452: "-πω (-pō | po)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> another form of the base of G4458<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an enclitic particle of indefiniteness; yet, even; used only in the comparative. See G3369, G3380, G3764, G3768, G4455 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4458<BR><I>See:</I> G3369<BR><I>See:</I> G3380<BR><I>See:</I> G3764<BR><I>See:</I> G3768<BR><I>See:</I> G4455<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4449 (be red), G4451 (burning), G4448 (burn), G4443 (fire), G4447 (of fire), G4450 (red), G4442 (fiery)<BR><B>Variants:</B> -πω, πώς G4803",
    4453: "πωλέω (pōléō | po-leh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably ultimately from πέλομαι (to be busy, to trade)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to barter (as a pedlar), i.e. to sell<BR><B>KJV:</B> sell, whatever is sold.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4449 (be red), G4451 (burning), G4448 (burn), G4443 (fire), G4447 (of fire), G4450 (red), G4442 (fiery)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πωλέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4376 מָכַר",
    4454: "πῶλος (pōlos | po'-los)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a \"foal\" or \"filly\", i.e. (specially), a young ass<BR><B>KJV:</B> colt.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4454 (colt)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πῶλος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1121 בֵּן, H3280 יַעֲלָה, H5895 עַיִר",
    4455: "πώποτε (pṓpote | po'-pot-e)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4452 and G4218<BR><B>Strong's:</B> at any time, i.e. (with negative particle) at no time<BR><B>KJV:</B> at any time, + never (…to any man), + yet, never man.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4452<BR><I>See:</I> G4218<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4454 (colt)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πώποτε",
    4456: "πωρόω (pōróō | po-ro'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently from πῶρος (a kind of stone)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to petrify, i.e. (figuratively) to indurate (render stupid or callous)<BR><B>KJV:</B>  blind, harden.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4457 (blindness), G3975 (wax gross), G4456 (blind)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πωρόω, πηρόω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3543 כָּהָה",
    4457: "πώρωσις (pṓrōsis | po'-ro-sis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4456<BR><B>Strong's:</B> stupidity or callousness<BR><B>KJV:</B> blindness, hardness.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4456<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4457 (blindness), G3975 (wax gross), G4456 (blind)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πώρωσις, πήρωσις",
    4458: "-πώς (-pṓs | poce)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from the base of G4225<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an enclitic particle of indefiniteness of manner; somehow or anyhow; used only in composition<BR><B>KJV:</B> haply, by any (some) means, perhaps. See G1513, G3381 . Compare G4459 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4225<BR><I>See:</I> G4459<BR><I>See:</I> G1513<BR><I>See:</I> G3381<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4457 (blindness), G3975 (wax gross), G4456 (blind)<BR><B>Variants:</B> -πώς, πώς, ποταπῶς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7665 שָׁבַר",
    4459: "πῶς (pōs | poce)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from the base of G4226<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an interrogative particle of manner; in what way? (sometimes the question is indirect, how?); also as exclamation, how much!<BR><B>KJV:</B> how, after (by) what manner (means), that. (Occasionally unexpressed in English).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4226<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4457 (blindness), G3975 (wax gross), G4456 (blind)<BR><B>Variants:</B> πῶς",
    4460: "Ῥαάβ (Rhaáb | hrah-ab')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (G7343)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Raab (i.e. Rachab), a Canaanitess<BR><B>KJV:</B> Rahab. See also H4477 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G7343<BR><I>See:</I> H4477<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4460 (Rahab)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Ῥαάβ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7342 רָחָב, H7343 רָחָב",
    4461: "ῥαββί (rhabbí | hrab-bee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (H7227 with pronominal suffix)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> my master, i.e Rabbi, as an official title of honor<BR><B>KJV:</B> Master, Rabbi.<BR><I>See:</I> H7227<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4462 (Lord), G4461 (Master)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ῥαββί<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7227 רַב",
    4462: "ῥαββονί (rhabboní | hrab-bon-ee'), or ῥαββουνί (rhabbouní | hrab-boo-nee')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Chaldee origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> corresponding to G4461<BR><B>KJV:</B> Lord, Rabboni.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4461<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4462 (Lord), G4461 (Master)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ῥαββονί, ῥαββουνί, ῥαββωνί, ραββουνι",
    4463: "ῥαβδίζω (rhabdízō | hrab-did'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4464<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to strike with a stick, i.e. bastinado<BR><B>KJV:</B> beat (with rods).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4464<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4463 (beat), G4464 (rod), G4465 (serjeant)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ῥαβδίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2251 חָבַט",
    4464: "ῥάβδος (rhábdos | hrab'-dos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G4474<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a stick or wand (as a cudgel, a cane or a baton of royalty)<BR><B>KJV:</B> rod, sceptre, staff.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4474<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4463 (beat), G4464 (rod), G4465 (serjeant)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ῥάβδος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2415 חֹטֵר, H4294 מַטֶּה, H4731 מַקֵּל, H4938 מִשְׁעֵנָה, H6086 עֵץ, H7626 שֵׁבֶט, H8275 שַׁרְבִיט",
