    4619: "σιτιστός (sitistós | sit-is-tos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of G4621<BR><B>Strong's:</B> grained, i.e. fatted<BR><B>KJV:</B> fatling.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4621<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4617 (sift)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σιτιστός",
    4620: "σιτόμετρον (sitómetron | sit-om'-et-ron)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4621 and G3358<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a grain-measure, i.e. (by implication) ration (allowance of food)<BR><B>KJV:</B> portion of meat.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4621<BR><I>See:</I> G3358<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4617 (sift)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σιτόμετρον, σιτομέτριον",
    4621: "σῖτος (sîtos | see'-tos), also plural irregular neuter σῖτα (sîta | see'-tah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> grain, especially wheat<BR><B>KJV:</B> corn, wheat.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4617 (sift)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σῖτος, σιτίον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H400 אֹכֶל, H1249 בַּר, H1430 גָּדִישׁ, H1715 דָּגָן, H2406 חִטָּה, H3899 לֶחֶם, H3899 לֶחֶם, H5669 עָבוּר, H6182 עֲרִיסָה, H7667 שֶׁבֶר",
    4622: "Σιών (Siṓn | see-own')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (H6726)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Sion (i.e. Tsijon), a hill of Jerusalem; figuratively, the Church (militant or triumphant)<BR><B>KJV:</B> Sion.<BR><I>See:</I> H6726<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4622 (Sion)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Σιών<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6726 צִיֹּון",
    4623: "σιωπάω (siōpáō | see-o-pah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from σιωπή (silence, i.e. a hush<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, muteness, i.e. involuntary stillness, or inability to speak; and thus differing from G4602, which is rather a voluntary refusal or indisposition to speak, although the terms are often used synonymously); to be dumb (but not deaf also, like 2974 properly); figuratively, to be calm (as quiet water)<BR><B>KJV:</B> dumb, (hold) peace.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4602<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4622 (Sion)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σιωπάω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1819 דָּמָה, H1826 דָּמַם, H2013 הָסָה, H2308 חָדַל, H2790 חָרַשׁ, H2814 חָשָׁה, H5535 סָכַת, H5956 עָלַם",
    4624: "σκανδαλίζω (skandalízō | skan-dal-id'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4625<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to entrap, i.e. trip up (figuratively, stumble (transitively) or entice to sin, apostasy or displeasure)<BR><B>KJV:</B> (make to) offend.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4625<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4625 (occasion to fall), G4624 (offend)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκανδαλίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3782 כָּשַׁל",
    4625: "σκάνδαλον (skándalon | skan'-dal-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (\"scandal\"); probably from a derivative of G2578<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a trap-stick (bent sapling), i.e. snare (figuratively, cause of displeasure or sin)<BR><B>KJV:</B> occasion to fall (of stumbling), offence, thing that offends, stumblingblock.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2578<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4625 (occasion to fall), G4624 (offend)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκάνδαλον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1848 דׇּפִי, H3689 כֶּסֶל, H4170 מֹוקֵשׁ, H4383 מִכְשֹׁול",
    4626: "σκάπτω (skáptō | skap'-to)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to dig<BR><B>KJV:</B> dig.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4625 (occasion to fall), G4624 (offend)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκάπτω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5737 עֲדַר",
    4627: "σκάφη (skáphē | skaf'-ay)<BR><BR><B>Strong's:</B> a \"skiff\" (as if dug out), or yawl (carried aboard a large vessel for landing)<BR><B>KJV:</B> boat.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4625 (occasion to fall), G4624 (offend)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκάφη",
    4628: "σκέλος (skélos | skel'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently from σκέλλω<BR><B>Strong's:</B> (to parch; through the idea of leanness); the leg (as lank)<BR><B>KJV:</B> leg.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4625 (occasion to fall), G4624 (offend)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκέλος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3409 יָרֵךְ, H3767 כָּרָע, H7176 קֶרֶת, H7272 רֶגֶל, H7785 שֹׁוק",
    4629: "σκέπασμα (sképasma | skep'-as-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of σκέπας (a covering<BR><B>Strong's:</B> perhaps akin to the base of G4649 through the idea of noticeableness); clothing<BR><B>KJV:</B> raiment.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4649<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4625 (occasion to fall), G4624 (offend)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκέπασμα",
    4630: "Σκευᾶς (Skeuâs | skyoo-as')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> left-handed; Scevas (i.e. Scævus), an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Sceva.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4625 (occasion to fall), G4624 (offend)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Σκευᾶς",
    4631: "σκευή (skeuḗ | skyoo-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4632<BR><B>Strong's:</B> furniture, i.e. spare tackle<BR><B>KJV:</B> tackling.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4632<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4632 (goods), G4631 (tackling)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκευή",
    4632: "σκεῦος (skeûos | skyoo'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain affinity<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a vessel, implement, equipment or apparatus (literally or figuratively [specially, a wife as contributing to the usefulness of the husband])<BR><B>KJV:</B> goods, sail, stuff, vessel.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4632 (goods), G4631 (tackling)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκεῦος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3627 כְּלִי, H4478 מָן",
    4633: "σκηνή (skēnḗ | skay-nay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently akin to G4632 and G4639<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a tent or cloth hut (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> habitation, tabernacle.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4639<BR><I>See:</I> G4632<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2681 (lodge), G4638 (tabernacle), G4635 (tent-maker), G4637 (dwell), G4636 (tabernacle), G4633 (habitation), G1981 (rest upon), G4634 (tabernacles)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκηνή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H168 אֹהֶל, H2691 חָצֵר, H4908 מִשְׁכָּן, H5520 סֹךְ, H5521 סֻכָּה",
    4634: "σκηνοπηγία (skēnopēgía | skay-nop-ayg-ee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4636 and G4078<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the Festival of Tabernacles (so called from the custom of erecting booths for temporary homes)<BR><B>KJV:</B> tabernacles.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4636<BR><I>See:</I> G4078<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2681 (lodge), G4638 (tabernacle), G4635 (tent-maker), G4637 (dwell), G4636 (tabernacle), G4633 (habitation), G1981 (rest upon), G4634 (tabernacles)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκηνοπηγία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5521 סֻכָּה",
    4635: "σκηνοποιός (skēnopoiós | skay-nop-oy-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4633 and G4160<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a manufacturer of tents<BR><B>KJV:</B> tent-maker.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4633<BR><I>See:</I> G4160<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2681 (lodge), G4638 (tabernacle), G4635 (tent-maker), G4637 (dwell), G4636 (tabernacle), G4633 (habitation), G1981 (rest upon), G4634 (tabernacles)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκηνοποιός",
    4636: "σκῆνος (skēnos | skay'-nos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4633<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a hut or temporary residence, i.e. (figuratively) the human body (as the abode of the spirit)<BR><B>KJV:</B> tabernacle.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4633<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2681 (lodge), G4638 (tabernacle), G4635 (tent-maker), G4637 (dwell), G4636 (tabernacle), G4633 (habitation), G1981 (rest upon), G4634 (tabernacles)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκῆνος",
    4637: "σκηνόω (skēnóō | skay-no'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4636<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to tent or encamp, i.e. (figuratively) to occupy (as a mansion) or (specially), to reside (as God did in the Tabernacle of old, a symbol of protection and communion)<BR><B>KJV:</B>  dwell.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4636<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2681 (lodge), G4638 (tabernacle), G4635 (tent-maker), G4637 (dwell), G4636 (tabernacle), G4633 (habitation), G1981 (rest upon), G4634 (tabernacles)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκηνόω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H167 אָהַל, H7931 שָׁכַן",
