    4639: "σκιά (skiá | skee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"shade\" or a shadow (literally or figuratively (darkness of error or an adumbration))<BR><B>KJV:</B>  shadow.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G644 (shadow), G4639 (shadow), G1982 (overshadow)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκιά<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6738 צֵל, H6757 צַלְמָוֶת",
    4640: "σκιρτάω (skirtáō | skeer-tah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> akin to σκαίρω (to skip)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to jump, i.e. sympathetically move (as the quickening of a fetus)<BR><B>KJV:</B> leap (for joy).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4640 (leap)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκιρτάω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6335 פּוּשׁ, H7533 רָצַץ, H7540 רָקַד",
    4641: "σκληροκαρδία (sklērokardía | sklay-rok-ar-dee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of a compound of G4642 and G2588<BR><B>Strong's:</B> hard-heartedness, i.e. (specially), destitution of (spiritual) perception<BR><B>KJV:</B> hardness of heart.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4642<BR><I>See:</I> G2588<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4641 (hardness of heart), G2589 (which knowest the hearts), G2588 (heart)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκληροκαρδία",
