    4643: "σκληρότης (sklērótēs | sklay-rot'-ace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4642<BR><B>Strong's:</B> callousness, i.e. (figuratively) stubbornness<BR><B>KJV:</B> hardness.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4642<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4641 (hardness of heart), G4643 (hardness), G4644 (stiffnecked), G4642 (fierce), G4645 (harden)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκληρότης<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2742 חֲרוּץ, H4170 מֹוקֵשׁ, H7190 קְשִׁי",
    4644: "σκληροτράχηλος (sklērotráchēlos | sklay-rot-rakh'-ay-los)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4642 and G5137<BR><B>Strong's:</B> hardnaped, i.e. (figuratively) obstinate<BR><B>KJV:</B> stiffnecked.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4642<BR><I>See:</I> G5137<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4641 (hardness of heart), G4643 (hardness), G4644 (stiffnecked), G4642 (fierce), G4645 (harden)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκληροτράχηλος",
    4645: "σκληρύνω (sklērýnō | sklay-roo'-no)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4642<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to indurate, i.e. (figuratively) render stubborn<BR><B>KJV:</B> harden.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4642<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4641 (hardness of heart), G4643 (hardness), G4644 (stiffnecked), G4642 (fierce), G4645 (harden)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκληρύνω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2388 חָזַק, H3513 כָּבַד, H7185 קָשָׁה, H7188 קָשַׁח",
    4646: "σκολιός (skoliós | skol-ee-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G4628<BR><B>Strong's:</B> warped, i.e. winding; figuratively, perverse<BR><B>KJV:</B> crooked, froward, untoward.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4628<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4646 (crooked)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκολιός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2019 הֲפַכְפַּךְ, H5637 סָרַר, H6121 עָקֹב, H6129 עֲקַלָּתֹון, H6140 עָקַשׁ, H6141 עִקֵּשׁ, H6141 עִקֵּשׁ, H6617 פָּתַל, H8417 תׇּהֳלָה, H8419 תַּהְפֻּכָה",
    4647: "σκόλοψ (skólops | skol'-ops)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> perhaps from the base of G4628 and G3700<BR><B>Strong's:</B> withered at the front, i.e. a point or prickle (figuratively, a bodily annoyance or disability)<BR><B>KJV:</B> thorn.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4628<BR><I>See:</I> G3700<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4647 (thorn)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκόλοψ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5518 סִיר, H5544 סִלֹּון, H7899 שֵׂךְ",
    4648: "σκοπέω (skopéō | skop-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4649<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to take aim at (spy), i.e. (figuratively) regard<BR><B>KJV:</B> consider, take heed, look at (on), mark. Compare G3700 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4649<BR><I>See:</I> G3700<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4648 (consider), G2685 (spy), G2684 (spy out), G4649 (mark)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκοπέω",
    4649: "σκοπός (skopós | skop-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from σκέπτομαι (to peer about (\"skeptic\")<BR><B>Strong's:</B> perhaps akin to G4626 through the idea of concealment; compare G4629); a watch (sentry or scout), i.e. (by implication) a goal<BR><B>KJV:</B> mark.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4626<BR><I>See:</I> G4629<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4648 (consider), G2685 (spy), G2684 (spy out), G4649 (mark)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκοπός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4307 מַטָּרָא, H4906 מַשְׂכִּית, H6822 צָפָה",
    4650: "σκορπίζω (skorpízō | skor-pid'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently from the same as G4651 (through the idea of penetrating)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to dissipate, i.e. (figuratively) put to flight, waste, be liberal<BR><B>KJV:</B> disperse abroad, scatter (abroad).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4651<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4650 (disperse abroad), G1287 (disperse)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκορπίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2114 זוּר, H2219 זָרָה, H5287 נָעַר, H6327 פּוּץ, H6340 פָּזַר, H6504 פָּרַד",
    4651: "σκορπίος (skorpíos | skor-pee'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from an obsolete σκέρπω (perhaps strengthened from the base of G4649 and meaning to pierce)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a \"scorpion\" (from its sting)<BR><B>KJV:</B> scorpion.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4649<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4650 (disperse abroad), G1287 (disperse)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκορπίος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6137 עַקְרָב",
    4652: "σκοτεινός (skoteinós | skot-i-nos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4655<BR><B>Strong's:</B> opaque, i.e. (figuratively) benighted<BR><B>KJV:</B> dark, full of darkness.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4655<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4652 (dark), G4653 (dark), G4655 (darkness), G4654 (darken), G4656 (be full of darkness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκοτεινός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H653 אֲפֵלָה, H2822 חֹשֶׁךְ, H4426 מְלִיצָה, H5399 נֶשֶׁף, H5642 סְתַר",
    4653: "σκοτία (skotía | skot-ee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4655<BR><B>Strong's:</B> dimness, obscurity (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> dark(-ness).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4655<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4652 (dark), G4653 (dark), G4655 (darkness), G4654 (darken), G4656 (be full of darkness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκοτία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H652 אֹפֶל, H2821 חָשַׁךְ",
    4654: "σκοτίζω (skotízō | skot-id-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4655<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to obscure (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> darken.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4655<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4652 (dark), G4653 (dark), G4655 (darkness), G4654 (darken), G4656 (be full of darkness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκοτίζω, σκοτίζομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2821 חָשַׁךְ",
