    4660: "σκύλλω (skýllō | skool'-lo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to flay, i.e. (figuratively) to harass<BR><B>KJV:</B> trouble(self).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4659 (of a sad countenance)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκύλλω",
    4661: "σκῦλον (skŷlon | skoo'-lon)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter from G4660<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something stripped (as a hide), i.e. booty<BR><B>KJV:</B> spoil.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4660<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4659 (of a sad countenance)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκῦλον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H957 בַּז, H4455 מַלְקֹוחַ, H7998 שָׁלָל",
