    4663: "σκώληξ (skṓlēx | sko'-lakes)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a grub, maggot or earth-worm<BR><B>KJV:</B> worm.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4663 (worm), G4662 (eaten of worms)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σκώληξ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7415 רִמָּה, H8438 תֹּולָע",
    4664: "σμαράγδινος (smarágdinos | smar-ag'-dee-nos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4665<BR><B>Strong's:</B> consisting of emerald<BR><B>KJV:</B> emerald.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4665<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4663 (worm), G4662 (eaten of worms)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σμαράγδινος",
    4665: "σμάραγδος (smáragdos | smar'-ag-dos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the emerald or green gem so called<BR><B>KJV:</B> emerald.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4663 (worm), G4662 (eaten of worms)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σμάραγδος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H923 בַּהַט, H1304 בָּרֶקֶת, H3095 יַהֲלֹם, H7718 שֹׁהַם",
    4666: "σμύρνα (smýrna | smoor'-nah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently strengthened for G3464<BR><B>Strong's:</B> myrrh<BR><B>KJV:</B> myrrh.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3464<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4666 (myrrh), G4669 (mingle with myrrh)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σμύρνα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4753 מֹר",
    4667: "Σμύρνα (Smýrna | smoor'-nah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> the same as G4666<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Smyrna, a place in Asia Minor<BR><B>KJV:</B> Smyrna.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4666<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4668 (in Smyrna), G4667 (Smyrna)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Σμύρνα, Ζμύρνα",
    4668: "Σμυρναῖος (Smyrnaîos | smoor-nah'-yos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4667<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Smyrnæan<BR><B>KJV:</B> in Smyrna.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4667<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4668 (in Smyrna), G4667 (Smyrna)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Σμυρναῖος G5045",
    4669: "σμυρνίζω (smyrnízō | smoor-nid'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4667<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to tincture with myrrh, i.e. embitter (as a narcotic)<BR><B>KJV:</B> mingle with myrrh.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4667<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4666 (myrrh), G4669 (mingle with myrrh)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σμυρνίζω",
    4670: "Σόδομα (Sódoma | sod'-om-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> plural of Hebrew origin (H5467)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Sodoma (i.e. Sedom), a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Sodom.<BR><I>See:</I> H5467<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4666 (myrrh), G4669 (mingle with myrrh)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Σόδομα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5467 סְדֹם",
    4671: "σοί (soí | soy)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> dative case of G4771<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to thee<BR><B>KJV:</B> thee, thine own, thou, thy.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4771<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4666 (myrrh), G4669 (mingle with myrrh)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σοί, σύ",
    4672: "Σολομών (Solomṓn | sol-om-one')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (H8010)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Solomon (i.e. Shelomoh), the son of David<BR><B>KJV:</B> Solomon.<BR><I>See:</I> H8010<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4672 (Solomon)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Σολομών, Σαλωμών, Σολομῶν<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H8010 שְׁלֹמֹה",
    4673: "σορός (sorós | sor-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably akin to the base of G4987<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a funereal receptacle (urn, coffin), i.e. (by analogy) a bier<BR><B>KJV:</B> bier.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4987<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4672 (Solomon)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σορός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H727 אָרֹון",
    4674: "σός (sós | sos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4771<BR><B>Strong's:</B> thine<BR><B>KJV:</B> thine (own), thy (friend).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4771<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4672 (Solomon)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σός",
    4675: "σοῦ (soû | soo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> genitive case of G4771<BR><B>Strong's:</B> of thee, thy<BR><B>KJV:</B> X home, thee, thine (own), thou, thy.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4771<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4672 (Solomon)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σοῦ, σύ",
    4676: "σουδάριον (soudárion | soo-dar'-ee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a sudarium (sweat-cloth), i.e. towel (for wiping the perspiration from the face, or binding the face of a corpse)<BR><B>KJV:</B> handkerchief, napkin.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4672 (Solomon)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σουδάριον",
    4677: "Σουσάννα (Sousánna | soo-san'-nah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (H7799 feminine)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> lily; Susannah (i.e. Shoshannah), an Israelitess<BR><B>KJV:</B> Susanna.<BR><I>See:</I> H7799<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4672 (Solomon)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Σουσάννα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7799 שׁוּשַׁן",
    4678: "σοφία (sophía | sof-ee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4680<BR><B>Strong's:</B> wisdom (higher or lower, worldly or spiritual)<BR><B>KJV:</B> wisdom.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4680<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4679 (cunningly devised), G4678 (wisdom), G4680 (wise)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σοφία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H999 בִּינָה, H1847 דַּעַת, H2451 חׇכְמָה, H4148 מוּסָר, H4284 מַחֲשָׁבָה, H7922 שֶׂכֶל",
    4679: "σοφίζω (sophízō | sof-id'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4680<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to render wise; in a sinister acceptation, to form \"sophisms\", i.e. continue plausible error<BR><B>KJV:</B> cunningly devised, make wise.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4680<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4679 (cunningly devised), G4678 (wisdom), G4680 (wise)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σοφίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H995 בִּין, H2450 חָכָם",
    4680: "σοφός (sophós | sof-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> akin to σαφής (clear)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> wise (in a most general application)<BR><B>KJV:</B> wise. Compare G5429 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5429<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4679 (cunningly devised), G4678 (wisdom), G4680 (wise)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σοφός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H995 בִּין, H2450 חָכָם, H2450 חָכָם, H2450 חָכָם, H2748 חַרְטֹם, H5228 נָכֹחַ",
    4681: "Σπανία (Spanía | span-ee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably of foreign origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Spania, a region of Europe<BR><B>KJV:</B> Spain.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4679 (cunningly devised), G4678 (wisdom), G4680 (wise)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Σπανία",
    4682: "σπαράσσω (sparássō | spar-as'-so)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> prolongation from σπαίρω (to grasp<BR><B>Strong's:</B> apparently strengthened from G4685 through the idea of spasmodic contraction); to mangle, i.e. convluse with epilepsy<BR><B>KJV:</B> rend, tear.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4685<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4679 (cunningly devised), G4678 (wisdom), G4680 (wise)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σπαράσσω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1607 גָּעַשׁ, H1993 הָמָה, H7993 שָׁלַךְ",
    4683: "σπαργανόω (sparganóō | spar-gan-o'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from σπάργανον (a strip<BR><B>Strong's:</B> from a derivative of the base of G4682 meaning to strap or wrap with strips); to swathe (an infant after the Oriental custom)<BR><B>KJV:</B> wrap in swaddling clothes.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4682<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4679 (cunningly devised), G4678 (wisdom), G4680 (wise)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σπαργανόω",
    4684: "σπαταλάω (spataláō | spat-al-ah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from σπατάλη (luxury)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be voluptuous<BR><B>KJV:</B> live in pleasure, be wanton.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4679 (cunningly devised), G4678 (wisdom), G4680 (wise)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σπαταλάω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H8252 שָׁקַט",
    4685: "σπάω (spáō | spah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to draw<BR><B>KJV:</B> draw (out).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4679 (cunningly devised), G4678 (wisdom), G4680 (wise)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σπάω, σπάομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4803 מָרַט, H5423 נָתַק, H5782 עוּר, H6605 פָּתַח, H8025 שָׁלַף",
    4686: "σπεῖρα (speîra | spi'-rah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of immediate Latin origin, but ultimately a derivative of G138 in the sense of its cognate G1507<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a coil (spira, \"spire\"), i.e. (figuratively) a mass of men (a Roman military cohort; also (by analogy) a squad of Levitical janitors)<BR><B>KJV:</B> band.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G1507<BR><I>See:</I> G138<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4679 (cunningly devised), G4678 (wisdom), G4680 (wise)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σπεῖρα",
    4687: "σπείρω (speírō | spi'-ro)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably strengthened from G4685 (through the idea of extending)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to scatter, i.e. sow (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> sow(- er), receive seed.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4685<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4586 (grave), G4687 (sow)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σπείρω, ἐπισπείρω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2219 זָרָה, H2232 זָרַע, H2236 זָרַק, H5080 נָדַח, H6327 פּוּץ, H6340 פָּזַר, H7760 שׂוּם",
    4688: "σπεκουλάτωρ (spekoulátōr | spek-oo-lat'-ore)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a speculator, i.e. military scout (spy or (by extension) life-guardsman)<BR><B>KJV:</B> executioner.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4586 (grave), G4687 (sow)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σπεκουλάτωρ",
    4689: "σπένδω (spéndō | spen'-do)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to pour out as a libation, i.e. (figuratively) to devote (one's life or blood, as a sacrifice) (\"spend\")<BR><B>KJV:</B> (be ready to) be offered.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4689 (be offered)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σπένδω, σπένδομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5258 נָסַךְ",
    4690: "σπέρμα (spérma | sper'-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4687<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something sown, i.e. seed (including the male \"sperm\"); by implication, offspring; specially, a remnant (figuratively, as if kept over for planting)<BR><B>KJV:</B> issue, seed.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4687<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4703 (seed), G4691 (babbler), G4702 (corn), G4690 (issue), G4701 (seed), G4687 (sow)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σπέρμα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H319 אַחֲרִית, H1121 בֵּן, H1320 בָּשָׂר, H2233 זֶרַע, H5209 נִין, H5220 נֶכֶד",
    4691: "σπερμολόγος (spermológos | sper-mol-og'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4690 and G3004<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a seed-picker (as the crow), i.e. (figuratively) a sponger, loafer (specially, a gossip or trifler in talk)<BR><B>KJV:</B> babbler.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4690<BR><I>See:</I> G3004<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4703 (seed), G4691 (babbler), G4702 (corn), G4690 (issue), G4701 (seed), G4687 (sow)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σπερμολόγος",
    4692: "σπεύδω (speúdō | spyoo'-do)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably strengthened from G4228<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to \"speed\" (\"study\"), i.e. urge on (diligently or earnestly); by implication, to await eagerly<BR><B>KJV:</B> (make, with) haste unto.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4228<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4703 (seed), G4691 (babbler), G4702 (corn), G4690 (issue), G4701 (seed), G4687 (sow)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σπεύδω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H553 אָמַץ, H926 בָּהַל, H1765 דָּחַף, H2363 חוּשׁ, H2648 חָפַז, H4116 מָהַר",
    4693: "σπήλαιον (spḗlaion | spay'-lah-yon)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a presumed derivative of σπέος (a grotto)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a cavern; by implication, a hiding-place or resort<BR><B>KJV:</B> cave, den.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4703 (seed), G4691 (babbler), G4702 (corn), G4690 (issue), G4701 (seed), G4687 (sow)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σπήλαιον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4631 מְעָרָה, H5341 נָצַר, H5595 סָפָה",
    4694: "σπιλάς (spilás | spee-las')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a ledge or reef of rock in the sea<BR><B>KJV:</B> spot (by confusion with G4696).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4696<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4703 (seed), G4691 (babbler), G4702 (corn), G4690 (issue), G4701 (seed), G4687 (sow)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σπιλάς",
    4695: "σπιλόω (spilóō | spee-lo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4696<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to stain or soil (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> defile, spot.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4696<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4703 (seed), G4691 (babbler), G4702 (corn), G4690 (issue), G4701 (seed), G4687 (sow)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σπιλόω",
    4696: "σπίλος (spílos | spee'-los)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a stain or blemish, i.e. (figuratively) defect, disgrace<BR><B>KJV:</B> spot.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4703 (seed), G4691 (babbler), G4702 (corn), G4690 (issue), G4701 (seed), G4687 (sow)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σπίλος, σπῖλος",
    4697: "σπλαγχνίζομαι (splanchnízomai | splangkh-nid'-zom-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> middle voice from G4698<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to have the bowels yearn, i.e. (figuratively) feel sympathy, to pity<BR><B>KJV:</B> have (be moved with) compassion.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4698<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2155 (pitiful), G4697 (have compassion), G4698 (bowels), G4184 (very pitiful)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σπλαγχνίζομαι",
    4698: "σπλάγχνον (splánchnon | splangkh'-non)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably strengthened from σπλήν (the \"spleen\")<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an intestine (plural); figuratively, pity or sympathy<BR><B>KJV:</B> bowels, inward affection, + tender mercy.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2155 (pitiful), G4697 (have compassion), G4698 (bowels), G4184 (very pitiful)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σπλάγχνον, σπλάγχνα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H990 בֶּטֶן, H7356 רַחַם",
    4699: "σπόγγος (spóngos | spong'-gos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> perhaps of foreign origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a \"sponge\"<BR><B>KJV:</B> spunge.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2155 (pitiful), G4697 (have compassion), G4698 (bowels), G4184 (very pitiful)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σπόγγος",
