    4712: "στάδιον (stádion | stad'-ee-on), or masculine (in plural) στάδιος (stádios | stad'-ee-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G2476 (as fixed)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a stade or certain measure of distance; by implication, a stadium or race-course<BR><B>KJV:</B> furlong, race.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2476<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4709 (diligently), G4710 (business), G4706 (very diligently), G4705 (diligent), G4707 (more diligent), G4708 (more carefully), G4704 (do diligence)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στάδιον",
    4713: "στάμνος (stámnos | stam'-nos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G2476 (as stationary)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a jar or earthen tank<BR><B>KJV:</B> pot.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2476<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4709 (diligently), G4710 (business), G4706 (very diligently), G4705 (diligent), G4707 (more diligent), G4708 (more carefully), G4704 (do diligence)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στάμνος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1228 בַּקְבֻּק, H6803 צִנְצֶנֶת",
