    4729: "στενοχωρέω (stenochōréō | sten-okh-o-reh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as G4730<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to hem in closely, i.e. (figuratively) cramp<BR><B>KJV:</B> distress, straiten.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4730<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4730 (anguish), G4728 (strait), G4729 (distress)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στενοχωρέω, στενοχωρέομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H213 אוּץ, H509 אָלַץ, H6887 צָרַר, H7114 קָצַר",
    4730: "στενοχωρία (stenochōría | sten-okh-o-ree'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a compound of G4728 and G5561<BR><B>Strong's:</B> narrowness of room, i.e. (figuratively) calamity<BR><B>KJV:</B> anguish, distress.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4728<BR><I>See:</I> G5561<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4730 (anguish), G4728 (strait), G4729 (distress)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στενοχωρία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4692 מָצֹור, H6695 צֹוק",
