    4733: "στερέωμα (steréōma | ster-eh'-o-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4732<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something established, i.e. (abstractly) confirmation (stability)<BR><B>KJV:</B> stedfastness.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4732<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4732 (establish), G4731 (stedfast), G4733 (stedfastness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στερέωμα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5553 סֶלַע, H7549 רָקִיעַ, H7834 שַׁחַק",
    4734: "Στεφανᾶς (Stephanâs | stef-an-as')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably contraction for στεφανωτός (crowned<BR><B>Strong's:</B> from G4737); Stephanas, a Christian<BR><B>KJV:</B> Stephanas.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4737<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4732 (establish), G4731 (stedfast), G4733 (stedfastness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Στεφανᾶς",
    4735: "στέφανος (stéphanos | stef'-an-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an apparently primary στέφω (to twine or wreathe)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a chaplet (as a badge of royalty, a prize in the public games or a symbol of honor generally; but more conspicuous and elaborate than the simple fillet, G1238), literally or figuratively<BR><B>KJV:</B> crown.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G1238<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4737 (crown), G4735 (crown)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στέφανος, στέφανοσ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H73 אַבְנֵט, H3632 כָּלִיל, H3880 לִוְיָה, H5850 עֲטָרָה",
    4736: "Στέφανος (Stéphanos | stef'-an-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> the same as G4735<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Stephanus, a Christian<BR><B>KJV:</B> Stephen.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4735<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4737 (crown), G4735 (crown)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Στέφανος, Στέφανοσ",
    4737: "στεφανόω (stephanóō | stef-an-o'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4735<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to adorn with an honorary wreath (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> crown.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4735<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4737 (crown), G4735 (crown)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στεφανόω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6279 עָתַר",
    4738: "στῆθος (stēthos | stay'-thos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G2476 (as standing prominently)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the (entire external) bosom, i.e. chest<BR><B>KJV:</B> breast.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2476<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4737 (crown), G4735 (crown)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στῆθος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1512 גָּחֹון, H2306 חֲדִי, H3820 לֵב",
    4739: "στήκω (stḗkō | stay'-ko)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the perfect tense of G2476<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be stationary, i.e. (figuratively) to persevere<BR><B>KJV:</B> stand (fast).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2476<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4739 (stand)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στήκω",
    4740: "στηριγμός (stērigmós | stay-rig-mos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4741<BR><B>Strong's:</B> stability (figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> stedfastness.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4741<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4740 (stedfastness), G4741 (fix), G793 (unstable), G1991 (confirm)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στηριγμός",
    4741: "στηρίζω (stērízō | stay-rid'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a presumed derivative of G2476 (like G4731)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to set fast, i.e. (literally) to turn resolutely in a certain direction, or (figuratively) to confirm<BR><B>KJV:</B> fix, (e-)stablish, stedfastly set, strengthen.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2476<BR><I>See:</I> G4731<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4740 (stedfastness), G4741 (fix), G793 (unstable), G1991 (confirm)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στηρίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H530 אֱמוּנָה, H5307 נָפַל, H5324 נָצַב, H5414 נָתַן, H5426 נְתַר, H5564 סָמַךְ, H5582 סָעַד, H5596 סָפַח, H7760 שׂוּם, H8551 תָּמַךְ, H8628 תָּקַע",
    4742: "στίγμα (stígma | stig'-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a primary στίζω (to \"stick\", i.e. prick)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a mark incised or punched (for recognition of ownership), i.e. (figuratively) scar of service<BR><B>KJV:</B> mark.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4742 (mark)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στίγμα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5351 נְקֻדָּה",
    4743: "στιγμή (stigmḗ | stig-may')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of G4742<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a point of time, i.e. an instant<BR><B>KJV:</B> moment.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4742<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4742 (mark)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στιγμή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6621 פֶּתַע",
    4744: "στίλβω (stílbō | stil'-bo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to gleam, i.e. flash intensely<BR><B>KJV:</B> shining.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4744 (shining)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στίλβω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3851 לַהַב, H6668 צָהַב, H7043 קָלַל",
    4745: "στοά (stoá | sto-ah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from G2476<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a colonnade or interior piazza<BR><B>KJV:</B> porch.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2476<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4744 (shining)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στοά, Στοά<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4201 מְזוּזָה, H6268 עַתִּיק, H7531 רִצְפָּה",
    4746: "στοιβάς (stoibás | stoy-bas')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a primary στείβω (to \"step\" or \"stamp\")<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a spread (as if tramped flat) of loose materials for a couch, i.e. (by implication) a bough of a tree so employed<BR><B>KJV:</B> branch.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4744 (shining)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στοιβάς, στιβάς",
