    4750: "στόμα (stóma | stom'-a)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably strengthened from a presumed derivative of the base of G5114<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the mouth (as if a gash in the face); by implication, language (and its relations); figuratively, an opening (in the earth); specially, the front or edge (of a weapon)<BR><B>KJV:</B> edge, face, mouth.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5114<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4750 (edge)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στόμα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1697 דָּבָר, H6310 פֶּה, H6433 פֻּם, H8193 שָׂפָה",
    4751: "στόμαχος (stómachos | stom'-akh-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4750<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an orifice (the gullet), i.e. (specially), the \"stomach\"<BR><B>KJV:</B> stomach.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4750<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4750 (edge)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στόμαχος",
    4752: "στρατεία (strateía | strat-i'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4754<BR><B>Strong's:</B> military service, i.e. (figuratively) the apostolic career (as one of hardship and danger)<BR><B>KJV:</B> warfare.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4754<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4760 (army), G4752 (warfare), G4759 (captain of the guard), G4753 (army), G4757 (soldier), G4754 (soldier), G4756 (host), G4758 (choose to be a soldier), G4755 (captain)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στρατεία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2428 חַיִל, H4475 מֶמְשָׁלָה, H4853 מַשָּׂא, H6635 צָבָא",
    4753: "στράτευμα (stráteuma | strat'-yoo-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4754<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an armament, i.e. (by implication) a body of troops (more or less extensive or systematic)<BR><B>KJV:</B> army, soldier, man of war.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4754<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4760 (army), G4752 (warfare), G4759 (captain of the guard), G4753 (army), G4757 (soldier), G4754 (soldier), G4756 (host), G4758 (choose to be a soldier), G4755 (captain)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στράτευμα",
    4754: "στρατεύομαι (strateúomai | strat-yoo'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> middle voice from the base of G4756<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to serve in a military campaign; figuratively, to execute the apostolate (with its arduous duties and functions), to contend with carnal inclinations<BR><B>KJV:</B> soldier, (go to) war(-fare).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4756<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4760 (army), G4752 (warfare), G4759 (captain of the guard), G4753 (army), G4757 (soldier), G4754 (soldier), G4756 (host), G4758 (choose to be a soldier), G4755 (captain)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στρατεύομαι, στρατεύω",
    4755: "στρατηγός (stratēgós | strat-ay-gos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G4756 and G71 or G2233<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a general, i.e. (by implication or analogy) a (military) governor (prætor), the chief (præfect) of the (Levitical) temple-wardens<BR><B>KJV:</B> captain, magistrate.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4756<BR><I>See:</I> G71<BR><I>See:</I> G2233<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4760 (army), G4752 (warfare), G4759 (captain of the guard), G4753 (army), G4757 (soldier), G4754 (soldier), G4756 (host), G4758 (choose to be a soldier), G4755 (captain)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στρατηγός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H323 אֲחַשְׁדַּרְפַּן, H4428 מֶלֶךְ, H5461 סָגָן, H5461 סָגָן, H5633 סֶרֶן, H8269 שַׂר",
    4756: "στρατιά (stratiá | strat-ee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of a derivative of στρατός (an army<BR><B>Strong's:</B> from the base of G4766, as encamped); camp-likeness, i.e. an army, i.e. (figuratively) the angels, the celestial luminaries<BR><B>KJV:</B> host.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4766<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4760 (army), G4752 (warfare), G4759 (captain of the guard), G4753 (army), G4757 (soldier), G4754 (soldier), G4756 (host), G4758 (choose to be a soldier), G4755 (captain)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στρατιά<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2428 חַיִל, H4475 מֶמְשָׁלָה, H4853 מַשָּׂא, H6635 צָבָא",
    4757: "στρατιώτης (stratiṓtēs | strat-ee-o'-tace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a presumed derivative of the same as G4756<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a camper-out, i.e. a (common) warrior (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> soldier.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4756<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4760 (army), G4752 (warfare), G4759 (captain of the guard), G4753 (army), G4757 (soldier), G4754 (soldier), G4756 (host), G4758 (choose to be a soldier), G4755 (captain)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στρατιώτης<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3318 יָצָא, H4102 מָהַהּ, H6633 צָבָא",
