    4760: "στρατόπεδον (stratópedon | strat-op'-ed-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G4756 and the same as G3977<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a camping-ground, i.e. (by implication) a body of troops<BR><B>KJV:</B> army.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4756<BR><I>See:</I> G3977<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4760 (army), G4752 (warfare), G4759 (captain of the guard), G4753 (army), G4757 (soldier), G4754 (soldier), G4756 (host), G4758 (choose to be a soldier), G4755 (captain)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στρατόπεδον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2428 חַיִל",
    4761: "στρεβλόω (streblóō | streb-lo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of G4762<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to wrench, i.e. (specially), to torture (by the rack), but only figuratively, to pervert<BR><B>KJV:</B>  wrest.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4762<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4760 (army), G4752 (warfare), G4759 (captain of the guard), G4753 (army), G4757 (soldier), G4754 (soldier), G4756 (host), G4758 (choose to be a soldier), G4755 (captain)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στρεβλόω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6617 פָּתַל",
    4762: "στρέφω (stréphō | stref'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> strengthened from the base of G5157<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to twist, i.e. turn quite around or reverse (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> convert, turn (again, back again, self, self about).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5157<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1994 (come again), G390 (abide), G1995 (conversion), G2692 (overthrow), G1294 (perverse), G2690 (overthrow), G4762 (convert), G3344 (pervert), G654 (bring again), G391 (conversation)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στρέφω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1550 גָּלִיל, H1641 גָּרַר, H2015 הָפַךְ, H5437 סָבַב, H6437 פָּנָה, H7613 שְׂאֵת, H7725 שׁוּב",
    4763: "στρηνιάω (strēniáō | stray-nee-ah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a presumed derivative of G4764<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be luxurious<BR><B>KJV:</B> live deliciously.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4764<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1994 (come again), G390 (abide), G1995 (conversion), G2692 (overthrow), G1294 (perverse), G2690 (overthrow), G4762 (convert), G3344 (pervert), G654 (bring again), G391 (conversation)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στρηνιάω",
    4764: "στρῆνος (strēnos | stray'-nos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> akin to G4731<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a \"straining\", \"strenuousness\" or \"strength\", i.e. (figuratively) luxury (voluptuousness)<BR><B>KJV:</B> delicacy.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4731<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1994 (come again), G390 (abide), G1995 (conversion), G2692 (overthrow), G1294 (perverse), G2690 (overthrow), G4762 (convert), G3344 (pervert), G654 (bring again), G391 (conversation)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στρῆνος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7600 שַׁאֲנָן",
    4765: "στρουθίον (strouthíon | stroo-thee'-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> diminutive of στρουθός (a sparrow)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a little sparrow<BR><B>KJV:</B> sparrow.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4765 (sparrow)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στρουθίον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3283 יָעֵן, H5698 עֶגְלָה, H6833 צִפֹּור",
    4766: "στρώννυμι (strṓnnymi | strone'-noo-mee), or simpler στρωννύω (strōnnýō | strone-noo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> prolongation from a still simpler στρόω (stróō | stro'-o)<BR>, (used only as an alternate in certain tenses) (probably akin to G4731 through the idea of positing)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to \"strew,\" i.e. spread (as a carpet or couch)<BR><B>KJV:</B> make bed, furnish, spread, strew.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4731<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4765 (sparrow)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στρώννυμι, στρωννύω, στρωννύω/στρώννυμι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2490 חָלַל, H3318 יָצָא, H3519 כָּבֹוד, H4272 מָחַץ, H4881 מְשׂוּכָה, H6428 פָּלַשׁ, H7502 רָפַד",
    4767: "στυγνητός (stygnētós | stoog-nay-tos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of an obsolete apparently primary στύγω (to hate)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> hated, i.e. odious<BR><B>KJV:</B> hateful.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4765 (sparrow)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στυγνητός, στυγητός",
    4768: "στυγνάζω (stygnázō | stoog-nad'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as G4767<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to render gloomy, i.e. (by implication) glower (be overcast with clouds, or sombreness of speech)<BR><B>KJV:</B> lower, be sad.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4767<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4765 (sparrow)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στυγνάζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3805 כֹתֶרֶת, H4676 מַצֵּבָה, H5977 עֹמֶד, H5982 עַמּוּד, H7175 קֶרֶשׁ, H8074 שָׁמֵם",
    4769: "στῦλος (stŷlos | stoo'-los)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from στύω (to stiffen<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly akin to the base of G2476); a post (\"style\"), i.e. (figuratively) support<BR><B>KJV:</B> pillar.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2476<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4769 (pillar)<BR><B>Variants:</B> στῦλος",
    4770: "Στωϊκός (Stōïkós | sto-ik-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4745<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a \"Stoic\" (as occupying a particular porch in Athens), i.e. adherent of a certin philosophy<BR><B>KJV:</B> Stoick.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4745<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4769 (pillar)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Στωϊκός, Στοϊκός",
    4771: "σύ (sý | soo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> the personal pronoun of the second person singular<BR><B>Strong's:</B> thou<BR><B>KJV:</B>  thou. See also G4571, G4671, G4675 ; and for the plural G5209, G5210, G5213, G5216 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4675<BR><I>See:</I> G4571<BR><I>See:</I> G4671<BR><I>See:</I> G5209<BR><I>See:</I> G5210<BR><I>See:</I> G5213<BR><I>See:</I> G5216<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4769 (pillar)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σύ",
