    4812: "συλαγωγέω (sylagōgéō | soo-lag-ogue-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G4813 and (the reduplicated form of) G71<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to lead away as booty, i.e. (figuratively) seduce<BR><B>KJV:</B> spoil.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4813<BR><I>See:</I> G71<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4807 (sycamine tree), G4810 (fig), G4811 (accuse falsely), G4809 (sycamore tree), G4808 (fig tree)<BR><B>Variants:</B> συλαγωγέω",
    4813: "συλάω (syláō | soo-lah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of σύλλω (to strip<BR><B>Strong's:</B> probably akin to G138 ; compare G4661); to despoil<BR><B>KJV:</B> rob.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G138<BR><I>See:</I> G4661<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4807 (sycamine tree), G4810 (fig), G4811 (accuse falsely), G4809 (sycamore tree), G4808 (fig tree)<BR><B>Variants:</B> συλάω",
    4814: "συλλαλέω (syllaléō | sool-lal-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4862 and G2980<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to talk together, i.e. converse<BR><B>KJV:</B> commune (confer, talk) with, speak among.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4862<BR><I>See:</I> G2980<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4807 (sycamine tree), G4810 (fig), G4811 (accuse falsely), G4809 (sycamore tree), G4808 (fig tree)<BR><B>Variants:</B> συλλαλέω",
