    4818: "συλλυπέω (syllypéō | sool-loop-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4862 and G3076<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to afflict jointly, i.e. (passive) sorrow at (on account of) someone<BR><B>KJV:</B> be grieved.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4862<BR><I>See:</I> G3076<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G253 (less sorrowful), G3077 (grief), G4036 (exceeding sorry), G4818 (be grieved), G3076 (cause grief)<BR><B>Variants:</B> συλλυπέω, συλλυπέομαι",
