    4950: "σύρτις (sýrtis | soor'-tis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4951<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a shoal (from the sand drawn thither by the waves), i.e. the Syrtis Major or great bay on the north coast of Africa<BR><B>KJV:</B> quicksands.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4951<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5273 (hypocrite), G505 (without dissimulation), G5272 (condemnation), G4942 (dissemble with), G5271 (feign)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σύρτις, Σύρτις",
    4951: "σύρω (sýrō | soo'-ro)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably akin to G138<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to trail<BR><B>KJV:</B> drag, draw, hale.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G138<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5273 (hypocrite), G505 (without dissimulation), G5272 (condemnation), G4942 (dissemble with), G5271 (feign)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σύρω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2119 זָחַל, H5498 סָחַב, H7857 שָׁטַף",
    4952: "συσπαράσσω (sysparássō | soos-par-as'-so)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4862 and G4682<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to rend completely, i.e. (by analogy) to convulse violently<BR><B>KJV:</B> throw down.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4862<BR><I>See:</I> G4682<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5273 (hypocrite), G505 (without dissimulation), G5272 (condemnation), G4942 (dissemble with), G5271 (feign)<BR><B>Variants:</B> συσπαράσσω, συνταράσσω",
