    4965: "Συχάρ (Sychár | soo-khar')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (H7941)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Sychar (i.e. Shekar), a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Sychar.<BR><I>See:</I> H7941<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4976 (fashion), G3345 (transfer), G4964 (conform to)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Συχάρ, Σιχάρ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7941 שֵׁכָר",
    4966: "Συχέμ (Sychém | soo-khem')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (H7927)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Sychem (i.e. Shekem), the name of a Canaanite and of a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Sychem.<BR><I>See:</I> H7927<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4976 (fashion), G3345 (transfer), G4964 (conform to)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Συχέμ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7926 שְׁכֶם, H7927 שְׁכֶם",
    4967: "σφαγή (sphagḗ | sfag-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4969<BR><B>Strong's:</B> butchery (of animals for food or sacrifice, or (figuratively) of men (destruction))<BR><B>KJV:</B> slaughter.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4969<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4968 (slain beast), G4967 (slaughter), G4969 (kill), G2695 (slay)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σφαγή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2026 הָרַג, H2028 הֲרֵגָה, H2719 חֶרֶב, H2873 טָבַח, H3589 כִּיד, H6993 קֶטֶל",
    4968: "σφάγιον (sphágion | sfag'-ee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a derivative of G4967<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a victim (in sacrifice)<BR><B>KJV:</B> slain beast.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4967<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4968 (slain beast), G4967 (slaughter), G4969 (kill), G2695 (slay)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σφάγιον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2113 זְוָעָה, H2874 טֶבַח, H5071 נְדָבָה",
    4969: "σφάζω (spházō | sfad'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to butcher (especially an animal for food or in sacrifice) or (generally) to slaughter, or (specially), to maim (violently)<BR><B>KJV:</B> kill, slay, wound.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4968 (slain beast), G4967 (slaughter), G4969 (kill), G2695 (slay)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σφάζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2026 הָרַג, H2076 זָבַח, H2873 טָבַח, H7819 שָׁחַט, H8158 שָׁסַף",
    4970: "σφόδρα (sphódra | sfod'-rah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter plural of σφοδρός<BR><B>Strong's:</B> (violent; of uncertain derivation) as adverb; vehemently, i.e. in a high degree, much<BR><B>KJV:</B>  exceeding(-ly), greatly, sore, very.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4968 (slain beast), G4967 (slaughter), G4969 (kill), G2695 (slay)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σφόδρα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3190 יָטַב, H3966 מְאֹד, H4390 מָלֵא, H5704 עַד, H5704 עַד, H7690 שַׂגִּיא",
    4971: "σφοδρῶς (sphodrōs | sfod-roce')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from the same as G4970<BR><B>Strong's:</B> very much<BR><B>KJV:</B> exceedingly.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4970<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4968 (slain beast), G4967 (slaughter), G4969 (kill), G2695 (slay)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σφοδρῶς",
    4972: "σφραγίζω (sphragízō | sfrag-id'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G4973<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to stamp (with a signet or private mark) for security or preservation (literally or figuratively); by implication, to keep secret, to attest<BR><B>KJV:</B> (set a, set to) seal up, stop.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4973<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2696 (seal), G4973 (seal), G4972 (seal up)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σφραγίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2856 חָתַם, H5640 סָתַם, H8552 תָּמַם",
    4973: "σφραγίς (sphragís | sfrag-ece')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably strengthened from G5420<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a signet (as fencing in or protecting from misappropriation); by implication, the stamp impressed (as a mark of privacy, or genuineness), literally or figuratively<BR><B>KJV:</B> seal.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5420<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2696 (seal), G4973 (seal), G4972 (seal up)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σφραγίς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2368 חֹותָם, H2397 חָח",
    4974: "σφυρόν (sphyrón | sfoo-ron')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a presumed derivative probably of the same as σφαῖρα (a ball, \"sphere\"<BR><B>Strong's:</B> compare the feminine σφῦρα, a hammer); the ankle (as globular)<BR><B>KJV:</B> ancle bone.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2696 (seal), G4973 (seal), G4972 (seal up)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σφυρόν, σφυδρόν<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H8455 תֹּותָח",
    4975: "σχεδόν (schedón | skhed-on')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a presumed derivative of the alternate of G2192 as adverb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> nigh, i.e. nearly<BR><B>KJV:</B> almost.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2192<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G2696 (seal), G4973 (seal), G4972 (seal up)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σχεδόν",
    4976: "σχῆμα (schēma | skhay'-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the alternate of G2192<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a figure (as a mode or circumstance), i.e. (by implication) external condition<BR><B>KJV:</B> fashion.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2192<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4976 (fashion), G3345 (transfer), G4964 (conform to)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σχῆμα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6596 פֹּת",
    4977: "σχίζω (schízō | skhid'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to split or sever (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> break, divide, open, rend, make a rent.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4977 (break), G4978 (division)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σχίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1234 בָּקַע, H7121 קָרָא",
