    4979: "σχοινίον (schoiníon | skhoy-nee'-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> diminutive of σχοῖνος<BR><B>Strong's:</B> (a rush or flag-plant; of uncertain derivation); a rushlet, i.e. grass-withe or tie (generally)<BR><B>KJV:</B> small cord, rope.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4977 (break), G4978 (division)<BR><B>Variants:</B> σχοινίον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2256 חֶבֶל, H2256 חֶבֶל, H5364 נִקְפָּה",
