    5008: "ταλιθά (talithá | tal-ee-thah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Chaldee origin (compare H2924)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the fresh, i.e. young girl; talitha (O maiden)<BR><B>KJV:</B> talitha.<BR><I>See:</I> H2924<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ταλιθά, θάβιτα, ταλιθα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2924 טָלֶה",
    5009: "ταμεῖον (tameîon | tam-i'-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter contraction of a presumed derivative of ταμίας (a dispenser or distributor<BR><B>Strong's:</B> akin to τέμνω, to cut); a dispensary or magazine, i.e. a chamber on the ground-floor or interior of an Oriental house (generally used for storage or privacy, a spot for retirement)<BR><B>KJV:</B> secret chamber, closet, storehouse.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1296 (instrumentality), G657 (bid farewell), G5021 (addict), G813 (unruly), G4367 (bid), G5292 (subjection), G1297 (commandment), G2004 (charge), G5293 (be under obedience), G506 (disobedient), G814 (disorderly), G1299 (appoint), G5001 (order), G812 (behave self disorderly), G392 (set in order)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ταμεῖον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H618 אָסָם, H2315 חֶדֶר, H4200 מֶזֶו, H8432 תָּוֶךְ",
