    5082: "τηλικοῦτος (tēlikoûtos | tay-lik-oo'-tos), or feminine τηλικαύτη (tēlikaútē | tay-lik-ow'-tay)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a compound of G3588 with G2245 and G3778<BR><B>Strong's:</B> such as this, i.e. (in (figurative) magnitude) so vast<BR><B>KJV:</B> so great, so mighty.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3588<BR><I>See:</I> G2245<BR><I>See:</I> G3778<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5065 (fourteenth), G5073 (fourfold), G5070 (four thousand), G5069 (quaternion), G5067 (four), G5062 (forty), G5064 (four), G5074 (fourfooted beast), G5075 (tetrarch), G5072 (four months), G5066 (four days), G5063 (forty years), G5071 (four hundred), G5076 (tetrarch), G5068 (foursquare)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τηλικοῦτος",
    5083: "τηρέω (tēréō | tay-reh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from τερός (a watch<BR><B>Strong's:</B> perhaps akin to G2334); to guard (from loss or injury, properly, by keeping the eye upon; and thus differing from G5442, which is properly to prevent escaping; and from G2892, which implies a fortress or full military lines of apparatus), i.e. to note (a prophecy; figuratively, to fulfil a command); by implication, to detain (in custody; figuratively, to maintain); by extension, to withhold (for personal ends; figuratively, to keep unmarried); by extension, to withhold (for personal ends; figuratively, to keep unmarried)<BR><B>KJV:</B> hold fast, keep(- er), (pre-, re-)serve, watch.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2334<BR><I>See:</I> G5442<BR><I>See:</I> G2892<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5084 (hold), G3906 (observe), G4933 (keep), G5083 (hold fast), G3907 (obervation), G1301 (keep)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τηρέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5341 נָצַר, H6845 צָפַן, H6965 קוּם, H7912 שְׁכַח, H8085 שָׁמַע, H8104 שָׁמַר",
    5084: "τήρησις (tḗrēsis | tay'-ray-sis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5083<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a watching, i.e. (figuratively) observance, or (concretely) a prison<BR><B>KJV:</B> hold.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5083<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5084 (hold), G3906 (observe), G4933 (keep), G5083 (hold fast), G3907 (obervation), G1301 (keep)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τήρησις",
    5085: "Τιβεριάς (Tiberiás | tib-er-ee-as')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5086<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Tiberias, the name of a town and a lake in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Tiberias.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5086<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5084 (hold), G3906 (observe), G4933 (keep), G5083 (hold fast), G3907 (obervation), G1301 (keep)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Τιβεριάς",
    5086: "Τιβέριος (Tibérios | tib-er'-ee-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> probably pertaining to the river Tiberis or Tiber; Tiberius, a Roman emperor<BR><B>KJV:</B> Tiberius.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5084 (hold), G3906 (observe), G4933 (keep), G5083 (hold fast), G3907 (obervation), G1301 (keep)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Τιβέριος",
    5087: "τίθημι (títhēmi | tith'-ay-mee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a prolonged form of a primary θέω (théō | theh'-o)<BR> (which is used only as alternate in certain tenses)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to place (in the widest application, literally and figuratively; properly, in a passive or horizontal posture, and thus different from G2476, which properly denotes an upright and active position, while G2749 is properly reflexive and utterly prostrate)<BR><B>KJV:</B> + advise, appoint, bow, commit, conceive, give, X kneel down, lay (aside, down, up), make, ordain, purpose, put, set (forth), settle, sink down.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2476<BR><I>See:</I> G2749<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3866 (committed unto), G3908 (allege), G3331 (change), G4286 (purpose), G114 (cast off), G5087 (+ advise), G2007 (add unto), G4388 (purpose), G115 (disannulling), G4369 (add), G3346 (carry over), G1936 (laying on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τίθημι, τίθημι/τιθέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H622 אָסַף, H935 בֹּוא, H1777 דִּין, H1875 דָּרַשׁ, H3322 יָצַג, H3332 יָצַק, H3427 יָשַׁב, H3455 יָשַׂם, H3559 כּוּן, H3772 כָּרַת, H4171 מוּר, H5060 נָגַע, H5117 נוּחַ, H5148 נָחָה, H5181 נָחַת, H5307 נָפַל, H5375 נָשָׂא, H5414 נָתַן, H5437 סָבַב, H5446 סְבַל, H5810 עָזַז, H5927 עָלָה, H6213 עָשָׂה, H6485 פָּקַד, H6680 צָוָה, H6965 קוּם, H6979 קוּר, H6983 קֹושׁ, H7311 רוּם, H7412 רְמָה, H7561 רָשַׁע, H7737 שָׁוָה, H7760 שׂוּם, H7896 שִׁית, H8104 שָׁמַר, H8371 שָׁתַת, H8628 תָּקַע",
    5088: "τίκτω (tíktō | tik'-to)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a strengthened form of a primary τέκω (tékō | tek'-o)<BR> (which is used only as alternate in certain tenses)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to produce (from seed, as a mother, a plant, the earth, etc.), literally or figuratively<BR><B>KJV:</B> bear, be born, bring forth, be delivered, be in travail.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3866 (committed unto), G3908 (allege), G3331 (change), G4286 (purpose), G114 (cast off), G5087 (+ advise), G2007 (add unto), G4388 (purpose), G115 (disannulling), G4369 (add), G3346 (carry over), G1936 (laying on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τίκτω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2029 הָרָה, H3205 יָלַד, H4422 מָלַט",
