    5090: "Τιμαῖος (Timaîos | tim'-ah-yos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably of Chaldee origin (compare H2931)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Timæus (i.e. Timay), an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Timæus.<BR><I>See:</I> H2931<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3866 (committed unto), G3908 (allege), G3331 (change), G4286 (purpose), G114 (cast off), G5087 (+ advise), G2007 (add unto), G4388 (purpose), G115 (disannulling), G4369 (add), G3346 (carry over), G1936 (laying on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Τιμαῖος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2931 טָמֵא",
    5091: "τιμάω (timáō | tim-ah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5093<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to prize, i.e. fix a valuation upon; by implication, to revere<BR><B>KJV:</B> honour, value.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5093<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5091 (honour), G5092 (honour), G5093 (dear), G5094 (costliness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τιμάω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1921 הָדַר, H3365 יָקַר, H3513 כָּבַד, H5375 נָשָׂא, H6186 עָרַךְ, H8254 שָׁקַל",
    5092: "τιμή (timḗ | tee-may')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5099<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a value, i.e. money paid, or (concretely and collectively) valuables; by analogy, esteem (especially of the highest degree), or the dignity itself<BR><B>KJV:</B> honour, precious, price, some.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5099<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5091 (honour), G5092 (honour), G5093 (dear), G5094 (costliness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τιμή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1926 הָדָר, H1935 הֹוד, H1952 הֹון, H3366 יְקָר, H3513 כָּבַד, H3519 כָּבֹוד, H3701 כֶּסֶף, H4242 מְחִיר, H4377 מֶכֶר, H5797 עֹז, H6187 עֵרֶךְ, H7613 שְׂאֵת",
    5093: "τίμιος (tímios | tim'-ee-os), including the comparative τιμιώτερος (timiṓteros | tim-ee-o'-ter-os), and the superlative τιμιώτατος (timiṓtatos | tim-ee-o'-tat-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5092<BR><B>Strong's:</B> valuable, i.e. (objectively) costly, or (subjectively) honored, esteemed, or (figuratively) beloved<BR><B>KJV:</B> dear, honourable, (more, most) precious, had in reputation.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5092<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5091 (honour), G5092 (honour), G5093 (dear), G5094 (costliness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τίμιος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2656 חֵפֶץ, H3368 יָקָר, H6337 פָּז, H7350 רָחֹוק",
    5094: "τιμιότης (timiótēs | tim-ee-ot'-ace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5093<BR><B>Strong's:</B> expensiveness, i.e. (by implication) magnificence<BR><B>KJV:</B> costliness.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5093<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5091 (honour), G5092 (honour), G5093 (dear), G5094 (costliness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τιμιότης",
    5095: "Τιμόθεος (Timótheos | tee-moth'-eh-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5092 and G2316<BR><B>Strong's:</B> dear to God; Timotheus, a Christian<BR><B>KJV:</B> Timotheus, Timothy.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5092<BR><I>See:</I> G2316<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5091 (honour), G5092 (honour), G5093 (dear), G5094 (costliness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Τιμόθεος",
    5096: "Τίμων (Tímōn | tee'-mone)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5092<BR><B>Strong's:</B> valuable; Timon, a Christian<BR><B>KJV:</B> Timon.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5092<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5091 (honour), G5092 (honour), G5093 (dear), G5094 (costliness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Τίμων",
    5097: "τιμωρέω (timōréō | tim-o-reh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a comparative of G5092 and οὖρος ouros (a guard)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, to protect one's honor, i.e. to avenge (inflict a penalty)<BR><B>KJV:</B> punish.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5092<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5091 (honour), G5092 (honour), G5093 (dear), G5094 (costliness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τιμωρέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7921 שָׁכֹל",
    5098: "τιμωρία (timōría | tee-mo-ree'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5097<BR><B>Strong's:</B> vindication, i.e. (by implication) a penalty<BR><B>KJV:</B> punishment.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5097<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5091 (honour), G5092 (honour), G5093 (dear), G5094 (costliness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τιμωρία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4112 מַהֲלֻמָּה, H6365 פִּיד, H8504 תְּכֵלֶת",
    5099: "τίνω (tínō | tee'-no)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> strengthened for a primary τίω (tíō | tee'-o)<BR> (which is only used as an alternate in certain tenses)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to pay a price, i.e. as a penalty<BR><B>KJV:</B> be punished with.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5091 (honour), G5092 (honour), G5093 (dear), G5094 (costliness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τίνω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6064 עָנַשׁ",
    5100: "τὶς (tìs | tis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> an enclitic indefinite pronoun<BR><B>Strong's:</B> some or any person or object<BR><B>KJV:</B> a (kind of), any (man, thing, thing at all), certain (thing), divers, he (every) man, one (X thing), ought, + partly, some (man, -body, - thing, -what), (+ that no-)thing, what(-soever), X wherewith, whom(-soever), whose(-soever).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5091 (honour), G5092 (honour), G5093 (dear), G5094 (costliness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τὶς, τις",
    5101: "τίς (tís | tis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably emphatic of G5100<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an interrogative pronoun, who, which or what (in direct or indirect questions)<BR><B>KJV:</B> every man, how (much), + no(-ne, thing), what (manner, thing), where (-by, -fore, -of, -unto, - with, -withal), whether, which, who(-m, -se), why.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5100<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5091 (honour), G5092 (honour), G5093 (dear), G5094 (costliness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τίς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H349 אֵיךְ, H639 אַף, H834 אֲשֶׁר, H834 אֲשֶׁר, H1116 בָּמָה, H2009 הִנֵּה, H2088 זֶה, H3642 כָּמַהּ, H4069 מַדּוּעַ, H4100 מָה, H4100 מָה, H4100 מָה, H4100 מָה, H4310 מִי, H5704 עַד, H6030 עָנָה",
    5102: "τίτλος (títlos | tit'-los)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a titulus or \"title\" (placard)<BR><B>KJV:</B> title.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5091 (honour), G5092 (honour), G5093 (dear), G5094 (costliness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τίτλος",
    5103: "Τίτος (Títos | tee'-tos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin but uncertain significance<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Titus, a Christian<BR><B>KJV:</B> Titus.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5091 (honour), G5092 (honour), G5093 (dear), G5094 (costliness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Τίτος",
    5104: "τοί (toí | toy)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably for the dative case of G3588<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an enclitic particle of asseveration by way of contrast; in sooth<BR><B>KJV:</B> (used only with other particles in the comparative, as G2544, G3305, G5105, G5106, etc.)<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3588<BR><I>See:</I> G2544<BR><I>See:</I> G3305<BR><I>See:</I> G5105<BR><I>See:</I> G5106<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5091 (honour), G5092 (honour), G5093 (dear), G5094 (costliness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τοί G5520",
    5105: "τοιγαροῦν (toigaroûn | toy-gar-oon')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5104 and G1063 and G3767<BR><B>Strong's:</B> truly for then, i.e. consequently<BR><B>KJV:</B> there-(where-)fore.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5104<BR><I>See:</I> G1063<BR><I>See:</I> G3767<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5091 (honour), G5092 (honour), G5093 (dear), G5094 (costliness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τοιγαροῦν, τοίγε",
    5106: "τοίνυν (toínyn | toy'-noon)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5104 and G3568<BR><B>Strong's:</B> truly now, i.e. accordingly<BR><B>KJV:</B> then, therefore.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5104<BR><I>See:</I> G3568<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5091 (honour), G5092 (honour), G5093 (dear), G5094 (costliness)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τοίνυν",
    5107: "τοιόσδε (toiósde | toy-os'-deh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (including the other inflections); from a derivative of 5104 and G1161<BR><B>Strong's:</B> such-like then, i.e. so great<BR><B>KJV:</B> such.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G1161<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5206 (adoption), G5107 (such)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τοιόσδε",
    5108: "τοιοῦτος (toioûtos | toy-oo'-tos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> (including the other inflections); from G5104 and G3778<BR><B>Strong's:</B> truly this, i.e. of this sort (to denote character or individuality)<BR><B>KJV:</B> like, such (an one).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5104<BR><I>See:</I> G3778<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5206 (adoption), G5107 (such)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τοιοῦτος",
    5109: "τοῖχος (toîchos | toy'-khos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> another form of G5038<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a wall<BR><B>KJV:</B> wall.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5038<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5109 (wall), G3319 (among), G3320 (middle wall)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τοῖχος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1447 גָּדֵר, H2346 חֹומָה, H2434 חַיִץ, H3796 כֹּתֶל, H7023 קִיר",
    5110: "τόκος (tókos | tok'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G5088<BR><B>Strong's:</B> interest on money loaned (as a produce)<BR><B>KJV:</B> usury.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5088<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5109 (wall), G3319 (among), G3320 (middle wall)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τόκος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5386 נְשִׁי, H5392 נֶשֶׁךְ, H8432 תָּוֶךְ",
    5111: "τολμάω (tolmáō | tol-mah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from τόλμα (boldness<BR><B>Strong's:</B> probably itself from the base of G5056 through the idea of extreme conduct); to venture (objectively or in act; while G2292 is rather subjective or in feeling); by implication, to be courageous<BR><B>KJV:</B> be bold, boldly, dare, durst.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5056<BR><I>See:</I> G2292<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G662 (be very bold), G5112 (the more boldly), G5113 (presumptuous), G5111 (be bold)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τολμάω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3947 לָקַח, H4390 מָלֵא",
    5112: "τολμηρότερον (tolmēróteron | tol-may-rot'-er-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of the compound of a derivative of the base of 5111 (as adverb)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> more daringly, i.e. with greater confidence than otherwise<BR><B>KJV:</B> the more boldly.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G662 (be very bold), G5112 (the more boldly), G5113 (presumptuous), G5111 (be bold)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τολμηρότερον, τολμηρός, τολμηροτέρως",
    5113: "τολμητής (tolmētḗs | tol-may-tace')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5111<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a daring (audacious) man<BR><B>KJV:</B> presumptuous.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5111<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G662 (be very bold), G5112 (the more boldly), G5113 (presumptuous), G5111 (be bold)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τολμητής",
    5114: "τομώτερος (tomṓteros | tom-o'-ter-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> comparative of a derivative of the primary τέμνω (to cut<BR><B>Strong's:</B> more comprehensive or decisive than G2875, as if by a single stroke; whereas that implies repeated blows, like hacking); more keen<BR><B>KJV:</B> sharper.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2875<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G662 (be very bold), G5112 (the more boldly), G5113 (presumptuous), G5111 (be bold)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τομώτερος, τομός",
    5115: "τόξον (tóxon | tox'-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G5088<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a bow (apparently as the simplest fabric)<BR><B>KJV:</B> bow.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5088<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G662 (be very bold), G5112 (the more boldly), G5113 (presumptuous), G5111 (be bold)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τόξον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H827 אַשְׁפָּה, H2671 חֵץ, H7198 קֶשֶׁת",
    5116: "τοπάζιον (topázion | top-ad'-zee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a presumed derivative (alternately) of τόπαζος<BR><B>Strong's:</B> (a \"topaz\"; of uncertain origin); a gem, probably the chrysolite<BR><B>KJV:</B> topaz.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G662 (be very bold), G5112 (the more boldly), G5113 (presumptuous), G5111 (be bold)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τοπάζιον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6337 פָּז, H6357 פִּטְדָה",
    5117: "τόπος (tópos | top'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a spot (general in space, but limited by occupancy; whereas G5561 is a large but participle locality), i.e. location (as a position, home, tract, etc.); figuratively, condition, opportunity; specially, a scabbard<BR><B>KJV:</B> coast, licence, place, X plain, quarter, + rock, room, where.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5561<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5117 (coast)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τόπος, Πόντος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1004 בַּיִת, H3027 יָד, H3653 כֵּן, H3733 כַּר, H4057 מִדְבָּר, H4161 מֹוצָא, H4349 מָכֹון, H4437 מַלְכוּ, H4583 מָעֹון, H4725 מָקֹום, H4999 נָאָה, H5066 נָגַשׁ, H5116 נָוֶה, H5159 נַחֲלָה, H5519 סָךְ, H5977 עֹמֶד, H6279 עָתַר, H8478 תַּחַת",
    5118: "τοσοῦτος (tosoûtos | tos-oo'-tos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from τόσος (so much<BR><B>Strong's:</B> apparently from G3588 and G3739) and G3778 (including its variations); so vast as this, i.e. such (in quantity, amount, number of space)<BR><B>KJV:</B> as large, so great (long, many, much), these many.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3588<BR><I>See:</I> G3739<BR><I>See:</I> G3778<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5117 (coast)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τοσοῦτος",
    5119: "τότε (tóte | tot'-eh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from (the neuter of) G3588 and G3753<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the when, i.e. at the time that (of the past or future, also in consecution)<BR><B>KJV:</B> that time, then.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3753<BR><I>See:</I> G3588<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5117 (coast)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τότε",
    5120: "τοῦ (toû | too)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> properly, the genitive case of G3588<BR><B>Strong's:</B> sometimes used for G5127 ; of this person<BR><B>KJV:</B> his.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3588<BR><I>See:</I> G5127<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5117 (coast)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τοῦ, ὁ G3836",
    5121: "τοὐναντίον (tounantíon | too-nan-tee'-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> contraction for the neuter of G3588 and G1726<BR><B>Strong's:</B> on the contrary<BR><B>KJV:</B> contrariwise.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3588<BR><I>See:</I> G1726<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5117 (coast)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τοὐναντίον, τὸ ἐναντίον",
    5122: "τοὔνομα (toúnoma | too'-no-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> contraction for the neuter of G3588 and G3686<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the name (is)<BR><B>KJV:</B> named.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3588<BR><I>See:</I> G3686<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5117 (coast)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τοὔνομα, τὸ ὄνομα",
    5123: "τουτέστι (toutésti | toot-es'-tee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> contraction for G5124 and G2076<BR><B>Strong's:</B> that is<BR><B>KJV:</B> that is (to say).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2076<BR><I>See:</I> G5124<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5117 (coast)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τουτέστι, τουτέστιν G4047, G5542",
    5124: "τοῦτο (toûto | too'-to)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter singular nominative or accusative case of G3778<BR><B>Strong's:</B> that thing<BR><B>KJV:</B> here (-unto), it, partly, self(-same), so, that (intent), the same, there(-fore, -unto), this, thus, where(-fore).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3778<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5117 (coast)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τοῦτο, οὗτος",
    5125: "τούτοις (toútois | too'-toice)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> dative case plural masculine or neuter of G3778<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to (for, in, with or by) these (persons or things)<BR><B>KJV:</B> such, them, there(-in, -with), these, this, those.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3778<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5117 (coast)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τούτοις, οὗτος",
    5126: "τοῦτον (toûton | too'-ton)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> accusative case singular masculine of G3778<BR><B>Strong's:</B> this (person, as objective of verb or preposition)<BR><B>KJV:</B> him, the same, that, this.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3778<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5117 (coast)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τοῦτον, οὗτος",
    5127: "τούτου (toútou | too'-too)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> genitive case singular masculine or neuter of G3778<BR><B>Strong's:</B> of (from or concerning) this (person or thing)<BR><B>KJV:</B> here(-by), him, it, + such manner of, that, thence(-forth), thereabout, this, thus.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3778<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5117 (coast)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τούτου, οὗτος",
    5128: "τούτους (toútous | too'-tooce)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> accusative case plural masculine of G3778<BR><B>Strong's:</B> these (persons, as objective of verb or preposition)<BR><B>KJV:</B> such, them, these, this.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3778<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5117 (coast)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τούτους, οὗτος",
    5129: "τούτῳ (toútōi | too'-to)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> dative case singular masculine or neuter of G3778<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to (in, with or by) this (person or thing)<BR><B>KJV:</B> here(-by, -in), him, one, the same, there(-in), this.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3778<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5117 (coast)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τούτῳ, οὗτος",
    5130: "τούτων (toútōn | too'-tone)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> genitive case plural masculine or neuter of G3778<BR><B>Strong's:</B> of (from or concerning) these (persons or things)<BR><B>KJV:</B> such, their, these (things), they, this sort, those.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3778<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5117 (coast)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τούτων, οὗτος",
    5131: "τράγος (trágos | trag'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G5176<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a he-goat (as a gnawer)<BR><B>KJV:</B> goat.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5176<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5117 (coast)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τράγος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6260 עַתּוּד, H6842 צָפִיר, H8495 תַּיִשׁ",
    5132: "τράπεζα (trápeza | trap'-ed-zah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably contracted from G5064 and G3979<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a table or stool (as being four-legged), usually for food (figuratively, a meal); also a counter for money (figuratively, a broker's office for loans at interest)<BR><B>KJV:</B> bank, meat, table.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5064<BR><I>See:</I> G3979<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5132 (bank), G5133 (exchanger)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τράπεζα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3899 לֶחֶם, H6341 פַּח, H7607 שְׁאֵר, H7979 שֻׁלְחָן",
    5133: "τραπεζίτης (trapezítēs | trap-ed-zee'-tace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5132<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a money-broker or banker<BR><B>KJV:</B> exchanger.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5132<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5132 (bank), G5133 (exchanger)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τραπεζίτης",
    5134: "τραῦμα (traûma | trow'-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of τιτρώσκω (to wound<BR><B>Strong's:</B> akin to the base of G2352, G5147, G5149, etc.); a wound<BR><B>KJV:</B> wound.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2352<BR><I>See:</I> G5147<BR><I>See:</I> G5149<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5132 (bank), G5133 (exchanger)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τραῦμα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2483 חֳלִי, H2490 חָלַל, H5424 נֶתֶק, H6481 פָּצַע",
    5135: "τραυματίζω (traumatízō | trow-mat-id'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5134<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to inflict a wound<BR><B>KJV:</B> wound.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5134<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5132 (bank), G5133 (exchanger)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τραυματίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2342 חוּל, H2490 חָלַל, H6481 פָּצַע",
    5136: "τραχηλίζω (trachēlízō | trakh-ay-lid'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5137<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to seize by the throat or neck, i.e. to expose the gullet of a victim for killing (generally, to lay bare)<BR><B>KJV:</B> opened.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5137<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5132 (bank), G5133 (exchanger)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τραχηλίζω, τραχηλίζομαι",
    5137: "τράχηλος (tráchēlos | trakh'-ay-los)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from G5143 (through the idea of mobility)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the throat (neck), i.e. (figuratively) life<BR><B>KJV:</B> neck.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5143<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5132 (bank), G5133 (exchanger)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τράχηλος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1621 גַּרְגְּרֹות, H1627 גָּרֹון, H6203 עֹרֶף, H6676 צַוַּאר",
    5138: "τραχύς (trachýs | trakh-oos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> perhaps strengthened from the base of G4486 (as if jagged by rents)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> uneven, rocky (reefy)<BR><B>KJV:</B> rock, rough.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4486<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5132 (bank), G5133 (exchanger)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τραχύς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H386 אֵיתָן, H7406 רֶכֶס",
    5139: "Τραχωνῖτις (Trachōnîtis | trakh-o-nee'-tis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of G5138<BR><B>Strong's:</B> rough district; Trachonitis, a region of Syria<BR><B>KJV:</B> Trachonitis.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5138<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5132 (bank), G5133 (exchanger)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Τραχωνῖτις",
    5140: "τρεῖς (treîs | trice), or neuter τρία (tría | tree'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary (plural) number<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"three\"<BR><B>KJV:</B> three.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5154 (third), G5140 (three), G5153 (three thousand), G5151 (three times), G5152 (third loft)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρεῖς, Τρεῖς ταβέρναι, Τρεῖς",
    5141: "τρέμω (trémō | trem'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> strengthened from a primary τρέω (to \"dread\", \"terrify\")<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to \"tremble\" or fear<BR><B>KJV:</B> be afraid, trembling.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5154 (third), G5140 (three), G5153 (three thousand), G5151 (three times), G5152 (third loft)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρέμω",
    5142: "τρέφω (tréphō | tref'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary verb (properly, τρέφω<BR><B>Strong's:</B> but perhaps strengthened from the base of G5157 through the idea of convolution); properly, to stiffen, i.e. fatten (by implication, to cherish (with food, etc.), pamper, rear)<BR><B>KJV:</B> bring up, feed, nourish.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5157<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5154 (third), G5140 (three), G5153 (three thousand), G5151 (three times), G5152 (third loft)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρέφω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H398 אָכַל, H1431 גָּדַל, H2110 זוּן, H2342 חוּל, H2421 חָיָה, H3557 כּוּל, H4770 מַרְבֵּק, H7200 רָאָה",
    5143: "τρέχω (tréchō | trekh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary verb (properly, θρέχω<BR><B>Strong's:</B> compare G2359); which uses δρέμω (drémō | drem'-o)<BR> (the base of G1408) as alternate in certain tenses; to run or walk hastily (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> have course, run.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2359<BR><I>See:</I> G1408<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4274 (forerunner), G5143 (have course), G1408 (course)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρέχω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1750 דּוּץ, H7323 רוּץ",
    5144: "τριάκοντα (triákonta | tree-ak'-on-tah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> the decade of G5140<BR><B>Strong's:</B> thirty<BR><B>KJV:</B> thirty.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5140<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4274 (forerunner), G5143 (have course), G1408 (course)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τριάκοντα",
    5145: "τριακόσιοι (triakósioi | tree-ak-os'-ee-oy)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> plural from G5140 and G1540<BR><B>Strong's:</B> three hundred<BR><B>KJV:</B> three hundred.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5140<BR><I>See:</I> G1540<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4274 (forerunner), G5143 (have course), G1408 (course)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τριακόσιοι",
    5146: "τρίβολος (tríbolos | trib'-ol-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5140 and G956<BR><B>Strong's:</B> properly, a crow-foot (three-pronged obstruction in war), i.e. (by analogy) a thorny plant (caltrop)<BR><B>KJV:</B> brier, thistle.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5140<BR><I>See:</I> G956<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4274 (forerunner), G5143 (have course), G1408 (course)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρίβολος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1863 דַּרְדַּר, H2757 חָרִיץ, H6791 צֵן",
    5147: "τρίβος (tríbos | tree'-bos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from τρίβω (to \"rub\"<BR><B>Strong's:</B> akin to τείρω, τρύω, and the base of G5131, G5134); a rut or worn track<BR><B>KJV:</B> path.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5131<BR><I>See:</I> G5134<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4274 (forerunner), G5143 (have course), G1408 (course)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρίβος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H734 אֹרַח, H1870 דֶּרֶךְ, H4546 מְסִלָּה, H4570 מַעְגָּל, H5410 נָתִיב, H7635 שָׁבִיל",
    5148: "τριετία (trietía | tree-et-ee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a compound of G5140 and G2094<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a three years' period (triennium)<BR><B>KJV:</B> space of three years.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5140<BR><I>See:</I> G2094<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4274 (forerunner), G5143 (have course), G1408 (course)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τριετία",
    5149: "τρίζω (trízō | trid'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to creak (squeak), i.e. (by analogy) to grate the teeth (in frenzy)<BR><B>KJV:</B> gnash.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4274 (forerunner), G5143 (have course), G1408 (course)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρίζω",
    5150: "τρίμηνον (trímēnon | trim'-ay-non)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a compound of G5140 and G3376 as noun<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a three months' space<BR><B>KJV:</B> three months.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5140<BR><I>See:</I> G3376<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4274 (forerunner), G5143 (have course), G1408 (course)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρίμηνον, τρίμηνος",
    5151: "τρίς (trís | trece)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from G5140<BR><B>Strong's:</B> three times<BR><B>KJV:</B> three times, thrice.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5140<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5154 (third), G5140 (three), G5153 (three thousand), G5151 (three times), G5152 (third loft)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρίς",
    5152: "τρίστεγον (trístegon | tris'-teg-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a compound of G5140 and G4721 as noun<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a third roof (story)<BR><B>KJV:</B> third loft.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5140<BR><I>See:</I> G4721<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5154 (third), G5140 (three), G5153 (three thousand), G5151 (three times), G5152 (third loft)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρίστεγον, τρίστεγος",
    5153: "τρισχίλιοι (trischílioi | tris-khil'-ee-oy)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5151 and G5507<BR><B>Strong's:</B> three times a thousand<BR><B>KJV:</B> three thousand.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5151<BR><I>See:</I> G5507<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5154 (third), G5140 (three), G5153 (three thousand), G5151 (three times), G5152 (third loft)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρισχίλιοι",
    5154: "τρίτος (trítos | tree'-tos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> ordinal from G5140<BR><B>Strong's:</B> third; neuter (as noun) a third part, or (as adverb) a (or the) third time, thirdly<BR><B>KJV:</B> third(-ly).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5140<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5154 (third), G5140 (three), G5153 (three thousand), G5151 (three times), G5152 (third loft)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρίτος, τρίτον",
    5155: "τρίχινος (tríchinos | trikh'-ee-nos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G2359<BR><B>Strong's:</B> hairy, i.e. made of hair (mohair)<BR><B>KJV:</B> of hair.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2359<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5154 (third), G5140 (three), G5153 (three thousand), G5151 (three times), G5152 (third loft)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρίχινος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H8181 שֵׂעָר",
    5156: "τρόμος (trómos | trom'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5141<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a \"trembling\", i.e. quaking with fear<BR><B>KJV:</B> + tremble(-ing).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5141<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5154 (third), G5140 (three), G5153 (three thousand), G5151 (three times), G5152 (third loft)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρόμος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H367 אֵימָה, H4172 מֹורָא, H4288 מְחִתָּה, H5892 עִיר, H6343 פַּחַד, H7461 רַעַד, H7461 רַעַד, H7578 רְתֵת",
    5157: "τροπή (tropḗ | trop-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an apparently primary τρέπω to turn<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a turn (\"trope\"), i.e. revolution (figuratively, variation)<BR><B>KJV:</B> turning.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5154 (third), G5140 (three), G5153 (three thousand), G5151 (three times), G5152 (third loft)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τροπή",
    5158: "τρόπος (trópos | trop'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as G5157<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a turn, i.e. (by implication) mode or style (especially with preposition or relative prefix as adverb, like); figuratively, deportment or character<BR><B>KJV:</B> (even) as, conversation, (+ like) manner, (+ by any) means, way.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5157<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5159 (suffer the manners), G5158 (as)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρόπος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H834 אֲשֶׁר, H834 אֲשֶׁר, H1697 דָּבָר, H2940 טַעַם, H6040 עֳנִי",
    5159: "τροποφορέω (tropophoréō | trop-of-or-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5158 and G5409<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to endure one's habits<BR><B>KJV:</B> suffer the manners.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5158<BR><I>See:</I> G5409<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5159 (suffer the manners), G5158 (as)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τροποφορέω, τροφοφορέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5375 נָשָׂא, H5375 נָשָׂא",
    5160: "τροφή (trophḗ | trof-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5142<BR><B>Strong's:</B> nourishment (literally or figuratively); by implication, rations (wages)<BR><B>KJV:</B> food, meat.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5142<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5162 (nurse), G5160 (food)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τροφή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H400 אֹכֶל, H1715 דָּגָן, H2964 טֶרֶף, H3899 לֶחֶם, H4202 מָזֹון",
    5161: "Τρόφιμος (Tróphimos | trof'-ee-mos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5160<BR><B>Strong's:</B> nutritive; Trophimus, a Christian<BR><B>KJV:</B> Trophimus.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5160<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5162 (nurse), G5160 (food)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Τρόφιμος",
    5162: "τροφός (trophós | trof-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5142<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a nourisher, i.e. nurse<BR><B>KJV:</B> nurse.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5142<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5162 (nurse), G5160 (food)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τροφός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3243 יָנַק",
    5163: "τροχιά (trochiá | trokh-ee-ah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5164<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a track (as a wheel-rut), i.e. (figuratively) a course of conduct<BR><B>KJV:</B> path.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5164<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5162 (nurse), G5160 (food)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τροχιά<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4570 מַעְגָּל",
    5164: "τροχός (trochós | trokh-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5143<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a wheel (as a runner), i.e. (figuratively) a circuit of physical effects<BR><B>KJV:</B> course.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5143<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5162 (nurse), G5160 (food)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τροχός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H212 אֹופָן, H1534 גַּלְגַּל, H4173 מֹורַג",
    5165: "τρύβλιον (trýblion | troob'-lee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a presumed derivative of uncertain affinity<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a bowl<BR><B>KJV:</B> dish.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5162 (nurse), G5160 (food)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρύβλιον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3709 כַּף, H7086 קְעָרָה",
    5166: "τρυγάω (trygáō | troo-gah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of τρύγω (to dry) meaning ripe fruit (as if dry)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to collect the vintage<BR><B>KJV:</B> gather.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5162 (nurse), G5160 (food)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρυγάω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1219 בָּצַר, H1869 דָּרַךְ, H2490 חָלַל, H2554 חָמַס, H6168 עָרָה, H7114 קָצַר",
    5167: "τρυγών (trygṓn | troo-gone')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from τρύζω (to murmur<BR><B>Strong's:</B> akin to G5149, but denoting a duller sound); a turtle-dove (as cooing)<BR><B>KJV:</B> turtle-dove.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5149<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5167 (turtle-dove), G4058 (dove)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρυγών<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H8447 תֹּור",
    5168: "τρυμαλιά (trymaliá | troo-mal-ee-ah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of τρύω (to wear away<BR><B>Strong's:</B> akin to the base of G5134, G5147 and G5176); an orifice, i.e. needle's eye<BR><B>KJV:</B> eye. Compare G5169 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5169<BR><I>See:</I> G5134<BR><I>See:</I> G5147<BR><I>See:</I> G5176<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5167 (turtle-dove), G4058 (dove)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρυμαλιά<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2288 חֲגָו, H4492 מִנְהָרָה, H5357 נָקִיק, H5595 סָפָה",
    5169: "τρύπημα (trýpēma | troo'-pay-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of the base of G5168<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an aperture, i.e. a needle's eye<BR><B>KJV:</B> eye.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5168<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5167 (turtle-dove), G4058 (dove)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρύπημα, τρῆμα",
    5170: "Τρύφαινα (Trýphaina | troo'-fahee-nah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5172<BR><B>Strong's:</B> luxurious; Tryphæna, a Christian woman<BR><B>KJV:</B> Tryphena.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5172<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5167 (turtle-dove), G4058 (dove)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Τρύφαινα",
    5171: "τρυφάω (trypháō | troo-fah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5172<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to indulge in luxury<BR><B>KJV:</B> live in pleasure.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5172<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5167 (turtle-dove), G4058 (dove)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρυφάω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5727 עָדַן, H6026 עָנַג",
    5172: "τρυφή (tryphḗ | troo-fay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from θρύπτω (to break up or (figuratively) enfeeble, especially the mind and body by indulgence)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> effeminacy, i.e. luxury or debauchery<BR><B>KJV:</B> delicately, riot.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5167 (turtle-dove), G4058 (dove)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρυφή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H134 אֶדֶן, H8588 תַּעֲנוּג, H8597 תִּפְאָרָה",
    5173: "Τρυφῶσα (Tryphōsa | troo-fo'-sah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5172<BR><B>Strong's:</B> luxuriating; Tryphosa, a Christian female<BR><B>KJV:</B> Tryphosa.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5172<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5167 (turtle-dove), G4058 (dove)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Τρυφῶσα",
    5174: "Τρωάς (Trōás | tro-as')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from Τρός (a Trojan)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the Troad (or plain of Troy), i.e. Troas, a place in Asia Minor<BR><B>KJV:</B> Troas.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5167 (turtle-dove), G4058 (dove)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Τρωάς, Τρῳάς",
    5175: "Τρωγύλλιον (Trōgýllion | tro-gool'-lee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Trogyllium, a place in Asia Minor<BR><B>KJV:</B> Trogyllium.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5167 (turtle-dove), G4058 (dove)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Τρωγύλλιον G5590, G5591",
    5176: "τρώγω (trṓgō | tro'-go)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably strengthened from a collateral form of the base of G5134 and G5147 through the idea of corrosion or wear<BR><B>Strong's:</B> or perhaps rather of a base of G5167 and G5149 through the idea of a craunching sound; to gnaw or chew, i.e. (generally) to eat<BR><B>KJV:</B> eat.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5167<BR><I>See:</I> G5149<BR><I>See:</I> G5134<BR><I>See:</I> G5147<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5176 (eat)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τρώγω",
    5177: "τυγχάνω (tynchánō | toong-khan'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably for an obsolete τύχω (for which the middle voice of another alternate τεύχω (to make ready or bring to pass) is used in certain tenses<BR><B>Strong's:</B> akin to the base of G5088 through the idea of effecting; properly, to affect; or (specially), to hit or light upon (as a mark to be reached), i.e. (transitively) to attain or secure an object or end, or (intransitively) to happen (as if meeting with); but in the latter application only impersonal (with G1487), i.e. perchance; or (present participle) as adjective, usual (as if commonly met with, with G3756, extraordinary), neuter (as adverb) perhaps; or (with another verb) as adverb, by accident (as it were)<BR><B>KJV:</B> be, chance, enjoy, little, obtain, X refresh…self, + special. Compare G5180 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5180<BR><I>See:</I> G5088<BR><I>See:</I> G1487<BR><I>See:</I> G3756<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1783 (intercession), G5177 (be), G5241 (make intercession for), G1793 (deal with)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τυγχάνω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4672 מָצָא",
    5178: "τυμπανίζω (tympanízō | toom-pan-id'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of G5180 (meaning a drum, \"tympanum\")<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to stretch on an instrument of torture resembling a drum, and thus beat to death<BR><B>KJV:</B> torture.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5180<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1783 (intercession), G5177 (be), G5241 (make intercession for), G1793 (deal with)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τυμπανίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H8427 תָּוָה",
    5179: "τύπος (týpos | too'-pos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5180<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a die (as struck), i.e. (by implication) a stamp or scar; by analogy, a shape, i.e. a statue, (figuratively) style or resemblance; specially, a sampler (\"type\"), i.e. a model (for imitation) or instance (for warning)<BR><B>KJV:</B> en-(ex-)ample, fashion, figure, form, manner, pattern, print.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5180<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G499 (figure), G5296 (form), G5179 (en-ample)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τύπος, τυπικῶς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6754 צֶלֶם, H8403 תַּבְנִית",
    5180: "τύπτω (týptō | toop'-to)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary verb (in a strengthened form)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to \"thump\", i.e. cudgel or pummel (properly, with a stick or bastinado), but in any case by repeated blows; thus differing from G3817 and G3960, which denote a (usually single) blow with the hand or any instrument, or G4141 with the fist (or a hammer), or G4474 with the palm; as well as from G5177, an accidental collision); by implication, to punish; figuratively, to offend (the conscience)<BR><B>KJV:</B> beat, smite, strike, wound.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3817<BR><I>See:</I> G3960<BR><I>See:</I> G4141<BR><I>See:</I> G4474<BR><I>See:</I> G5177<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5180 (beat)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τύπτω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2505 חָלַק, H5062 נָגַף, H5221 נָכָה",
    5181: "Τύραννος (Týrannos | too'-ran-nos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a provincial form of the derivative of the base of G2962<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a \"tyrant\"; Tyrannus, an Ephesian<BR><B>KJV:</B> Tyrannus.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2962<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5180 (beat)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Τύραννος, Τύραννοσ",
    5182: "τυρβάζω (tyrbázō | toor-bad'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from τύρβη (Latin turba, a crowd<BR><B>Strong's:</B> akin to G2351); to make \"turbid\", i.e. disturb<BR><B>KJV:</B> trouble.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2351<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5182 (trouble), G2350 (make ado), G2351 (tumult)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τυρβάζω, θορυβάζω",
    5183: "Τύριος (Týrios | too'-ree-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5184<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Tyrian, i.e. inhabitant of Tyrus<BR><B>KJV:</B> of Tyre.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5184<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5182 (trouble), G2350 (make ado), G2351 (tumult)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Τύριος",
    5184: "Τύρος (Týros | too'-ros)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (H6865): Tyrus (i.e. Tsor), a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Tyre.<BR><I>See:</I> H6865<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5182 (trouble), G2350 (make ado), G2351 (tumult)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Τύρος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6865 צֹר",
    5185: "τυφλός (typhlós | toof-los')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from, G5187<BR><B>Strong's:</B> opaque (as if smoky), i.e. (by analogy) blind (physically or mentally)<BR><B>KJV:</B> blind.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5187<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5186 (blind), G5185 (blind)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τυφλός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5787 עִוֵּר",
    5186: "τυφλόω (typhlóō | toof-lo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5185<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to make blind, i.e. (figuratively) to obscure<BR><B>KJV:</B> blind.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5185<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5186 (blind), G5185 (blind)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τυφλόω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5787 עִוֵּר",
    5187: "τυφόω (typhóō | toof-o'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of G5188<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to envelop with smoke, i.e. (figuratively) to inflate with self-conceit<BR><B>KJV:</B> high-minded, be lifted up with pride, be proud.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5188<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5186 (blind), G5185 (blind)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τυφόω, τυφόομαι",
    5188: "τύφω (týphō | too'-fo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to make a smoke, i.e. slowly consume without flame<BR><B>KJV:</B> smoke.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5186 (blind), G5185 (blind)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τύφω, τύφομαι",
    5189: "τυφωνικός (typhōnikós | too-fo-nee-kos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of G5188<BR><B>Strong's:</B> stormy (as if smoky)<BR><B>KJV:</B> tempestuous.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5188<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5186 (blind), G5185 (blind)<BR><B>Variants:</B> τυφωνικός",
    5190: "Τυχικός (Tychikós | too-khee-kos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of G5177<BR><B>Strong's:</B> fortuitous, i.e. fortunate; Tychicus, a Christian<BR><B>KJV:</B> Tychicus.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5177<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5186 (blind), G5185 (blind)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Τυχικός",
    5191: "ὑακίνθινος (hyakínthinos | hoo-ak-in'-thee-nos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5192<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"hyacinthine\" or \"jacinthine\", i.e. deep blue<BR><B>KJV:</B> jacinth.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5192<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5186 (blind), G5185 (blind)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑακίνθινος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H8476 תַּחַשׁ, H8504 תְּכֵלֶת",
    5192: "ὑάκινθος (hyákinthos | hoo-ak'-in-thos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the \"hyacinth\" or \"jacinth\", i.e. some gem of a deep blue color, probably the zirkon<BR><B>KJV:</B>  jacinth.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5186 (blind), G5185 (blind)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑάκινθος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H8476 תַּחַשׁ, H8504 תְּכֵלֶת",
    5193: "ὑάλινος (hyálinos | hoo-al'-ee-nos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5194<BR><B>Strong's:</B> glassy, i.e. transparent<BR><B>KJV:</B> of glass.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5194<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5186 (blind), G5185 (blind)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑάλινος",
    5194: "ὕαλος (hýalos | hoo'-al-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> perhaps from the same as G5205 (as being transparent like rain)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> glass<BR><B>KJV:</B> glass.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5205<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5186 (blind), G5185 (blind)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὕαλος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2137 זְכוּכִית",
    5195: "ὑβρίζω (hybrízō | hoo-brid'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5196<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to exercise violence, i.e. abuse<BR><B>KJV:</B> use despitefully, reproach, entreat shamefully (spitefully).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5196<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5195 (use despitefully), G1796 (do despite unto), G5196 (harm), G5197 (despiteful)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑβρίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1343 גֵּאֶה, H1343 גֵּאֶה, H5937 עָלַז, H7043 קָלַל",
    5196: "ὕβρις (hýbris | hoo'-bris)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228<BR><B>Strong's:</B> insolence (as over-bearing), i.e. insult, injury<BR><B>KJV:</B> harm, hurt, reproach.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5195 (use despitefully), G1796 (do despite unto), G5196 (harm), G5197 (despiteful)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὕβρις<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1344 גֵּאָה, H1347 גָּאֹון, H1466 גֵּוָה, H2087 זָדֹון, H3944 לָצֹון, H5947 עַלִּיז, H7312 רוּם",
    5197: "ὑβριστής (hybristḗs | hoo-bris-tace')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5195<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an insulter, i.e. maltreater<BR><B>KJV:</B> despiteful, injurious.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5195<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5195 (use despitefully), G1796 (do despite unto), G5196 (harm), G5197 (despiteful)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑβριστής<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1341 גֵּא, H1343 גֵּאֶה, H7312 רוּם",
    5198: "ὑγιαίνω (hygiaínō | hoog-ee-ah'-ee-no)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5199<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to have sound health, i.e. be well (in body); figuratively, to be uncorrupt (true in doctrine)<BR><B>KJV:</B> be in health, (be safe and) sound, (be) whole(-some).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5199<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5198 (be in health), G5199 (sound)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑγιαίνω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7965 שָׁלֹום, H7999 שָׁלַם",
    5199: "ὑγιής (hygiḗs | hoog-ee-ace')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G837<BR><B>Strong's:</B> healthy, i.e. well (in body); figuratively, true (in doctrine)<BR><B>KJV:</B> sound, whole.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G837<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5198 (be in health), G5199 (sound)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑγιής<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2416 חַי, H2421 חָיָה, H7965 שָׁלֹום",
    5200: "ὑγρός (hygrós | hoo-gros')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G5205<BR><B>Strong's:</B> wet (as if with rain), i.e. (by implication) sappy (fresh)<BR><B>KJV:</B> green.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5205<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5198 (be in health), G5199 (sound)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑγρός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3892 לַח, H7373 רָטֹב",
    5201: "ὑδρία (hydría | hoo-dree-ah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5204<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a water-jar, i.e. receptacle for family supply<BR><B>KJV:</B> water-pot.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5204<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5198 (be in health), G5199 (sound)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑδρία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3537 כַּד",
    5202: "ὑδροποτέω (hydropotéō | hoo-drop-ot-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a compound of G5204 and a derivative of G4095<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be a water-drinker, i.e. to abstain from vinous beverages<BR><B>KJV:</B> drink water.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5204<BR><I>See:</I> G4095<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5198 (be in health), G5199 (sound)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑδροποτέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4325 מַיִם",
    5203: "ὑδρωπικός (hydrōpikós | hoo-dro-pik-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a compound of G5204 and a derivative of G3700 (as if looking watery)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be \"dropsical\"<BR><B>KJV:</B> have the dropsy.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5204<BR><I>See:</I> G3700<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5198 (be in health), G5199 (sound)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑδρωπικός",
    5204: "ὕδωρ (hýdōr | hoo'-dore), and genitive case, ὕδατος (hýdatos | hoo'-dat-os)<BR><BR>, etc.<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G5205<BR><B>Strong's:</B> water (as if rainy) literally or figuratively<BR><B>KJV:</B> water.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5205<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5204 (water)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὕδωρ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4325 מַיִם, H4726 מָקֹור, H5140 נָזַל",
    5205: "ὑετός (hyetós | hoo-et-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a primary ὕω (to rain)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> rain, especially a shower<BR><B>KJV:</B> rain.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5204 (water)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑετός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1652 גָּשַׁם, H1653 גֶּשֶׁם, H4306 מָטַר, H4306 מָטַר, H4325 מַיִם, H7722 שֹׁוא, H7858 שֶׁטֶף",
    5206: "υἱοθεσία (huiothesía | hwee-oth-es-ee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a presumed compound of G5207 and a derivative of G5087<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the placing as a son, i.e. adoption (figuratively, Christian sonship in respect to God)<BR><B>KJV:</B> adoption (of children, of sons).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5207<BR><I>See:</I> G5087<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5206 (adoption), G5107 (such)<BR><B>Variants:</B> υἱοθεσία",
    5207: "υἱός (huiós | hwee-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a \"son\" (sometimes of animals), used very widely of immediate, remote or figuratively, kinship<BR><B>KJV:</B> child, foal, son.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5206 (adoption), G5107 (such)<BR><B>Variants:</B> υἱός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H376 אִישׁ, H1004 בַּיִת, H1121 בֵּן, H1247 בַּר, H2233 זֶרַע, H3206 יֶלֶד, H4940 מִשְׁפָּחָה",
    5208: "ὕλη (hýlē | hoo-lay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> perhaps akin to G3586<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a forest, i.e. (by implication) fuel<BR><B>KJV:</B> matter.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3586<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5206 (adoption), G5107 (such)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὕλη<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3121 יָוֵן, H5521 סֻכָּה, H8068 שָׁמִיר",
    5209: "ὑμᾶς (hymâs | hoo-mas')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> accusative case of G5210<BR><B>Strong's:</B> you (as the objective of a verb or preposition)<BR><B>KJV:</B> ye, you (+ -ward), your (+ own).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5210<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5206 (adoption), G5107 (such)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑμᾶς, σύ",
    5210: "ὑμεῖς (hymeîs | hoo-mice')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> irregular plural of G4771<BR><B>Strong's:</B> you (as subjective of verb)<BR><B>KJV:</B> ye (yourselves), you.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4771<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5206 (adoption), G5107 (such)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑμεῖς, σύ",
    5211: "Ὑμεναῖος (Hymenaîos | hoo-men-ah'-yos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from Ὑμήν (the god of weddings)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"hymenæal\"; Hymenæus, an opponent of Christianity<BR><B>KJV:</B> Hymenæus.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5206 (adoption), G5107 (such)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Ὑμεναῖος, Ὑμέναιος",
    5212: "ὑμέτερος (hyméteros | hoo-met'-er-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5210<BR><B>Strong's:</B> yours, i.e. pertaining to you<BR><B>KJV:</B> your (own).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5210<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5206 (adoption), G5107 (such)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑμέτερος",
    5213: "ὑμῖν (hymîn | hoo-min')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> irregular dative case of G5210<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to (with or by) you<BR><B>KJV:</B> ye, you, your(-selves).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5210<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5206 (adoption), G5107 (such)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑμῖν, σύ",
    5214: "ὑμνέω (hymnéō | hoom-neh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5215<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to hymn, i.e. sing a religious ode; by implication, to celebrate (God) in song<BR><B>KJV:</B> sing a hymn (praise unto).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5215<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5214 (sing a hymn), G5215 (hymn)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑμνέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1984 הָלַל, H2167 זָמַר, H3034 יָדָה, H3045 יָדַע, H7442 רָנַן, H7892 שִׁיר",
    5215: "ὕμνος (hýmnos | hoom'-nos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently from a simpler (obsolete) form of ὑδέω (to celebrate<BR><B>Strong's:</B> probably akin to G103 ; compare H5667); a \"hymn\" or religious ode (one of the Psalms)<BR><B>KJV:</B> hymn.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G103<BR><I>See:</I> H5667<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5214 (sing a hymn), G5215 (hymn)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὕμνος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1984 הָלַל, H5058 נְגִינָה, H7892 שִׁיר, H8416 תְּהִלָּה, H8605 תְּפִלָּה",
    5216: "ὑμῶν (hymōn | hoo-mone')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> genitive case of G5210<BR><B>Strong's:</B> of (from or concerning) you<BR><B>KJV:</B> ye, you, your (own, -selves).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5210<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5214 (sing a hymn), G5215 (hymn)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑμῶν, σύ",
    5217: "ὑπάγω (hypágō | hoop-ag'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G71<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to lead (oneself) under, i.e. withdraw or retire (as if sinking out of sight), literally or figuratively<BR><B>KJV:</B> depart, get hence, go (a-)way.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G71<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5217 (depart)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπάγω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1980 הָלַךְ",
    5218: "ὑπακοή (hypakoḗ | hoop-ak-o-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5219<BR><B>Strong's:</B> attentive hearkening, i.e. (by implication) compliance or submission<BR><B>KJV:</B> obedience, (make) obedient, obey(-ing).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5219<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5218 (obedience), G1522 (hear), G1873 (hear), G191 (give audience), G3878 (neglect to hear), G5219 (hearken), G5255 (obedient), G3876 (disobedience), G189 (audience)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπακοή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6038 עֲנָוָה",
    5219: "ὑπακούω (hypakoúō | hoop-ak-oo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G191<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to hear under (as a subordinate), i.e. to listen attentively; by implication, to heed or conform to a command or authority<BR><B>KJV:</B> hearken, be obedient to, obey.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G191<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5218 (obedience), G1522 (hear), G1873 (hear), G191 (give audience), G3878 (neglect to hear), G5219 (hearken), G5255 (obedient), G3876 (disobedience), G189 (audience)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπακούω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H238 אָזַן, H3985 מָאֵן, H5401 נָשַׁק, H6030 עָנָה, H7181 קָשַׁב, H7760 שׂוּם, H8003 שָׁלֵם, H8085 שָׁמַע",
    5220: "ὕπανδρος (hýpandros | hoop'-an-dros)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G435<BR><B>Strong's:</B> in subjection under a man, i.e. a married woman<BR><B>KJV:</B> which hath an husband.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G435<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5218 (obedience), G1522 (hear), G1873 (hear), G191 (give audience), G3878 (neglect to hear), G5219 (hearken), G5255 (obedient), G3876 (disobedience), G189 (audience)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὕπανδρος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H8478 תַּחַת",
    5221: "ὑπαντάω (hypantáō | hoop-an-tah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and a derivative of G473<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to go opposite (meet) under (quietly), i.e. to encounter, fall in with<BR><B>KJV:</B> (go to) meet.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G473<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5222 (meeting), G2658 (attain), G5221 (meet)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπαντάω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7136 קָרָה",
    5222: "ὑπάντησις (hypántēsis | hoop-an'-tay-sis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5221<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an encounter or concurrence (with G1519 for infinitive, in order to fall in with)<BR><B>KJV:</B> meeting.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5221<BR><I>See:</I> G1519<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5222 (meeting), G2658 (attain), G5221 (meet)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπάντησις<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6440 פָּנִים, H7121 קָרָא",
    5223: "ὕπαρξις (hýparxis | hoop'-arx-is)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5225<BR><B>Strong's:</B> existency or proprietorship, i.e. (concretely) property, wealth<BR><B>KJV:</B> goods, substance.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5225<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5222 (meeting), G2658 (attain), G5221 (meet)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὕπαρξις<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1952 הֹון, H3426 יֵשׁ, H4735 מִקְנֶה, H7399 רְכוּשׁ",
    5224: "ὑπάρχοντα (hypárchonta | hoop-ar'-khon-tah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter plural of present participle active of G5225 as noun<BR><B>Strong's:</B> things extant or in hand, i.e. property or possessions<BR><B>KJV:</B> goods, that which one has, things which (one) possesseth, substance, that hast.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5225<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5222 (meeting), G2658 (attain), G5221 (meet)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπάρχοντα, ὑπάρχω",
    5225: "ὑπάρχω (hypárchō | hoop-ar'-kho)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G756<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to begin under (quietly), i.e. come into existence (be present or at hand); expletively, to exist (as copula or subordinate to an adjective, participle, adverb or preposition, or as an auxiliary to a principal (verb)<BR><B>KJV:</B> after, behave, live.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G756<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5222 (meeting), G2658 (attain), G5221 (meet)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπάρχω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H202 אֹון, H205 אָוֶן, H1961 הָיָה, H3426 יֵשׁ, H3885 לוּן, H4735 מִקְנֶה, H7399 רְכוּשׁ",
    5226: "ὑπείκω (hypeíkō | hoop-i'-ko)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and εἴκω (to yield, be \"weak\")<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to surrender<BR><B>KJV:</B> submit self.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5222 (meeting), G2658 (attain), G5221 (meet)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπείκω",
    5227: "ὑπεναντίος (hypenantíos | hoop-en-an-tee'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G1727<BR><B>Strong's:</B> under (covertly) contrary to, i.e. opposed or (as noun) an opponent<BR><B>KJV:</B> adversary, against.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G1727<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5222 (meeting), G2658 (attain), G5221 (meet)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπεναντίος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H340 אָיַב, H6862 צַר, H6965 קוּם, H8130 שָׂנֵא",
    5228: "ὑπέρ (hypér | hoop-er')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary preposition<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"over\", i.e. (with the genitive case) of place, above, beyond, across, or causal, for the sake of, instead, regarding; with the accusative case superior to, more than<BR><B>KJV:</B> (+ exceeding, abundantly) above, in (on) behalf of, beyond, by, + very chiefest, concerning, exceeding (above, -ly), for, + very highly, more (than), of, over, on the part of, for sake of, in stead, than, to(-ward), very. In the comparative, it retains many of the above applications.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5228 (above)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπέρ, ὑπερεγώ",
    5229: "ὑπεραίρομαι (hyperaíromai | hoop-er-ah'-ee-rom-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> middle voice from G5228 and G142<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to raise oneself over, i.e. (figuratively) to become haughty<BR><B>KJV:</B> exalt self, be exalted above measure.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G142<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5228 (above)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπεραίρομαι, ὑπεραίρω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5375 נָשָׂא, H5674 עָבַר, H5927 עָלָה",
    5230: "ὑπέρακμος (hypérakmos | hoop-er'-ak-mos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and the base of G188<BR><B>Strong's:</B> beyond the \"acme\", i.e. figuratively (of a daughter) past the bloom (prime) of youth<BR><B>KJV:</B> + pass the flower of (her) age.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G188<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5228 (above)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπέρακμος",
    5231: "ὑπεράνω (hyperánō | hoop-er-an'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and G507<BR><B>Strong's:</B> above upward, i.e. greatly higher (in place or rank)<BR><B>KJV:</B> far above, over.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G507<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5228 (above)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπεράνω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4606 מֵעָל, H5921 עַל, H5945 עֶלְיֹון",
    5232: "ὑπεραυξάνω (hyperauxánō | hoop-er-owx-an'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and G837<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to increase above ordinary degree<BR><B>KJV:</B> grow exceedingly.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G837<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G837 (grow), G5232 (grow exceedingly)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπεραυξάνω",
    5233: "ὑπερβαίνω (hyperbaínō | hoop-er-bah'-ee-no)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and the base of G939<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to transcend, i.e. (figuratively) to overreach<BR><B>KJV:</B> go beyond.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G939<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3845 (transgress), G5233 (go beyond), G531 (unchangeable), G3847 (breaking), G3848 (breaker)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερβαίνω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1801 דָּלַג, H3254 יָסַף, H5472 סוּג, H5674 עָבַר",
    5234: "ὑπερβαλλόντως (hyperballóntōs | hoop-er-bal-lon'-toce)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from present participle active of G5235<BR><B>Strong's:</B> excessively<BR><B>KJV:</B> beyond measure.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5235<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5234 (beyond measure), G5236 (abundance), G5235 (exceeding)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερβαλλόντως",
    5235: "ὑπερβάλλω (hyperbállō | hoop-er-bal'-lo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and G906<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to throw beyod the usual mark, i.e. (figuratively) to surpass (only active participle supereminent)<BR><B>KJV:</B> exceeding, excel, pass.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G906<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5234 (beyond measure), G5236 (abundance), G5235 (exceeding)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερβάλλω",
    5236: "ὑπερβολή (hyperbolḗ | hoop-er-bol-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5235<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a throwing beyond others, i.e. (figuratively) supereminence; adverbially (with G1519 or G2596) pre- eminently<BR><B>KJV:</B> abundance, (far more) exceeding, excellency, more excellent, beyond (out of) measure.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5235<BR><I>See:</I> G1519<BR><I>See:</I> G2596<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5234 (beyond measure), G5236 (abundance), G5235 (exceeding)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερβολή",
    5237: "ὑπερείδω (hypereídō | hoop-er-i'-do)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and G1492<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to overlook, i.e. not punish<BR><B>KJV:</B> wink at.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G1492<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5234 (beyond measure), G5236 (abundance), G5235 (exceeding)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερείδω, παροράω, ὑπεροράω, ὑπερεῖδον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4604 מַעַל, H5956 עָלַם",
    5238: "ὑπερέκεινα (hyperékeina | hoop-er-ek'-i-nah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and the neuter plural of G1565<BR><B>Strong's:</B> above those parts, i.e. still farther<BR><B>KJV:</B> beyond.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G1565<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5234 (beyond measure), G5236 (abundance), G5235 (exceeding)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερέκεινα",
    5239: "ὑπερεκτείνω (hyperekteínō | hoop-er-ek-ti'-no)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and G1614<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to extend inordinately<BR><B>KJV:</B> stretch beyond.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G1614<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1614 (cast), G5239 (stretch beyond), G1616 (X instantly), G1618 (without ceasing)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερεκτείνω",
    5240: "ὑπερεκχύνω (hyperekchýnō | hoop-er-ek-khoo'-no)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and the alternate form of G1632<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to pour out over, i.e. (passively) to overflow<BR><B>KJV:</B> run over.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G1632<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1614 (cast), G5239 (stretch beyond), G1616 (X instantly), G1618 (without ceasing)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερεκχύνω, ὑπερεκπερισσοῦ, ὑπερεκπερισσῶς, ὑπερεκχύννω, ὑπερεκχύννομαι, ὑπερεκχύν(ν)ω",
    5241: "ὑπερεντυγχάνω (hyperentynchánō | hoop-er-en-toong-khan'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and G1793<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to intercede in behalf of<BR><B>KJV:</B> make intercession for.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G1793<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1783 (intercession), G5177 (be), G5241 (make intercession for), G1793 (deal with)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερεντυγχάνω",
    5242: "ὑπερέχω (hyperéchō | hoop-er-ekh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and G2192<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to hold oneself above, i.e. (figuratively) to excel; participle (as adjective, or neuter as noun) superior, superiority<BR><B>KJV:</B> better, excellency, higher, pass, supreme.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G2192<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5247 (authority), G5242 (better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερέχω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H117 אַדִּיר, H553 אָמַץ, H5736 עֲדַף, H6186 עָרַךְ, H8133 שְׁנָא",
    5243: "ὑπερηφανία (hyperēphanía | hoop-er-ay-fan-ee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5244<BR><B>Strong's:</B> haughtiness<BR><B>KJV:</B> pride.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5244<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5247 (authority), G5242 (better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερηφανία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1215 בֶּצַע, H1347 גָּאֹון, H2087 זָדֹון, H7312 רוּם, H7588 שָׁאֹון",
    5244: "ὑπερήφανος (hyperḗphanos | hoop-er-ay'-fan-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and G5316<BR><B>Strong's:</B> appearing above others (conspicuous), i.e. (figuratively) haughty<BR><B>KJV:</B> proud.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G5316<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5247 (authority), G5242 (better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερήφανος, ὑπερλίαν<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1343 גֵּאֶה, H1364 גָּבֹהַּ, H2086 זֵד, H3887 לוּץ, H6184 עָרִיץ, H7293 רַהַב, H7312 רוּם",
    5245: "ὑπερνικάω (hypernikáō | hoop-er-nik-ah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and G3528<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to vanquish beyond, i.e. gain a decisive victory<BR><B>KJV:</B> more than conquer.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G3528<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3527 (Nicanor), G3534 (victory), G3528 (conquer), G3529 (victory), G5245 (more than conquer)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερνικάω",
    5246: "ὑπέρογκος (hypéronkos | hoop-er'-ong-kos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and G3591<BR><B>Strong's:</B> bulging over, i.e. (figuratively) insolent<BR><B>KJV:</B> great swelling.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G3591<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3527 (Nicanor), G3534 (victory), G3528 (conquer), G3529 (victory), G5245 (more than conquer)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπέρογκος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1419 גָּדֹול, H6382 פֶּלֶא, H7185 קָשָׁה",
    5247: "ὑπεροχή (hyperochḗ | hoop-er-okh-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5242<BR><B>Strong's:</B> prominence, i.e. (figuratively) superiority (in rank or character)<BR><B>KJV:</B> authority, excellency.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5242<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5247 (authority), G5242 (better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπεροχή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1364 גָּבֹהַּ, H6967 קֹומָה",
    5248: "ὑπερπερισσεύω (hyperperisseúō | hoop-er-per-is-syoo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and G4052<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to super-abound<BR><B>KJV:</B> abound much more, exceeding.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G4052<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5248 (abound much more), G4050 (abundance), G4057 (exceedingly), G5249 (beyond measure), G4052 (abound), G4051 (abundance), G4053 (exceeding abundantly above)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερπερισσεύω",
    5249: "ὑπερπερισσῶς (hyperperissōs | hoop-er-per-is-soce')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and G4057<BR><B>Strong's:</B> superabundantly, i.e. exceedingly<BR><B>KJV:</B> beyond measure.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G4057<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5248 (abound much more), G4050 (abundance), G4057 (exceedingly), G5249 (beyond measure), G4052 (abound), G4051 (abundance), G4053 (exceeding abundantly above)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερπερισσῶς",
    5250: "ὑπερπλεονάζω (hyperpleonázō | hoop-er-pleh-on-ad'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and G4121<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to superabound<BR><B>KJV:</B> be exceeding abundant.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G4121<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4121 (abound), G5250 (be exceeding abundant)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερπλεονάζω",
    5251: "ὑπερυψόω (hyperypsóō | hoop-er-oop-so'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and G5312<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to elevate above others, i.e. raise to the highest position<BR><B>KJV:</B> highly exalt.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G5312<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5312 (exalt), G5310 (most high), G5251 (highly exalt), G5311 (be exalted), G5313 (height)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερυψόω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5927 עָלָה, H6184 עָרִיץ, H7311 רוּם",
    5252: "ὑπερφρονέω (hyperphronéō | hoop-er-fron-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5228 and G5426<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to esteem oneself overmuch, i.e. be vain or arrogant<BR><B>KJV:</B> think more highly.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><I>See:</I> G5426<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5312 (exalt), G5310 (most high), G5251 (highly exalt), G5311 (be exalted), G5313 (height)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερφρονέω",
    5253: "ὑπερῷον (hyperōion | hoop-er-o'-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a derivative of G5228<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a higher part of the house, i.e. apartment in the third story<BR><B>KJV:</B> upper chamber (room).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5228<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5312 (exalt), G5310 (most high), G5251 (highly exalt), G5311 (be exalted), G5313 (height)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπερῷον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5950 עֲלִילִיָּה",
    5254: "ὑπέχω (hypéchō | hoop-ekh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G2192<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to hold oneself under, i.e. endure with patience<BR><B>KJV:</B> suffer.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G2192<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5312 (exalt), G5310 (most high), G5251 (highly exalt), G5311 (be exalted), G5313 (height)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπέχω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5375 נָשָׂא, H5445 סָבַל",
    5255: "ὑπήκοος (hypḗkoos | hoop-ay'-ko-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5219<BR><B>Strong's:</B> attentively listening, i.e. (by implication) submissive<BR><B>KJV:</B> obedient.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5219<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5218 (obedience), G1522 (hear), G1873 (hear), G191 (give audience), G3878 (neglect to hear), G5219 (hearken), G5255 (obedient), G3876 (disobedience), G189 (audience)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπήκοος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4522 מַס, H5647 עָבַד, H8085 שָׁמַע",
    5256: "ὑπηρετέω (hypēretéō | hoop-ay-ret-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5257<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be a subordinate, i.e. (by implication) subserve<BR><B>KJV:</B> minister (unto), serve.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5257<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5257 (minister), G5256 (minister)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπηρετέω",
    5257: "ὑπηρέτης (hypērétēs | hoop-ay-ret'-ace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and a derivative of ἐρέσσω (to row)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an under-oarsman, i.e. (generally) subordinate (assistant, sexton, constable)<BR><B>KJV:</B> minister, officer, servant.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5257 (minister), G5256 (minister)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπηρέτης<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3596 כִּילַי, H5650 עֶבֶד",
    5258: "ὕπνος (hýpnos | hoop'-nos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an obsolete primary (perhaps akin to G5259 through the idea of subsilience)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> sleep, i.e. (figuratively) spiritual torpor<BR><B>KJV:</B> sleep.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G879 (fall asleep), G1798 (dream), G1853 (X out of sleep), G5258 (sleep), G1797 (dream), G1852 (awake out of sleep)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὕπνος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2377 חָזֹון, H2472 חֲלֹום, H3463 יָשֵׁן, H8142 שֵׁנָה, H8142 שֵׁנָה",
    5259: "ὑπό (hypó | hoop-o')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary preposition<BR><B>Strong's:</B> under, i.e. (with the genitive case) of place (beneath), or with verbs (the agency or means, through); (with the accusative case) of place (whither (underneath) or where (below) or time (when (at))<BR><B>KJV:</B> among, by, from, in, of, under, with. In the comparative, it retains the same general applications, especially of inferior position or condition, and specially, covertly or moderately.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G879 (fall asleep), G1798 (dream), G1853 (X out of sleep), G5258 (sleep), G1797 (dream), G1852 (awake out of sleep)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπό",
    5260: "ὑποβάλλω (hypobállō | hoop-ob-al'-lo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G906<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to throw in stealthily, i.e. introduce by collusion<BR><B>KJV:</B> suborn.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G906<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G879 (fall asleep), G1798 (dream), G1853 (X out of sleep), G5258 (sleep), G1797 (dream), G1852 (awake out of sleep)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑποβάλλω",
    5261: "ὑπογραμμός (hypogrammós | hoop-og-ram-mos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a compound of G5259 and G1125<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an underwriting, i.e. copy for imitation (figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> example.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G1125<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4270 (before ordain), G1121 (bill), G1124 (scripture), G1123 (written), G5261 (example), G1125 (describe)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπογραμμός",
    5262: "ὑπόδειγμα (hypódeigma | hoop-od'-igue-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5263<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an exhibit for imitation or warning (figuratively, specimen, adumbration)<BR><B>KJV:</B> en-(ex-)ample, pattern.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5263<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5262 (en-ample), G323 (shewing), G1166 (shew), G3856 (make a public example), G322 (appoint), G1165 (make a shew)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπόδειγμα",
    5263: "ὑποδείκνυμι (hypodeíknymi | hoop-od-ike'-noo-mee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G1166<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to exhibit under the eyes, i.e. (figuratively) to exemplify (instruct, admonish)<BR><B>KJV:</B> show, (fore-)warn.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G1166<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5262 (en-ample), G323 (shewing), G1166 (shew), G3856 (make a public example), G322 (appoint), G1165 (make a shew)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑποδείκνυμι, ὑποδεικνύω, ὑποδείκνυμι/ὑποδεικνύω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H995 בִּין, H2324 חֲוָא, H3046 יְדַע, H3384 יָרָה, H5046 נָגַד, H5608 סָפַר, H7200 רָאָה, H7919 שָׂכַל",
    5264: "ὑποδέχομαι (hypodéchomai | hoop-od-ekh'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G1209<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to admit under one's roof, i.e. entertain hospitably<BR><B>KJV:</B> receive.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G1209<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5262 (en-ample), G323 (shewing), G1166 (shew), G3856 (make a public example), G322 (appoint), G1165 (make a shew)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑποδέχομαι",
    5265: "ὑποδέω (hypodéō | hoop-od-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G1210<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to bind under one's feet, i.e. put on shoes or sandals<BR><B>KJV:</B> bind on, (be) shod.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G1210<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5266 (shoe), G5265 (bind on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑποδέω, ὑποδέομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5274 נָעַל",
    5266: "ὑπόδημα (hypódēma | hoop-od'-ay-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5265<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something bound under the feet, i.e. a shoe or sandal<BR><B>KJV:</B> shoe.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5265<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5266 (shoe), G5265 (bind on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπόδημα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5274 נָעַל",
    5267: "ὑπόδικος (hypódikos | hoop-od'-ee-kos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G1349<BR><B>Strong's:</B> under sentence, i.e. (by implication) condemned<BR><B>KJV:</B> guilty.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G1349<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5267 (guilty)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπόδικος",
    5268: "ὑποζύγιον (hypozýgion | hoop-od-zoog'-ee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a compound of G5259 and G2218<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an animal under the yoke (draught-beast), i.e. (specially), a donkey<BR><B>KJV:</B> ass.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G2218<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5267 (guilty)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑποζύγιον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H860 אָתֹון, H2543 חֲמֹור",
    5269: "ὑποζώννυμι (hypozṓnnymi | hoop-od-zone'-noo-mee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G2224<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to gird under, i.e. frap (a vessel with cables across the keel, sides and deck)<BR><B>KJV:</B> undergirt.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G2224<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5267 (guilty)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑποζώννυμι",
    5270: "ὑποκάτω (hypokátō | hoop-ok-at'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G2736<BR><B>Strong's:</B> down under, i.e. beneath<BR><B>KJV:</B> under.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G2736<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5267 (guilty)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑποκάτω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4295 מַטָּה, H8478 תַּחַת",
    5271: "ὑποκρίνομαι (hypokrínomai | hoop-ok-rin'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> middle voice from G5259 and G2919<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to decide (speak or act) under a false part, i.e. (figuratively) dissemble (pretend)<BR><B>KJV:</B> feign.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G2919<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5273 (hypocrite), G505 (without dissimulation), G5272 (condemnation), G4942 (dissemble with), G5271 (feign)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑποκρίνομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6030 עָנָה",
    5272: "ὑπόκρισις (hypókrisis | hoop-ok'-ree-sis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5271<BR><B>Strong's:</B> acting under a feigned part, i.e. (figuratively) deceit (\"hypocrisy\")<BR><B>KJV:</B> condemnation, dissimulation, hypocrisy.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5271<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5273 (hypocrite), G505 (without dissimulation), G5272 (condemnation), G4942 (dissemble with), G5271 (feign)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπόκρισις",
    5273: "ὑποκριτής (hypokritḗs | hoop-ok-ree-tace')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5271<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an actor under an assumed character (stage-player), i.e. (figuratively) a dissembler (\"hypocrite\"<BR><B>KJV:</B> hypocrite.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5271<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5273 (hypocrite), G505 (without dissimulation), G5272 (condemnation), G4942 (dissemble with), G5271 (feign)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑποκριτής<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2611 חָנֵף",
    5274: "ὑπολαμβάνω (hypolambánō | hoop-ol-am-ban'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G2983<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to take from below, i.e. carry upward; figuratively, to take up, i.e. continue a discourse or topic; mentally, to assume (presume)<BR><B>KJV:</B> answer, receive, suppose.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G2983<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπολαμβάνω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H270 אָחַז, H935 בֹּוא, H1802 דָּלָה, H1819 דָּמָה, H2803 חָשַׁב, H3498 יָתַר, H6030 עָנָה, H7475 רַעְיֹון",
    5275: "ὑπολείπω (hypoleípō | hoop-ol-i'-po)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5295 and G3007<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to leave under (behind), i.e. (passively) to remain (survive)<BR><B>KJV:</B> be left.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5295<BR><I>See:</I> G3007<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G353 (receive up), G4301 (come aforehand), G2638 (apprehend), G4356 (receiving), G3880 (receive), G1949 (catch), G354 (taking up), G5274 (answer), G4355 (receive), G423 (blameless), G2983 (accept), G3335 (eat), G3336 (taking)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπολείπω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H680 אָצַל, H1633 גָּרַם, H3322 יָצַג, H3498 יָתַר, H5736 עֲדַף, H5800 עָזַב, H5975 עָמַד, H7604 שָׁאַר, H7662 שְׁבַק, H7760 שׂוּם",
    5276: "ὑπολήνιον (hypolḗnion | hoop-ol-ay'-nee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a presumed compound of G5259 and G3025<BR><B>Strong's:</B> vessel or receptacle under the press, i.e. lower wine-vat<BR><B>KJV:</B> winefat.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G3025<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5276 (winefat), G3025 (winepress)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπολήνιον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3342 יֶקֶב",
    5277: "ὑπολιμπάνω (hypolimpánō | hoop-ol-im-pan'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a prolonged form for G5275<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to leave behind, i.e. bequeath<BR><B>KJV:</B> leave.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5275<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5276 (winefat), G3025 (winepress)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπολιμπάνω, ἀπολιμπάνω",
    5278: "ὑπομένω (hypoménō | hoop-om-en'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G3306<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to stay under (behind), i.e. remain; figuratively, to undergo, i.e. bear (trials), have fortitude, persevere<BR><B>KJV:</B> abide, endure, (take) patient(-ly), suffer, tarry behind.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G3306<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5278 (abide), G3887 (abide), G5281 (enduring), G1696 (continue), G4037 (wait for), G3306 (abide), G3438 (abode)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπομένω, ἀπομένω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2342 חוּל, H2442 חָכָה, H2934 טָמַן, H3176 יָחַל, H3427 יָשַׁב, H3557 כּוּל, H4102 מָהַהּ, H6960 קָוָה, H6965 קוּם",
    5279: "ὑπομιμνήσκω (hypomimnḗskō | hoop-om-im-nace'-ko)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G3403<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to remind quietly, i.e. suggest to the (middle voice, one's own) memory<BR><B>KJV:</B> put in mind, remember, bring to (put in) remembrance.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G3403<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5278 (abide), G3887 (abide), G5281 (enduring), G1696 (continue), G4037 (wait for), G3306 (abide), G3438 (abode)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπομιμνήσκω, ὑπομιμνῄσκω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2142 זָכַר",
    5280: "ὑπόμνησις (hypómnēsis | hoop-om'-nay-sis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5279<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a reminding or (reflexively) recollection<BR><B>KJV:</B> remembrance.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5279<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G364 (remembrance), G5280 (remembrance)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπόμνησις<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H8416 תְּהִלָּה",
    5281: "ὑπομονή (hypomonḗ | hoop-om-on-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5278<BR><B>Strong's:</B> cheerful (or hopeful) endurance, constancy<BR><B>KJV:</B> enduring, patience, patient continuance (waiting).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5278<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5278 (abide), G3887 (abide), G5281 (enduring), G1696 (continue), G4037 (wait for), G3306 (abide), G3438 (abode)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπομονή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4723 מִקְוֶה",
    5282: "ὑπονοέω (hyponoéō | hoop-on-o-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G3539<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to think under (privately), i.e. to surmise or conjecture<BR><B>KJV:</B> think, suppose, deem.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G3539<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3559 (admonition), G5282 (think), G2657 (behold), G3539 (consider), G1270 (thought), G2133 (benevolence), G1271 (imagination), G3540 (device), G4307 (providence), G279 (impenitent), G4306 (provide), G1425 (hard to be understood), G2132 (agree), G453 (fool), G5283 (surmising), G3563 (mind), G3340 (repent), G1771 (intent), G454 (folly)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπονοέω",
    5283: "ὑπόνοια (hypónoia | hoop-on'-oy-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5282<BR><B>Strong's:</B> suspicion<BR><B>KJV:</B> surmising.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5282<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3559 (admonition), G5282 (think), G2657 (behold), G3539 (consider), G1270 (thought), G2133 (benevolence), G1271 (imagination), G3540 (device), G4307 (providence), G279 (impenitent), G4306 (provide), G1425 (hard to be understood), G2132 (agree), G453 (fool), G5283 (surmising), G3563 (mind), G3340 (repent), G1771 (intent), G454 (folly)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπόνοια<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7475 רַעְיֹון",
    5284: "ὑποπλέω (hypopléō | hoop-op-leh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G4126<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to sail under the lee of<BR><B>KJV:</B> sail under.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G4126<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3559 (admonition), G5282 (think), G2657 (behold), G3539 (consider), G1270 (thought), G2133 (benevolence), G1271 (imagination), G3540 (device), G4307 (providence), G279 (impenitent), G4306 (provide), G1425 (hard to be understood), G2132 (agree), G453 (fool), G5283 (surmising), G3563 (mind), G3340 (repent), G1771 (intent), G454 (folly)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑποπλέω",
    5285: "ὑποπνέω (hypopnéō | hoop-op-neh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G4154<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to breathe gently, i.e. breeze<BR><B>KJV:</B> blow softly.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G4154<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3559 (admonition), G5282 (think), G2657 (behold), G3539 (consider), G1270 (thought), G2133 (benevolence), G1271 (imagination), G3540 (device), G4307 (providence), G279 (impenitent), G4306 (provide), G1425 (hard to be understood), G2132 (agree), G453 (fool), G5283 (surmising), G3563 (mind), G3340 (repent), G1771 (intent), G454 (folly)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑποπνέω",
    5286: "ὑποπόδιον (hypopódion | hoop-op-od'-ee-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a compound of G5259 and G4228<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something under the feet, i.e. a foot-rest (figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> footstool.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G4228<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3559 (admonition), G5282 (think), G2657 (behold), G3539 (consider), G1270 (thought), G2133 (benevolence), G1271 (imagination), G3540 (device), G4307 (providence), G279 (impenitent), G4306 (provide), G1425 (hard to be understood), G2132 (agree), G453 (fool), G5283 (surmising), G3563 (mind), G3340 (repent), G1771 (intent), G454 (folly)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑποπόδιον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1916 הֲדֹם",
    5287: "ὑπόστασις (hypóstasis | hoop-os'-tas-is)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a compound of G5259 and G2476<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a setting under (support), i.e. (figuratively) concretely, essence, or abstractly, assurance (objectively or subjectively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> confidence, confident, person, substance.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G2476<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5287 (confidence)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑπόστασις<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2465 חֶלֶד, H3351 יְקוּם, H3666 כִּנְעָה, H4241 מִחְיָה, H4613 מׇעֳמָד, H4673 מַצָּב, H4853 מַשָּׂא, H5324 נָצַב, H5475 סֹוד, H7551 רָקַם, H8431 תֹּוחֶלֶת, H8499 תְּכוּנָה, H8615 תִּקְוָה",
    5288: "ὑποστέλλω (hypostéllō | hoop-os-tel'-lo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5259 and G4724<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to withhold under (out of sight), i.e. (reflexively) to cower or shrink, (figuratively) to conceal (reserve)<BR><B>KJV:</B> draw (keep) back, shun, withdraw.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5259<BR><I>See:</I> G4724<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5288 (draw back), G1291 (charge), G4958 (short), G2689 (apparel), G2687 (appease), G1992 (\"epistle), G1989 (write), G5289 (draw back), G1293 (difference), G4724 (avoid)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑποστέλλω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1481 גּוּר, H3607 כָּלָא, H6075 עָפַל, H6440 פָּנִים",
    5289: "ὑποστολή (hypostolḗ | hoop-os-tol-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5288<BR><B>Strong's:</B> shrinkage (timidity), i.e. (by implication) apostasy<BR><B>KJV:</B> draw back.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5288<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5288 (draw back), G1291 (charge), G4958 (short), G2689 (apparel), G2687 (appease), G1992 (\"epistle), G1989 (write), G5289 (draw back), G1293 (difference), G4724 (avoid)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὑποστολή",
