    5395: "φλόξ (phlóx | flox)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a primary φλέγω (to \"flash\" or \"flame\")<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a blaze<BR><B>KJV:</B> flame(-ing).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5387 (kindly affectioned), G5384 (friend), G5377 (lover of God), G5369 (lover of pleasure), G5383 (love to have the preeminence), G2705 (kiss), G5370 (kiss), G5373 (friendship), G5367 (lover of own self), G5368 (kiss)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φλόξ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H784 אֵשׁ, H2131 זִיקָה, H3827 לַבָּה, H3851 לַהַב, H3852 לֶהָבָה, H7008 קִיטֹור, H7632 שָׁבִיב, H7957 שַׁלְהֶבֶת",
    5396: "φλυαρέω (phlyaréō | floo-ar-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5397<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be a babbler or trifler, i.e. (by implication) to berate idly or mischievously<BR><B>KJV:</B> prate against.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5397<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5387 (kindly affectioned), G5384 (friend), G5377 (lover of God), G5369 (lover of pleasure), G5383 (love to have the preeminence), G2705 (kiss), G5370 (kiss), G5373 (friendship), G5367 (lover of own self), G5368 (kiss)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φλυαρέω",
    5397: "φλύαρος (phlýaros | floo'-ar-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from φλύω (to bubble)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a garrulous person, i.e. prater<BR><B>KJV:</B> tattler.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5387 (kindly affectioned), G5384 (friend), G5377 (lover of God), G5369 (lover of pleasure), G5383 (love to have the preeminence), G2705 (kiss), G5370 (kiss), G5373 (friendship), G5367 (lover of own self), G5368 (kiss)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φλύαρος",
    5398: "φοβερός (phoberós | fob-er-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5401<BR><B>Strong's:</B> frightful, i.e. (objectively) formidable<BR><B>KJV:</B> fearful, terrible.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5401<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5387 (kindly affectioned), G5384 (friend), G5377 (lover of God), G5369 (lover of pleasure), G5383 (love to have the preeminence), G2705 (kiss), G5370 (kiss), G5373 (friendship), G5367 (lover of own self), G5368 (kiss)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φοβερός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H366 אָיֹם, H1763 דְּחַל, H3372 יָרֵא, H4172 מֹורָא",
    5399: "φοβέω (phobéō | fob-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5401<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to frighten, i.e. (passively) to be alarmed; by analogy, to be in awe of, i.e. revere<BR><B>KJV:</B> be (+ sore) afraid, fear (exceedingly), reverence.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5401<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5400 (fearful sight), G5399 (be afraid), G5401 (be afraid)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φοβέω, φοβέομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1481 גּוּר, H1672 דָּאַג, H1763 דְּחַל, H2342 חוּל, H2730 חָרֵד, H2865 חָתַת, H3025 יָגֹר, H3372 יָרֵא, H3372 יָרֵא, H5128 נוּעַ, H6206 עָרַץ, H6342 פָּחַד, H6399 פְּלַח, H7264 רָגַז, H7493 רָעַשׁ, H7760 שׂוּם",
    5400: "φόβητρον (phóbētron | fob'-ay-tron)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a derivative of G5399<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a frightening thing, i.e. terrific portent<BR><B>KJV:</B> fearful sight.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5399<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5400 (fearful sight), G5399 (be afraid), G5401 (be afraid)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φόβητρον, φόβητρον/φόβηθρον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2283 חָגָא",
    5401: "φόβος (phóbos | fob'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a primary φέβομαι (to be put in fear)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> alarm or fright<BR><B>KJV:</B> be afraid, + exceedingly, fear, terror.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5400 (fearful sight), G5399 (be afraid), G5401 (be afraid)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φόβος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H367 אֵימָה, H1763 דְּחַל, H2730 חָרֵד, H2844 חַת, H3374 יִרְאָה, H6184 עָרִיץ, H6343 פַּחַד, H7413 רָמָה",
    5402: "Φοίβη (Phoíbē | foy'-bay)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of φοῖβος (bright<BR><B>Strong's:</B> probably akin to the base of G5457); Phœbe, a Christian woman<BR><B>KJV:</B> Phebe.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5457<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5400 (fearful sight), G5399 (be afraid), G5401 (be afraid)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Φοίβη",
    5403: "Φοινίκη (Phoiníkē | foy-nee'-kay)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5404<BR><B>Strong's:</B> palm-country; Phœnice (or Phœnicia), a region of Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Phenice, Phenicia.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5404<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5400 (fearful sight), G5399 (be afraid), G5401 (be afraid)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Φοινίκη",
    5404: "φοῖνιξ (phoînix | foy'-nix)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a palm-tree<BR><B>KJV:</B> palm (tree).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5400 (fearful sight), G5399 (be afraid), G5401 (be afraid)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φοῖνιξ, φοῖνιξ1, φοῖνιξ/φοίνιξ, φοίνιξ",
    5405: "Φοῖνιξ (Phoînix | foy'-nix)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably the same as G5404<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Phœnix, a place in Crete<BR><B>KJV:</B> Phenice.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5404<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5400 (fearful sight), G5399 (be afraid), G5401 (be afraid)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Φοῖνιξ",
    5406: "φονεύς (phoneús | fon-yooce')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5408<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a murderer (always of criminal (or at least intentional) homicide; which G443 does not necessarily imply; while G4607 is a special term for a public bandit)<BR><B>KJV:</B> murderer.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5408<BR><I>See:</I> G443<BR><I>See:</I> G4607<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5400 (fearful sight), G5399 (be afraid), G5401 (be afraid)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φονεύς",
    5407: "φονεύω (phoneúō | fon-yoo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5406<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be a murderer (of)<BR><B>KJV:</B> kill, do murder, slay.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5406<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5400 (fearful sight), G5399 (be afraid), G5401 (be afraid)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φονεύω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2026 הָרַג, H2763 חָרַם, H5221 נָכָה, H7523 רָצַח",
    5408: "φόνος (phónos | fon'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an obsolete primary φένω (to slay)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> murder<BR><B>KJV:</B> murder, + be slain with, slaughter.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5400 (fearful sight), G5399 (be afraid), G5401 (be afraid)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φόνος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1818 דָּם, H2719 חֶרֶב, H6297 פֶּגֶר, H6310 פֶּה, H7523 רָצַח",
    5409: "φορέω (phoréō | for-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5411<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to have a burden, i.e. (by analogy) to wear as clothing or a constant accompaniment<BR><B>KJV:</B> bear, wear.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5411<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φορέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3254 יָסַף",
    5410: "Φόρον (Phóron | for'-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a forum or market-place; only in comparative with G675 ; a station on the Appian road<BR><B>KJV:</B> forum.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G675<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Φόρον, φόρον, Ἀππίου~Φόρον, Ἀππίου Φόρον",
    5411: "φόρος (phóros | for'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5342<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a load (as borne), i.e. (figuratively) a tax (properly, an individual assessment on persons or property; whereas G5056 is usually a general toll on goods or travel)<BR><B>KJV:</B> tribute.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5342<BR><I>See:</I> G5056<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φόρος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1094 בְּלֹוא, H1980 הָלַךְ, H4060 מִדָּה, H4522 מַס, H6064 עָנַשׁ",
    5412: "φορτίζω (phortízō | for-tid'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5414<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to load up (properly, as a vessel or animal), i.e. (figuratively) to overburden with ceremony (or spiritual anxiety)<BR><B>KJV:</B> lade, by heavy laden.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5414<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φορτίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7809 שָׁחַד",
    5413: "φορτίον (phortíon | for-tee'-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> diminutive of G5414<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an invoice (as part of freight), i.e. (figuratively) a task or service<BR><B>KJV:</B> burden.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5414<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φορτίον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4853 מַשָּׂא, H5520 סֹךְ",
    5414: "φόρτος (phórtos | for'-tos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5342<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something carried, i.e. the cargo of a ship<BR><B>KJV:</B> lading.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5342<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φόρτος G5846",
    5415: "Φορτουνᾶτος (Phortounâtos | for-too-nat'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"fortunate\"; Fortunatus, a Christian<BR><B>KJV:</B> Fortunatus.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Φορτουνᾶτος, Φορτουνάτος",
    5416: "φραγέλλιον (phragéllion | frag-el'-le-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a derivative from the base of G5417<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a whip, i.e. Roman lash as a public punishment<BR><B>KJV:</B> scourge.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5417<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φραγέλλιον",
    5417: "φραγελλόω (phragellóō | frag-el-lo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a presumed equivalent of the Latin flagellum<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to whip, i.e. lash as a public punishment<BR><B>KJV:</B> scourge.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φραγελλόω, φλαγελλόω",
    5418: "φραγμός (phragmós | frag-mos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5420<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a fence, or inclosing barrier (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> hedge (+ round about), partition.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5420<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φραγμός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1447 גָּדֵר, H1448 גְּדֵרָה, H4189 מֹושְׁכָה, H4881 מְשׂוּכָה, H5823 עָזַק, H6556 פֶּרֶץ",
    5419: "φράζω (phrázō | frad'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably akin to G5420 through the idea of defining<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to indicate (by word or act), i.e. (specially), to expound<BR><B>KJV:</B>  declare.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5420<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φράζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H995 בִּין, H2244 חָבָא, H3384 יָרָה",
    5420: "φράσσω (phrássō | fras'-so)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a strengthening form of the base of G5424<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to fence or inclose, i.e. (specially), to block up (figuratively, to silence)<BR><B>KJV:</B> stop.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5424<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φράσσω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H331 אָטַם, H5472 סוּג, H5480 סוּךְ, H5526 סָכַךְ, H5640 סָתַם, H7515 רָפַשׂ",
    5421: "φρέαρ (phréar | freh'-ar)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a hole in the ground (dug for obtaining or holding water or other purposes), i.e. a cistern or well; figuratively, an abyss (as a prison)<BR><B>KJV:</B> well, pit.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φρέαρ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H875 בְּאֵר, H953 בֹּור, H1460 גֵּו",
    5422: "φρεναπατάω (phrenapatáō | fren-ap-at-ah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5423<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be a mind-misleader, i.e. delude<BR><B>KJV:</B> deceive.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5423<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φρεναπατάω",
    5423: "φρεναπάτης (phrenapátēs | fren-ap-at'-ace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5424 and G539<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a mind-misleader, i.e. seducer<BR><B>KJV:</B> deceiver.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5424<BR><I>See:</I> G539<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5411 (tribute), G4376 (offering), G1313 (differing), G4851 (be better for), G399 (bear), G5413 (burden), G5412 (lade), G5414 (lading), G5342 (be), G2018 (add), G4374 (bring), G5409 (bear), G1308 (be better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φρεναπάτης",
    5424: "φρήν (phrḗn | frane)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from an obsolete φράω (to rein in or curb; compare G5420)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the midrif (as a partition of the body), i.e. (figuratively and by implication, of sympathy) the feelings (or sensitive nature; by extension (also in the plural) the mind or cognitive faculties)<BR><B>KJV:</B> understanding.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5420<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5430 (wisely), G877 (folly), G5428 (prudence), G5429 (wise), G5424 (understanding), G5427 (mind), G878 (fool), G5426 (set the affection on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φρήν<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3685 כְּסִיל, H3820 לֵב, H4486 מַנְדַּע",
    5425: "φρίσσω (phríssō | fris'-so)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to \"bristle\" or chill, i.e. shudder (fear)<BR><B>KJV:</B> tremble.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5430 (wisely), G877 (folly), G5428 (prudence), G5429 (wise), G5424 (understanding), G5427 (mind), G878 (fool), G5426 (set the affection on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φρίσσω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3735 כָּרָא, H5568 סָמַר, H5590 סָעַר",
    5426: "φρονέω (phronéō | fron-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5424<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to exercise the mind, i.e. entertain or have a sentiment or opinion; by implication, to be (mentally) disposed (more or less earnestly in a certain direction); intensively, to interest oneself in (with concern or obedience)<BR><B>KJV:</B> set the affection on, (be) care(-ful), (be like-, + be of one, + be of the same, + let this) mind(-ed), regard, savour, think.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5424<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5430 (wisely), G877 (folly), G5428 (prudence), G5429 (wise), G5424 (understanding), G5427 (mind), G878 (fool), G5426 (set the affection on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φρονέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H995 בִּין, H2450 חָכָם, H7919 שָׂכַל",
    5427: "φρόνημα (phrónēma | fron'-ay-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5426<BR><B>Strong's:</B> (mental) inclination or purpose<BR><B>KJV:</B> (be, + be carnally, + be spiritually) mind(-ed).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5426<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5430 (wisely), G877 (folly), G5428 (prudence), G5429 (wise), G5424 (understanding), G5427 (mind), G878 (fool), G5426 (set the affection on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φρόνημα",
    5428: "φρόνησις (phrónēsis | fron'-ay-sis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5426<BR><B>Strong's:</B> mental action or activity, i.e. intellectual or moral insight<BR><B>KJV:</B> prudence, wisdom.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5426<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5430 (wisely), G877 (folly), G5428 (prudence), G5429 (wise), G5424 (understanding), G5427 (mind), G878 (fool), G5426 (set the affection on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φρόνησις<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H999 בִּינָה, H1847 דַּעַת, H2451 חׇכְמָה, H3820 לֵב, H6195 עׇרְמָה, H7307 רוּחַ, H7922 שֶׂכֶל, H8394 תָּבוּן",
    5429: "φρόνιμος (phrónimos | fron'-ee-mos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5424<BR><B>Strong's:</B> thoughtful, i.e. sagacious or discreet (implying a cautious character; while G4680 denotes practical skill or acumen; and G4908 indicates rather intelligence or mental acquirement); in a bad sense conceited (also in the comparative)<BR><B>KJV:</B> wise(-r).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5424<BR><I>See:</I> G4680<BR><I>See:</I> G4908<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5430 (wisely), G877 (folly), G5428 (prudence), G5429 (wise), G5424 (understanding), G5427 (mind), G878 (fool), G5426 (set the affection on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φρόνιμος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H995 בִּין, H2450 חָכָם, H4209 מְזִמָּה, H6175 עָרוּם, H8394 תָּבוּן",
    5430: "φρονίμως (phronímōs | fron-im'-oce)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from G5429<BR><B>Strong's:</B> prudently<BR><B>KJV:</B> wisely.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5429<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5430 (wisely), G877 (folly), G5428 (prudence), G5429 (wise), G5424 (understanding), G5427 (mind), G878 (fool), G5426 (set the affection on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φρονίμως",
    5431: "φροντίζω (phrontízō | fron-tid'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of G5424<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to exercise thought, i.e. be anxious<BR><B>KJV:</B> be careful.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5424<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5430 (wisely), G877 (folly), G5428 (prudence), G5429 (wise), G5424 (understanding), G5427 (mind), G878 (fool), G5426 (set the affection on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φροντίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1672 דָּאַג, H2803 חָשַׁב, H3372 יָרֵא, H6342 פָּחַד",
    5432: "φρουρέω (phrouréō | froo-reh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a compound of G4253 and G3708<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be a watcher in advance, i.e. to mount guard as a sentinel (post spies at gates); figuratively, to hem in, protect<BR><B>KJV:</B> keep (with a garrison). Compare G5083 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4253<BR><I>See:</I> G3708<BR><I>See:</I> G5083<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5430 (wisely), G877 (folly), G5428 (prudence), G5429 (wise), G5424 (understanding), G5427 (mind), G878 (fool), G5426 (set the affection on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φρουρέω",
    5433: "φρυάσσω (phryássō | froo-as'-so)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> akin to G1032, G1031<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to snort (as a spirited horse), i.e. (figuratively) to make a tumult<BR><B>KJV:</B> rage.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G1031<BR><I>See:</I> G1032<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5430 (wisely), G877 (folly), G5428 (prudence), G5429 (wise), G5424 (understanding), G5427 (mind), G878 (fool), G5426 (set the affection on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φρυάσσω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7283 רָגַשׁ",
    5434: "φρύγανον (phrýganon | froo'-gan-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a presumed derivative of φρύγω (to roast or parch<BR><B>Strong's:</B> akin to the base of G5395); something desiccated, i.e. a dry twig<BR><B>KJV:</B> stick.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5395<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5430 (wisely), G877 (folly), G5428 (prudence), G5429 (wise), G5424 (understanding), G5427 (mind), G878 (fool), G5426 (set the affection on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φρύγανον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2738 חָרוּל, H7110 קֶצֶף, H7179 קַשׁ",
    5435: "Φρυγία (Phrygía | froog-ee'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably of foreign origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Phrygia, a region of Asia Minor<BR><B>KJV:</B> Phrygia.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5430 (wisely), G877 (folly), G5428 (prudence), G5429 (wise), G5424 (understanding), G5427 (mind), G878 (fool), G5426 (set the affection on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Φρυγία",
    5436: "Φύγελλος (Phýgellos | foog'-el-los)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from G5343<BR><B>Strong's:</B> fugitive; Phygellus, an apostate Christian<BR><B>KJV:</B> Phygellus.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5343<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5430 (wisely), G877 (folly), G5428 (prudence), G5429 (wise), G5424 (understanding), G5427 (mind), G878 (fool), G5426 (set the affection on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Φύγελλος, Φύγελος, Φύγελος/Φύγελλος",
    5437: "φυγή (phygḗ | foog-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5343<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a fleeing, i.e. escape<BR><B>KJV:</B> flight.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5343<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5430 (wisely), G877 (folly), G5428 (prudence), G5429 (wise), G5424 (understanding), G5427 (mind), G878 (fool), G5426 (set the affection on)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φυγή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1272 בָּרַח, H4498 מָנֹוס, H5127 נוּס",
    5438: "φυλακή (phylakḗ | foo-lak-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5442<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a guarding or (concretely, guard), the act, the person; figuratively, the place, the condition, or (specially), the time (as a division of day or night), literally or figuratively<BR><B>KJV:</B> cage, hold, (im-)prison(-ment), ward, watch.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5442<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5438 (cage), G5441 (keeper), G5442 (beward), G5439 (imprison)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φυλακή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H615 אָסִיר, H821 אַשְׁמֻרָה, H3608 כֶּלֶא, H4115 מַהְפֶּכֶת, H4307 מַטָּרָא, H4525 מַסְגֵּר, H4685 מָצֹוד, H4931 מִשְׁמֶרֶת, H5341 נָצַר",
    5439: "φυλακίζω (phylakízō | foo-lak-id'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5441<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to incarcerate<BR><B>KJV:</B> imprison.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5441<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5438 (cage), G5441 (keeper), G5442 (beward), G5439 (imprison)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φυλακίζω",
    5440: "φυλακτήριον (phylaktḗrion | foo-lak-tay'-ree-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a derivative of G5442<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a guard-case, i.e. \"phylactery\" for wearing slips of Scripture texts<BR><B>KJV:</B>  phylactery.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5442<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5438 (cage), G5441 (keeper), G5442 (beward), G5439 (imprison)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φυλακτήριον",
    5441: "φύλαξ (phýlax | foo'-lax)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5442<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a watcher or sentry<BR><B>KJV:</B> keeper.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5442<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5438 (cage), G5441 (keeper), G5442 (beward), G5439 (imprison)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φύλαξ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6697 צוּר, H8104 שָׁמַר",
    5442: "φυλάσσω (phylássō | foo-las'-so)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably from G5443 through the idea of isolation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to watch, i.e. be on guard (literally of figuratively); by implication, to preserve, obey, avoid<BR><B>KJV:</B> beward, keep (self), observe, save. Compare G5083 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5443<BR><I>See:</I> G5083<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5438 (cage), G5441 (keeper), G5442 (beward), G5439 (imprison)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φυλάσσω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1961 הָיָה, H2095 זְהַר, H2421 חָיָה, H5341 נָצַר, H5425 נָתַר, H6113 עָצָר, H6213 עָשָׂה, H6487 פִּקָּדֹון, H6822 צָפָה, H8085 שָׁמַע, H8104 שָׁמַר",
    5443: "φυλή (phylḗ | foo-lay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5453 (compare G5444)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an offshoot, i.e. race or clan<BR><B>KJV:</B> kindred, tribe.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5453<BR><I>See:</I> G5444<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5443 (kindred)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φυλή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H524 אֻמָּה, H1004 בַּיִת, H1471 גֹּוי, H3816 לְאֹם, H4138 מֹולֶדֶת, H4294 מַטֶּה, H4940 מִשְׁפָּחָה, H7626 שֵׁבֶט",
    5444: "φύλλον (phýllon | fool'-lon)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as G5443<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a sprout, i.e. leaf<BR><B>KJV:</B> leaf.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5443<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5443 (kindred)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φύλλον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5929 עָלֶה, H6074 עֳפִי",
    5445: "φύραμα (phýrama | foo'-ram-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a prolonged form of φύρω (to mix a liquid with a solid<BR><B>Strong's:</B> perhaps akin to G5453 through the idea of swelling in bulk), mean to knead; a mass of dough<BR><B>KJV:</B> lump.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5453<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5443 (kindred)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φύραμα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4863 מִשְׁאֶרֶת, H6182 עֲרִיסָה",
    5446: "φυσικός (physikós | foo-see-kos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5449<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"physical\", i.e. (by implication) instinctive<BR><B>KJV:</B> natural. Compare G5591 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5449<BR><I>See:</I> G5591<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5446 (natural), G5447 (naturally), G5449 (kind)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φυσικός",
    5447: "φυσικῶς (physikōs | foo-see-koce')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from G5446<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"physically\", i.e. (by implication) instinctively<BR><B>KJV:</B> naturally.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5446<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5446 (natural), G5447 (naturally), G5449 (kind)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φυσικῶς",
    5448: "φυσιόω (physióō | foo-see-o'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5449 in the primary sense of blowing<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to inflate, i.e. (figuratively) make proud (haughty)<BR><B>KJV:</B> puff up.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5449<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5448 (puff up), G5450 (swelling)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φυσιόω",
    5449: "φύσις (phýsis | foo'-sis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5453<BR><B>Strong's:</B> growth (by germination or expansion), i.e. (by implication) natural production (lineal descent); by extension, a genus or sort; figuratively, native disposition, constitution or usage<BR><B>KJV:</B> (man-)kind, nature(-al).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5453<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5446 (natural), G5447 (naturally), G5449 (kind)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φύσις",
    5450: "φυσίωσις (physíōsis | foo-see'-o-sis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5448<BR><B>Strong's:</B> inflation, i.e. (figuratively) haughtiness<BR><B>KJV:</B> swelling.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5448<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5448 (puff up), G5450 (swelling)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φυσίωσις",
    5451: "φυτεία (phyteía | foo-ti'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5452<BR><B>Strong's:</B> trans-planting, i.e. (concretely) a shrub or vegetable<BR><B>KJV:</B> plant.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5452<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5448 (puff up), G5450 (swelling)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φυτεία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4302 מַטָּע, H5193 נָטַע",
    5452: "φυτεύω (phyteúō | foot-yoo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of G5453<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to set out in the earth, i.e. implant; figuratively, to instil doctrine<BR><B>KJV:</B> plant.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5453<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5448 (puff up), G5450 (swelling)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φυτεύω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5193 נָטַע, H5341 נָצַר, H6213 עָשָׂה, H8362 שָׁתַל",
    5453: "φύω (phýō | foo'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> a primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> probably originally, to \"puff\" or blow, i.e. to swell up; but only used in the implied sense, to germinate or grow (sprout, produce), literally or figuratively<BR><B>KJV:</B> spring (up).<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5448 (puff up), G5450 (swelling)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φύω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H5193 נָטַע, H5927 עָלָה, H6509 פָּרָה, H6779 צָמַח",
    5454: "φωλεός (phōleós | fo-leh-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivative<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a burrow or lurking-place<BR><B>KJV:</B> hole.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5448 (puff up), G5450 (swelling)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φωλεός",
    5455: "φωνέω (phōnéō | fo-neh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5456<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to emit a sound (animal, human or instrumental); by implication, to address in words or by name, also in imitation<BR><B>KJV:</B> call (for), crow, cry.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5456<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4859 (consent), G2019 (cry), G4857 (concord), G4858 (music), G4856 (agree together), G5455 (call), G5456 (noise)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φωνέω, ἐμφωνέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1898 הָגָה, H1898 הָגָה, H5375 נָשָׂא, H6850 צָפַף, H7121 קָרָא, H7891 שִׁיר, H8628 תָּקַע",
    5456: "φωνή (phōnḗ | fo-nay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably akin to G5316 through the idea of disclosure<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a tone (articulate, bestial or artificial); by implication, an address (for any purpose), saying or language<BR><B>KJV:</B> noise, sound, voice.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5316<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G4859 (consent), G2019 (cry), G4857 (concord), G4858 (music), G4856 (agree together), G5455 (call), G5456 (noise)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φωνή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H565 אִמְרָה, H1600 גָּעָה, H1697 דָּבָר, H1995 הָמֹון, H2201 זַעַק, H3956 לָשֹׁון, H4687 מִצְוָה, H5100 נְהָמָה, H6310 פֶּה, H6618 פְּתַלְתֹּל, H6963 קֹול, H8193 שָׂפָה, H8467 תְּחִנָּה, H8643 תְּרוּעָה",
    5457: "φῶς (phōs | foce)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from an obsolete φάω (to shine or make manifest, especially by rays<BR><B>Strong's:</B> compare G5316, G5346); luminousness (in the widest application, natural or artificial, abstract or concrete, literal or figurative)<BR><B>KJV:</B> fire, light.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5316<BR><I>See:</I> G5346<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5462 (light), G2017 (give light), G5457 (fire), G5458 (light), G2020 (begin to dawn), G5460 (bright), G5461 (enlighten), G5459 (day star)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φῶς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H216 אֹור, H5043 נֶבְרְשָׁא, H5051 נֹגַהּ, H5094 נְהִיר, H5216 נִיר",
    5458: "φωστήρ (phōstḗr | foce-tare')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5457<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an illuminator, i.e. (concretely) a luminary, or (abstractly) brilliancy<BR><B>KJV:</B> light.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5457<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5462 (light), G2017 (give light), G5457 (fire), G5458 (light), G2020 (begin to dawn), G5460 (bright), G5461 (enlighten), G5459 (day star)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φωστήρ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2096 זֹהַר, H3974 מָאֹור",
    5459: "φωσφόρος (phōsphóros | foce-for'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5457 and G5342<BR><B>Strong's:</B> light-bearing (\"phosphorus\"), i.e. (specially), the morning-star (figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> day star.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5457<BR><I>See:</I> G5342<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5462 (light), G2017 (give light), G5457 (fire), G5458 (light), G2020 (begin to dawn), G5460 (bright), G5461 (enlighten), G5459 (day star)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φωσφόρος",
    5460: "φωτεινός (phōteinós | fo-ti-nos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5457<BR><B>Strong's:</B> lustrous, i.e. transparent or well-illuminated (figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> bright, full of light.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5457<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5462 (light), G2017 (give light), G5457 (fire), G5458 (light), G2020 (begin to dawn), G5460 (bright), G5461 (enlighten), G5459 (day star)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φωτεινός",
    5461: "φωτίζω (phōtízō | fo-tid'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5457<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to shed rays, i.e. to shine or (transitively) to brighten up (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> enlighten, illuminate, (bring to, give) light, make to see.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5457<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5462 (light), G2017 (give light), G5457 (fire), G5458 (light), G2020 (begin to dawn), G5460 (bright), G5461 (enlighten), G5459 (day star)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φωτίζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H215 אֹור, H224 אוּרִים, H3384 יָרָה, H5050 נָגַהּ, H5102 נָהַר, H5214 נִיר, H7200 רָאָה",
    5462: "φωτισμός (phōtismós | fo-tis-mos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5461<BR><B>Strong's:</B> illumination (figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> light.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5461<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5462 (light), G2017 (give light), G5457 (fire), G5458 (light), G2020 (begin to dawn), G5460 (bright), G5461 (enlighten), G5459 (day star)<BR><B>Variants:</B> φωτισμός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H216 אֹור, H3974 מָאֹור",
