    5493: "χείμαῤῥος (cheímarrhos | khi'-mar-hros)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G5494 and G4482<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a storm-runlet, i.e. winter-torrent<BR><B>KJV:</B> brook.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5494<BR><I>See:</I> G4482<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5479 (gladness), G4796 (rejoice in), G2168 (thank), G2169 (thankfulness), G5485 (acceptable), G5486 (gift), G5463 (farewell), G5484 (be- cause of), G2170 (thankful), G5487 (make accepted), G884 (unthankful), G5483 (deliver)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χείμαῤῥος, χείμαρρος, χειμάρρους",
    5494: "χειμών (cheimṓn | khi-mone')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of χέω<BR><B>Strong's:</B> (to pour; akin to the base of 5490 through the idea of a channel), meaning a storm (as pouring rain); by implication, the rainy season, i.e. winter<BR><B>KJV:</B> tempest, foul weather, winter.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5479 (gladness), G4796 (rejoice in), G2168 (thank), G2169 (thankfulness), G5485 (acceptable), G5486 (gift), G5463 (farewell), G5484 (be- cause of), G2170 (thankful), G5487 (make accepted), G884 (unthankful), G5483 (deliver)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χειμών<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1653 גֶּשֶׁם, H5638 סְתָו",
    5495: "χείρ (cheír | khire)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> perhaps from the base of G5494 in the sense of its congener the base of G5490 (through the idea of hollowness for grasping)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the hand (literally or figuratively (power); especially (by Hebraism) a means or instrument)<BR><B>KJV:</B> hand.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5494<BR><I>See:</I> G5490<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5499 (made by hands), G886 (made without hands), G5495 (hand), G5498 (handwriting), G5497 (some to lead by the hand), G5496 (lead by the hand), G5500 (choose)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χείρ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2651 חֹפֶן, H3027 יָד, H3225 יָמִין, H3581 כֹּחַ, H3709 כַּף, H8168 שֹׁעַל, H8420 תָּו",
    5496: "χειραγωγέω (cheiragōgéō | khi-rag-ogue-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5497<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be a hand-leader, i.e. to guide (a blind person)<BR><B>KJV:</B> lead by the hand.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5497<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5499 (made by hands), G886 (made without hands), G5495 (hand), G5498 (handwriting), G5497 (some to lead by the hand), G5496 (lead by the hand), G5500 (choose)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χειραγωγέω",
    5497: "χειραγωγός (cheiragōgós | khi-rag-o-gos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5495 and a reduplicated form of G71<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a hand-leader, i.e. personal conductor (of a blind person)<BR><B>KJV:</B> some to lead by the hand.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5495<BR><I>See:</I> G71<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5499 (made by hands), G886 (made without hands), G5495 (hand), G5498 (handwriting), G5497 (some to lead by the hand), G5496 (lead by the hand), G5500 (choose)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χειραγωγός",
    5498: "χειρόγραφον (cheirógraphon | khi-rog'-raf-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> neuter of a compound of G5495 and G1125<BR><B>Strong's:</B> something hand-written (\"chirograph\"), i.e. a manuscript (specially, a legal document or bond (figuratively))<BR><B>KJV:</B> handwriting.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5495<BR><I>See:</I> G1125<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5499 (made by hands), G886 (made without hands), G5495 (hand), G5498 (handwriting), G5497 (some to lead by the hand), G5496 (lead by the hand), G5500 (choose)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χειρόγραφον",
    5499: "χειροποίητος (cheiropoíētos | khi-rop-oy'-ay-tos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5495 and a derivative of G4160<BR><B>Strong's:</B> manufactured, i.e. of human construction<BR><B>KJV:</B> made by (make with) hands.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5495<BR><I>See:</I> G4160<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5499 (made by hands), G886 (made without hands), G5495 (hand), G5498 (handwriting), G5497 (some to lead by the hand), G5496 (lead by the hand), G5500 (choose)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χειροποίητος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H457 אֱלִיל",
    5500: "χειροτονέω (cheirotonéō | khi-rot-on-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a comparative of G5495 and τείνω (to stretch)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be a hand-reacher or voter (by raising the hand), i.e. (generally) to select or appoint<BR><B>KJV:</B> choose, ordain.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5495<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5499 (made by hands), G886 (made without hands), G5495 (hand), G5498 (handwriting), G5497 (some to lead by the hand), G5496 (lead by the hand), G5500 (choose)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χειροτονέω",
    5501: "χείρων (cheírōn | khi'-rone)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> irregular comparative of G2556<BR><B>Strong's:</B> from an obsolete equivalent χέρης (of uncertain derivation); more evil or aggravated (physically, mentally or morally)<BR><B>KJV:</B> sorer, worse.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G2556<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5499 (made by hands), G886 (made without hands), G5495 (hand), G5498 (handwriting), G5497 (some to lead by the hand), G5496 (lead by the hand), G5500 (choose)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χείρων",
    5502: "χερουβίμ (cheroubím | kher-oo-beem')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> plural of Hebrew origin (H3742)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"cherubim\" (i.e. cherubs or kerubim)<BR><B>KJV:</B> cherubims.<BR><I>See:</I> H3742<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5502 (cherubims)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χερουβίμ, Χερούβ, Χεροῦβ, Χερουβίμ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3742 כְּרוּב",
    5503: "χήρα (chḗra | khay'-rah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of a presumed derivative apparently from the base of G5490 through the idea of deficiency<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a widow (as lacking a husband), literally or figuratively<BR><B>KJV:</B> widow.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5490<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5503 (widow)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χήρα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H490 אַלְמָנָה, H1565 גַּלְמוּד",
    5504: "χθές (chthés | khthes)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"yesterday\"; by extension, in time past or hitherto<BR><B>KJV:</B> yesterday.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5503 (widow)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χθές, ἐχθές<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H8543 תְּמֹול",
    5505: "χιλιάς (chiliás | khil-ee-as')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5507<BR><B>Strong's:</B> one thousand (\"chiliad\")<BR><B>KJV:</B> thousand.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5507<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5507 (thousand), G5506 (captain), G5505 (thousand)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χιλιάς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H505 אֶלֶף",
    5506: "χιλίαρχος (chilíarchos | khil-ee'-ar-khos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5507 and G757<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the commander of a thousand soldiers (\"chiliarch\"; i.e. colonel<BR><B>KJV:</B> (chief, high) captain.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5507<BR><I>See:</I> G757<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5507 (thousand), G5506 (captain), G5505 (thousand)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χιλίαρχος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H441 אַלּוּף, H8269 שַׂר",
    5507: "χίλιοι (chílioi | khil'-ee-oy)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> plural of uncertain affinity<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a thousand<BR><B>KJV:</B> thousand.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5507 (thousand), G5506 (captain), G5505 (thousand)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χίλιοι",
    5508: "Χίος (Chíos | khee'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Chios, an island in the Mediterranean<BR><B>KJV:</B> Chios.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5507 (thousand), G5506 (captain), G5505 (thousand)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Χίος, χίος",
    5509: "χιτών (chitṓn | khee-tone')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of foreign origin (H3801)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a tunic or shirt<BR><B>KJV:</B> clothes, coat, garment.<BR><I>See:</I> H3801<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5507 (thousand), G5506 (captain), G5505 (thousand)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χιτών<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H899 בֶּגֶד, H3801 כְּתֹנֶת, H3801 כְּתֹנֶת, H4055 מַד, H4598 מְעִיל",
    5510: "χιών (chiṓn | khee-one')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> perhaps akin to the base of G5490 (G5465) or G5494 (as descending or empty)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> snow<BR><B>KJV:</B> snow.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5490<BR><I>See:</I> G5465<BR><I>See:</I> G5494<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5507 (thousand), G5506 (captain), G5505 (thousand)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χιών<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7950 שֶׁלֶג, H8517 תְּלַג",
    5511: "χλαμύς (chlamýs | khlam-ooce')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a military cloak<BR><B>KJV:</B> robe.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5507 (thousand), G5506 (captain), G5505 (thousand)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χλαμύς",
    5512: "χλευάζω (chleuázō | khlyoo-ad'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative probably of G5491<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to throw out the lip, i.e. jeer at<BR><B>KJV:</B> mock.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5491<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5507 (thousand), G5506 (captain), G5505 (thousand)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χλευάζω, διαχλευάζω",
    5513: "χλιαρός (chliarós | khlee-ar-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from χλίω (to warm)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> tepid<BR><B>KJV:</B> lukewarm.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5507 (thousand), G5506 (captain), G5505 (thousand)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χλιαρός",
    5514: "Χλόη (Chlóē | khlo'-ay)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of apparently a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"green\"; Chloë, a Christian female<BR><B>KJV:</B> Chloe.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5507 (thousand), G5506 (captain), G5505 (thousand)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Χλόη, χλόη",
    5515: "χλωρός (chlōrós | khlo-ros')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as G5514<BR><B>Strong's:</B> greenish, i.e. verdant, dun-colored<BR><B>KJV:</B> green, pale.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5514<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5507 (thousand), G5506 (captain), G5505 (thousand)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χλωρός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2682 חָצִיר, H3418 יֶרֶק, H3836 לָבָן, H3892 לַח, H6168 עָרָה, H6212 עֶשֶׂב, H7879 שִׂיחַ",
    5516: "χξϛ (chx stigma | khee xee stig'-ma)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> the 22nd, 14th and an obsolete letter (G4742 as a cross) of the Greek alphabet (intermediate between the 5th and 6th), used as numbers; denoting respectively 600, 60 and 6<BR><B>Strong's:</B> 666 as a numeral<BR><B>KJV:</B> six hundred threescore and six.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4742<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5507 (thousand), G5506 (captain), G5505 (thousand)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χξϛ, χιϚ’, χξϚ’ G5940, G5947, G5953",
    5517: "χοϊκός (choïkós | kho-ik-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5522<BR><B>Strong's:</B> dusty or dirty (soil-like), i.e. (by implication) terrene<BR><B>KJV:</B> earthy.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5522<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5517 (earthy)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χοϊκός",
    5518: "χοῖνιξ (choînix | khoy'-nix)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a chœnix or certain dry measure<BR><B>KJV:</B> measure.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5517 (earthy)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χοῖνιξ<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1324 בַּת",
    5519: "χοῖρος (choîros | khoy'-ros)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a hog<BR><B>KJV:</B> swine.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5517 (earthy)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χοῖρος",
    5520: "χολάω (choláō | khol-ah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5521<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be bilious, i.e. (by implication) irritable (enraged, \"choleric\")<BR><B>KJV:</B> be angry.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5521<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5517 (earthy)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χολάω",
    5521: "χολή (cholḗ | khol-ay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> feminine of an equivalent perhaps akin to the same as 5514 (from the greenish hue)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"gall\" or bile, i.e. (by analogy) poison or an anodyne (wormwood, poppy, etc.)<BR><B>KJV:</B> gall.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5517 (earthy)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χολή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3939 לַעֲנָה, H4845 מְרֵרָה, H7218 רֹאשׁ",
    5522: "χόος (chóos | kho'-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G5494<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a heap (as poured out), i.e. rubbish; loose dirt<BR><B>KJV:</B> dust.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5494<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5517 (earthy)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χόος, χοῦς",
    5523: "Χοραζίν (Chorazín | khor-ad-zin')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Chorazin, a place in Palestine<BR><B>KJV:</B> Chorazin.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5517 (earthy)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Χοραζίν, Χωραζίν, χοραζίν",
    5524: "χορηγέω (chorēgéō | khor-ayg-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a compound of G5525 and G71<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be a dance-leader, i.e. (generally) to furnish<BR><B>KJV:</B> give, minister.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5525<BR><I>See:</I> G71<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5525 (dancing), G5524 (give)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χορηγέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2110 זוּן, H3557 כּוּל",
    5525: "χορός (chorós | khor-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain derivation<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a ring, i.e. round dance (\"choir\"<BR><B>KJV:</B> dancing.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5525 (dancing), G5524 (give)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χορός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1974 הִלּוּל, H2256 חֶבֶל, H4234 מָחֹול, H4246 מְחֹלָה",
    5526: "χορτάζω (chortázō | khor-tad'-zo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5528<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to fodder, i.e. (generally) to gorge (supply food in abundance)<BR><B>KJV:</B> feed, fill, satisfy.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5528<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5528 (blade), G5526 (feed), G5527 (sustenance)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χορτάζω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7646 שָׂבַע",
    5527: "χόρτασμα (chórtasma | khor'-tas-mah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5526<BR><B>Strong's:</B> forage, i.e. food<BR><B>KJV:</B> sustenance.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5526<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5528 (blade), G5526 (feed), G5527 (sustenance)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χόρτασμα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4554 מִסְפֹּוא, H6212 עֶשֶׂב",
    5528: "χόρτος (chórtos | khor'-tos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a \"court\" or \"garden\", i.e. (by implication, of pasture) herbage or vegetation<BR><B>KJV:</B> blade, grass, hay.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5528 (blade), G5526 (feed), G5527 (sustenance)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χόρτος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1877 דֶּשֶׁא, H2682 חָצִיר, H6212 עֶשֶׂב, H7179 קַשׁ",
    5529: "Χουζᾶς (Chouzâs | khood-zas')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of uncertain origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Chuzas, an officer of Herod<BR><B>KJV:</B> Chuza.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5528 (blade), G5526 (feed), G5527 (sustenance)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Χουζᾶς, χουζᾶς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4596 מְעִי, H4671 מֹץ, H6083 עָפָר",
    5530: "χράομαι (chráomai | khrah'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> middle voice of a primary verb (perhaps rather from G5495, to handle)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to furnish what is needed; (give an oracle, \"graze\" (touch slightly), light upon, etc.), i.e. (by implication) to employ or (by extension) to act towards one in a given manner<BR><B>KJV:</B> entreat, use. Compare G5531 ; G5534 .<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5531<BR><I>See:</I> G5495<BR><I>See:</I> G5534<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5528 (blade), G5526 (feed), G5527 (sustenance)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χράομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H113 אָדֹון, H1167 בַּעַל, H3190 יָטַב, H6213 עָשָׂה, H6743 צָלַח, H7592 שָׁאַל",
    5531: "χράω (chráō | khrah'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably the same as the base of G5530<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to loan<BR><B>KJV:</B> lend.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5530<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5528 (blade), G5526 (feed), G5527 (sustenance)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χράω, κίχρημι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3867 לָוָה",
    5532: "χρεία (chreía | khri'-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the base of G5530 or G5534<BR><B>Strong's:</B> employment, i.e. an affair; also (by implication) occasion, demand, requirement or destitution<BR><B>KJV:</B> business, lack, necessary(-ity), need(-ful), use, want.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5534<BR><I>See:</I> G5530<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5528 (blade), G5526 (feed), G5527 (sustenance)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χρεία<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2818 חֲשַׁח, H2819 חַשְׁחוּת, H6878 צֹרֶךְ",
    5533: "χρεωφειλέτης (chreōpheilétēs | khreh-o-fi-let'-ace)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of G5531 and G3781<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a loan-ower, i.e. indebted person<BR><B>KJV:</B> debtor.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5531<BR><I>See:</I> G3781<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5528 (blade), G5526 (feed), G5527 (sustenance)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χρεωφειλέτης, χρεοφειλέτης, χρεοφειλέτης/χρεωφειλέτης",
    5534: "χρή (chrḗ | khray)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> third person singular of the same as G5530 or G5531 used impersonally<BR><B>Strong's:</B> it needs (must or should) be<BR><B>KJV:</B> ought.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5530<BR><I>See:</I> G5531<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5528 (blade), G5526 (feed), G5527 (sustenance)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χρή",
