    5539: "χρήσιμος (chrḗsimos | khray'-see-mos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5540<BR><B>Strong's:</B> serviceable<BR><B>KJV:</B> profit.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5540<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5539 (profit), G5540 (use)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χρήσιμος, χρήσιμον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1215 בֶּצַע, H6743 צָלַח",
    5540: "χρῆσις (chrēsis | khray'-sis)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5530<BR><B>Strong's:</B> employment, i.e. (specially), sexual intercourse (as an occupation of the body)<BR><B>KJV:</B> use.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5530<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5539 (profit), G5540 (use)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χρῆσις<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7592 שָׁאַל",
    5541: "χρηστεύομαι (chrēsteúomai | khraste-yoo'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> middle voice from G5543<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to show oneself useful, i.e. act benevolently<BR><B>KJV:</B> be kind.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5543<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5542 (good words), G5541 (be kind), G5544 (gentleness), G5543 (better)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χρηστεύομαι",
