    5546: "Χριστιανός (Christianós | khris-tee-an-os')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5547<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a Christian, i.e. follower of Christ<BR><B>KJV:</B> Christian.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5547<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5545 (anointing), G5580 (false Christ), G5546 (Christian), G500 (antichrist), G5547 (Christ), G5548 (anoint)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Χριστιανός, χριστιανός",
    5547: "Χριστός (Christós | khris-tos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5548<BR><B>Strong's:</B> anointed, i.e. the Messiah, an epithet of Jesus<BR><B>KJV:</B> Christ.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5548<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5545 (anointing), G5580 (false Christ), G5546 (Christian), G500 (antichrist), G5547 (Christ), G5548 (anoint)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Χριστός, χριστός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1325 בַּת",
    5548: "χρίω (chríō | khree'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably akin to G5530 through the idea of contact<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to smear or rub with oil, i.e. (by implication) to consecrate to an office or religious service<BR><B>KJV:</B> anoint.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5530<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5545 (anointing), G5580 (false Christ), G5546 (Christian), G500 (antichrist), G5547 (Christ), G5548 (anoint)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χρίω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3251 יָסַךְ, H4886 מָשַׁח, H5480 סוּךְ",
