    5554: "χρυσοδακτύλιος (chrysodaktýlios | khroo-sod-ak-too'-lee-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5557 and G1146<BR><B>Strong's:</B> gold-ringed, i.e. wearing a golden finger-ring or similar jewelry<BR><B>KJV:</B> with a gold ring.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5557<BR><I>See:</I> G1146<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5550 (+ years old), G5549 (delay), G5551 (spend time)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χρυσοδακτύλιος",
    5555: "χρυσόλιθος (chrysólithos | khroo-sol'-ee-thos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5557 and G3037<BR><B>Strong's:</B> gold-stone, i.e. a yellow gem (\"chrysolite\")<BR><B>KJV:</B> chrysolite.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5557<BR><I>See:</I> G3037<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5550 (+ years old), G5549 (delay), G5551 (spend time)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χρυσόλιθος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H8658 תַּרְשִׁישׁ",
    5556: "χρυσόπρασος (chrysóprasos | khroo-sop'-ras-os)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5557 and πράσον (a leek)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> a greenish-yellow gem (\"chrysoprase\")<BR><B>KJV:</B> chrysoprase.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5557<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5550 (+ years old), G5549 (delay), G5551 (spend time)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χρυσόπρασος",
    5557: "χρυσός (chrysós | khroo-sos')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> perhaps from the base of G5530 (through the idea of the utility of the metal)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> gold; by extension, a golden article, as an ornament or coin<BR><B>KJV:</B> gold.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5530<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5550 (+ years old), G5549 (delay), G5551 (spend time)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χρυσός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2091 זָהָב, H2742 חֲרוּץ",
    5558: "χρυσόω (chrysóō | khroo-so'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5557<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to gild, i.e. bespangle with golden ornaments<BR><B>KJV:</B> deck.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5557<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5550 (+ years old), G5549 (delay), G5551 (spend time)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χρυσόω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2645 חָפָה, H6823 צָפָה",
    5559: "χρώς (chrṓs | khroce)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably akin to the base of G5530 through the idea of handling<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the body (properly, its surface or skin)<BR><B>KJV:</B> body.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5530<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5550 (+ years old), G5549 (delay), G5551 (spend time)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χρώς<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H216 אֹור, H1320 בָּשָׂר",
    5560: "χωλός (chōlós | kho-los')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> \"halt\", i.e. limping<BR><B>KJV:</B> cripple, halt, lame.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5550 (+ years old), G5549 (delay), G5551 (spend time)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χωλός<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6455 פִּסֵּחַ",
