    5565: "χωρίς (chōrís | kho-rece')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> adverb from G5561<BR><B>Strong's:</B> at a space, i.e. separately or apart from (often as preposition)<BR><B>KJV:</B> beside, by itself, without.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5561<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5550 (+ years old), G5549 (delay), G5551 (spend time)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χωρίς",
    5566: "χῶρος (chōros | kho'-ros)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Latin origin<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the north-west wind<BR><B>KJV:</B> north west.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5550 (+ years old), G5549 (delay), G5551 (spend time)<BR><B>Variants:</B> χῶρος",
    5567: "ψάλλω (psállō | psal'-lo)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably strengthened from ψάω (to rub or touch the surface<BR><B>Strong's:</B> compare G5597); to twitch or twang, i.e. to play on a stringed instrument (celebrate the divine worship with music and accompanying odes)<BR><B>KJV:</B> make melody, sing (psalms).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5597<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5567 (make melody), G5568 (psalm)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ψάλλω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H2167 זָמַר, H5059 נָגַן",
