    5590: "ψυχή (psychḗ | psoo-khay')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5594<BR><B>Strong's:</B> breath, i.e. (by implication) spirit, abstractly or concretely (the animal sentient principle only; thus distinguished on the one hand from G4151, which is the rational and immortal soul; and on the other from G2222, which is mere vitality, even of plants: these terms thus exactly correspond respectively to the Hebrew H5315, H7307 and H2416)<BR><B>KJV:</B> heart (+ -ily), life, mind, soul, + us, + you.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5594<BR><I>See:</I> G4151<BR><I>See:</I> G2222<BR><I>See:</I> H5315<BR><I>See:</I> H7307<BR><I>See:</I> H2416<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G1374 (double minded), G5591 (natural), G5590 (heart), G3642 (feebleminded), G404 (refresh), G403 (revival)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ψυχή<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H376 אִישׁ, H2416 חַי, H3820 לֵב, H3824 לֵבָב, H5315 נֶפֶשׁ, H7307 רוּחַ",
