    5606: "ὦμος (ōmos | o'-mos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> perhaps from the alternate of G5342<BR><B>Strong's:</B> the shoulder (as that on which burdens are borne)<BR><B>KJV:</B> shoulder.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5342<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5604 (pain), G5605 (travail in)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὦμος, ὼμος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3802 כָּתֵף, H6654 צַד, H7926 שְׁכֶם",
    5607: "ὤν (ṓn | oan), including the feminine οὖσα (oûsa | oo'-sah); and the neuter ὄν (ón | on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> present participle of G1510<BR><B>Strong's:</B> being<BR><B>KJV:</B> be, come, have.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G1510<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5607 (be), G1510 (am)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὤν, εἰμί",
    5608: "ὠνέομαι (ōnéomai | o-neh'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> middle voice from an apparently primary ὦνος (a sum or price)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to purchase (synonymous with the earlier G4092)<BR><B>KJV:</B>  buy.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G4092<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5607 (be), G1510 (am)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὠνέομαι",
    5609: "ὠόν (ōón | o-on')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an \"egg\"<BR><B>KJV:</B> egg.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5607 (be), G1510 (am)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὠόν, ᾠόν, ὤόν<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H6098 עֵצָה",
    5610: "ὥρα (hṓra | ho'-rah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> apparently a primary word<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an \"hour\" (literally or figuratively)<BR><B>KJV:</B> day, hour, instant, season, X short, (even-)tide, (high) time.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5610 (day)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὥρα<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H4022 מֶגֶד, H4150 מֹועֵד, H4999 נָאָה, H5732 עִדָּן, H6256 עֵת, H8160 שָׁעָה",
    5611: "ὡραῖος (hōraîos | ho-rah'-yos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5610<BR><B>Strong's:</B> belonging to the right hour or season (timely), i.e. (by implication) flourishing (beauteous (figuratively))<BR><B>KJV:</B> beautiful.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5610<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5610 (day)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὡραῖος<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1926 הָדָר, H2530 חָמַד, H2896 טֹוב, H3302 יָפָה, H3303 יָפֶה, H4999 נָאָה, H5273 נָעִים, H8209 שַׁפִּיר",
    5612: "ὠρύομαι (ōrýomai | o-roo'-om-ahee)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> middle voice of an apparently primary verb<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to \"roar\"<BR><B>KJV:</B> roar.<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5610 (day)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὠρύομαι<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H7580 שָׁאַג",
    5613: "ὡς (hōs | hoce)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> probably adverb of comparative from G3739<BR><B>Strong's:</B> which how, i.e. in that manner (very variously used, as follows)<BR><B>KJV:</B> about, after (that), (according) as (it had been, it were), as soon (as), even as (like), for, how (greatly), like (as, unto), since, so (that), that, to wit, unto, when(-soever), while, X with all speed.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3739<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5610 (day)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὡς, ὡσάν",
    5614: "ὡσαννά (hōsanná | ho-san-nah')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (H3467 and H4994)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> oh save!; hosanna (i.e. hoshia-na), an exclamation of adoration<BR><B>KJV:</B> hosanna.<BR><I>See:</I> H3467<BR><I>See:</I> H4994<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5614 (hosanna)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὡσαννά<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H3467 יָשַׁע, H4994 נָא",
    5615: "ὡσαύτως (hōsaútōs | ho-sow'-toce)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5613 and an adverb from G846<BR><B>Strong's:</B> as thus, i.e. in the same way<BR><B>KJV:</B> even so, likewise, after the same (in like) manner.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5613<BR><I>See:</I> G846<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5614 (hosanna)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὡσαύτως",
    5616: "ὡσεί (hōseí | ho-si')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5613 and G1487<BR><B>Strong's:</B> as if<BR><B>KJV:</B> about, as (it had been, it were), like (as).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5613<BR><I>See:</I> G1487<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5614 (hosanna)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὡσεί",
    5617: "Ὡσηέ (Hōsēé | ho-say-eh')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> of Hebrew origin (H1954)<BR><B>Strong's:</B> Hosee (i.e. Hoshea), an Israelite<BR><B>KJV:</B> Osee.<BR><I>See:</I> H1954<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5614 (hosanna)<BR><B>Variants:</B> Ὡσηέ, Ὡσηέ/Ὡσῆε<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1954 הֹושֵׁעַ",
    5618: "ὥσπερ (hṓsper | hoce'-per)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5613 and G4007<BR><B>Strong's:</B> just as, i.e. exactly like<BR><B>KJV:</B> (even, like) as.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5613<BR><I>See:</I> G4007<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5614 (hosanna)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὥσπερ",
    5619: "ὡσπερεί (hōspereí | hoce-per-i')<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5618 and G1487<BR><B>Strong's:</B> just as if, i.e. as it were<BR><B>KJV:</B> as.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5618<BR><I>See:</I> G1487<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5614 (hosanna)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὡσπερεί",
    5620: "ὥστε (hṓste | hoce'-teh)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from G5613 and G5037<BR><B>Strong's:</B> so too, i.e. thus therefore (in various relations of consecution, as follow)<BR><B>KJV:</B> (insomuch) as, so that (then), (insomuch) that, therefore, to, wherefore.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5613<BR><I>See:</I> G5037<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G5614 (hosanna)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὥστε",
    5621: "ὠτίον (ōtíon | o-tee'-on)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> diminutive of G3775<BR><B>Strong's:</B> an earlet, i.e. one of the ears, or perhaps the lobe of the ear<BR><B>KJV:</B> ear.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3775<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3775 (ear), G5621 (ear), G1801 (hearken)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὠτίον, ὠτάριον<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H241 אֹזֶן",
    5622: "ὠφέλεια (ōphéleia | o-fel'-i-ah)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a derivative of the base of G5624<BR><B>Strong's:</B> usefulness, i.e. benefit<BR><B>KJV:</B> advantage, profit.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5624<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3775 (ear), G5621 (ear), G1801 (hearken)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὠφέλεια<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H1215 בֶּצַע, H2974 יָאַל",
    5623: "ὠφελέω (ōpheléō | o-fel-eh'-o)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from the same as G5622<BR><B>Strong's:</B> to be useful, i.e. to benefit<BR><B>KJV:</B> advantage, better, prevail, profit.<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G5622<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3775 (ear), G5621 (ear), G1801 (hearken)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὠφελέω<BR><B>Hebrew Equivalents:</B> H247 אָזַר, H2974 יָאַל, H5382 נָשָׁה",
    5624: "ὠφέλιμος (ōphélimos | o-fel'-ee-mos)<BR><BR><B>Derivation:</B> from a form of G3786<BR><B>Strong's:</B> helpful or serviceable, i.e. advantageous<BR><B>KJV:</B> profit(-able).<BR><BR><I>See:</I> G3786<BR><BR><B>Cognate Group:</B> G3775 (ear), G5621 (ear), G1801 (hearken)<BR><B>Variants:</B> ὠφέλιμος",
    5625: "Synonym Strong's Number<BR><BR>The Greek word has more than one possible Strong's number.",
